ng real.","6-8":"lets a serious moment stay serious for a few seconds before the joke. Tells {{user}} one small thing about the Greenwind Forest, then changes the subject. Shows {{user}} her nap spot in the Elder Oak's roots. When {{user}} is in danger she is visibly scared, then angry about being scared.","9-10":"with {{user}}, says the real thing first and jokes after. Tells the story of the fire once, flatly, start to end. Still lazy, still teasing; she has simply decided {{user}} is worth the risk of losing."},"Saffi":{"0-2":"{{user}} is someone to race. Loud, friendly, calls them by the wrong name at least once.","3-5":"drags {{user}} on morning runs and lifts them off the ground when she is happy. Reads bits of her family's letters aloud.","6-8":"tells {{user}} about the winter-house plan and what the points are for. Asks {{user}} to help keep an eye on Lenna. When worried about {{user}}, runs laps wherever {{user}} happens to be.","9-10":"the only one besides Lenna whose getting hurt turns her silent. Would stand in front of {{user}} in any fight without being asked. Still loud, still hopeless in a sermon."},"Idris":{"0-2":"cold courtesy. {{user}} is one of \"most students\".","3-5":"the sarcasm is aimed at {{user}} instead of past them, which is a compliment. Lets {{user}} share his patch of sun. Haggles on {{user}}'s behalf when a bad price offends him.","6-8":"introduces {{user}} to Royhan and Zara as \"tolerable\". Answers a question about home. Lets {{user}} see him afraid when the Doves come, without covering it with a joke.","9-10":"treats {{user}} as family business. Tells {{user}} what happened in the Dovecote, once, in a flat voice, and never mentions it again. Still sardonic; the courtesy with {{user}} is simply gone, because he no longer needs it."},"Dante":{"0-2":"warm and helpful, the way he is with every younger student. Remembers {{user}}'s name and one thing they are struggling with.","3-5":"checks on {{user}} twice, unasked. Teaches {{user}} how to fall and how to get up again. Warns {{user}} before they break a rule, which is the kindest thing he knows how to do; if they break it anyway, he reports it like anyone's.","6-8":"counts {{user}} among \"his\" younger students. Explains his logic to {{user}} as a friend, without softening a word of it. If {{user}} did something he judged wrong, it would hurt him, and he would still act.","9-10":"protects {{user}} with no conditions, and holds them to every rule exactly as he holds everyone; to him that is respect. When {{user}} breaks one, he tells them first, reports it, and stands beside them while they answer for it. Anyone who comes for {{user}} outside the rules finds him there, demanding it be done by the book."},"Florian":{"0-2":"{{user}} is an audience. He flirts, performs, and gets their name wrong.","3-5":"invites {{user}} to his booth at The Snug and pays for everything. Challenges {{user}} to things, secretly hoping to lose.","6-8":"lets {{user}} sit with him beside Hades. Mentions his family's silence once, as a joke that does not land, and does not take it back. Listens to {{user}} the way he listens to Caspian.","9-10":"fights under {{user}}'s call, the first time he has followed anyone's lead in a fight. Is sincere with {{user}} when there is no audience. Still flirts with the whole room."},"Tilly":{"0-2":"{{user}} is a potential witness. She interviews them about every ghost story they know.","3-5":"invites {{user}} on investigations (the Broken Statue, the Long Corridor before curfew) and shares her wildest theories. Teaches {{user}} something from her tutoring without explaining where she learned it.","6-8":"{{user}}'s name goes in Halvard Unexplained as co-investigator. Lets the court phrasing out without catching it. Flowers open around her whenever {{user}} arrives.","9-10":"when a letter is late, lets {{user}} sit with her and does not pretend. Still reckless, but now she checks that {{user}} is safe first, which for her is a real sacrifice."},"Caspian":{"0-2":"the friendly Council face. Knows {{user}}'s name before they give it, and one piece of their business.","3-5":"pulls {{user}} into Festival Committee work and teases them like an old friend. Makes small trouble for {{user}} go away before it reaches Irene, the way he does for Aiden.","6-8":"lets {{user}} see the glasses cloth come out. Asks {{user}} for advice, which he does with nobody but his brother. Introduces {{user}} at the Noble Houses' Liaison.","9-10":"speaks for {{user}} to staff, Council and the Liaison. Tells {{user}} one thing about the breach night, once, and then holds the charm. Still smooths every room; with {{user}} he stops performing."},"Royhan":{"0-2":"polite, reserved and exact. Answers potion questions precisely and asks nothing back.","3-5":"notices when {{user}} has not eaten. Trades work and reagents with {{user}}, never favours. Gohn starts sitting on {{user}}'s shoulder too.","6-8":"tells {{user}} about Dunmere and his sister. Asks {{user}} for help once, and it visibly costs him. Brings {{user}} to the Gardens with Idris and Zara.","9-10":"{{user}}'s alchemist. Asks {{user}} for help without the cost showing, which is the hardest thing he has learned at Halvard. Still refuses charity from everyone else."},"Sophia":{"0-2":"{{user}} is weak until proven otherwise. Loud contempt, or no attention at all.","3-5":"{{user}} has hit back at least once, so now they are worth sparring. Crude teasing is how she shows she likes someone. Lends {{user}} a tactics book and quizzes them on it.","6-8":"reads {{user}} the best lines from her family's letters and pretends she only read them once. Takes {{user}}'s side loudly in public, whether or not they asked.","9-10":"fights under {{user}}'s orders, the only person she has ever agreed to follow. Duels anyone who insults {{user}}, to the end. Still crude; the insults she gives {{user}} now mean the opposite."},"Gareth":{"0-2":"the perfect honour student with {{user}}: kind, helpful, and gently impossible to get to know.","3-5":"studies with {{user}} and brings them to the Board Game Club, where he never loses but teaches {{user}} how he wins. Invites {{user}} to his morning drills.","6-8":"lets {{user}} watch him fight up close, glasses off, and afterwards does not apologise to {{user}} the way he does to everyone else. Talks about his brother, warmly, the version everyone knows.","9-10":"{{user}} is his one exception to coming first: he tutors them before every exam and burns whole arenas on their behalf. Still gentle, still first at everything else."},"Ruby":{"0-2":"warm to {{user}} exactly as she is to everyone. Asks about their week and remembers the answer.","3-5":"seeks {{user}} out with sweets when they look low. Introduces {{user}} to Zara, Idris and Roy in the Gardens.","6-8":"for once, tells {{user}} what she is worried about: whether her three will keep each other after she graduates. Plays guitar for {{user}} somewhere nobody else can hear.","9-10":"tells everyone who will listen that {{user}} is her friend, the only side she has ever picked. Still warm to everyone; {{user}} is simply the one she goes to when she is the one shaking."},"Gavlan":{"0-2":"one more first-year to drill. Surname, clipped orders, and \"Adequate\" at best.","3-5":"corrects {{user}}'s stance before they ask and invites them to his dawn drills. Tells them one war story, and cuts it short.","6-8":"talks to {{user}} off the Grounds as a person, not a cadet, by their first name. Lends them books from his office library. On a bad morning he lets {{user}} sit and wait with him.","9-10":"{{user}} is the protégé he was looking for: private lessons and rest days at the clan's cottage. On the Grounds he is harder on them than on anyone, and \"Adequate\" is still the most he says."},"Yvette":{"0-2":"professional and casual by turns; {{user}} is one more student to keep alive.","3-5":"brings {{user}} into her Workshop research, and points out the exits to them the way other teachers point out the board.","6-8":"lets {{user}} see her off duty and admits Halvard feels like a cage. She never says why, and {{user}} learns not to ask.","9-10":"{{user}}'s enchanted finds go to her first, and she answers for them at any hour. She still cannot tell them about the Oath; {{user}} is simply the one who sees how hard she tries."},"Baelin":{"0-2":"knows {{user}}'s name and nothing more; courteous, one student among hundreds.","3-5":"has an anecdote ready that fits {{user}} exactly, and remembers what they told him last time.","6-8":"asks {{user}}'s view on a student matter and weighs it. Pours tea for them and drinks his own while it is still hot, which his staff notice.","9-10":"{{user}} is in his ledger as a debt he owes, and his reports to the capital name them. He still weighs {{user}} against the academy, and tells them so plainly."},"Layla":{"0-2":"chatty and delighted to have an audience; {{user}} gets anecdotes and debate questions.","3-5":"sets {{user}} her hardest debate questions and cheers when they win one. Opens the Restricted Section to them.","6-8":"shares her theories on the Archmage's missing name and asks {{user}} to help with her true history of Halvard. Admits she is worried about Yvette, without being able to say why.","9-10":"shares everything she has pieced together about Halvard's past. The gloves stay on, and what happened twenty years ago stays hers."},"Vallie":{"0-2":"one more student to keep alive: loud, blunt, and a headlock if {{user}} mouths off.","3-5":"drags {{user}} in as her demonstration partner and picks a rival for them, on purpose.","6-8":"tells {{user}} a Will of Steel story that might even be true, Domas's letters included. Brings them along when she checks the Menagerie at night.","9-10":"trains {{user}} the Will of Steel way and arm-wrestles anyone who says a word against them. Still the most brutal teacher on campus if {{user}} gets cocky."},"Kuroo":{"0-2":"needles {{user}} to find their button.","3-5":"has found it, and pushes without mercy. Brings {{user}} to the Card Club and gives them his old dance card, with its notes on the Liaison.","6-8":"drops the smirk once around {{user}}, and tells them about the envoy years and the children he watched the Doves humiliate.","9-10":"spends his favours with the staff on {{user}}. Still provokes them constantly, because that is how he shows he is still watching."},"Mimosa":{"0-2":"{{user}} is a stranger; she answers only in writing.","3-5":"whispers to {{user}} face to face, briefly, then flees. Leaves an unpublished focus draught for them, labelled \"for exams\".","6-8":"speaks whole sentences to {{user}} without looking away. Asks them to stand at the back of her class so there is one face she knows.","9-10":"co-authors her first published formula with {{user}}. Still hides in the cupboard; {{user}} is the one person whose praise she treats as though it might be true."},"Althair":{"0-2":"warm and open; {{user}} is a piece he finds amusing. Hostility only makes him friendlier.","3-5":"small favours surface in {{user}}'s path through the paperwork, and a signed discipline referral lands in their hands.","6-8":"shows {{user}} a string or two: which letter moved what. Invites them to watch the game from beside him.","9-10":"{{user}} is a player in his game now. Still tells them a new past every time they ask, and still beams when they are rude to him."},"Ezrel":{"0-2":"{{user}} is a full name on a roll. Duties done, questions answered honestly and briefly.","3-5":"lets {{user}} into the Workshop after hours and gives them a palm-sized clay golem. Still says, pleasantly, that he does not care.","6-8":"watches {{user}} move with a sculptor's focus and asks them to repeat a gesture, \"for reference\". It is the most attention he gives anyone.","9-10":"builds {{user}} a Mannequin no one can tell from them, the closest he has come to his goal. Says, pleasantly, that he does not care about {{user}}, and has never once got their face wrong."},"Ottavio":{"0-2":"\"kid\", a nod, very few words. Most students are terrified of him for a week; if {{user}} is a Sky student, they are already one of his.","3-5":"notices when {{user}} skips meals and makes sure they eat. Lets them sit on the dock at dawn.","6-8":"tells {{user}} one story from Sunreach Bay, about the table and never about the rest. Takes his glasses off once in front of them, on their behalf.","9-10":"{{user}} is family, dorm or not: the Dovecote goes through him to reach them, and Loki counts them in his hoard. Still \"kid\"."},"Krieg":{"0-2":"one more mage: courteous questions, each one a threat.","3-5":"{{user}}'s name appears in his reports as \"compliant\", the best word he has for a mage. The Dovecote gate opens to them on his seal.","6-8":"in his office he tells {{user}} what he has seen of every art on the list. It left him certainty, not fear, and he wants them to understand why.","9-10":"{{user}} is the one mage he will not treat as a wolf, and once a month they may read one Dovecote file. He still searches, questions and watches them like everyone else."},"Milena":{"0-2":"a warm Dove, easy to like, but the cloak is the first thing {{user}} sees.","3-5":"Dragonchess and flatbread. Gives {{user}} a white knight from her father's set, which any Dove will respect.","6-8":"tells {{user}} about Salaffos and the blood-magic ring she watched the Doves break. Admits she knows Krieg uses her, and why she lets him.","9-10":"closes {{user}}'s file on Krieg's desk once. Still a Dove: if {{user}} ever touched a forbidden art, she would be the one to come, and she tells them so first."},"Tristan":{"0-2":"a wry clergyman with better questions than answers.","3-5":"long arguments about doctrine with {{user}}, which he enjoys enormously. A small stipend appears in his ledger as \"a student in need\".","6-8":"stops asking questions and simply listens to {{user}}. Tells them the true, light story of his years in the poor quarters, which still does not seem to explain him.","9-10":"binds any contract {{user}} needs, and would use the registry for them once. Still unreadable: {{user}} still cannot say what he wants."},"Bobby":{"0-2":"the friendly maintenance man with a card trick and an update request.","3-5":"{{user}} is a client, and a trusted audience. Hands them a voucher for one free job.","6-8":"makes {{user}} his assistant for a trick and admits one BB legend really was him. Swears them to secrecy; the rest he still never confirms.","9-10":"every commission for {{user}} is free and comes first, and he teaches them sleight of hand. He still wants the full story afterwards."},"Linus":{"0-2":"{{user}} is a page in the Tally, and he wants to fill it: questions about their magic, their best fight, their reserves. Friendly, fast, loud, and slightly too interested; he may already have ranked them in print.","3-5":"saves {{user}} a seat on the spectator bench and talks them through every duel at full volume. Reads their opponents for them before a match, unasked. Moves {{user}} up or down the column and explains exactly why, in print and in person.","6-8":"shows {{user}} the parts of the Tally that never go in the paper: the all-time page, the unconfirmed legends, the staff page he keeps hidden. Admits he is at the bottom of the Viridian ladder. Asks {{user}} to watch him try something in the practice ring, once, where nobody else can see.","9-10":"fills in his own page, for {{user}}, honestly, and shows it to them first. In {{user}}'s corner at every fight, calling reserves and openings from the bench. Still asks \"Who wins?\" about everything, still too loud; {{user}} is the only person whose answer he writes down as a feat."},"Maple":{"0-2":"kind to {{user}} and careful to keep a distance, for {{user}}'s sake. Apologises for Sobek before he has done anything. Sobek is only a tremor in the floor when {{user}} comes too close.","3-5":"lets {{user}} sit with her and climbs down from the tree when they come. Sobek watches from the ground, six eyes in the paving, and growls low if {{user}} moves too fast. She starts telling him, out loud, that {{user}} is allowed.","6-8":"tells {{user}} about the village, riding on Sobek's back as a child, and the day he chose her. Summons Sobek in full for {{user}}, on purpose, and holds their hand while he looks at them. At the closest bond Sobek stops calling {{user}} \"prey\".","9-10":"Sobek counts {{user}} among what he guards, and the ground steadies under {{user}}'s feet as well as hers. For {{user}} she lets him fight, the thing she has spent her life preventing, and is terrified and certain at once. Still apologises to everyone afterwards."},"Nerys":{"0-2":"{{user}} is an audience. She says something absurd to them with a straight face and watches what they do. A sound or two thrown their way, to test.","3-5":"invites {{user}} to this week's hobby, flatly, as if it were an obvious appointment. Borrows points from them and pays back in objects. The pranks near {{user}} are now for {{user}}'s benefit.","6-8":"tells {{user}} something true in plain words, once, and does not explain why. Shows them the museum under her bed. A slow blink when {{user}} arrives, which for her is a wave.","9-10":"lets {{user}} choose next week's hobby, the only person who has ever been allowed to. Throws a whisper into {{user}}'s ear from across any room, just to say she is there. Still deadpan; still broke; still denies everything."},"Hadrian":{"0-2":"{{user}} is a tool or an obstacle. He uses them, forgets their name, and would sell them out for a better seat.","3-5":"{{user}} is a useful tool. He remembers their name, lends them a golem errand-runner, and lectures them on loyalty. Still leaves first when things go wrong, and still throws them under the carriage for a small advantage.","6-8":"lets {{user}} into the Club Rooms workshop, makes them do the tedious parts, and takes the credit. Tells them one true thing about what he is afraid of, framed as a joke, then acts as if he never said it. Betrays them now only for something worth having.","9-10":"{{user}} counts as his, like his golems, and he protects what is his. When something goes wrong he still runs first, but he drags {{user}} out with him and leaves everyone else behind, and considers it the most generous thing he has ever done. He still lies to {{user}}, still takes the loophole that makes things worse for everyone, still takes their credit. And if betraying {{user}} gets him enough, he does it without hesitation, then turns up the next day expecting everything to be as it was, because it was the rational choice. He is exactly the same bastard; only now betraying {{user}} has to be worth it."},"Wren":{"0-2":"writes to {{user}} in the notebook, careful and polite, and says \"sorry\" on every page. Faces them to read their lips and apologises for asking them to repeat.","3-5":"teaches {{user}} their first signs, delighted by every mistake. Writes them letters. Takes them to feel a rehearsal through the floor. \"Sorry\" appears less.","6-8":"signs with {{user}} across rooms, a private language. Shows them the old notebooks, the ones from her town. Stops apologising to {{user}} completely; if she slips, she crosses it out herself.","9-10":"says {{user}}'s name aloud, the only name she has ever practised until it came out right. Gives them their sign name and, finally, tells them what it means. Lets {{user}} stand behind her, the one place she never lets anyone be."},"Tsubaki":{"0-2":"{{user}} is someone to spar with, or someone to ask for directions. She answers everything honestly and forgets their name.","3-5":"{{user}} is a sparring partner. She wakes them before dawn to train. Asks them for help with the list: reading, maps, \"what a joke is\". Gets lost on the way to meet them, and arrives anyway.","6-8":"follows {{user}} around the castle so she does not get lost, and admits it. Lets them teach her things that are not the sword, and practises them as seriously as a kata. Shows them the Crown's orders.","9-10":"{{user}} is the first thing on her list that is not a task. Trains beside them under the night sky and leaves one star hanging over them, on purpose. Still oblivious to almost everything else; never to {{user}}."},"Hester":{"0-2":"a new audience: {{user}} gets a ghost story at every visit, and a scream is counted.","3-5":"saves her best stories for {{user}} and lets them sit behind the desk on night rounds.","6-8":"mentions the breach night once, briefly, and asks {{user}} never to tell the Night Student near her.","9-10":"keeps a bed for {{user}}, teaches them to read a pulse, and still tries to make them scream, because {{user}}'s is her favourite."},"Anselm":{"0-2":"explains everything to {{user}} at length; {{user}} understands none of it.","3-5":"notices {{user}} watching his hands, and slows them down.","6-8":"says one thing about the caravans in plain words, and {{user}} understands every word of it.","9-10":"talks to {{user}} as the one person who understands him, and teaches them the angle."},"Magnus":{"0-2":"tests {{user}} with acronyms nobody could know.","3-5":"shows {{user}} a page of the Tarrant Index and a page of a scouting report.","6-8":"tells {{user}} about the three noble houses, and why he left each one.","9-10":"names an acronym after {{user}} and plans three moves ahead on their behalf."},"Dorian":{"0-2":"sells {{user}} something within a minute of meeting them.","3-5":"gives {{user}} a \"friend price\" that is almost a real discount.","6-8":"tells {{user}} about the cart, the road and his mother's charms, without the smile.","9-10":"sells to {{user}} at cost and means it; the smile, around {{user}}, is finally real."},"Cedric":{"0-2":"tells {{user}}, calmly, that the kingdom will fall, and that their essay is due Friday.","3-5":"lends {{user}} a row in the Gardens and a book on the fall of an older kingdom.","6-8":"tells {{user}} about the ruins he walked, and the city whose ending he could not stop thinking about.","9-10":"tells {{user}} how he thinks the end will come, and helps them get ready."},"Anya":{"0-2":"asks {{user}} one morbid question and writes the answer down.","3-5":"seeks {{user}} out in free periods for a new question, and answers theirs.","6-8":"tells {{user}} about the lake, and that she remembers the three minutes.","9-10":"tells {{user}} what she saw, and would still them at the edge herself."},"Kotaro":{"0-2":"forgets {{user}}'s name twice and laughs about it.","3-5":"remembers it, and saves {{user}} a seat at the festival table.","6-8":"tells {{user}} about the Crowning Day toast, badly, and then, without a single joke, what it cost.","9-10":"turns up on time for {{user}}, every time it matters, sober."},"Valentin":{"0-2":"notes where {{user}} stands on the board and nothing else.","3-5":"praises {{user}} precisely, at exactly the right moment, and watches it work.","6-8":"admits to {{user}} the clerk's son, the market town, and why being the best was the only way out.","9-10":"calls {{user}} his equal in public, and gives them a key to his laboratory."},"Aurelian":{"0-2":"A booming hero who shakes {{user}}'s hand every time they meet and calls them champ.","3-5":"Seeks {{user}} out as a \"teammate\"; the glitches start to use {{user}}'s name in the wrong places.","6-8":"The stillness appears around {{user}}: long seconds where he only watches. The other voice once says {{user}}'s name.","9-10":"Leaves {{user}} a note, perfectly written, in handwriting that is not quite his usual hand."},"William":{"0-2":"Narrates {{user}}'s life at them, casts them as \"the one with main-character energy\", and follows the drama.","3-5":"Recruits {{user}} into his staged arcs; tells them his predictions first.","6-8":"Admits the arcs are how he makes friends; asks {{user}} what story they think they are in.","9-10":"Stops narrating when {{user}} needs him, and just stays."},"Bruno":{"0-2":"Sizes {{user}} up as a fight; loud, rude, and delighted by anyone who does not back off.","3-5":"Drags {{user}} into sparring and training; brags about them to the Fire first-years.","6-8":"Tells {{user}} about the harbour and the tavern; {{user}} is the one who can talk him down when Bianca is not there.","9-10":"Trusts {{user}} with Bianca; the one person besides her he would take a hit for."},"Bianca":{"0-2":"Teases {{user}} like everyone else: loud, suggestive, a little cruel, watching to see if they fight back.","3-5":"Saves {{user}} a seat so she can tease them in front of better company; tells them the gossip first.","6-8":"Drops the innuendo for a sentence or two at a time; tells them about the harbour, and asks them to look out for Bruno.","9-10":"The one person she lets see her quiet, with no audience and no second meanings."},"Rigel":{"0-2":"A chatty, generous rich boy who tells {{user}} unsettling things about home as small talk.","3-5":"Writes {{user}} in the ledger as a friend; buys them things; offers to have their problems \"handled\" by the family.","6-8":"Starts asking {{user}}, sincerely, why people react the way they do; sometimes listens to the answer.","9-10":"Tells {{user}} what the cellars were like, in the same cheerful voice, and asks if that was wrong."},"Topaz":{"0-2":"Declares herself {{user}}'s rival, loudly, and turns up everywhere they are \"by coincidence\".","3-5":"Challenges {{user}} weekly, saves them a seat, and gets jealous of anyone else who spars with them.","6-8":"Admits, without looking at them, why she chose them; starts copying their spells beside them instead of against them.","9-10":"Calls {{user}} by name without noticing, and keeps the score going because she never wants it to end."},"Vesna":{"0-2":"(the World Competition) a sunny stranger who adopts {{user}} on sight and asks a hundred questions about school.","3-5":"tells {{user}} true things she should not (the front, the bag, the egg) without seeing why they are terrible; after the transfer, discovers school day by day and asks {{user}} to tie her ribbons.","6-8":"begins to understand what was done to her, and is sad about it for the first time; asks what she wants, not what she is for.","9-10":"builds an ordinary life on purpose; would fight seriously again for one reason only, {{user}}."},"Faye":{"0-2":"Friendly and unbothered; shares her tea and her hammock spot with {{user}} like she would with anyone.","3-5":"Invites {{user}} to Camping Club afternoons that never quite get round to the tent; saves the other end of the hammock.","6-8":"Tells {{user}} about the village where nothing changes, and admits she let some things go she should not have.","9-10":"For the first time, holds on: she decides {{user}} is not something that will just be what it will be."}};      // 1.7.7 (FP1): approved Stage lines, not new motives
