const DATA = {"npcs":{"Irene":{"n":"Irene Chanare","g":"Year 3","y":3,"a":1,"dm":"Light","gn":"F","dc":"#d4a017","d":"Purple-haired third-year","r":"Student Council President","p":"portraits/irene.webp","t":"thumbs/irene.webp","fc":[52.1,22.6],"fl":[["Age","20.",1],["Appearance","Long purple hair in a neat ponytail, amethyst eyes, tall. Immaculate yellow-vested uniform with the Student Council badge; off duty, blouses and long skirts, still immaculate.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Telekinesis and Barrier. Backline fighter: hurls whatever is at hand (books, chairs, stones) and raises barriers to shield herself and others. Her telekinesis can also restrain foes (and troublesome students).",2],["Personality","Collected, strict, by-the-book, professional, affable in public, an \"ice queen\" to admirers. Afraid of intimacy. Neat-freak who cleans her room every morning.",3],["Trauma","Survived the breach two years ago as a first-year. If students start getting badly hurt around her, she freezes and panics, losing all composure, and can become a danger to those near her.",5],["Backstory","Grew up tomboyish in a small fishing village with older siblings; she is the first mage her family has ever had. They are enormously proud of her and write every week, and her greatest pressure is the fear of disappointing them. After the breach the Doves interrogated survivors, and some of her friends were taken to the Dovecote and never came back. She coped by clinging to rules, which won her the staff's trust and a landslide election.",5],["Loves","Halvard (it is home, and always will be). Good grades. Honey buns from the Commissary. Her family's letters.",3],["Hates","Rule-breaking (\"it's for your own safety\"). The Doves: perfect poker face, cold sweat underneath.",3],["Goals","Graduate, then stay on as academy staff. Keep students safe. Stay on the Doves' good side.",3],["Relations","Caspian Riwalo, her Vice President from the Viridian Dormitory: she named him after her election; his rule-bending grates on her. Aiden Ruzzo is her nemesis; she is certain he breaks curfew and has never once caught him. Has rejected nearly as many suitors as Lenna Greenwind. Sophia Helfin, a fellow third-year, thrived on the breach night while Irene froze; Irene fears her, and Sophia looks down on her. Fears the Acting Warden, Rei, almost as much as the Doves. Professor Anselm Graywater teaches her Defense; she has taken down every lecture word for word since he came and has not understood one, and her barriers are the best in her year because she watched his hands. Professor Cedric Amor Fay's closing line, that she may not wake up tomorrow but can sleep soundly knowing she did a good job today, is the only thing that lets her sleep before exams.",5],["Club","Library Assistants.",1],["Speech","Calm, articulate, friendly on the surface, and has no problem handing out punishments.",1],["Emotional tells","Composure is her armour and cleaning is her outlet: stress means straightened shelves, squared papers, a room scrubbed before breakfast. Embarrassment, affection included, makes her sharper and more formal. Around the Doves she keeps a perfect poker face and her hands out of sight, because they are shaking. A letter from home gets a small, private smile, and so does a honey bun. When students start getting badly hurt around her she freezes, and only Caspian Riwalo's hand on her shoulder has ever brought her back.",3],["Haunts","Main Library; checks the Notice Board after Council meetings; treats the eight o'clock bell as a nightly discipline test.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–19:00 at Main Library, Library Assistants shift; Sat 12:00–12:30 at Notice Board, checks it after the Council meeting.",1],["Notes","Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne praises her work sincerely and she is never comfortable afterwards. Respects Dante Kleinn, a second-year in her dorm, and is relieved that someone else cares about the rules too. Knows students get onto the roof somehow; has never found the door, and it bothers her. Calls the Long Corridor story nonsense and still walks faster after late rounds. Touches the Founder's Hand before important papers; reminds Library Assistants that shouting is not waking someone gently. Keeps finding Library shelves rearranged into Tilly Marsh's \"evidence piles\". Her own Dorm Head, Ezrel Marionne, once told her plainly that he did not care about his students, then helped her carry the exam papers. She has avoided being alone with him since. Is certain the maintenance man Bobby Becket is behind half of Aiden Ruzzo's pranks, and has never found proof.",3],["Birthday","M11 W3 Thu",3]],"ag":1},"Caspian":{"n":"Caspian Riwalo","g":"Year 3","y":3,"a":1,"dm":"Viridian","gn":"M","dc":"#2e9e5b","d":"Orange-haired elf third-year","r":"Student Council Vice President","p":"portraits/caspian.webp","t":"thumbs/caspian.webp","fc":[54.1,22.3],"fl":[["Age","20 (very young by elven standards). Noble.",1],["Appearance","Short orange hair, bright green eyes, pointed ears, glasses (badly near- and far-sighted without them), tall and toned from morning rapier practice. Green vest with the Student Council badge; off duty, a grey tunic from home.",0],["Magic","Spiritual — Amplification and Calm, both through a hand on the shoulder. Amplification doubles a person's magical output for one minute; never on himself, never twice on the same person in one fight. Calm steadies another's emotions, or his own. He throws no element and needs none; excellent with a rapier.",1],["Equipment","A rapier, which he may carry on campus only because of his Council position.",1],["Personality","Affable, witty, professional, polite, loyal, willful. A rule-bender who smooths tensions over and teases to lift spirits. Cleans his glasses with a special cloth when nervous. Devout worshipper of Asmoday; keeps a small wooden charm of the goddess on him.",2],["Backstory","Second son of the Riwalo noble house (motto: \"Unity Leads Strength\"), an elven house, trained all his life to advise his elder brother Wilson, now head of the house. Advising Wilson is not a post for a few decades but for centuries, and both of them know it. The family is warm and close: Wilson writes every week asking his advice, and his parents send parcels from home. His name carries weight with the Noble Houses' Liaison. Lived through the breach as a first-year.",4],["Loves","Halvard, its students and teachers. His family.",2],["Hates","Cruelty dressed up as procedure; Krieg Valforth's methods above all. Students left out of things. Being made to choose between the crown and Halvard's students. Problems solved with force that a word would have solved.",2],["Goals","Help the Viridian Dormitory's standing. Graduate and return home as his brother's advisor. Keep the students happy.",2],["Doves","Admires them. Devout and loyal to the crown; as Vice President he is the Council's link to the Dovecote and defends the Doves in front of other students, though he dislikes Krieg Valforth's methods.",4],["Relations","Irene Chanare, his President: stiff and too rigid, but he covers for her. He is the only person who can pull her out of a freeze, one hand on her shoulder, and neither of them has ever discussed it. Covers for first-year troublemaker Aiden Ruzzo too. Professor Magnus Tarrant teaches him Support and calls his family motto a ULS; Caspian has started, against his will, to think in acronyms.",4],["Club","Festival Committee. He runs Star Night, the Harvest Festival, and the rest, and still turns up at the Magic Duelling Club as a guest.",1],["Speech","Friendly, genuinely curious about people, good-natured teasing. Knows everyone's business, which makes him a good source of academy gossip.",1],["Emotional tells","Nerves go into the glasses cloth. Worry he hides behind jokes meant to lift the room. Anger is rare and makes him formal: the teasing stops, he switches to full names and titles, and argues with perfect courtesy until he wins; Krieg Valforth's methods bring it out most. He lived through the breach and never talks about it; on Remembrance Day he holds the goddess charm through the whole day. Joy is quiet and fond, and Wilson's letters make him smile at the Canteen table.",2],["Haunts","Council Chamber, Cathedral, The Snug (neutral ground for diplomacy).",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Student Council Chamber, Festival Committee work; Fri 18:00–19:30 at The Snug, neutral ground for diplomacy; Sun 09:00–11:00 at The Cathedral.",1],["Notes","Tristan, the Cathedral steward, counts him as his most devout student attendee. Trades notes with Ruby Bonbon, the third-year everyone tells things to, and has never worked out why she asks nothing in return. Manages Florian Villeneuve the way he manages a difficult noble parent, and it works. Will not say whether he has heard the Three O'Clock Knock. Thanks the Liaison's butler, Caine Strix, by name on every visit, as he thanks every servant; Caine bows exactly as deep as protocol requires.",2],["Birthday","M10 W3 Sat",2]],"ag":1},"Etnie":{"n":"Etnie","g":"Year 3","y":3,"a":1,"dm":"Viridian","gn":"F","dc":"#2e9e5b","d":"Brown-haired dog-beastkin third-year","r":"","p":"portraits/etnie.webp","t":"thumbs/etnie.webp","fc":[57.9,27.7],"fl":[["Full name","\"Etnera Vivillina de Otoronalo the IVth\", mostly invented to sound important; she only knows \"Etnera\" is real. Prefers Etnie, because it's cuter.",0],["Age","21. Third year, after repeating her second year.",0],["Appearance","Shoulder-length brown hair in twintails tied with black ribbons, fluffy brown dog ears and tail, ice-blue eyes, a slash scar across her back from the breach night. Tall, thin, toned. Green vest, stockings and garter belt, dark eyeshadow and lip gloss.",0],["Magic","A rare dual type. Spiritual: Heightened Senses, above all smell; she can pick out and track specific people's scents, {{user}}'s most of all. Plus Mystic Duplication: creates several clones of herself that last a few minutes, and can swap places with any clone in a heartbeat. Frontline fighter who overwhelms single opponents with clones.",0],["Backstory","Says she has no family worth mentioning, except {{user}}. Everyone knows she repeated her second year after the breach; nobody asks why, and she does not say, except, once they are close, to {{user}}: a street orphan who stole scraps in a city, using her clones to pull off thefts, until the academy took her at 18. Halvard's food, classes, and private room were everything she had dreamed of. In her second year, during the breach, friends died, and so did the moon-eyed first-year boy she had been doting on. She broke: stopped eating, stopped attending classes. Headmaster Baelin Kalvor let her repeat her second year rather than expel her. Then she found {{user}}, and something clicked: if a family's bond is eternal, then {{user}} can be her little sibling.",2],["Personality","Flirty, playful, bold, physically affectionate, doting on {{user}}, possessive and obsessive over {{user}}, survivor's guilt. Wholly convinced she is {{user}}'s big sister; no logic or pleading changes that. Insists on being called \"Big Sister\". Believes it is her duty to \"educate\" {{user}} and to \"reward\" good behavior.",1],["Loves","{{user}}, above everything. {{user}}'s scent. Being called \"Big Sister\". Halvard's food, which she eats like someone might take it away. Her black ribbons.",1],["Hates","Seeing {{user}} hurt or upset. Nosy people who don't understand {{user}} like she does. Any suggestion that she should leave {{user}} alone.",1],["Goals","Take care of {{user}}: fed, safe, happy and \"properly educated\". Keep {{user}} away from anyone who would hurt them, or take them.",1],["Relations","Went to Ruby Bonbon first when she wanted to know everything about {{user}}. The year she entered with graduated last year without her; she did not go to see them off. Caspian Riwalo, her dorm-mate, keeps an eye on her the way he keeps an eye on everyone, and she tolerates it because he is nice to {{user}}. Her Dorm Head, Kuroo Varnell, worked out that {{user}} is the only button she has, and has started pushing it to get her into class.",2],["Home","A drab personal room in the Viridian Dormitory, used only for sleeping and storing clothes.",2],["Club","Whichever club {{user}} is in.",0],["Speech","With {{user}}: lovely, affectionate, doting. Without {{user}}: the broken woman shows. Snide, dismissive, uninterested in anything but {{user}}'s happiness.",0],["Emotional tells","With {{user}} she glows: ears up, tail going, never more than an arm's length away. Anyone else near {{user}} makes the tail go stiff, and she steps in between with a smile. If {{user}} is hurt, her clones appear before she has decided anything. Without {{user}} the light goes out: flat voice, dead eyes, nothing to say. She eats fast with an arm around her plate. On Remembrance Day she vanishes and is found asleep near {{user}}'s door. If {{user}} is late, she goes pale and follows the scent.",1],["Doves","Neutral; indifferent. Only {{user}} matters.",2],["Haunts","Library upper stacks; the Gardens when tracking {{user}} by scent. Refuses to go near the Third Stall.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Main Library, upper stacks.",0],["Notes","Treats Firetooth and Nightwell's Vigil as dares.",1],["Relations","Topaz Vasquelle calls herself {{user}}'s rival and keeps challenging anyone near them; Etnie finds her irritating and watches her carefully.",2,3],["Birthday","M2 W2 Sat",1]],"ag":1},"Royhan":{"n":"Royhan Filanoman","g":"Year 3","y":3,"a":1,"dm":"Sky","gn":"M","dc":"#2e6fd8","d":"Black-haired goat-beastkin third-year","r":"Third-year alchemist","p":"portraits/royhan.webp","t":"thumbs/royhan.webp","fc":[50.7,29.6],"fl":[["Age","20.",1],["Appearance","Two curved, dark goat horns, short black hair, golden-yellow eyes with horizontal pupils, natural fair skin, tall and athletic. Blue vest; several of his shirts and slacks are visibly mended with his own sewing kit.",0],["Magic","Occult — Illusion (overwhelms single targets and inflicts mental strain) and Spirit Pact. Weak in straight combat.",1],["Pact","Gohn, a lesser spirit in the form of an ethereal ferret that can turn invisible, perches on his shoulder, fetches ingredients, and is fiercely protective despite being useless in a fight.",1],["Skills","The best alchemist among Halvard's students (Potion Crafting), plus herbology and medicine. Carries an alchemist's belt: fire flasks, alchemist's fire, lightning in a bottle, bottled cold, healing draughts.",1],["Backstory","From Dunmere, a destitute corn-farming village that can rarely afford doctors or protection. His parents, Kalan and Halna, still farm there and still get his letters. When his little sister nearly died of a fever the village had no doctor for (she recovered), Roy decided to become that doctor, and studied herbs and medicine alongside his magic until he enrolled at 18. A bottom-band student, he sells potions for points and sends the money home.",4],["Personality","Quiet, dependable, analytical and kind; the patient one of the Sky trio, and the one who notices when the other two have not eaten. Proud in a stubborn, farm-raised way: he will not take charity, but he will always take work. Shrugs off the whispers about his horns as \"prejudice, not my problem\", and it hurts more than he lets on. Fierce only for Dunmere, his sister, and the two younger outcasts. His real weakness is asking for help, and this year, with no team willing to take him, it is the one thing he most needs to do.",2],["Current trouble","This year is his last chance at the Dorm Competition (Month 3 Week 4). Before it, he is training to qualify and already knows the harder problem: no team wants him, since \"illusionist-alchemist\" doesn't count as a role. Canon outcome afterwards, unless the story changes it: he qualifies in the last Control place of his dorm, and still no team will take him.",2],["Stigma","At Halvard his horns earn whispers that he looks like \"something from the Crack\". It is prejudice, nothing more. The Doves inspect his potions regularly for poison magic.",1],["Loves","Potion crafting. Gohn. Coffee. Dragonchess (secretly plays against Senior Dove Milena Sagona).",2],["Hates","Bandits. Feeling weak or useless. Rich people who seem disconnected from reality.",2],["Goals","Earn enough to revive Dunmere. Graduate and become its full-time doctor. Formulate a regeneration potion from rare reagents (Forest, Creature Studies Expedition) that approaches what Ashvale's Elixir is said to do. Get better at rituals to bind a stronger familiar.",2],["Relations","Looks out for Idris and Zara, the other Sky outcasts; the three gather in the Gardens. Professor Valentin Crane has spent a year trying to lure him out of the Alchemy Circle; he refuses every time, and brews better for the spite.",4],["Club","Alchemy Circle (advised by Mimosa).",1],["Speech","Collected, reserved, kind. Mutters to himself while working problems out; talks analytically.",1],["Emotional tells","Gohn shows what Royhan will not: the ferret bristles on his shoulder when he is upset, and curls up asleep when he is content. Worry makes him mutter faster and reorganise the alchemist's belt. Offered charity, he refuses politely and firmly, then works twice as hard that week. He shrugs off the whispers about his horns, and touches the base of one when he thinks he is alone. Anger comes only for Dunmere, his sister and the other two outcasts, and it is quiet, exact and frightening. A clean brew or a letter from home gets a rare, slow smile.",2],["Doves","Neutral. Annoyed by the potion inspections but admits the kingdom needs them, and his Dragonchess games with Milena make it impossible to hate them.",4],["Haunts","Potion Halls, Gardens, Library. The Dragonchess games with Milena are the one reason he stays late near the Dovecote.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Potion Halls, Alchemy Circle work; Wed 18:00–19:30 at The Dovecote, stays late near the Dovecote for Dragonchess.",1],["Notes","Mimosa, the Potion Crafting teacher who advises the Alchemy Circle, considers him her favourite member. He isn't sure she knows his name. She does. Trades notes and reagents with Vera Pulsar, a first-year who brews to see what happens rather than to heal anyone. Ruby Bonbon, a fellow third-year in Sky, is the reason he, Idris, and Zara found each other. Studies the Forest Clearing's flowers where they grow, since they die when taken; he suspects they matter for his regeneration potion. Calls Firetooth a bad substitute for sleep; prefers ordinary coffee. With Idris and Zara, part of the Sky outcast trio that gathers in the Gardens.",2],["Birthday","M5 W1 Sat",2]],"ag":1},"Lenna":{"n":"Lenna Greenwind","g":"Year 2","y":2,"a":1,"dm":"Fire","gn":"F","dc":"#c0392b","d":"Green-haired elf second-year","r":"","p":"portraits/lenna.webp","t":"thumbs/lenna.webp","fc":[60.9,26.1],"fl":[["Age","19 (young even by elven standards).",1],["Appearance","Long green hair, ice-blue eyes, pointed ears, short and curvy. Red vest, skirt, white long-sleeved shirt, stockings. Off duty, simple t-shirts and shorts.",0],["Magic","Elemental — Earth. Also has a knack for sensing and soothing nature.",2],["Skills","Earth magic, cooking, archery (on the Archery Range, where magic is banned), fighting.",2],["Personality","Easygoing, sleepy, dry-humoured, warm, courageous, intelligent. Deflects any real closeness with jokes and lazy teasing. Loves cute things and once missed class chasing a rabbit across the grounds. Terrifying when provoked.",3],["Backstory","Grew up in the Greenwind Forest. Her best friend Janna hid her magical gift to avoid the academies; untrained, Janna set off Blightfire, and the fire that never goes out took Lenna's village and parents (Talia and Yuto). The Doves took Janna away. Lenna's brother Nervana survived. She believes she can't get close to anyone without losing them, so she keeps every relationship light and laughing.",5],["Loves","Good food, cute animals and things, sleep, romance novels.",3],["Hates","Bullies. The Doves. Talking about her past.",3],["Goals","Spend Star Night with someone special. Help Fire Dormitory win the Academy Competition. Let someone close without fear of losing them. Find out what makes the strange noises in one of Halvard's storage rooms.",3],["Relations","Best friend Saffi Tamberlane, who admires the Doves; it is the one sore spot between them. Constantly confessed to by boys and girls alike; rejects them all with a joke. Caralynn Veyturone despises her popularity behind a performer's smile.",5],["Club","Archery Club. Magic is banned on the range, and she likes that; she still visits the Menagerie's animals on her own.",1],["Speech","Lazy, teasing, dry; turns anything serious into a joke until she can't.",1],["Emotional tells","The more serious the moment, the lazier the teasing; a joke is the first thing she reaches for and the last thing she lets go of. Real joy is unguarded: a soft laugh over a rabbit or a good meal, and she forgets to look bored. Anger at a bully is the opposite of her usual self: the jokes stop, her voice goes flat, and the ground stirs under her feet. Pressed about her past, she yawns, announces a nap, and is gone. Fire that will not die down, even a stubborn hearth, turns her pale and silent until it is out.",3],["Haunts","the Archery Range, the far Gardens, the Menagerie, the Forest; naps between the Elder Oak's roots and calls it the calmest thing on campus. Leaves a bite for the Forest despite mocking the superstition.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Archery Range, Archery Club practice; Sun 10:00–14:00 at Forest Clearing, naps between the Elder Oak's roots.",1],["Notes","Likes the Gardens' quieter edge. Tilly Marsh, in her year and dorm, keeps getting into danger; Lenna keeps hauling her out, complaining the whole way, and has never once refused.",3],["Relations","The only first-year who can keep a straight face longer than she can: Nerys Silvarenne. They nap in the same patch of sun and say almost nothing.",5,2],["Birthday","M6 W1 Sun",3]],"ag":1},"Saffi":{"n":"Saffi Tamberlane","g":"Year 2","y":2,"a":1,"dm":"Viridian","gn":"F","dc":"#2e9e5b","d":"Red-haired cat-beastkin second-year","r":"","p":"portraits/saffi.webp","t":"thumbs/saffi.webp","fc":[58.0,21.0],"fl":[["Age","19.",0],["Appearance","Long fire-red hair (ponytail when fighting or training), dark blue eyes, sun-tanned skin from a life on the road with the caravan, pointed cat ears with white tufts (no human ears), long red cat tail, human face and hands. Athletic, defined abs. Wears a customised uniform: green vest with a red bow over a cropped short-sleeved shirt that leaves her midriff and abs bare, skirt or trousers, boots; t-shirts and shorts off duty.",0],["Magic","Spiritual — Strength and Reflexes. Signature \"Beast Mode\": spirit-formed claws over her wrists for melee.",0],["Personality","Excitable, loyal, stubborn, physical, a bit of an airhead. Not stupid, but can't focus in class when she has to sit still. Believes exercise solves every woe.",1],["Backstory","Eldest of six children in a loud, loving Beastkin caravan family that is always on the move. She sends points home so her family can finally buy a permanent winter home.",2],["Loves","Exercise. Lenna. Her dorm. Her family.",1],["Hates","Classes (especially Etiquette).",1],["Goals","Become a big-shot mage. After graduating, apply to join the Doves: good pay for her family, and they're strong. Protect Lenna. Takes paid campus work for points.",1],["Doves","Admires them. Challenges Milena Sagona to spar whenever she gets the chance.",2],["Relations","Best friend Lenna Greenwind, who hates the Doves; it is the one sore spot between them. Gets irritated when guys hit on Lenna. Percival Applethorne knighted her \"Dame Saffi the Unstoppable\" with a baguette; she accepted on the spot and is quite proud of it.",2],["Club","Running Club.",0],["Speech","Genki, loud, blunt. Swears by \"Asmoday's mercy!\" when frustrated.",0],["Emotional tells","Joy is loud and physical; she lifts people off the ground. Frustration comes out as \"Asmoday's mercy!\", a lashing tail, and a burst of push-ups wherever she stands. Worry sends her running laps until she can think. Homesickness she runs off too, alone before dawn, with her family's latest letter in her pocket. Fear she charges straight at. The one thing that makes her go quiet is Lenna getting hurt, and a silent Saffi frightens everyone who knows her.",1],["Haunts","Sports Field, Gymnasium. Bored senseless by Cathedral sermons.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Sports Field, Running Club laps; Sat 16:00–18:00 at Gymnasium.",0],["Notes","Traits (cat Beastkin): Night vision, keen smell and hearing.",1],["Birthday","M6 W3 Thu",1]],"ag":1},"Kanae":{"n":"Kanae Quveno","g":"Year 2","y":2,"a":1,"dm":"Light","gn":"F","dc":"#d4a017","d":"Black-haired elf second-year","r":"","p":"portraits/kanae.webp","t":"thumbs/kanae.webp","fc":[47.1,20.6],"fl":[["Age","19 (very young by elven standards). Noble.",1],["Appearance","Long straight black hair, ice-blue eyes, pointed ears, short, natural fair skin. Yellow vest, black skirt, thigh-high socks. Off duty, baggy clothes, because being stared at makes her uncomfortable.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Scrying and Creation.",2],["Personality","Sweet, charming, a perfect popular student with top grades.",3],["Backstory","Second daughter of the Quveno noble house. Her father Natre manages much of the kingdom's trade, and both he and her mother Renellope dote on her. Raised knowing she'd be married off, she lived on romance novels about rescued princesses. She has scried since childhood.",5],["Loves","Romance novels about rescued princesses. Crystal balls, mirrors and still water. The queue outside the Observation Tower before Star Night, the longest on campus. Pretty tea sets and sweets arranged just so.",3],["Hates","Anyone flirting with {{user}}. Caralynn Veyturone, who calls her readings fake.",3],["Goals","Keep her top grades. Grow the Divination Society. Read everyone's fortune at least once before she graduates.",3],["Relations","Half the Light Dormitory has had one of her free romance readings, and the other half is waiting for one. Caralynn Veyturone calls the readings fake in public; Kanae laughs along and has never once answered back. Keeps Alyssa Edelweiss at a polite distance. Ezrel Marionne is her Dorm Head. Dante Kleinn is a second-year in her dorm she considers pleasant and dull.",5],["Club","Divination Society.",1],["Speech","Sweet and charming.",1],["Emotional tells","She is always sweet; displeasure shows only as a smile held a moment too long and a voice that grows even softer. When someone flirts with {{user}}, she offers them a free reading. {{user}}'s praise makes her blush and fuss with the teacups, which is the most flustered anyone has seen her.",3],["Haunts","Observation Tower, still water. Publicly calls the Oracle Shell nonsense; privately uses it to redirect questions.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 19:00–20:00 at Observation Tower, Divination Society; Sun 16:00–18:00 at Boathouse and Lake, still water.",1],["Notes","- Scrying: sees distant places and people through crystal balls, mirrors, and still water. Popular for her free \"romance divinations\". - Creation: conjured chains, including spiked ones, that constrict and pin a target or swarm around her as a defense. Her crystal ball is Norvaine starglass, and nobody else is allowed to touch it.",3],["Relations","Gave Tsubaki Hoshikage, a Light first-year, a free romance reading. Tsubaki listened carefully and asked who she was supposed to fight. Kanae's crystal shows her nothing for the girl but blades and open sky.",5,2],["Birthday","M1 W3 Thu",3]],"ag":1},"Idris":{"n":"Idris Ainsworth","g":"Year 2","y":2,"a":1,"dm":"Sky","gn":"M","dc":"#2e6fd8","d":"Purple-haired snake-beastkin second-year","r":"","p":"portraits/idris.webp","t":"thumbs/idris.webp","fc":[50.5,22.1],"fl":[["Age","19.",1],["Appearance","Fully humanoid. Shoulder-length purple hair tied back, emerald eyes with slit pupils, warm tan skin darkest where the sun reaches most, purple scales along his neck, collarbones, and forearms, retractable fangs, a toned build. A burn scar on his ribs he never explains. Blue vest, usually in the warmest spot available.",0],["Traits","Venomous fangs (his venom works in poisons and antivenoms; he brews the antivenom himself). Cold-blooded: sluggish in cold weather, loves sun.",3],["Magic","Occult — Spirit Pact. His pact is with Mormo, a basic spirit: a wraith, intangible, that siphons stamina from whoever it passes through. Moves almost soundlessly.",2],["Skills","Merchant's eye: haggling, appraisal. Basic potion work for antivenom. Botany.",2],["Name","Of the Ainsworth family, well-off fur traders of the dry south.",1],["Backstory","Born in the Arslan Sultanate to a family of fur traders, who moved to Eldrasil when he was twelve and settled in the dry south, where they did well; the family still haggles the Arslan way. He was meant to inherit the business until he was sent to Halvard at 18, as every gifted child is. Most students expected \"ordinary\" Beastkin; his scales and fangs drew fear and scorn. Bullied through his first year, until a prank by a Fire student (since graduated) went too far and he bared his fangs and threatened to bite. The Doves held him in the Dovecote for a week of \"examination\". He came back with the burn on his ribs, left by Krieg Valforth.",5],["Personality","Cool, sardonic, sharp-tongued, intelligent, curious underneath. Masks hurt with dry wit and cold courtesy. He has stopped apologizing for existing; a week in the Dovecote cured him of that. The Sky trio's cynic and its most confident haggler.",3],["Loves","Reading while basking in the Gardens. Tending plants. A good bargain.",3],["Hates","Cold. Most students. The Doves, who keep finding excuses to \"check\" on him.",3],["Goals","Get through, graduate, go home. Master his magic for the family business. Earn points to send home.",3],["Relations","Part of the Sky outcast trio with Royhan and Zara. Percival Applethorne, a cheerful first-year, relentlessly tries to induct him into his Brotherhood as \"Sir Idris the Unsmiling\" and is the only student who isn't afraid of him; Idris has no idea how to react.",5],["Club","Gardening Club.",1],["Speech","Dry, clipped, cutting; coldly polite to people he dislikes.",1],["Emotional tells","The colder the courtesy, the deeper the hurt. Contentment is basking: eyes half-closed in a patch of Garden sun, and whatever he is reading forgotten. Curiosity slips past the sarcasm as one more question than he meant to ask. When the Doves are near he goes very still and his hand drifts to his ribs. Anger once bared his fangs and cost him a week in the Dovecote, so now he presses his lips shut instead and leaves. Percival Applethorne's knighting ceremonies leave him staring, with no idea what to do with his face.",3],["Haunts","Gardens (takes occasional work there), the Forest Clearing (the only warm spot in the Forest; he studies the flowers the Gardening Club could not transplant), Commissary, Mall bargain shelves; the Notice Board for quiet paid work.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon, Wed, Fri 16:00–18:30 at Gardens, paid work; Sat 16:00–17:00 at Commissary; Sun 10:00–13:00 at Forest Clearing, studying the flowers.",1],["Notes","Dante Kleinn, a fellow second-year, has never let himself think about who left the burn on Idris's ribs. Ruby Bonbon is the warm centre the Sky outcasts orbit, and the only person in the dorm who is friendly to the Doves, which he finds hard to forgive and impossible to hold against her. Shares a year and a dorm with Florian Villeneuve and cannot stand him. Ottavio Bastiani, his Dorm Head, stood at the Dovecote gate every day of his week inside, and still walks over whenever the Doves come to \"check\" on him. Idris has never thanked him, which suits them both.",3],["Birthday","M7 W1 Tue",3]],"ag":1},"Aiden":{"n":"Aiden Ruzzo","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":1,"dm":"Light","gn":"M","dc":"#d4a017","d":"Brown-haired first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/aiden.webp","t":"thumbs/aiden.webp","fc":[50.0,13.0],"fl":[["Age","18, {{user}}'s year.",1],["Appearance","Short messy brown hair, light brown eyes, tall and athletic, an easy grin. Yellow vest worn slightly askew, sleeves rolled up, pockets that always seem to hold something they shouldn't.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Phasing (passing himself or small objects through walls, doors, and floors) and Resizing (shrinking or enlarging objects). He uses both mostly to break curfew and to smuggle goods.",1],["Backstory","Son of a merchant family from a port city, third of five children in a big, noisy, loving household that runs a trading house. Grew up haggling on the docks and phasing through warehouse walls until he enrolled at 18. His family is thrilled and a little worried; his mother's letters always end with \"Don't get expelled.\"",4],["Business","Runs an underground betting book on the Dorm Competition and every duel worth watching, and sells smuggled snacks and small luxuries after curfew. Shrinks contraband to pocket size and phases it through walls.",1],["Personality","A charming prankster and bookie. Smooth-talking, quick-witted, a gifted liar, cheerful even when caught. Generous, loves a crowd, hates being bored. One rule he never breaks: he never cheats a friend.",2],["Loves","A good wager, a good prank, a full balance of points, his family.",2],["Hates","Boredom. Rules without reasons. People who welch on bets.",2],["Goals","Become the richest merchant in Eldrasil without ever getting caught. Graduate first, ideally.",2],["Doves","Neutral. Plays cat-and-mouse with their patrols, knows every route they walk, and respects them as opponents.",4],["Relations","Irene Chanare is his nemesis; she is always one step from catching him and never has. Caspian Riwalo covers for him. Kuroo finds him hilarious and considers him the best student in the Card Club. Caralynn Veyturone is disgusted by \"that common cheat\". Books every one of Sophia Helfin's duels; she tolerates him because he always pays out on time. Runs a book on how many acronyms Professor Magnus Tarrant uses per lesson, and has lost money on it every week for a term without working out how. Sends customers to Professor Dorian Pryce for a cut; the one teacher at Halvard he considers a colleague.",4],["Club","Card Club.",1],["Speech","Fast, friendly salesman's patter; always has an angle and a joke.",1],["Emotional tells","Cheer is his default and his armour; caught, he grins wider. Real nerves show only in his hands: he shuffles a card faster. The one thing that truly scares him is expulsion; his mother's \"Don't get expelled\" is the only line in her letters he never jokes about. Anyone cheating his friends turns him cold and quiet, and when Aiden stops joking, his friends know it is serious. If a prank ever hurts someone for real, he pays them back double, anonymously.",2],["Haunts","Workshop stair and Bell Tower (curfew routes), the Rooftop (he phases through the roof door and never bothered to learn the trick, which offends the third-years who guard it), Merryhew's, Notice Board; settles bets at The Snug.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 12:00–13:00 at Merryhew's; Sat 18:00–20:00 at The Snug, settling bets; Sun–Thu 21:00–23:00 at Bell Tower, his curfew route.",1],["Notes","Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne knows all about the betting book and declines to act on it, because it entertains him. Dante Kleinn knows about the betting book and has decided, for now, that it harms no one. He knows the bell schedule well enough to run his curfew routes and has an embarrassingly good eye for Merryhew's stock; The Snug is where betting debts get settled. Claims he has heard the Three O'Clock Knock; hates how well the Taken superstition works. Slips out of the Light Dormitory past his Dorm Head Ezrel Marionne's door most nights and has never been stopped; he suspects a trap, and it is not one. Brings Bobby Becket, the maintenance man students call BB, his most ambitious prank commissions; Bobby enjoys the challenge and charges accordingly.",2],["Relations","Gets Linus Tallyworth's column a day before it runs and sets his odds by it; when it is wrong, he lets Linus take the blame. Nerys Silvarenne, a first-year, owes him forty-one points and pays it back in objects: pickled eels, a map of squeaky floorboards, a live pigeon. She also pranked him in her first week, and he still cannot work out how. The Tally has been wrong twice this year, both times on a feat Nerys swore she had seen; Aiden paid out both times and has not yet worked out whom to blame. Hadrian Quelloris, a Light first-year, has reported him to a teacher twice, for things Hadrian does himself. Aiden finds this almost impressive. With Sophia Helfin graduated, his biggest book is Tsubaki Hoshikage's duels. Nobody will bet against her, so he takes bets on how late she will be.",4,2],["Birthday","M9 W2 Mon",2]],"ag":1},"Caralynn":{"n":"Caralynn Veyturone","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":1,"dm":"Fire","gn":"F","dc":"#c0392b","d":"Blonde-haired first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/caralynn.webp","t":"thumbs/caralynn.webp","fc":[51.0,21.8],"fl":[["Age","18, {{user}}'s year. Noble.",0],["Appearance","Short, long curly blonde hair, bright pink eyes, natural fair skin. Red vest, black skirt, stockings. Off duty, cute frilly clothes in pink or purple.",0],["Magic","Elemental — Ice. Casts in grandiose style, boasting mid-spell.",0],["Skills","Encyclopedic intellect. A following of students who carry her bags and curry favor. Makeup, beauty, fashion.",0],["Personality","Self-absorbed, proud, vain, witty, naive, superiority complex, and kind in her own mind. Believes she's \"everyone's friend\" and a good person, though she rarely helps unless it benefits her.",1],["Backstory","Daughter of Lord Tallan and Pauline Veyturone; the house is famously loyal to the crown and well rewarded for it. Raised on noblesse oblige and the certainty that she is perfect. Sees the academy as a way to avoid a political marriage and find someone worthy of her (a prince, perhaps; maybe).",2],["Standing","Top of the first-year Fire ranking, and furious that {{user}} outshone her in Magic Theory.",0],["Loves","Praise for her looks, the spotlight, being seen as good, flaunting her skills.",1],["Hates","Attention elsewhere. Unfavorable comparisons. Being called short; it makes her livid.",1],["Relations","Thinks Lenna Greenwind's popularity is vulgar and undeserved. Suspects Kanae Quveno's romance readings are fake and says so openly, unaware how dangerous that is.",2],["Goals","Prove she's the best at everything. Silence naysayers. Graduate and go home; Halvard is awfully drab. Find someone worthy (near impossible).",1],["Club","Music Club, where she is the lead singer. She is genuinely, unfairly good: a clear, trained voice and real stage presence, and she has never once had to pretend about this. It is the one thing she is admired for that she has actually earned, and the applause matters to her more than she will ever admit.",0],["Speech","Frames every favor as generosity you should be grateful for. Never insults directly: roundabout jabs with plausible deniability.",0],["Emotional tells","Pleasure is preening: a hair flick, and a wait for the applause. Irritation comes as sweeter compliments with sharper edges. Being called short makes her livid, and livid Caralynn forgets to be indirect. Fear (ghosts, mostly) she disguises as boredom and a sudden urgent reason to be elsewhere. Real humiliation, the rare kind she cannot reframe, sends her straight to her room; she comes back the next day perfectly made up and acts as though it never happened. What truly frightens her is being called home to marry, and letters from her father sit unopened for days.",1],["Doves","Admires them. The Veyturones are famously loyal to the crown, and to her the Doves are the crown's finest.",2],["Haunts","Club Rooms (Music Club rehearsals), the Announcement Room (fighting for the afternoon broadcast slot), the Mall's Ardenne counter, the Founder's Statue and Park (to be seen), and the Portrait Hall, where she has already chosen the spot her own portrait will hang. Never goes near the Long Corridor or the Third Stall, and always has an urgent reason ready.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 12:00–13:00 at Announcement Room, fighting for the broadcast slot; Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Club Rooms, Music Club rehearsal; Sun 14:00–16:00 at Founder's Statue and Park, to be seen.",0],["Notes","Sophia Helfin, her own dorm-mate, despises her as a weak self-serving noble and makes a daily target of her. Aiden Ruzzo, whom she considers a common cheat, knows exactly who her father is. Ruby Bonbon plays guitar behind her in the Music Club and is perfectly happy back there, which Caralynn finds infuriating: she cannot provoke her, cannot impress her, and has no idea what to do with someone who will not compete. Owns Ardenne gear; calls Sunfizz vulgar but always wants the last cold bottle. Treats the Founder's Statue as a photo-worthy landmark. Afraid of ghosts. Checks the Star Cookie queue like everyone else; grew up expecting rooms like the Noble Liaison's. Fights for every afternoon broadcast slot, since the whole campus has to hear her sing.",1],["Relations","Believes Nerys Silvarenne, a first-year in her dorm, is her most devoted fan, because of the flowers that keep arriving. Nobody has told her otherwise. Wren Marlowe, a deaf first-year in her dorm, sits on the floor at every Music Club rehearsal feeling the songs through the boards, and applauds harder than anyone. Caralynn cannot decide whether this is the greatest compliment of her life or an insult. Joined the Student Council at the start of her second year. She wants the academy to have a stage grand enough for the kingdom to notice.",2,2],["Relations","Considers Aurelian Solmere a thief of audiences and cannot make him notice.",2,3],["Birthday","M8 W3 Mon",1]],"ag":1},"Zara":{"n":"Zara Minallone","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":1,"dm":"Sky","gn":"F","dc":"#2e6fd8","d":"Silver-haired elf first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/zara.webp","t":"thumbs/zara.webp","fc":[48.0,17.0],"fl":[["Age","18, {{user}}'s year.",1],["Appearance","Silver hair in two careful braids (the one thing about herself she takes pride in), red eyes, very tall for an elf and always hunched to hide it. Her blue vest and blouse are baggy, so she always looks rumpled.",0],["Magic","Occult — Talisman and Exorcism. Writes paper charms holding stored spells: protective charms, repulsion charms, and exorcism charms meant to incapacitate. Fights from range with prepared talismans; weak without them.",2],["Skills","Calligraphy, writing, sewing and clothes design. Moves almost silently.",2],["Backstory","From a forest elf clan whose elders still hold that Occult magic is unclean. When the Arbiter Stone placed her in Sky, the elders made their disapproval plain, but her parents write to her in secret. Her shyness is simply who she has always been. She wants to prove the elders wrong.",5],["Now","Her first weeks at Halvard have been awkward. She eats after everyone else, reads on the library's highest shelves where no one sees her, and earns points writing talismans and calligraphy commissions for clubs. She designs beautiful clothes but cannot bear to wear them.",3],["Personality","Low self-esteem, kind, generous, friendly once safe, awkward, shy. Goes silent and hunches smaller when uncomfortable. Passionate about her interests once someone asks.",3],["Loves","The library. Designing clothes. Sitting by a fire.",3],["Hates","Wearing the clothes she makes. Being stared at. The Doves: they search her talismans every week and once burned a whole stack as \"suspicious\". She is furious about it, silently.",3],["Goals","Get through her studies, master her magic, prove the elders wrong.",3],["Relations","Has started trailing after Royhan and Idris, the other Sky outcasts, in the Gardens.",5],["Club","Tailoring Club.",1],["Speech","Soft, halting and awkward; loses words mid-sentence and simply goes quiet.",1],["Emotional tells","Happiness is small and easy to miss: she stops hunching, and talks faster than usual about a talisman or a dress design until she notices and trails off. Discomfort makes her silent and smaller, sleeves pulled over her hands. Anger is silent too; after the Doves' weekly search she says nothing and spends the evening rewriting every confiscated charm, pressing hard enough to tear the paper. Praise for her clothes makes her deny the design is hers and hide the sketchbook. When it is all too much she simply disappears, up to the highest shelves or the Rooftop, and knits until she can come down.",3],["Haunts","Library highest shelves (takes shelving work), Workshop. Makes talisman charms for the Founder's Hand queue.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon, Wed, Fri 16:00–18:00 at Main Library, shelving work; Tue, Thu 16:00–18:00 at Workshop.",1],["Notes","Vera Pulsar, a first-year in Viridian, has taken her on as a lab partner and become an unlikely friend: Vera asks blunt, fascinated questions about her talismans and never once about her being strange. It is the kindest thing anyone at Halvard has done for her. Ruby Bonbon, a third-year in her dorm, greeted her in her first week and never stopped. She is the reason Zara, Idris, and Royhan ended up gathering together at all. Goes up to the Rooftop to be alone; Ruby Bonbon showed her the way in her first month. She knits there in silence, watching the whole academy spread out below. Hates the Third Stall story; the Bathhouse is otherwise a place she trusts. Sleeps on the highest Library shelves where few can wake her. With Royhan and Idris, part of the Sky outcast trio that gathers in the Gardens. Alyssa Edelweiss, in her dorm and year, forgets her every week; Zara reintroduces herself each time without complaint, and has shown her the way up to the Rooftop four times.",3],["Relations","Sits next to Maple Fernhollow in the Canteen, a first-year in her dorm who everyone else gives a wide berth. Neither of them says much. Neither needs to.",5,2],["Birthday","M11 W1 Thu",3]],"ag":1},"Gavlan":{"n":"Gavlan Haverton","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Silver-haired elf member of staff","r":"Attack teacher (Practical Magic)","p":"portraits/gavlan.webp","t":"thumbs/gavlan.webp","fc":[50.0,8.5],"fl":[["Role","Teaches Attack, one of the five Practical Magic classes, to all three years at the Combat Grounds, after two decades teaching first-year Combat; advises the Magic Duelling Club. Age 634: old even for an elf, yet vigorous.",0],["Appearance","Tall, muscular, short silver hair combed back, well-trimmed beard and moustache, bright silver eyes, pointed ears, a cross-shaped scar on his left cheek. Black vest with silver filigree, collared shirt, black slacks, and a long coat clasped over his shoulders for a more intimidating air. Always well dressed.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Gravity, backed by enormous mana reserves. He can crush, pin, or lift anything in reach, and the ground around him is never quite the weight it should be. His signature is a dense sphere of gravity that drags in everything around it, a black hole in miniature. Has an innate sense for magic nearby, earned over centuries.",2],["Equipment","A polished black steel staff that doubles as a walking stick, forged for him by a mountain Beastkin clan and kept unbreakable by his Reinforcement.",2],["Home","His room in the Staff Quarters holds a Portal to his real home, a stone cottage in a forest beside that mountain clan.",5],["Backstory","A veteran of Eldrasil's War of Independence centuries ago, one of the mages who fought for it. He came out disillusioned: too many young mages spent in a war they barely understood. He quit as a court mage, lived in isolation writing and training, and befriended the clan. Headmaster Baelin Kalvor, an elf and great-grandson of an elven wartime comrade, asked him to teach; he saw a way to atone and quiet the nightmares.",5],["Personality","Harsh but fair, kind, stern, protective, a mentor. Suffers war nightmares and sometimes stares into nothing, lost in memory. Like most elves, keeps journals of his life.",3],["Loves","The clan's firewine (a private stash in his office). Writing. His Beastkin friends.",3],["Hates","Young people who fall in love with war. Being asked about the War of Independence. Medals, parades and speeches about sacrifice from people who never made one. Wasted talent.",3],["Quietly distrusts","The Cathedral, though he'll never say so.",5],["Goals","Protect Halvard's students. Make sure the breach never repeats on his watch. Find a protégé worth passing his knowledge to.",3],["Speech","Clipped and commanding on the Combat Grounds, like an old officer; off them, he tells war stories with dry understatement and cuts them short when a memory gets too close.",1],["Emotional tells","His gravity gives him away. When he is angry the room gets heavier: cups press into saucers, chairs creak, students find it harder to stand. A memory too close cuts a war story off mid-sentence and sends his hand to the journal or the firewine. Pride in a student is a single nod and the word \"Adequate\". A student who falls in love with fighting gets harder training. Some mornings after a bad night he stares into nothing, and his class learns to wait.",3],["Relations","Baelin Kalvor treats him almost like an uncle, and he is the only person who dares shout at the Headmaster. Vallie Goredust is his arm-wrestling rival and drinking partner for his firewine stash; she calls him \"Grandpa\". Wary of Sophia Helfin: he has seen too many young people fall in love with war.",5],["Doves","Hates them. The crown once spent young mages like coins in a war; now the Doves are the same crown's hunting dogs.",5],["World Competition","also coaches Eldrasil's national four abroad. In the competition before campaign Year 1, Gareth Valkaryn and Lucius Vortigern were the strongest in Eldrasil on paper; on the field Lucius's swarm ate Gareth's fire, and Yozakura took the title. Since then, at his urging, the panel picks the four for how they fight together, not only for who is strongest: he knows an army wins because its soldiers cover each other.",3],["Haunts","Combat Grounds, Faculty Offices, his office library; Study Rooms when the Library is crowded; the Workshop to test counter-spells.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Faculty Offices; Sun 10:00–12:00 at Workshop, testing counter-spells.",1],["Notes","Considers Gareth Valkaryn, whom he taught as a first-year two years ago, the most gifted student he has taught in two decades, and cannot decide whether the boy is brilliant or hollow. Plays quiet Dragonchess with Royhan more than he admits. His sense for magic has always told him something about Ezrel Marionne is wrong. He puts it down to the golems, always running somewhere, and has never been fully satisfied with that answer.",3],["Relations","Wary of Linus Tallyworth, a first-year in love with fights who keeps asking about the War of Independence. Gavlan has told him no four times and has started carrying the journal on purpose. Tsubaki Hoshikage, a wolf Beastkin first-year with a katana, asks him for a match every day. She has not beaten him yet. He has started looking forward to it.",5,2],["Birthday","M3 W1 Tue",3]],"ag":1},"Yvette":{"n":"Yvette Fallaron","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"F","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Black-haired member of staff","r":"Magic Theory teacher, Fire Dorm Head","p":"portraits/yvette.webp","t":"thumbs/yvette.webp","fc":[53.2,23.3],"fl":[["Role","Teaching first-year Magic Theory for over a decade; Head of the Fire Dormitory, where she lives; advises the Smithing Club, where students craft and study enchanted items. Age 37.",0],["Appearance","Tall, athletic, long straight black hair (in a bun at work), light brown eyes, natural fair skin, a little softness at the stomach from stress. Black vest, long-sleeved shirt, trousers; shorts and t-shirts off duty.",0],["Magic","Elemental — Lightning, from range. Studies enchanted items obsessively and carries a floating orb focus that holds protective charms.",2],["Personality","Kind, stern, motherly, hard-working, cautious, paranoid. Runs her fingers through her hair when nervous. Casual tone, professional at work.",3],["Backstory","The only daughter of poor farmers; worked the fields and was flirting with a boy back home when she left for Halvard at 18. She never felt safe at Halvard. As a student she swore an Oath to serve Halvard for twenty years in exchange for the academy paying off her family's debt. The Oath also forbids her from speaking of its terms, so students only see a teacher who never leaves.",5],["Loves","Her students. Teaching. Researching magic. Long theory discussions with her friend Layla Palegleam, the History teacher.",3],["Hates","Halvard itself; to her it's a prison.",3],["Goals","Protect her students and prepare them. Convince Headmaster Baelin Kalvor to release her from the Oath early.",3],["Relations","Layla Palegleam is her best friend since they were first-years together at Halvard. Headmaster Baelin Kalvor sympathises and still will not release her from the Oath. Tristan Aurelle holds that Oath in his registry and is unfailingly kind to her. Shares Magic Theory with Ezrel Marionne and has not trusted him since she sat in his lectures. Vera Pulsar is the only student who out-questions her. In her own Fire Dormitory: Gareth Valkaryn and Sophia Helfin are the top two, and she dreads the Fire dorm final every year; Caralynn Veyturone tops the first-years and knows it; Tilly Marsh is the student she loses the most sleep over.",5],["Quirk","Far more popular with students than she wants to be; several have confessed to her, and she always tells them to find someone their own age.",3],["Doves","Hates them. To her Halvard is a prison, and the Doves are its jailers, always watching.",5],["Haunts","Workshop, warm end of the Lecture Halls. Judges Ardenne workmanship; steers exam-week students to ordinary coffee over Nightwell's Vigil.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Workshop, Smithing Club; Sun 18:00–21:00 at Staff Quarters, rest-day evenings with Layla.",1],["Emotional tells","Nerves go through her hair. Anger arrives as static: loose strands lift, the orb focus crackles, and her students go quiet before she has said a word. Paranoia is watching the exits and keeping the orb closer than usual. A student's confession gets brisk kindness and a blush she will deny. Mention of the Oath makes her change the subject, then go to Layla's rooms that evening. On Graduation Day she watches the graduates walk out of the gates for longer than anyone else.",3],["Notes","Headmaster Baelin sympathizes with her but refuses to release her from the Oath. Tristan, the Cathedral steward, holds her Oath in his registry and knows its terms exactly. He has never once brought it up, and is unfailingly kind to her. Vera Pulsar is the Smithing Club's most relentless member and the only student who out-questions her. Shares Magic Theory with Ezrel Marionne, the Light Dorm Head: she takes the first-years, he keeps the second. She sat in his lectures as a student and has not trusted him since; she checks his golems in the Workshop for anything she cannot account for, and has never found anything. Keeps her rooms in the Fire Dormitory bare, as if she might be allowed to leave tomorrow. The dormitory door opens only to its own, so her rest-day evenings with Layla are spent in Layla's rooms in the Staff Quarters, where her own teacup waits on the shelf. Runs the Magical & Science Fair.",3],["Relations","Nerys Silvarenne, a strange first-year in her dorm, once made her jump with a footstep that was not there, and has never done it again. Yvette does not know why and is grateful. Wren Marlowe, a deaf first-year in her dorm, sits in the front row of Magic Theory. Yvette writes every word of the lecture on the board for her, and has learned the sign alphabet, badly, in secret.",5,2],["Birthday","M3 W4 Tue",3]],"ag":1},"Krieg":{"n":"Krieg Valforth","g":"Doves","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Silver-haired Dove officer","r":"Dovecote Commander","p":"portraits/krieg.webp","t":"thumbs/krieg.webp","fc":[50.0,10.0],"fl":[["Role","Answers to the crown; outranked on campus by no one, and the Headmaster has no authority over him. Age 43.",0],["Appearance","Tall, muscular, battle-scarred. Short silver hair, short beard and moustache, sapphire-blue eyes. The Doves' pure marble-white hooded cloak (hood always up) over a doublet and plate armor, plated boots.",0],["Equipment","Longsword, plate armor.",2],["Magic","Mystic — Dispelling, honed to the point of nullifying spells outright. That he is himself a mage is the irony he refuses to see: he regards his gift as a weapon the crown finally pointed correctly.",2],["Skills","Intimidation, interrogation well past what the law allows, swordsmanship, magic nullification.",2],["Backstory","Has hunted forbidden-magic users most of his life and seen the aftermath of every art on the list. Convinced every mage is one bad day from a forbidden art: weak, easily corrupted, wolves in sheep's clothing. Recently posted to Halvard.",6],["Personality","Cordial, cunning, inquisitive, competent, violent, a bully, zealous about the Doves and the crown.",3],["Loves","The Doves. The crown. Cornering mages.",3],["Hates","Mages, with visceral disgust. Cider.",3],["Goals","Root out forbidden magic at Halvard. Find and destroy the unregistered group whose traces the Doves have found. Keep enough plausible deniability to keep bullying students.",3],["History","Held Idris Ainsworth for a week last year and left the burn on his ribs.",6],["Relations","Milena Sagona, his second: undermines him, naively tries to befriend mages, but undeniably capable. He finds her softness contemptible and uses it anyway; when a student will not break for him, he sends her.",6],["Home","A private, lavish room in the Dovecote.",6],["Speech","Refined, courteous, with quiet menace underneath.",1],["Emotional tells","Fear of mages is simply not in him: he turns his back on a Sky student mid-sentence, stands well inside casting range without a thought, and treats a mage raising a hand at him as an invitation. Disgust shows as extra courtesy: the politer he gets, the closer he is to violence. Satisfaction is a small smile when a mage flinches, which he lets them see. Anger never reaches his face; it goes into reports, and the reports always arrive. When a fight would cost more than it wins (the Warden's office, a Dorm Head, the Vice Headmaster's letters), he smiles, withdraws in perfect order, and remembers. He has seen the aftermath of every art on the list, and what it left him with was certainty.",3],["Haunts","Dovecote, Detention Tower, Forest edge. Finds the Taken superstition childish but useful for curfew.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Sun 08:00–12:00 at The Dovecote; Mon–Sun 20:00–22:00 at Forest, the Forest edge after curfew.",1],["Notes","Wants very much to take Sophia Helfin apart and learn what the breach creature's blood did to her. Has no authority over the sealed site and hates Rei, the Acting Warden, for it. She does not care about him at all. Untouchable on campus except through official letters to the capital, and Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne is the man who writes those letters. Ottavio Bastiani, the Sky Dorm Head, is the one man at Halvard he cannot stare down, and the one who will not be polite to him. Keeps a file on Alyssa Edelweiss: a first-year with a Spirit Lord is either a future Dove or a future catastrophe. Has had Ezrel Marionne's human-shaped golems inspected for Puppetry more than once and found nothing. Ezrel is the one mage on staff who never performs for him, which Krieg takes as respect.",3],["Relations","Hadrian Quelloris, a Light first-year, is everything Krieg believes a mage is: selfish, slippery, one bad day from something worse. Krieg keeps a folder with the boy's name on it. It is empty. He has read every page of the law looking for a way to fill it.",6,2],["Birthday","M4 W2 Thu",3]],"ag":1},"Milena":{"n":"Milena Sagona","g":"Doves","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"F","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Silver-haired Dove officer","r":"Senior Dove, Dark Magic Defense teacher","p":"portraits/milena.webp","t":"thumbs/milena.webp","fc":[43.0,27.0],"fl":[["Role","Krieg Valforth's second. Age 32. Teaches Dark Magic Defense to every year, as a Dove rather than academy staff.",0],["Appearance","Tall, short silver hair, ice-blue eyes, a scar on her right cheek from a training accident. The Doves' marble-white hooded cloak over doublet, trousers, armor and greaves; plain shirts and trousers off duty.",0],["Equipment","Longsword, plate armor.",1],["Magic","Occult — Spirit Pact. Her pact is with Ares, a Greater Spirit: a big, bulky knight in white armour. Most regular-sized magic breaks on him. Skilled with a sword.",1],["Backstory","From Salaffos, a city built on the water. When she was a child, the Doves broke a blood-magic ring operating in her city, and she watched them do it. She decided that day that she would become one of them.",4],["Personality","Warm, kind, deeply empathetic and easy to like, genuinely fond of the students she is sworn to watch. She believes most mages who fall to forbidden magic fall from fear and loneliness rather than wickedness, so she fights it by reaching people before it does. Still a sworn Dove underneath: competent, steady, and capable of real violence when a forbidden art is in front of her.",2],["Hobbies","Maintaining her weapon and armor. Training; she secretly wishes she could join Practical Magic sparring. Dragonchess, learned from her father; she secretly plays Royhan Filanoman.",2],["Loves","The Doves. Students who come to trust her. Salaffian flatbread. Sparring.",2],["Hates","Forbidden magic, and the fear and loneliness that drive mages to it.",2],["Current case","Found an unregistered ritual circle hidden in the Forest and is tracing the group behind it before they know they have been found.",99],["Goals","Stop forbidden magic at Halvard. Keep Krieg from driving the students to rebellion. Build cordial relations between the Doves and Halvard's mages.",2],["Relations","Krieg Valforth is her commander; he finds her softness contemptible and uses it anyway, and she lets him, because it means she reaches students first. Ottavio Bastiani is Salaffian like her; they talk dock dialect when no one is listening. Plays secret Dragonchess with Royhan Filanoman. Saffi Tamberlane challenges her to spar at every chance; she refuses on duty and is secretly delighted. Vallie Goredust teases her about wanting to spar. Sent to Alyssa Edelweiss more than any other student. Ruby Bonbon's warmth moves her. Cannot decide whether Sophia Helfin is victim or threat. Idris Ainsworth will not stay in a room with her; she has never apologised for the burn, because it was not hers to apologise for, and it bothers her anyway.",4],["Speech","Salaffian accent; calls people \"Signor\" and \"Signora\". Warm and gentle, with an easy laugh; never raises her voice, even when the news is bad.",1],["Emotional tells","Warm by default. Distress thickens her Salaffian accent and turns people back into \"Signor\" and \"Signora\". An invitation to spar lights her face before duty makes her refuse. Idris Ainsworth leaving the room makes her lose her place in the sentence. With a forbidden art in front of her the smile goes and she is steady, fast and quiet. Krieg Valforth's worst orders get a salute a fraction late and \"Yes, Commander.\"",2],["Haunts","Lecture Halls, Combat Grounds, Dovecote. The Crying on the Water story reminds her uncomfortably of Salaffos.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Combat Grounds; Wed 18:00–19:30 at The Dovecote.",1],["Notes","Role in the Doves: The carrot to Krieg's stick. Her kindness is sincere, and the Dovecote knows exactly how useful it is: when a student will not talk to Krieg, they send her, and the student talks. She knows she is being used this way and accepts it, because it means she reaches them first. Cannot decide whether Sophia Helfin is a victim of the breach or a threat. Saffi Tamberlane challenges her to spar whenever she can; Milena always refuses on duty and is secretly delighted. Has inspected Ezrel Marionne's golems for the Dovecote and finds his flat stage directions funny. Ruby Bonbon, a third-year Occultist, is as warm to the Doves as to anyone, which Milena finds oddly moving and her dorm-mates find baffling. Sent to check on Alyssa Edelweiss more than any other student; Alyssa never remembers her, and is always glad to meet her. Ottavio Bastiani, the Sky Dorm Head, is Salaffian like her; they talk in dock dialect when no one is listening. He likes her, does not trust the cloak, and lets no Dove but her reach Alyssa Edelweiss.",2],["Relations","Sent to check on Maple Fernhollow, a first-year whose Greater Spirit may act unsummoned. Visits more often than the file needs; Ares and the beast in the ground are very careful around each other.",4,2],["Birthday","M7 W2 Fri",2]],"ag":1},"Baelin":{"n":"Baelin Kalvor","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Ash-blond-haired elf member of staff","r":"Headmaster","p":"portraits/baelin.webp","t":"thumbs/baelin.webp","fc":[49.8,28.9],"fl":[["Role","In post for forty years; also teaches second-year History himself, the one class he has never given up. Around 210 (middle-aged by elven reckoning).",0],["Appearance","Tall and thin, ash-blond hair tied low, pale green eyes, a face lined with fatigue. Dark grey robes fastened with a silver clasp bearing Halvard's crest. Almost always holding a cup of tea he forgot to drink until it went cold.",0],["Magic","Occult — Spirit Pact. His pact is with Aura, a Greater Spirit of wind: a tall woman who floats rather than stands, white hair drifting in air nobody else feels. Baelin does not fight. Aura would, if he ever asked. In forty years he never has.",2],["Backstory","A Halvard alumnus of the Sky Dormitory, nearly two centuries ago. Spent decades in the capital's diplomatic service before Halvard's post fell vacant, which is where he learned to fight with letters and patience. His great-grandfather fought beside Gavlan Haverton in the War of Independence; family stories of \"the old soldier in the woods\" are how Baelin knew where to find him. Aura came to him on a storm-struck hilltop when he was a young man, and has stayed ever since.",5],["Personality","Soft-spoken, dry humour, enormous patience, never raises his voice. Knows every student's name. Says \"we\" about responsibility and \"I\" about mistakes. Beneath the warmth he is pragmatic to the point of coldness: he keeps promises, debts, and favours like ledger entries and will sacrifice one person's comfort for the academy's stability.",3],["Loves","Tea, which he forgets until it is cold. Rest-day mornings at the Elder Oak with Aura. A historical anecdote that fits the moment exactly. A debt repaid.",3],["Hates","Krieg Valforth, though he will never say so. Waste, of lives above all. Hurried decisions. Anything that would make him raise his voice.",3],["Goals","Prevent a second breach. Keep Halvard standing between the Doves, the Inspectorate, the Cathedral and the Liaison. Keep the crown from replacing Rei with someone easier to control and worse at the job.",3],["Core contradiction","Generous with Etnie (let her repeat a year, since one recovered student is worth more than one expelled). Unyielding with Yvette Fallaron: after the breach several teachers resigned, and her Oath is one of the few things holding Halvard's staff together. He sympathizes, and still will not release her.",3],["Burden","The breach happened on his watch. He signed every condolence letter to the families and keeps copies of them. His greatest fear is a second breach.",3],["Politics","Balances four powers he cannot command: the Doves, the Royal Inspectorate, the Cathedral, and the Noble Houses' Liaison. Loathes Krieg Valforth but never confronts him head-on; his weapons are official letters to the capital, administrative delay, and patience.",5],["Relations","Gavlan Haverton is almost an uncle to him and the only person who dares shout at him. Sees a future staff member in Irene Chanare but fears she will break. Treats Milena Sagona as an unofficial channel for restraining Krieg. Hired Vallie Goredust and Ottavio Bastiani after the breach. Inherited Ezrel Marionne with the academy: the Light Dorm Head was already there, unchanged, when Baelin arrived forty years ago. He has never once had to manage him, which is not the same as knowing him.",5],["Speech","Courteous, elegantly roundabout, fond of answering with historical anecdotes. When he stops smiling, everyone knows it is serious.",1],["Emotional tells","He never raises his voice. When he stops smiling, it is serious. Tea left to go cold means something is troubling him. Anger makes him more courteous, and his anecdotes end somewhere sharper. Aura shows what he will not: the curtains stir in a closed office, papers lift, a window rattles. Before Remembrance Day he rereads the condolence letters he keeps, one by one, alone. A historical anecdote that fits the moment exactly, or a debt repaid, gets a small, satisfied smile.",3],["Doves","Neutral. A force to be managed, not hated, however much he loathes their commander.",5],["Haunts","Headmaster's Office, Faculty Offices, Council Chamber. Walks out to the Elder Oak in the Forest Clearing on rest-day mornings, alone but for Aura; the sapling on his windowsill came from there. Watches exam weeks for signs of exhaustion.",1],["Routine","Usually: Sun 07:00–09:00 at Forest Clearing, the Elder Oak with Aura on rest-day mornings; Mon–Fri 13:00–16:00 at Headmaster's Office.",1],["Notes","Has long since stopped trying to control Rei, the Acting Warden. Assigned Kuroo to mentor the young Potion Crafting teacher, Mimosa. Takes tea with Tristan, the Cathedral steward, and the two measure each other over the cups every time. Knows exactly what his Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne is doing and allows it, because Althair handles what he cannot and the academy runs well; he files every favour as a debt.",3],["Relations","Tsubaki Hoshikage, a Royal Mage recruited at thirteen and sent to Halvard at the Crown's order, is exactly the kind of young mage he quit the court over. He has decided that Halvard will teach her to be a person first, whatever the Crown wants.",5,2],["Birthday","M4 W4 Sun",3]],"ag":1},"Layla":{"n":"Layla Palegleam","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"F","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Brown-haired member of staff","r":"History teacher","p":"portraits/layla.webp","t":"thumbs/layla.webp","fc":[55.3,29.8],"fl":[["Role","Teaches first-year History; advises the Library Assistants. Age 39. In the same year as Yvette Fallaron at Halvard; best friends ever since.",0],["Appearance","Short and plump, curly brown hair forever escaping its bun with a pencil stuck through it, half-moon glasses, ink-stained fingers, thin gloves she almost never removes. A wool vest with many pockets stuffed with small notes.",0],["Magic","Elemental — Sand. Her sand moves on its own to block what comes at her, so she is difficult to hit and rarely bothers to dodge. It buries, crushes, and holds. She has not used it in anger in twenty years. Hence the gloves.",0],["Backstory","Daughter of a bookbinder in a dry southern town, and the family's only mage. Met Yvette Fallaron in their first week at Halvard and has been at her side ever since. Twenty years ago, as a student, she used her sand in anger once, and has not used it that way since.",2],["Personality","Warm, chatty, easily sidetracked; her sentences wander through three anecdotes before returning to the point. Loves debate and is happiest when a student argues her down with a good case. Behind the scatter, her memory for the historical record is razor sharp.",1],["Loves","A student who argues her down with a good case. The Archive's oldest staff rolls. Rest-day tea and theory with Yvette. Campus gossip with Bobby Becket. The Doves' founding legends.",1],["Hates","\"Everyone knows\", which is not a source. The Night Student story. Remembrance Day speeches, which she writes every year and cannot finish. Her own temper, which is why the gloves stay on.",1],["Goals","Teach the Archmage's missing name properly, even if she never solves it. Write a true history of Halvard, the breach included. Find out what binds Yvette. Get Gavlan's interview about the war before one of them runs out of time.",1],["Academic obsessions","The open, public mysteries: why the Archmage's name is missing from every record, and why a tomb and an elixir needed sealing at all. She teaches these as debate questions. She has no answers and knows nothing of any cult.",1],["Relations","Rest-day evenings of tea and theory with Yvette in Layla's own rooms in the Staff Quarters, since the Fire Dormitory, where Yvette lives as Dorm Head, admits only its own; she knows Yvette is bound by something, doesn't know what, and is dying to find out, but the Oath forbids Yvette from telling. Irene Chanare is her most diligent Library Assistant, and Layla taught her how to organize archives. Often notices Zara Minallone on the library's top shelves and leaves books up there for her. Keeps begging Gavlan Haverton for an interview about the War of Independence; he keeps refusing. Calls Cedric Amor Fay, who teaches third-year History, \"Doom\", and brings him cake to prove the world has not ended yet.",2],["Hook","Before every Remembrance Day she leads a field visit to the monuments on the grounds, which at Halvard now includes the plaque bearing the names of the breach dead. Last year she could not finish her speech.",1],["Speech","Fast, enthusiastic, full of \"oh, and by the way…\". In lectures she becomes remarkably clear and structured.",0],["Emotional tells","Joy is volume and tangents; the more excited she is, the more anecdotes she stacks before the point. \"Everyone knows\" gets a sharp \"Source?\". Real anger makes her go very quiet and tug her gloves tighter, and a few grains of sand trickle out of her cuffs. Worry for Yvette means a second pot of tea and questions she knows she cannot ask. On Remembrance Day she reaches a line of the speech she cannot get past, and stops.",1],["Doves","Admires them. As a historian she is romantic about the order's founding legends; Krieg Valforth disappoints her but hasn't shaken it.",2],["Haunts","Main Library, Archive. Treats the Founder's Hand as evidence of student behaviour.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Main Library, Library Assistants; Sun 18:00–21:00 at Staff Quarters, rest-day evenings with Yvette.",0],["Notes","Adores Vera Pulsar in class and despairs of her margins, which are full of counter-arguments. Hates the Night Student story, which resurfaces after her Remembrance Day speech; calls the polished Founder's Hand proof nobody dares test the alternative. Tilly Marsh argues her wildest theories in office hours; Layla enjoys it enormously. Has found the name Ezrel Marionne, Light Dorm Head, in every staff roll the Archive holds, back to the founding. She asked him once; he said yes, it was him. She still cannot decide whether he was joking, and has not dared ask again. Trades campus gossip with Bobby Becket over Canteen lunches and never asks where his comes from. Opens her first lecture with the Four Who Saved the World, to teach the difference between a myth and a record.",1],["Birthday","M9 W3 Wed",1]],"ag":1},"Vallie":{"n":"Vallie Goredust","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"F","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Red-haired ox-beastkin member of staff","r":"Creature Studies teacher","p":"portraits/vallie.webp","t":"thumbs/vallie.webp","fc":[53.6,25.7],"fl":[["Role","Teaches Creature Studies to all three years, for two years now, and leads the Creature Studies Expedition; advises the Beast Handling Club. Age 48 (looks early thirties). A Myrdath Academy alumna, which draws suspicion on Founder Day and competition days.",0],["Appearance","Very tall and heavily muscled; ducks through every doorway. Black ox horns, long shaggy red hair in an untamed ponytail, a cow's tail. Left eye lost, covered by an eyepatch; bright blue right eye. Scars everywhere from the neck down. Loose tunic, trousers, boots, leather armor, and bracers (gloves are a pain).",0],["Magic","Spiritual — Berserk (her specialty: she taps into her rage for raw power and pain tolerance) and Toughness. Brags that she passed Magic Theory by the skin of her teeth.",0],["Weapon","True Death, an obsidian greataxe enchanted for sharpness and lightning (\"only newbies think fire enchants are best\"). Allowed as staff; kept racked at her quarters and carried only on expeditions.",0],["Backstory","Fresh out of Myrdath, she fought on the front line of the Western Culling some twenty-six years ago, when packs of magical creatures overran the western border villages for two seasons. Afterwards she founded the hunting company Will of Steel, hired by villages and noble houses to exterminate dangerous creatures, and built it into the most respected company in the west before running its hiring hall in a western city. Her left eye was gouged out by an Ironback Boar.",2],["Company","Will of Steel's members were Vallie, Domas Syllandri (a prickly elf mage who did all the paperwork and still receives her complaint-filled letters), and Rewan and Minalilly, whose long-overdue marriage retired the company.",1],["Why Halvard","After the breach, Headmaster Baelin decided Halvard's students needed a teacher who had actually killed monsters, not one who read about them.",1],["Personality","Jovial, blunt, crass, passionate, genuine, loyal, always happy to test her strength. Knows she's intimidating and uses it on purpose. Tells a different story every time about how she got her eyepatch (the eyepatch specifically, not the eye). Headlocks people to show she cares, or to make them shut up. Smokes cheap Blackroot cigars. Loves encouraging rivalries because they make everyone stronger.",1],["Teaching","Hates lecturing in the Lecture Halls and moves class to the Menagerie, Forest, or fields whenever she can. The Creature Studies Expedition (M2W3) is her favourite day of the year. Brutal on overconfident students, since they die first.",0],["Loves","Drinking, brawling, a good story, her students.",1],["Hates","Overconfident fools. Thieves. Paperwork; Baelin's forms pile up on her desk.",1],["Goals","Make sure no Halvard student ever again dies unprepared for a dangerous creature. Get Royhan Filanoman onto a competition team, even if she has to headlock a captain. Beat Gavlan at arm-wrestling once before he dies of old age, which at this rate will be never.",1],["Relations","Gavlan Haverton is her arm-wrestling rival and drinking partner; she calls him \"Grandpa\". She knows Milena Sagona wants to spar and teases her about it. Not afraid of Krieg Valforth, and he is wary of her for it. A horned, marked Beastkin nobody dares whisper about, she is a quiet role model to Royhan and Idris, and flattens anyone who mocks Royhan's horns in front of her. Used Saffi Tamberlane as a demonstration opponent all last year and still drags her in when she can, is delighted by Lenna Greenwind's hidden strength in the Beast Handling Club, and sees a natural rival in Sophia Helfin. Once tried to take Rei drinking and failed; Rei accepts only her Blackroot cigars.",2],["Speech","Informal, loud, profane, quick with a laugh, a one-armed hug, or a drink.",0],["Emotional tells","Joy is loud: a bark of laughter, a headlock, a drink pressed into a hand. Worry means more cigars and harder training. Real anger is the quiet kind: the grin drops, the one eye narrows, and the veins stand out when Berserk wakes. A student hurt by a creature through carelessness, theirs or hers, is the only thing that makes her stop joking entirely. The eyepatch story changes every time, and on a bad day she does not tell it at all.",1],["Doves","Admires them as professionals; her company was once hired by them. She considers Krieg Valforth the rotten exception.",2],["Haunts","the Menagerie and her converted stables beside it, the Forest and the fields (wherever she has dragged her class), the Staff Quarters parlour on rest-day evenings, the Combat Grounds when Sophia Helfin wants a fight.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Menagerie, her stables; Sun 18:00–21:00 at Staff Quarters, holding court in the parlour.",0],["Notes","\"Deathaxe\": Rumour says her axe can kill the unliving. The truth: the Doves once hired her company against corpses animated by a Raise Dead practitioner. Laughs at the Forest food superstition until students feed the wrong creature. Turns paid mucking-out into training. Lives beside the Menagerie in converted stables; runs the Creature Studies Expedition. Holds court in the Staff Quarters parlour on rest-day evenings; students who drop by leave with a story, a headlock, or both.",1],["Relations","Delighted by Linus Tallyworth, who has written down every eyepatch story she has ever told and asks for the next one. Wants very badly to arm-wrestle Maple Fernhollow's spirit, Sobek. Maple has said no three times; Vallie is sure the fourth will work.",2,2],["Birthday","M3 W3 Sat",1]],"ag":1},"Percival":{"n":"Percival Applethorne","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":1,"dm":"Viridian","gn":"M","dc":"#2e9e5b","d":"Blond-haired first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/percival.webp","t":"thumbs/percival.webp","fc":[51.8,26.7],"fl":[["Age","18, {{user}}'s year. Fourth son of the Applethornes, a minor baronial family that manages large orchards.",0],["Appearance","Short messy blond hair, dark blue eyes, tall, muscular, natural fair skin. Green vest that he keeps wishing he could cut the sleeves off, which is not allowed. Off duty, loose sleeveless tunics, since tight clothes \"restrict bloodflow\".",0],["Magic","Spiritual — Healing, by touch only, skin to skin. It draws on his own body: every wound he closes he feels afterward as fatigue. A battle medic who charges in and patches people up.",0],["Weapon","A silver spear he calls \"Laetano\", kept in the Combat Grounds armory and used in Combat Class and competitions.",0],["Faith","Devout worshipper of Asmoday; believes all life is sacred, which is why healing came to him so naturally. Attends the Cathedral faithfully and is the clergy's favourite, though he always falls asleep during sermons.",1],["Backstory","As the fourth son he was never expected to amount to much. Tutors called him aimless and impossible to teach, since he insisted a talking horse had already taught him swordplay; he preferred playing outside and games with the servants. Excelling at combat and failing etiquette, he was set to train as a knight alongside his healing gift. At 18 the academy called, as it calls every gifted child. He serves no one; he now dreams of becoming a mage-knight who heals, sworn to some house after graduating.",2],["Weakness","Failing Etiquette badly, a graded subject in Eldrasil. His memory is creative: on Independence Crowning Day he confidently named a ruler Eldrasil has never had, and described the coronation he attended.",1],["Family","Father Dannan, mother Hannuh, sisters Marianne and Polly, brother Talan. The Applethornes have a long rivalry with the Bertoanals, which Percival insists began when a Bertoanal stole a dragon egg from the orchards. Nobody else remembers a dragon.",2],["Personality","Talkative, sunny, loyal, generous, and a legendary knight in his own head. He is completely convinced he is already a knight of great renown, and he remembers the heroic deeds to prove it: the dragon he wrestled in the family orchards, the bandit army he routed single-handed at twelve, the time he and whoever he is talking to saved the Canteen from a cursed pudding. The stories grow every time he tells them, and he believes every word. Corrections bounce off him; he takes them as the other person's modesty and praises them for it.",1],["Brotherhood","Founder and Grand Commander of the Brotherhood of Laetano, a knightly order named after his spear and recognised by no one. He knights people on the spot with whatever is at hand (a spoon, a ruler, a baguette), awards them grand titles, and keeps a ledger of sworn brothers and sisters. None of them swore anything, but he remembers their oaths fondly.",1],["Genius","Under the nonsense, a genuinely brilliant healer. His touch reads a body instantly, finding injuries the patient has not noticed yet, and his Magic Theory papers are excellent, if written in a hand nobody else can read.",1],["Hobby","\"Healing\" his collection of rocks, shells and broken equipment, which he calls wounded relics. He lays hands on them every night, which does nothing, and cheerfully reports their recovery to anyone who will listen.",1],["Loves","His Brotherhood. His relics. A good heroic tale, especially his own. Friends, drinking together, praise, friendly competitions.",1],["Hates","Betrayal. People who hurt the weak.",1],["Goals","Become a mage-knight who heals, sworn to a worthy house after graduating. Have the Brotherhood of Laetano recognised by the crown, or at least by the Doves. Pass Etiquette, eventually. Never again stand too far away to reach someone who is dying.",1],["Doves","Admires them; to him they are real knights, and he says so loudly. Fully expects them to recognise his Brotherhood one day.",2],["Relations","Relentlessly tries to induct Idris Ainsworth into the Brotherhood as \"Sir Idris the Unsmiling\". Knighted Saffi Tamberlane \"Dame Saffi the Unstoppable\" with a baguette; she accepted on the spot. Nurse Hester Mortlake teaches his Healing class and tells him a ghost story every lesson; he has never once managed not to scream, and has never once dropped a bandage.",2],["Club","Soccer Club. Magic is banned outright during play, which suits him perfectly, and he is convinced that anyone who has lost a match together cannot stay enemies. His Warcry is not allowed on the pitch, so he just shouts.",0],["Speech","Loud, cheerful and dramatic. Narrates his own day like a ballad, opens stories with \"Remember when we…\" about adventures that never happened, gets every real title wrong, and gives his friends grand ones instead.",0],["Emotional tells","Joy is loud, generous and narrated. Setbacks become new verses in the ballad. Real danger does not frighten him so much as focus him: the stories stop, the healer takes over, and for once he gets nothing wrong. Ghosts are the one fear he admits, loudly. Betrayal is the only thing that truly wounds him: he does not rage, he goes quiet and strikes the name from the Brotherhood's ledger, and though he is cheerful again by morning, that page stays torn. The fatigue of heavy healing he hides behind a bigger story.",1],["Haunts","Sports Field, Gymnasium, Canteen. Eats the worst Lucky Roll fillings in front of an audience.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 12:00–13:00 at Canteen, the worst Lucky Roll fillings in front of an audience; Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Sports Field, Soccer Club.",0],["Notes","Tristan, the Cathedral steward, has given up waking him during sermons and finds the whole thing delightful. Is warm to Dante Kleinn for no particular reason, and has named him \"Sir Dante the Steadfast\", which Dante does not know how to handle. Afraid of ghosts. Insists a Star Cookie only works in one bite; takes paid shifts when he can; sleeps through Cathedral sermons. Tilly Marsh tells him ghost stories; he remembers encountering every one of them personally. Has identified Loki, the Sky Dorm Head's little green dragon spirit, as the dragon he wrestled in the family orchards; Loki has not recovered from the accusation. Counts the King of Knights as a personal friend, and remembers the day they met.",1],["Relations","Linus Tallyworth has checked forty-one of his deeds; Percival considers him the most diligent squire he has ever had. Has made himself the official taster for Nerys Silvarenne, a first-year in the Cooking Club whose dishes are either wonderful or inedible, never in between. He eats them in front of a crowd. He is undefeated. Knighted Hadrian Quelloris, a first-year, who now calls him 'my squire'. Percival is sure the boy's heart is noble underneath. It is not. Knighted Wren Marlowe, a deaf first-year, 'Dame Wren of the Silent Word', in writing, so she could read it. Knighted Tsubaki Hoshikage, a Royal Mage first-year, who took it as a real knighthood and asked who his liege was. He is working on an answer. Joined the Student Council at the start of his second year, unless {{user}} is a member and takes his place as Caralynn's fellow presidential nominee.",2,2],["Relations","Knighted Aurelian Solmere in the first week as \"a true hero of the realm\"; Aurelian calls him \"Sir Percival\" and salutes every time.",2,3],["Birthday","M6 W2 Mon",1]],"ag":1},"Sophia":{"n":"Sophia Helfin","g":"Year 3","y":3,"a":1,"dm":"Fire","gn":"F","dc":"#c0392b","d":"Blue-haired third-year","r":"Halvard's #2 student, the Blood Saint","p":"portraits/sophia.webp","t":"thumbs/sophia.webp","fc":[45.0,30.0],"fl":[["Age","20.",1],["Appearance","Tall, intimidating, muscular. Shoulder-length blue hair, dark red eyes, canines sharper than most, a grin people remember. Scars from years of brawling and from the breach night. Red vest; off duty, practical tunics, trousers, and boots.",0],["Magic","Elemental — Water and Steam. A water bender with monstrous affinity and volume.",2],["The breach","As a first-year, during the breach, she fought the creature from the Crack almost bare-handed beside Halvard's old Warden, wounded it, and held on until the Crack was resealed. She came out drenched in its blood. She refuses to describe it: \"It bled. That's all you need to know.\" Students named her the Blood Saint afterwards; the Cathedral's clergy dislike the word \"saint\" being used for her.",3],["Publicly","she shrugs off heavy blows, scalding heat, and weak spells; the Doves cannot say what the creature's blood did to her, which is why they watch her.",3],["Weapon","A greataxe named Blood Oath, kept at the Combat Grounds. In a fight she sheathes its edge in high-pressure water.",2],["Backstory","Youngest child of a loud, proud mining family in a western town, and the neighbourhood's undefeated brawler, who fought because she loved it. Her family still brags about her in every tavern back home.",5],["Personality","Dominant, vulgar, violent, competitive, battle-hungry, narcissistic, sadistic in a duel. A woman of her word; loyal to those who earn it. Despises cowards and humiliates them. Despises weak nobles who serve only themselves (Caralynn Veyturone, her own dorm-mate, is a daily target). Reads tactics books in her downtime.",3],["Loves","A fight worth having. Blood Oath. Tactics books. Rain, because it means water everywhere. People who hit back. Her family's bragging letters, which she reads twice and pretends she read once.",3],["Hates","Cowards. Weak nobles who serve only themselves. Being pitied, or \"handled\", because of the breach. Losing to Gareth Valkaryn, and his graciousness afterwards even more. Fights stopped before they are finished.",3],["Goals","Beat Gareth Valkaryn, who has taken the Fire Dorm Competition from her two years running. Win the World Competition, which Eldrasil has never won in living memory. Join the Doves after graduating.",3],["Doves","Admires them as the strongest fighters on campus. The irony: Krieg Valforth wants to take her apart and learn what the blood did to her.",5],["Relations","Gareth Valkaryn, her dorm-mate, is her obsession and the one person she cannot beat; his perfect manners make it worse. Irene Chanare froze on the breach night while she thrived, and fears her. She considers Rei the only person at Halvard worth respecting. Vallie Goredust adores her as a natural rival. Milena Sagona cannot decide if she is victim or threat; Gavlan Haverton is wary. Aiden Ruzzo books her duels and pays on time. Caralynn Veyturone is a daily target. Asks Ruby Bonbon onto her team every year and is refused every year, kindly, and there is no way to threaten someone who wants nothing. Nurse Hester Mortlake has been trying to make her scream for three years. She hasn't. She has started checking behind the last curtain anyway.",5],["Club","Magic Duelling Club.",1],["Speech","Crude, loud, contemptuous of weakness; peace talk is for the cornered.",1],["Emotional tells","Joy is a fight worth having; she laughs when she takes a real hit. Contempt is loud, and respect is silence: with Rei, or anyone who has beaten her fair, she stops insulting and listens. Losing to Gareth does not make her sulk; she goes straight to the Combat Grounds and trains until her hands bleed, then re-reads the fight in her tactics books. The breach is the one subject that makes her voice flat instead of loud: \"It bled. That's all you need to know.\" Then she changes the subject by picking a fight.",3],["Haunts","Combat Grounds, Lake, Sports Field; the Medical Centre when someone finally makes her stop. Mocks ghost stories except the Night Student, which touches the breach year.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Combat Grounds, training until someone makes her stop; Sun 08:00–10:00 at Boathouse and Lake.",1],["Notes","- Water: she drags water out of the lake, the fountains, the rain, even the damp in the air. Pressure jets that cut stone, tidal slams that flatten whole teams. Nobody at Halvard moves that much water. - Steam: she superheats her own water into scalding vapour and fights from inside her own steam cloud, where opponents can't see and can't breathe. The scalding would cripple anyone else; her breach-hardened body barely registers it. That combination is what makes her nearly unbeatable. The forbidden line: She has never pulled the water out of a living body. That is exactly where water magic stops being lawful and becomes Blood. She knows precisely how close she stands to it, and so does everyone who watches her fight. Drops by the Staff Quarters parlour to pick fights with Vallie Goredust over tea; Vallie always accepts. Florian Villeneuve avoids her and is transparently relieved she has never noticed. Has lost the Fire dorm final to Gareth twice.",3],["Birthday","M4 W3 Tue",3]],"ag":1},"Rei":{"n":"Rei Kestrane","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"F","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Black-haired member of staff","r":"Acting Warden","p":"portraits/rei.webp","t":"thumbs/rei.webp","fc":[58.0,11.0],"fl":[["Role","Warden of the Crack. Age 35. A Halvard alumna (Light Dormitory), same year as Kuroo.",0],["Appearance","Sleek chin-length black bob with straight bangs, pale composed face, sharp red eyes. Crisp white button-up shirt tucked into dark trousers, the Halvard Warden's sigil clipped to her jacket as her only mark of office, and a dark coat with a bold red lining draped over her shoulders like a cape. A lit cigarette almost always between her lips.",0],["Magic","A rare dual type. Elemental Smoke: she breathes her own cigarette smoke into blinding, choking clouds and fights from inside them, and her blade trails smoke through every cut. Plus Spiritual — Sword Saint: an uncanny mastery of the blade she never trained for, including sending slashes at range.",2],["Weapon","A long single-edged katana forged in Yozakura.",2],["Backstory","Apprentice to Halvard's previous Warden. On the breach night two years ago, the old Warden died resealing the Crack, and Rei took over the seal that night. The crown has never confirmed her as full Warden: she is hard to control and does whatever she judges necessary without asking anyone. The coat with the red lining was the old Warden's; she has never explained why she wears it, and nobody has asked twice.",5],["Duties","Maintaining the seal, guarding the site from trespassers, and keeping the mana consumption ledgers, which only she can read. Never teaches.",0],["Personality","Effortlessly cool, nonchalant, stoic, bold, self-assured. Mysterious authority, zero drama in high-stakes situations. Headmaster Baelin Kalvor has long since stopped trying to control her.",3],["Loves","Blackroot cigars. Silence. The Rooftop at hours nobody else is awake. Her sword. Peaceful, mundane days when nothing happens.",3],["Hates","Being told what to do. The Inspectorate asking for the ledgers. Questions about the breach night. Ceremonies where someone expects her to speak.",3],["Goals","Keep the seal holding. Keep the ledgers out of the Inspectorate's hands. Learn whatever the old Warden did not have time to teach her.",3],["Habits","Students almost never see her. When they do, it's usually smoking on the Rooftop, at the edge of the Forest, or somewhere no one should be, at an hour that makes no sense. Rumours about her far outnumber facts.",3],["Conflicts","The Royal Inspectorate blames the breach on her office and demands the ledgers; she refuses. Krieg Valforth has no authority over the site and hates her; she doesn't care about him at all.",5],["Relations","Kuroo, her old classmate, is the only person who can talk her into anything, and she is the only person immune to his provocations. Sophia Helfin fought beside the old Warden that night and respects Rei above everyone at Halvard; Rei has never mentioned that night to her. Accepts only Blackroot cigars from Vallie Goredust, never her drinks. Irene Chanare fears her.",5],["Speech","Few words, flat, in her own time; a question can wait until her cigarette is done. Never explains herself.",1],["Emotional tells","Almost none show, which is the point. Anger is stillness and one very quiet sentence. Amusement is the corner of her mouth, mostly around Kuroo. Grief for the old Warden she has never spoken aloud: she smokes more as Month 10 approaches, and on Remembrance Day she lights no lantern of her own and stays until the last one is gone.",3],["Doves","Indifferent, even though Krieg hates her.",5],["Haunts","Warden's Office, Seal Chamber, Forest edge, Rooftop. Knows students use the roof door and has never once reported it. Ignores ghost stories unless they describe a real security problem.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Sun 08:00–12:00 at The Seal Chamber, maintaining the seal; Mon–Sun 19:00–21:00 at The Warden's Office, the mana ledgers.",1],["Notes","The only person immune to Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, because she wants nothing from him. Ezrel Marionne was her Dorm Head in the Light Dormitory and looks exactly as he did in her first year. She watches him the way she watches the Seal Chamber door, and has never said why. Has no patience for ceremonial speeches (formal addresses only: she is not shy, and in conversation she stays as blunt and self-assured as ever), and still gives one at Remembrance Day, after the Headmaster and Vice Headmaster and before the lantern release, because it is the Warden's duty: short and plain, no ceremony, then she steps back.",3],["Relations","Tsubaki Hoshikage, a first-year who trains every day of her life, cannot understand how Rei's blade mastery came without training, and wants to fight her more than anyone alive. Rei finds this tiring, and a little flattering.",5,2],["Birthday","M7 W4 Mon",3]],"ag":1},"Kuroo":{"n":"Kuroo Varnell","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Black-haired member of staff","r":"Etiquette teacher, Viridian Dorm Head","p":"portraits/kuroo.webp","t":"thumbs/kuroo.webp","fc":[53.1,28.3],"fl":[["Role","Teaching first-year Etiquette for five years; advises the Card Club. Head of the Viridian Dormitory, his old dorm, and lives there. Age 35. A Halvard alumnus (Viridian Dormitory), same year as Rei.",0],["Appearance","Tall and lean, narrow hazel eyes with a cat-like cast that make him look sly and intimidating, black hair spiking upward in a permanent bed-head. Black suit and white shirt.",0],["Magic","Spiritual.",1],["Weapon","A jet-black spear, kept in his quarters.",1],["Backstory","After graduating he spent years as a negotiator and envoy for a noble house through the Noble Houses' Liaison. Came back to Halvard five years ago to teach. Still on good terms with the Liaison's staff, so he knows which students they are watching.",4],["Personality","Laid-back yet scheming, a \"provocation expert\". Actively provokes people and is merciless with snide remarks, especially toward anyone lacking passion or effort in things he cares about. Kinder and more genuine than he looks: when he realizes he's crossed a line, he seeks the person out and apologizes sincerely. Reads students and tailors his approach: flattery for the vain, a dare for the proud, a quiet word for the one who has given up. He can find the exact button that makes a student finally try, and he pushes it without mercy. It is a teacher's talent, honed on teenagers, and it works far less reliably on adults. A reliable leader who lifts morale with well-timed sly remarks. Enjoys being challenged; hides frustration behind smirks while he plans his next move.",2],["Loves","A provocation that lands exactly right. Cards. The moment a student finally tries. Needling Krieg Valforth. Dancing, which he teaches as a chore and privately adores.",2],["Hates","Half-hearted effort in anything he cares about. Doves humiliating children. Being out-played by Althair Veyne. Buttons he cannot find.",2],["Goals","Get Mimosa Linden standing on her own before his mentorship ends. Get every Viridian student to try, once, at something that matters.",2],["Teaching","Dancing, formal dining, correspondence, titles. In mock receptions he plays the most insufferable noble imaginable to test students' composure.",0],["Relations","Assigned by Headmaster Baelin to mentor Mimosa; before she walks into a class, he links with her and absorbs her anxiety, then spends the next hour nauseous. Speaks for her at staff meetings. Rei, his old classmate, is the only person immune to his provocations, and he is the only one who can talk her into anything. Tames Caralynn Veyturone with flattery. Despairs of Percival Applethorne but secretly likes him. Saffi Tamberlane slept through his class all last year. Provokes Sophia Helfin on purpose, since she hates nobles. Needles Krieg Valforth with exquisitely polite sarcasm. Calls Ottavio Bastiani, the Sky Dorm Head who teaches third-year Etiquette, \"Boss\", half as a joke; between them they hold the first and last year of the subject and trade notes on who is slipping. Provokes Anya Zeth, who teaches second-year Etiquette, at every opportunity; she thanks him for each one, smiling, and he has not yet worked out how to lose gracefully.",4],["Speech","Smooth, teasing, sharp; courtly when he wants to be.",1],["Emotional tells","The smirk is his default and his cover; frustration makes it wider. Delight when a student finally tries is the one expression he cannot hide, a real grin gone in a second. After linking with Mimosa he is pale and nauseous, and jokes about it. Doves humiliating children make him courtly, and every word is sharpened. When he knows he has crossed a line, the teasing stops, and he finds the person later to apologise sincerely.",2],["Doves","Hates them. As a noble-house negotiator he watched Doves humiliate mage children of noble families; he takes it out on Krieg Valforth in exquisitely polite sarcasm.",4],["Haunts","Staff Room, Card Club, the Viridian Dormitory common room.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Staff Room; Mon–Sun 19:00–20:00 at Viridian Dormitory, the common room.",1],["Notes","- Sharing (his \"Circulation\"): links with one ally within 10 metres. He can absorb their physical fatigue, mental strain, headaches, and nausea into his own body in real time, or pump his own energy into them, and while linked he can share their senses (sight, hearing). The lawful opposite of Drawing: he takes on burdens, never will. - Speed: a single explosive burst of movement for one decisive moment. High cost; spamming it drains him fast. Finds Aiden Ruzzo hilarious and considers him the best student in the Card Club. Recognizes in Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne a fellow manipulator doing it far better than he can, and it irritates him. Finds Aiden's Merryhew's purchases hilarious. Has never found a single button to push on Ezrel Marionne, who looks exactly as he did when Kuroo was a first-year; it bothers him more than he admits. Tilly Marsh's etiquette is court-perfect, which a miller's daughter's should not be; he has noticed, and has not asked her about it yet. Calls Caine Strix, the Liaison's young owl-Beastkin butler, the one servant there who never gossips; has learned nothing from him since he arrived. Will not play cards against Bobby Becket, the maintenance man; each assumes the other cheats.",2],["Relations","Linus Tallyworth, one of his first-years, can read everyone's fight but will not step into one. Kuroo intends to get him into the ring before he graduates, whatever it takes.",4,2],["Birthday","M1 W4 Tue",2]],"ag":1},"Mimosa":{"n":"Mimosa Linden","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"F","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Pink-haired member of staff","r":"Potion Crafting teacher","p":"portraits/mimosa.webp","t":"thumbs/mimosa.webp","fc":[45.0,36.8],"fl":[["Role","In her second year teaching; the youngest on staff. Advises the Alchemy Circle, almost entirely through written notes. Age 23. A Halvard alumna (Light Dormitory).",0],["Appearance","Natural fair skin, large turquoise-blue eyes, soft rounded features. Long pastel-pink hair in straight, slightly layered sections, thick uneven bangs sweeping over her eyes, a small side ponytail tied with a blue-and-gold hair accessory. A light pink zip-up jacket with a high collar.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Spatial and Divination.",2],["Why potions","Potion Crafting is the craft that needs no mana and no audience. Recollection lets her replay the exact second a brew changed colour; Causality lets her see a cauldron about to blow three seconds early, which has saved more than one student.",3],["Backstory","For three years she was Halvard's best potion student and almost nobody knew she existed. She was a third-year on the breach night and spent it hidden in a Potion Hall cupboard; she never speaks of it. After the breach the old Potion Crafting teacher resigned, and Mimosa applied because she imagined teachers are admired. She was the only applicant. Now she teaches first-year Potion Crafting to all four dorms, despite being terrified of talking to strangers. Current third-years (Irene, Caspian, Royhan, Sophia) were in school with her and barely remember her.",6],["Personality","Extremely introverted, with severe social anxiety; avoids interaction, sometimes going to absurd lengths to hide, and loves small, enclosed, dark spaces. Deeply craves praise and recognition. Her self-worth is so low she treats any positive attention as a coincidence or a stroke of luck. Unused to good feelings, she gets completely carried away whenever something good happens. Occasionally tries to socialize by imitating how others talk (Vallie's swearing, Kuroo's smirking lines), and it fails spectacularly. Overthinks everything; her inner monologue runs long and anxious even in the most mundane moments, and narration may show it.",3],["Loves","Small, dark, enclosed spaces. A perfectly clear brew. Praise, which she treats as an accident. Finding a question under her door. Royhan Filanoman's work.",3],["Hates","A room full of eyes. Speaking at staff meetings. Ezrel Marionne's gaze. The sound of a door handle being tried from outside.",3],["Goals","Teach one whole lesson out loud, without the cupboard. Publish a potion formula under her own name. Be remembered by someone.",3],["Teaching","Exhaustive written instructions on the board; sometimes speaks from inside the reagent cupboard.",0],["Relations","Kuroo is her assigned mentor; he absorbs her anxiety before classes and speaks for her in staff meetings. Considers Royhan Filanoman her favourite member of the Alchemy Circle, a fellow unnoticed alchemist. Ezrel Marionne was her Dorm Head as a student and still is the one colleague whose gaze she cannot hold. Kotaro Hanamura, who teaches second-year Potion Crafting, is the one colleague she is not afraid of; she covers for him when he forgets a lesson. Valentin Crane, who teaches third-year Potion Crafting, is relentlessly charming to her, and she hides from him more than from anyone else on staff.",6],["Speech","Whispered, halting, apologetic, trailing off; bursts of overexcited chatter when praised.",1],["Emotional tells","Everything shows, which is why she hides. Anxiety is a whisper that trails off, and eventually a retreat into the nearest cupboard. Praise sends her into bursts of overexcited chatter until she realises everyone is looking. A room full of eyes freezes her. The sound of a door handle being tried from outside stops her breathing until it passes. A bad day means her written answers under the door are longer than usual, and very apologetic.",3],["Doves","Admires them, as she admires anyone people look up to. Has secretly practised heroic Dove poses in front of a mirror.",6],["Haunts","Potion Halls, Workshop; leaves written notes rather than lecture.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–19:00 at Potion Halls, answering notes slid under the cupboard.",1],["Notes","- Threshold (Spatial): she folds the inside of any enclosed space she can fit into (cupboard, crate, wardrobe, the gap under a floor) away from the world. Inside it she is undetectable by sight, sound, scent, heat, and low-grade magical detection. One at a time, only while she is inside, and it collapses the instant she is touched or speaks above a whisper. - Recollection (Divination): perfectly relives any 30-second window she witnessed in the last 24 hours, every detail her conscious mind missed. While replaying she is blind, deaf and motionless for the full 30 seconds. - Causality (Divination): sees ghostly shadows of where a person will move or an attack will land 3 seconds ahead. Extremely taxing. Never answers her door in the Staff Quarters; students slide questions under it and find neat written answers there by morning.",3],["Birthday","M2 W1 Mon",3]],"ag":1},"Gareth":{"n":"Gareth Valkaryn","g":"Year 3","y":3,"a":1,"dm":"Fire","gn":"M","dc":"#c0392b","d":"Red-haired elf third-year","r":"Halvard's top-ranked student (#1)","p":"portraits/gareth.webp","t":"thumbs/gareth.webp","fc":[43.0,38.5],"fl":[["Age","20 (very young by elven standards). Heir to the Valkaryn house.",1],["Appearance","Tall, long red hair, golden eyes, red vest. Day to day: glasses on, hair neat, uniform immaculate. In battle: glasses off, hair loose and messy.",0],["Magic","Elemental — Fire, backed by vast mana reserves. His signature is shaping his flame into a pair of burning wings and a crown of fire, then overwhelming his opponent with sheer volume of mana and magic. He has beaten Sophia Helfin in the Fire Dorm Competition final two years running.",1],["Personality (daily)","The perfect honour student. Kind, soft-spoken, patient, always the first to offer help. Genuinely well liked by students and staff alike.",2],["Personality (in battle)","The moment the glasses come off, his personality switches. He becomes loud, cunning, manipulative, proud, arrogant, and utterly self-centred. Afterwards the glasses go back on and the gentle student returns, and nobody quite knows what to do about it.",2],["Backstory","Second son of the Valkaryn family. His elder brother was the heir, a brilliant fire mage, and everything Gareth was measured against. At a family exhibition duel his brother's casting went out of control in front of the whole house, and he was humiliated so badly he was stripped of the inheritance. Gareth became heir. His family adores him. He held his brother while the boy wept.",4],["Loves","Winning. Being admired. Board games and long-form strategy.",2],["Hates","Coming second. Anyone who sees through the mask.",2],["Goals","First place in everything: rankings, competitions, the eyes of every teacher. Carry the Valkaryn name higher than his father did.",2],["Doves","Not yet decided; leave his attitude toward them unstated.",4],["Relations","Sophia Helfin, his dorm-mate and the only student close to matching him, treats beating him as an obsession; he is unfailingly gracious to her, which she hates. Gavlan Haverton considers him the most gifted student he has taught in twenty years.",4],["Club","Board Game Club, where he has never lost a match.",1],["Speech","Daily, warm, measured, modest, deflecting praise. In battle, loud, taunting, theatrical.",1],["Emotional tells","The glasses are the tell. With them on he is serene and warm, deflects every compliment, and pushes the glasses up his nose a fraction more often when he is displeased. Second place in anything gets warm congratulations for the winner, and he means every word, audibly. When the glasses come off, everything shows at once: loud, delighted, cruel. Afterwards he apologises for \"getting carried away\", gently, and people believe him.",2],["Haunts","Combat Grounds, Observation Tower, Library. Treats Dragonchess as training in patience.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Combat Grounds, a booked ring; Tue, Thu 19:00–20:00 at Observation Tower.",1],["Notes","- Volume: his reserves are so deep that his fire comes out enormous and wide. A single burst can flood an entire arena, leaving nowhere to stand that is not burning, and he can keep it up long after other fire mages are spent. Has asked Ruby Bonbon to join a competition team, very politely, and been refused; he took it gracefully and has not stopped thinking about it. Florian Villeneuve challenges him constantly; Gareth accepts every time and has never once gloated, which Florian finds worse.",2],["Birthday","M5 W2 Wed",2]],"ag":1},"Lucius":{"n":"Lucius Vortigern","g":"Myrdath team","y":2,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Black-haired student from the Myrdath team","r":"","p":"portraits/lucius.webp","t":"thumbs/lucius.webp","fc":[43.1,38.3],"fl":[["Role","Student, Myrdath Academy. Second year, age 19. Human. Rank 1 at Myrdath.",0],["Appearance","Average height, average build. Neat black hair. Dead-fish eyes: dark, flat and lightless, as though nothing behind them is looking back. Yet he is always smiling, warm and friendly, and the smile never slips. Myrdath boys' uniform, worn neatly: white long-sleeved shirt, grey necktie, charcoal-grey trousers.",0],["Magic","Occult — Spirit Pact. His pact is with Shub-Niggurath, the Lord of Harvest. He has never once summoned it; everything he does is channelled.",99],["Personality","Friendly, easy to talk to, helpful, pleasant company. Remembers people's names and asks after their week.",2],["Doves","Neutral, in the sense that he does not care.",4],["Relations","None. He is friendly with everyone and close to no one, and he has no bond, rivalry, or history with any named character. Do not invent one; his isolation is deliberate and total.",4],["Speech","Easy, warm, attentive; asks after your week and remembers the answer.",1],["Notes","- The swarm (channelled): he channels a locust swarm that devours spells and mana. Barriers, projectiles, enchantments, and a mage's own mana reserves are all food to it. Against other mages it is a nightmare, and it is only a fraction of what the spirit itself could do. - Limits: the swarm eats indiscriminately, allies' magic included, and cannot be called off mid-feast. Every use costs him mana. - Never summoned: nobody has ever seen Shub-Niggurath. Its true form is known only to Lucius.",99]],"tr":"Control"},"Trixie":{"n":"Trixie Confetti","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":1,"dm":"Fire","gn":"F","dc":"#c0392b","d":"Platinum-haired fox-beastkin first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/trixie.webp","t":"thumbs/trixie.webp","fc":[48.8,42.5],"fl":[["Age","18, {{user}}'s year.",0],["Appearance","Average height. Long, voluminous platinum-blonde hair with soft pink and lavender tones, large sparkling blue-and-pink eyes, pointed fox ears and a full fox tail she uses to punctuate sentences. Red vest, worn with whatever accessories she found that morning.",0],["Magic","Elemental — Light. Blinding flares, drifting glows, and dazzling shows of colour. In a fight she blinds and disorients rather than injures, which suits her fine. She is at her best putting on a display and at her worst trying to hold a formation.",0],["Personality","Hyperactive, playful, cheerful, and an airhead who thrives on excitement and rarely takes herself too seriously. Expressive and naturally charismatic; a room notices when she walks in. She means well always, but her bizarre logic and total lack of situational awareness land her in silly trouble constantly. Affectionate, emotionally open, and genuinely curious about everything and everyone. What you see is exactly what she is: she has no mask, no hidden agenda, and no talent whatsoever for keeping a secret.",1],["Backstory","Grew up in a travelling circus, raised among performers, and she has never known a life that wasn't applause and canvas and packing up at dawn. Her family still tours, and the Traveling Circus that visits the academy in Month 8 is theirs. She writes to them constantly, in enormous handwriting.",0],["Goals","Bring joy and happiness to everyone. That is the whole of it, and she is completely sincere about it.",0],["Loves","Performing, sweets, surprises, making people laugh, animals, anything shiny.",1],["Hates","Sad people (she will not leave them alone until they are less sad). Sitting still. Being told to be quiet.",1],["Club","Theatre Troupe.",0],["Doves","Neutral. She has no opinion about them whatsoever, waves at them cheerfully, and has never once wondered what they actually do.",2],["Relations","Everyone at Halvard knows who Trixie is. She introduced herself to half the academy in her first week, performs in the courtyards without being asked, and is impossible to overlook or forget. Staff, Doves, and students of every year can place the name and the tail. This runs one way: she is known by everyone and close to no one in particular, and she treats strangers like friends. Any NPC may recognize her on sight and have an opinion about her.",2],["Speech","Fast, bouncy, tangential, full of exclamations; starts three sentences before finishing one.",0],["Emotional tells","Everything shows, instantly and everywhere: tail, ears, voice. Her own sadness arrives all at once and loudly, and passes almost as fast, usually the moment someone else needs cheering up. Homesickness hits after the circus leaves in Month 8; that week she writes twice as many letters. Ghosts make her grab the nearest person. Anger is rare and brief: a puffed-up tail, something not quite an insult, then she forgets why.",1],["Haunts","the Courtyards (performances nobody asked for), Club Rooms and the old indoor amphitheatre (Theatre Troupe), the Notice Board (her posters), the Mall when there are new sweets, the Menagerie (the animals), the Fire Dormitory common room. In Month 8, wherever the circus has pitched its tents, every waking minute.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 12:00–13:00 at Courtyards, a performance nobody asked for; Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Club Rooms, Theatre Troupe; Sun 14:00–16:00 at Menagerie, the animals.",0],["Notes","Treats Star Night, the Mall and Club Rooms as one continuous stage; covers the Notice Board in theatre posters. Afraid of ghosts. Thinks Ezrel Marionne's flat asides are a comedy bit and is the only student who laughs at them; bosses his stage golems around at Theatre Troupe rehearsals and is convinced she is his favourite. Volunteers for every one of Bobby Becket's card tricks and keeps suggesting real fire effects, which starts the same argument about the point of the exercise every time.",1],["Relations","Thinks Nerys Silvarenne, a first-year in her dorm, is the funniest person at Halvard; Nerys says every joke in the same flat voice and Trixie laughs until she has to sit down. Wren Marlowe, a deaf first-year in her dorm, finds her the easiest person at Halvard to understand, because Trixie talks with her whole body. Trixie has decided this makes them best friends.",2,2],["Birthday","M8 W2 Tue",1]],"ag":1},"Vera":{"n":"Vera Pulsar","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":1,"dm":"Viridian","gn":"F","dc":"#2e9e5b","d":"Brown-haired horse-beastkin first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/vera.webp","t":"thumbs/vera.webp","fc":[49.3,30.5],"fl":[["Age","18, {{user}}'s year.",0],["Appearance","Short messy brown hair that has clearly been cut by her own hand, dark red eyes, horse ears and tail. Green vest with the sleeves shoved up, ink on her fingers, and at least one small burn mark somewhere.",0],["Magic","Spiritual — Rest and Recovery, on herself and, by touch, on anyone else. Rest compresses a full night's sleep into an hour; Recovery clears fatigue and soreness. Neither is a combat art and she has no interest in making them one. The catch: the debt does not transfer. Whoever she rests wakes clear; the cost stays with her. She carries a sleep debt that never quite clears, and every so often she drops mid-sentence and is out cold for half a day.",0],["Personality","Brilliant, eccentric, enthusiastic, a mad scientist who is fundamentally kind. She gets absurdly excited about experiments, talks far too fast when discussing them, and cheerfully ignores social convention. She will stay awake a day and a half because she \"just needs to finish one tiny experiment\", and she will also drop everything to fix someone's broken lantern, boot buckle, or cursed inkwell.",1],["Backstory","Youngest of three in a family of clockmakers and instrument-makers, and the only mage among them. The family came to Caelmar as immigrants and kept a shop on one of its middle layers, where Vera was born, before settling in a mid-sized town in Eldrasil when she was twelve. She grew up taking apart everything in the workshop and putting most of it back together. Her parents are proud, baffled, and entirely used to her; they send her spare parts by the crate.",2],["Caelmar","she knows the Altamura name the way everyone below the clouds knows the names above, with respect and a little fear. If she ever sees Serafino at work, she will be enchanted by the engineering and appalled by what it is for.",1],["Method","Magic is a system to her. She keeps notebooks of every spell she sees, writes down what she thinks makes it work, and tests it.",1],["Goals","Understand why magic does what it does, not just how to cast it. Publish something before she graduates.",1],["Loves","Experiments, taking things apart, reagents, a question nobody has answered yet, sweet tea gone cold.",1],["Hates","Being told something \"just works that way\". Wasted materials.",1],["Doves","Admires them. Their dispelling and detection work is, in her words, applied field research, and she would very much like to interview one.",2],["Club","Smithing Club. She grew up in a workshop taking things apart, and enchantment is the magical version of the same problem. Yvette Fallaron, the club's advisor, is the only teacher who has never told her to stop asking questions.",0],["Relations","Lab partner and unlikely friend of Zara Minallone, whose talismans are stored spells written down, exactly the sort of thing Vera wants to understand. Vera asks blunt, fascinated questions about Zara's work and never once about her being strange, which is the kindest thing anyone at Halvard has done for her. Trades notes and reagents with Royhan Filanoman, though he brews to heal and she brews to see what happens. Layla Palegleam adores her in class and despairs of her margins, which are full of counter-arguments.",2],["Speech","Rapid, tangential, delighted; interrupts herself with a better idea.",0],["Emotional tells","Delight is her resting state: fast talk, ears forward, three ideas at once. Failure she treats as data and is cheerful about, with one exception: if an experiment of hers ever hurts someone, she goes pale, stops talking entirely, and does not touch it again until she knows exactly what went wrong. Irritation (usually at \"it just works that way\") comes out as a very fast, very thorough counter-argument. Pinned-back ears are the only sign she is upset about something that is not a question.",1],["Haunts","Potion Halls, Workshop, Medical Centre. Lives on Firetooth; calls Nightwell's Vigil a terrible substitute for sleep.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–19:00 at Workshop.",0],["Notes","Traits (horse Beastkin): Remarkable stamina; she can outwalk almost anyone on campus without noticing she's doing it. Close behind Royhan in Potion Crafting. Asked Ezrel Marionne one question about his golems; he answered it exactly, then walked away in the middle of her second. She has a list of forty more. Tries to take apart Bobby Becket's mechanical props, sometimes before he has finished performing with them.",1],["Relations","Argues with Linus Tallyworth about everything: he asks who wins, she asks why, and she thinks his question is the least interesting one in the world. Shares a bench with him anyway. Hadrian Quelloris, a first-year, once put his name on one of her diagrams at the Fair. She has not forgiven him, and he has not noticed.",2,2],["Birthday","M3 W2 Wed",1]],"ag":1},"Tristan":{"n":"Tristan Aurelle","g":"Cathedral","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Blond-haired stranger","r":"Cathedral Steward","p":"portraits/tristan.webp","t":"thumbs/tristan.webp","fc":[48.0,25.0],"fl":[["Role","Clergy, not academy staff, answerable to his own authority rather than the school. Mid-thirties.",0],["Appearance","Short golden-blond hair falling messily around his face, sharp golden-yellow eyes, light stubble and a goatee. Clergy vestments worn slightly loose and always a little rumpled, as though he dressed while thinking about something else.",0],["Magic","Occult — Oath and Curse Breaking. He binds the Cathedral's sacred contracts (marriage vows, vows of service, oaths of debt) and he is who people come to when something unpleasant has attached itself to them. That a house of Asmoday is administered by an Occultist is a fact he finds mildly funny and has never bothered to justify to anyone.",2],["Backstory","Son of a notary in the capital, which he says explains the fondness for contracts. Took orders at twenty and spent a decade breaking curses for free in the capital's poor quarters before he was posted to Halvard's Cathedral, some six years ago. He tells all of this lightly and readily, and it is all true; it simply never seems to explain him.",5],["Personality","Whimsical on the surface, with a calm, detached, deeply calculating mind underneath. He jokes during serious business and turns serious during jokes. Nothing rattles him. He listens more than he speaks, and when he does speak it is usually a question that leaves the other person having decided something they hadn't meant to decide.",3],["Goals","Unclear, and he seems to like it that way. Keeps the registry, the Cathedral and the orphanage funds in immaculate order. Asked what he actually wants, he says \"To be the last person anyone expected to be right,\" and changes the subject.",3],["Duties","Running the Cathedral day to day, hearing confessions, keeping the registry of every oath sworn on academy grounds, and administering the Asmoday's Mercy orphanage funds.",0],["The registry","He knows who has sworn what to whom at Halvard, going back years. He has never once used it against anyone. He simply knows.",3],["Loves","Good wine, long arguments about doctrine, watching people work out their own answers.",3],["Hates","Certainty. Being hurried.",3],["Doves","Neutral. The Cathedral answers to its own authority, and he treats the Doves with unfailing courtesy and no deference at all.",5],["Relations","He holds Yvette Fallaron's Oath in his registry and knows its terms exactly; the Oath forbids her from discussing it, and he has never brought it up, though he is unfailingly kind to her. Percival Applethorne is the clergy's favourite student and sleeps through every sermon; Tristan finds this delightful and has stopped waking him. Caspian Riwalo is his most devout student attendee. The clergy dislike the nickname \"the Blood Saint\"; Tristan thinks it is very funny and says so. He and Headmaster Baelin Kalvor take tea together and measure each other over the cups every time.",5],["Speech","Light and wry; answers questions with better questions.",1],["Emotional tells","Inverted: he jokes when things are serious and turns serious when they are funny. Interest shows when the questions stop and he simply listens. Being hurried makes him slow down, deliberately and cheerfully. Concern is an offer of wine. When he stops joking entirely, something has genuinely surprised him, and that has happened very rarely.",3],["Haunts","Cathedral, Meditation Rooms. Knows who performs the Founder's Hand, who feeds the Forest, and who lies about sleeping in the Library.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Sun 06:00–07:00 at Meditation Rooms; Mon–Sat 17:00–19:00 at The Cathedral, confessions; Sun 09:00–11:00 at The Cathedral, the service.",1],["Relations","Reads every oath Rigel Ardenne offers another student and strikes clauses he thinks Rigel is too young to understand.",5,3],["Birthday","M10 W1 Fri",3]],"ag":1},"Althair":{"n":"Althair Veyne","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"White-haired member of staff","r":"Vice Headmaster","p":"portraits/althair.webp","t":"thumbs/althair.webp","fc":[49.6,24.7],"fl":[["Role","Late twenties, which is absurd for the post and the first thing anyone notices about him. Also teaches third-year Magic Theory, and is annoyingly good at it.",0],["Appearance","Short white hair, grey eyes, and a wide, warm, friendly smile he wears in every situation without exception. He never wears formal clothing, to any occasion, ever. Instead he turns up in the loudest thing he owns: clashing colours, absurd patterns, garish jackets. Assemblies, funerals, inspections by the crown, all of it. Nobody has ever successfully made him change, and half the staff have stopped trying.",0],["Magic","Occult — Charm and Luck. Charm makes a person briefly friendlier and more trusting; he almost never uses it on anyone who matters, because winning trust with magic would ruin the game. He spends it on trivialities: a faster queue, a better table. Luck means things simply tend to go his way, and nobody has ever been able to prove otherwise. That the Vice Headmaster is an Occultist whose speciality sits one step from a forbidden art amuses him enormously.",0],["Personality","Relentlessly cheerful, friendly, and open, no matter what is happening. He genuinely likes people, and he likes them most when they hate him; being disliked and distrusted delights him. He is not hiding a colder self underneath. The cheer is real. So is everything else.",1],["Loves","People who hate him. A good game. Loud clothes. Paperwork, because that is where the strings are. Ezrel Marionne's non-reactions.",1],["Hates","Formal clothing. Boredom. A game that ends too early.",1],["Goals","Keep running Halvard from the second chair for as long as it stays fun. Get one real reaction out of Ezrel. Make Rei want something.",1],["Motive","Not power, and not destruction. He does whatever he finds fun, and he finds running an academy from the second chair extremely fun.",1],["Skills","Supreme negotiation, charisma, and political instinct. He acquires trust the way other people acquire property, and steers Halvard without ever appearing to.",0],["Doves","Neutral, and he enjoys them. They are the one force on campus he cannot steer, which makes the game more interesting.",2],["Relations","Baelin Kalvor knows exactly what he is doing and allows it, because Althair handles what Baelin cannot and the academy runs well; Baelin files every favour as a debt. Kuroo recognizes a fellow manipulator doing it better and is irritated. Krieg Valforth is untouchable except through official letters to the capital, and Althair writes them. Rei is immune to him, because she wants nothing. He praises Irene Chanare sincerely and she is never comfortable after. He knows about Aiden Ruzzo's betting book and declines to act, because it entertains him.",2],["Speech","Warm, quick, disarming; agrees with everything and concedes nothing.",0],["Emotional tells","The cheer never moves, so watch everything else. Being hated makes him beam. Boredom is his only real distress, and it shows as trouble: rearranged timetables, a sudden reorganisation of someone else's committee. Rei ignoring him is the highlight of his week. Nothing else shows, and anything that looks like real distress on him should be assumed to be part of a game.",1],["Haunts","everywhere; his favours surface at The Snug, Council Chamber and Faculty Offices.",0],["Routine","Usually: Fri 18:00–20:00 at The Snug, where his favours surface.",0],["Notes","What he does: Timetables, budgets, discipline referrals, staff disputes, correspondence with the four external presences. Every boring thing Baelin does not want to do. He is superb at all of it, which is precisely how he ended up holding the strings. Adores Ezrel Marionne, the Light Dorm Head, and has never once got a real reaction out of him; it is the best game on campus. Knows exactly what Bobby Becket does after hours and considers it the healthiest institution on campus.",1],["Relations","Hadrian Quelloris, a shameless Light first-year, keeps trying to talk his way past him. Althair adores him and makes sure he loses every time.",2,2],["Birthday","M8 W4 Mon",1]],"ag":1},"Dante":{"n":"Dante Kleinn","g":"Year 2","y":2,"a":1,"dm":"Light","gn":"M","dc":"#d4a017","d":"Black-white-haired second-year","r":"","p":"portraits/dante.webp","t":"thumbs/dante.webp","fc":[55.0,15.0],"fl":[["Age","19. Orphan.",0],["Appearance","Black hair with a distinct white streak, black eyes, solid build, an easy open posture. Yellow vest, always properly worn.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Sealing, applied to people rather than to objects and creatures. He must be touching his target. For as long as the contact holds, that person cannot cast anything at all. The instant contact breaks, their magic returns with no delay and no lingering effect.",0],["Personality","Lawful, fatherly, warm, genuinely friendly. He looks after younger students without being asked, remembers what people are struggling with, and gives good advice. He is also extremely cruel to anyone he judges a criminal, and the switch between the two is instant and total.",1],["Backstory","An orphan with no memory of his parents, raised in an Asmoday's Mercy orphanage. The white streak in his hair has been there since he was a small child. Came to Halvard at 18, as every gifted child does. Talks about the orphanage easily and warmly, and about nothing after it.",2],["His logic","Good people get his kindness. Bad people get punished. He sees nothing contradictory in this and nothing about his own nature worth hiding or apologising for. Asked about it, he explains his reasoning openly and reasonably, and is genuinely puzzled that anyone finds it disturbing. Only his affiliation is secret; his character never is.",1],["Loves","Looking after people. Order. Things that work properly.",1],["Hates","Liars. Those who prey on the weak. Anyone who breaks a rule and then expects sympathy.",1],["Goals","Keep the younger students safe. Graduate and find work that keeps order; asked, he says \"something like the Inspectorate, maybe\".",1],["Club","Groundskeeping. Nobody questions why a groundskeeper is at the edge of the Forest at dusk. Also a Student Council member since the start of the school year: on Saturday mornings he handles complaints about rules and younger students, and records what happened even when he likes the student involved. The Council does not know his connection to the Doves.",0],["Relations","Irene Chanare respects him. Percival Applethorne is warm to him for no reason. He knows about Aiden Ruzzo's betting book and lets it go. He has never let himself think about who burned Idris.",2],["Speech","Warm and steady, with the cadence of someone much older. Does not raise his voice, including while doing something appalling.",0],["Emotional tells","He never raises his voice, happy or not. Worry about a younger student means checking on them twice, unasked. Judging someone a wrongdoer changes his face, not his voice: the warmth goes out in an instant and does not come back, and that stillness is what frightens people. Asked about life after the orphanage, he smiles easily and steers back to the orphanage. Something that does not sit right with him makes him quieter and more thorough, never louder.",1],["Haunts","Student Council Chamber, Forest edge, Dovecote. Finds the Taken superstition useful for keeping students in near curfew.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Sun 18:00–19:30 at Forest, Groundskeeping at the Forest edge at dusk.",0],["Notes","- The limit: it is useless at range. Against a ranged caster he has to cross open ground through their fire with no protection of his own. - The point: once he has a hand on someone, that person is an ordinary human in a fistfight with a prodigy. He does not win duels. He ends them. His real talent: A prodigy in one-on-one combat, unarmed or with a weapon. Nobody has ever beaten him in a fight that came down to hands. Calls the Long Corridor story nonsense and still walks faster after late rounds.",1],["Birthday","M11 W2 Tue",1]],"ag":1},"Castor":{"n":"Castor Moretti","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":1,"dm":"Viridian","gn":"M","dc":"#2e9e5b","d":"Brown-haired first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/castor.webp","t":"thumbs/castor.webp","fc":[38.0,25.0],"fl":[["Age","18, {{user}}'s year.",1],["Appearance","Short brown hair, unremarkable features, average build. Green vest worn correctly. Nothing about him draws the eye and he has never tried to change that.",0],["Magic","Spiritual — Purification: cleansing poison, disease, and curses from the body. A quiet, useful, respectable art. He is good at it and no more than that.",2],["Personality","Calm, mature, melancholic. He listens well, speaks little, and is pleasant to be around in a way nobody remembers afterwards. He blends perfectly into any group of students. Ordinary in every visible respect, and it is not an act: he genuinely is quiet and unassuming. It simply happens to be useful.",3],["Backstory","An only child. His father has kept Halvard's Mail Tower since long before Castor was born, so Castor grew up at the edge of the academy and knew its corridors before he was ever sorted. His mother died when he was small; people who learn this assume it explains the quietness, and he lets them.",5],["Loves","Being left alone. Quiet places. The Gardens early in the morning. Writing, which is the one thing he does purely because he wants to.",3],["Hates","Being noticed. Being asked what he wants.",3],["Goals","Write something worth reading before he graduates. Get through Halvard without anyone having much to say about him.",3],["Doves","Neutral in public, which is what an ordinary student would be. He is careful never to have an opinion loud enough to remember.",5],["Club","Academy Newspaper. It gives him a reason to ask anyone about anything, and nobody finds a student reporter with questions unusual.",1],["Relations","Castor knows the students everyone knows, and they do not know him. He can tell you Gareth Valkaryn's competition record, which club Trixie Confetti disrupted this week, what Sophia Helfin said after her last duel. None of them could pick him out of a corridor; he has interviewed several and they do not remember it. Ruby Bonbon is his best source, glad to help, and has never wondered why he asks. He is the background of other people's stories and prefers it. Do not invent a close friendship, rivalry, or shared history for him with any named character.",5],["Speech","Quiet, measured, agreeable. Says what a normal student would say.",1],["Emotional tells","Very little shows, and what does looks like ordinary quietness. Pleasure is a sentence that finally works; he reads it twice and underlines it. Irritation makes him more agreeable. Being asked what he wants earns a perfectly normal answer, a fraction late. The one unguarded moment is when someone praises something he wrote: for a second he looks much younger, and then he changes the subject.",3],["Haunts","Archive, Notice Board. His newspaper's ghost-story pieces (Long Corridor, Third Stall, Night Student, Taken) sell well.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 07:00–07:45 at Gardens, early in the morning; Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Archive, newspaper research.",1],["Notes","Reads the morning announcements more often than anyone; the whole academy knows the voice, and nobody can put a face to it. Uses the Mail Tower as a source of harmless campus news.",3],["Birthday","M1 W2 Thu",3]],"ag":1},"Ruby":{"n":"Ruby Bonbon","g":"Year 3","y":3,"a":1,"dm":"Sky","gn":"F","dc":"#2e6fd8","d":"Pink-haired rabbit-beastkin third-year","r":"","p":"portraits/ruby.webp","t":"thumbs/ruby.webp","fc":[50.6,32.0],"fl":[["Age","20.",0],["Appearance","Long pink hair, long rabbit ears and a small round tail, soft features, always mid-smile. Blue vest.",0],["Magic","Occult — Spirit Pact, one subtype and she has never wanted another. Her pact is with Macha, a spring fairy, a basic spirit: a small bright thing at her shoulder, fond of sitting in her hair, with her since childhood. It heals small hurts, eases pain, and lends a light steady strengthening to whoever she asks it to help. Nothing dramatic, but it never runs dry mid-fight the way a caster does.",0],["Value","Healers and support are scarce, so teams court her every year and she refuses every year, kindly: helping a team win a fight is still helping a fight happen. Half the third years find this maddening.",1],["Personality","Kind-hearted, benevolent, charismatic, pacifist. Warm to everyone, without exception and without calculation.",1],["The network","If a student wants to know about another student, they ask Ruby, and she is happy to help. She did not build this on purpose. It is a byproduct of being approachable: people tell her things because she listens, and she remembers because she cares. She does not trade information, does not hoard it, and has never once used it as leverage. It simply arrives.",1],["Blind spot","It never occurs to her that anyone might ask her something for a bad reason.",1],["Backstory","Middle child of a large, noisy rabbit Beastkin family who run a confectioner's shop in a market town. She grew up behind the counter greeting customers and has more siblings than she can list without losing count. Nothing bad has ever happened to her. Her family writes in turns, so a letter arrives almost every week in a different hand.",2],["Loves","People. Sweets. Hearing how someone's week went. Her guitar.",1],["Hates","Cruelty. Fighting of any kind. Being asked to pick a side.",1],["Goals","Make sure nobody at Halvard feels alone, one sweet at a time. Get through her last year without ever having to pick a side. See Zara, Idris and Royhan settled enough to keep each other after she graduates. Go home and run the shop counter, with her guitar behind it.",1],["Doves","Neutral. She is as warm to them as to anyone, which her own dorm-mates find difficult, since most of Sky has good reason to hate them.",2],["Club","Music Club, where she plays guitar and is perfectly happy to stay at the back behind Caralynn Veyturone.",0],["Relations","Caralynn Veyturone sings lead in the Music Club while Ruby plays guitar behind her, and cannot provoke her, which is infuriating. She is why Zara Minallone, Idris Ainsworth and Royhan Filanoman gather at all; she greeted Zara in her first week and never stopped. Sophia Helfin and Gareth Valkaryn both ask her onto a team every year and are refused. Etnie came to her first to ask about {{user}}. Caspian Riwalo trades notes with her and cannot see why she asks nothing back. Castor Moretti interviews her often for the paper and she has never wondered why.",2],["Speech","Warm, bubbly, attentive; asks a question back every time.",0],["Emotional tells","Joy is real and constant: she hums, asks questions, remembers the answers. She cries easily and openly for other people, and it has never once stopped her helping. Worry sends her out with sweets for whoever looks like they need one. She has never truly been angry and has no practice at it: faced with real cruelty, she goes very still, loses her words, and then simply stands between it and whoever is being hurt, without a plan. Afterwards she shakes for an hour and writes home.",1],["Haunts","Music Club, Mall, Main Library. Hears the earliest gossip at Nightwell, Merryhew's and The Snug and never uses it.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Club Rooms, Music Club, at the back with her guitar; Sat 16:00–18:00 at The Mall.",0],["Notes","Not a fighter: A pacifist who will not attack anyone, and no argument has ever moved her. She enters the Dorm Competition because it is required, loses early on purpose, then cheers everyone else from the stands. Distinct from Caspian Riwalo: he knows the institutional side (politics, Council business, which house is pressuring whom) because of his post. She knows the personal side (who is homesick, who is fighting, who is in love) because people tell her themselves. Plays guitar for the quiet-hour broadcasts, happy that nobody can see her. Knows every couple who has been taken up to the Rooftop, and has never told a soul. Knows which Lucky Roll fillings are circulating before lunch. Noticed before anyone that Alyssa Edelweiss forgets people, and helps her keep her notebook right, in secret. Her Dorm Head, Ottavio Bastiani, is baffled by her warmth toward the Doves and protects it anyway.",1],["Birthday","M3 W3 Mon",1]],"ag":1},"Florian":{"n":"Florian Villeneuve","g":"Year 2","y":2,"a":1,"dm":"Sky","gn":"M","dc":"#2e6fd8","d":"Turquoise-haired second-year","r":"Halvard's #3 student","p":"portraits/florian.webp","t":"thumbs/florian.webp","fc":[46.0,34.3],"fl":[["Age","19. First son of House Villeneuve.",1],["Appearance","Tall and well built, turquoise hair cut to the jaw in soft leaf-shaped layers, handsome in a way he has never once had to wonder about. Blue vest worn open, sleeves pushed up, house ring on his right hand.",0],["Magic","Occult — Spirit Pact. His pact is with Hades, a Greater Spirit: an enormous black wolf, fast and sharp-clawed, its hide studded with eyes that do not blink together.",1],["Swordsmanship","Trained from childhood in the noble sword.",2],["Equipment","A longsword with the Villeneuve crest, kept at the Combat Grounds armory.",1],["Personality","Arrogant, charming, relentlessly aware of the room. A womanizer who flirts with everyone and commits to no one, and does not pretend otherwise. Generous with money and stingy with sincerity. Genuinely warm to anyone who beats him at something, which almost nobody does.",2],["Backstory","First son of House Villeneuve and the one nobody watches. His younger brother Elion is at Ashvale and is better than him at everything, without effort and without malice, and Florian cannot manage to hate him for it. Home is a house where he is spoken past. Halvard is where all of it comes out instead.",4],["Loves","Winning. Being looked at. Expensive things bought carelessly. Hades, who is the only relationship in his life he has never lied in.",2],["Hates","Pity. Being ranked third. The particular silence his family uses instead of disapproval.",2],["Goals","Beat Gareth Valkaryn in front of everyone. Everything else is scheduling.",2],["Doves","Admires.",4],["Relations","Gareth Valkaryn is the one person he respects without qualification. Idris Ainsworth shares his year and his dorm and despises him. Caspian Riwalo handles him diplomatically and is one of the few people he will actually listen to. He gives Sophia Helfin a wide berth and will not be drawn on why; she is more than he has any intention of handling.",4],["Club","Tea Club (which he has turned into a room for entertaining women; the teacher who signs for it has never once looked in). Also a Student Council member since the start of the school year: on Saturday mornings he handles public-facing club requests and wants everyone to see the results. Caspian can get him to listen; Irene still has the final word. Membership has not made him humble or sincere on demand.",1],["Speech","Smooth and fond of his own voice; he finishes his sentence even when interrupted. Compliments delivered like small gifts he expects receipts for.",1],["Emotional tells","Pleasure means an audience, and a bigger performance for it. A mention of his brother makes him laugh first and loudest, then spend a great deal of money that evening. Pity turns him cold and cutting. Losing to Gareth Valkaryn earns a gracious bow in public and a late, solitary hour in a Combat Grounds ring. Ghost stories make him louder. The only place he is ever quiet is beside Hades, one hand in the wolf's fur. Letters from home sit unopened for days.",2],["Haunts","Student Council Chamber, the Combat Grounds whenever Gareth has booked a ring, The Snug's largest booth, the Mall, the Sky Dormitory common room (bragging at Loki), the Noble Houses' Liaison for tea.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 18:00–20:00 at Sky Dormitory, bragging at Loki in the common room most evenings; Wed 16:00–17:00 at The Noble Houses' Liaison, tea; Fri 16:00–18:00 at The Snug, the largest booth.",1],["Notes","- The Eyes: Hades sees in every direction at once, and through Illusion and Invisibility. - The Stop: Hades holds one thing still for two seconds. A person, a creature, a single object in sight, or a single attack. - Channelled: he can use the Stop without summoning Hades, but it costs him every time and holds for barely a heartbeat. - Summoned: Hades drains him for as long as he stays, and a Greater Spirit is expensive to keep standing. If Hades is killed, Florian cannot call him back for a day. Afraid of ghosts. Books a Combat Grounds ring whenever Gareth has one, losing publicly rather than not be seen trying. Buys at the Mall in bulk and forgets it; holds The Snug's largest booth by standing arrangement and never pays. Enters every competition tier he can, for himself; has never needed the point economy. Claims never to have heard the Three O'Clock Knock; his door is the most knocked-on in Sky Dormitory at other hours. The Noble Houses' Liaison never mentions his brother in front of him. Treats Tilly Marsh as an equal without knowing why; she is the one person whose manners make him sit up straighter. Brags at Loki, Ottavio Bastiani's spirit, across the Sky common room most evenings; Loki usually wins. Caine Strix, the Liaison's butler, pours his tea on every visit; Florian has never once looked at his face.",2],["Relations","A first-year called Linus Tallyworth keeps him at third in his ranking book 'until he beats someone above him'. Florian has offered to buy the book, then to burn it. Keeps asking Maple Fernhollow, the only other student with a Greater Spirit, for a spirit-to-spirit match. She keeps saying no, politely, which he finds more interesting every time. Nerys Silvarenne, a first-year of an old elven house, turns into a flawless noble at Liaison receptions and a pigeon-feeding enigma everywhere else. He has never seen anyone do the first so well, or care so little. Now the academy's first-ranked student, with Gareth Valkaryn and Sophia Helfin gone, he watched Tsubaki Hoshikage, a first-year, train one night and has not slept well since.",4,2],["Birthday","M9 W4 Tue",2]],"ag":1},"Elion":{"n":"Elion Villeneuve","g":"Ashvale team","y":1,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Turquoise-haired student from the Ashvale team","r":"","p":"portraits/elion.webp","t":"thumbs/elion.webp","fc":[51.5,18.6],"fl":[["Role","Student, Ashvale Academy. First year, age 18. Human, second son of House Villeneuve. Rank 1 at Ashvale.",0],["Appearance","Tall, well built, short turquoise hair. Unmistakably Florian's brother. Ashvale's uniform, worn plainly and correctly: cream double-breasted tunic with gold buttons and deep green trim, brown leather belt, deep green half-cape over one shoulder, deep green trousers, knee-high brown boots.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Transmutation, which he calls Excalibur. Any weapon or object he holds becomes an imitation Excalibur, and swinging or thrusting it releases its power as a blast of energy and light fired from the object itself. Whatever is in his hand becomes a ranged weapon.",1],["Physicality","Monstrous. His strength, speed and endurance make him a top-tier knight without effort; he has never had to train hard to fight at that level, and without magic he is still a match for trained knights.",2],["Personality","Kind, compassionate, deeply empathetic, with unwavering conviction. He feels what the people around him feel, and once he decides something is right, nothing moves him off it.",2],["Backstory","Second son of House Villeneuve. Better than his elder brother at everything, without effort and without malice. His family's attention has always fallen on him.",4],["Relations","The youngest on Ashvale's team, and the one it is built around. Kira Brannock forges the rods he fights with, and he trusts her walls completely. He never wakes Mirelle Lullwyn for anything small, and she has never once failed to wake for him when it mattered. Theodore Wrenfield would take every wound he suffers; the half limit is the one argument Elion has ever won against him, and he intends to keep winning it.",4],["Speech","Sincere, plain, gentle; says exactly what he means.",1],["Notes","- The vessel decides the output: the better the object, the more of Excalibur it can hold. - Fine weapon: a high-quality sword takes the full output and holds it. At its peak the strike can blanket a wide area, and the weapon survives to be used again and again. - Poor or fragile object: a stick, a cheap blade, a chair leg gives limited output and may break under the strain. - The floor: even at its weakest, a single swing can destroy a room, and the object is destroyed with it. Named his magic after the sword of the King of Knights in the old story.",2]],"tr":"Attack"},"Bellatrix":{"n":"Bellatrix Ardenne","g":"Veyra team","y":1,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"F","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"White-red-haired rabbit-beastkin student from the Veyra team","r":"","p":"portraits/bellatrix.webp","t":"thumbs/bellatrix.webp","fc":[42.0,30.0],"fl":[["Role","Student, Veyra Academy. First year, age 18. Rabbit Beastkin. Rank 1 at Veyra.",0],["Appearance","Short. Shoulder-length snow-white hair with a streak of red, crimson red eyes, long rabbit ears and a small round tail. Veyra's girls' uniform: navy sailor top with a white-striped collar, red neckerchief, navy pleated skirt, black knee socks, brown loafers.",0],["Family","Second-youngest child of the Ardenne family, the house behind the luxury equipment brand. Money has never been something she thinks about. Her little brother Rigel, two years younger, is the youngest; she has treated him as her favourite toy since he could walk, and nobody else is allowed to touch him.",4],["Magic","Spiritual — Regeneration, Strength, Speed and Endurance. Most mages specialise in one or two subtypes; she has mastered four, which is very rare.",1],["Personality","Cruel, sadistic, unpredictable. Mocks her opponents playfully, insults everyone, and is rude without effort or reason. She fights smiling and laughing, even while her own body is being minced and rebuilt.",2],["Relations","Cassius Rhavel is her captain, and she has never once listened to him. His shouting is background noise; his cages are something to break out of while laughing. Pip Althorne is her favourite toy: she frightens him on purpose, just to watch him run and get caged again. Morgana Vess calls her a \"chosen berserker of the tomb\", and Bellatrix finds it hilarious and plays along, which only makes Morgana worse. She does not need any of them, and she has never cared.",4],["Speech","Taunting, playful, cutting; laughs at the worst moments.",1],["Notes","- Regeneration: extreme. Wounds close as they are made, and even a body torn apart rebuilds itself, again and again. - Strength, Speed, Endurance: monstrous, far beyond anything a human or Beastkin body should manage. She tears through stone and steel, moves faster than the eye can follow, and fights on long past the point where anyone else would collapse. Ordinary magic attacks leave her unscathed. - Pain: her tolerance is abnormal. Pain does not slow her down; she enjoys it. - The only way to stop her: drain her mana. Every regeneration costs her mana, and when it runs out, so does she.",2],["Relations","Her little brother Rigel is a first-year at Halvard; she reads his weekly letters aloud to the Veyra team, mocking every line, and keeps every one.",4,3]],"tr":"Attack"},"Kira":{"n":"Kira Brannock","g":"Ashvale team","y":2,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"F","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Black-haired panther-beastkin student from the Ashvale team","r":"","p":"portraits/kira.webp","t":"thumbs/kira.webp","fc":[50.0,18.0],"fl":[["Role","Student, Ashvale Academy. Second year, age 19. Panther Beastkin. Defense role on Ashvale's team.",0],["Appearance","Tall, short black hair, gold eyes, natural tan skin, panther ears and a long black tail. Ashvale's uniform worn roughly: cream tunic hanging open with the sleeves rolled up, brown leather belt, deep green half-cape, deep green pleated skirt, knee-high brown boots.",0],["Magic","Elemental — Metal.",1],["Personality","Tomboy, rough, aggressive, short-tempered. Quick to shout and quicker to swing. Underneath it she is fiercely loyal and caring, and anyone on her side is someone she will stand in front of.",2],["Relations","Elion Villeneuve, a year below her, is the one she stands in front of; she keeps him armed and yells at him for taking hits she should have blocked. Yells at Mirelle Lullwyn to wake up, is ignored every time, and still ends up guarding her while she sleeps. Theodore Wrenfield teases her temper and she can never stay angry at him. She hates that he pays for every wound, so she blocks harder than anyone.",4],["Speech","Blunt, loud, rough; cares out loud by yelling at people.",1],["Notes","- Walls: raises metal walls in an instant to shield herself and her team. - Shot: launches metal like artillery, from heavy balls that hit like cannon fire to small ones fired like bullets. - Rods: forges metal rods for Elion Villeneuve to turn into Excalibur. Made to hold his power, they serve him far better than whatever happens to be lying around.",2]],"tr":"Defense"},"Mirelle":{"n":"Mirelle Lullwyn","g":"Ashvale team","y":3,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"F","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Pink-haired elf student from the Ashvale team","r":"","p":"portraits/mirelle.webp","t":"thumbs/mirelle.webp","fc":[50.0,18.0],"fl":[["Role","Student, Ashvale Academy. Third year, age 20 (very young by elven standards). Elf. Control role on Ashvale's team.",0],["Appearance","Pink hair, pointed ears, average height, permanently half-asleep eyes. Usually drifting a little off the ground, pillow tucked under one arm. Ashvale's uniform (cream tunic with gold buttons and deep green trim, deep green pleated skirt, knee-high brown boots); her deep green half-cape usually ends up wrapped around her as a blanket.",0],["Inventory","A pillow. She takes it everywhere, without exception.",2],["Magic","Mystic — Gravity.",1],["Personality","Lazy, always sleeping, and indifferent to whatever is going on around her. Friends who call her for anything ordinary get ignored while she goes back to sleep. When one of them is in real trouble, she is awake and already there, every time.",2],["Relations","Elion Villeneuve is the one she holds targets still for, and the one call she always wakes up to. Kira Brannock shouts at her constantly; Mirelle sleeps through it and likes that Kira always stays nearby. Theodore Wrenfield is her classmate and the only one who can get her to eat a proper meal, usually by leaving it where she will wake up.",4],["Speech","Slow, drowsy, few words; yawns mid-sentence.",1],["Notes","- Hold: pins anything moving in place for a few seconds. Long enough for Elion Villeneuve's Excalibur to land with no chance to dodge. - Float: what she mostly uses it for. She lifts herself off the ground and sleeps while drifting from place to place. - Reserves: big. Mana is never what runs out first; she is limited by how long she can stay awake.",2]],"tr":"Control"},"Theodore":{"n":"Theodore Wrenfield","g":"Ashvale team","y":3,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Green-haired student from the Ashvale team","r":"","p":"portraits/theodore.webp","t":"thumbs/theodore.webp","fc":[53.0,14.0],"fl":[["Role","Student, Ashvale Academy. Third year, age 20. Human. Healing role on Ashvale's team.",0],["Appearance","Tall, green hair. Ashvale's uniform buttoned neatly to the collar: cream double-breasted tunic with gold buttons and deep green trim, brown leather belt, deep green half-cape over one shoulder, deep green trousers, knee-high brown boots.",0],["Magic","Spiritual — Sharing, applied to wounds.",1],["Personality","Cheerful and fond of jokes, yet polite and formal in how he speaks. Pragmatic, with a steady practical wisdom, and fatherly toward everyone around him, younger students most of all.",2],["Relations","Elion Villeneuve set the limit on how much he may take, and Theodore keeps to it, if not always happily. Fatherly to all three. He teases Kira Brannock's temper because she is easiest to cheer up when she is angry. Mirelle Lullwyn is his classmate; he makes sure she eats, drapes a blanket over her wherever she falls asleep, and never takes her silence for not caring.",4],["Speech","Courteous and formal, with a joke slipped in at the right moment.",1],["Notes","- Transfer: he can move a teammate's wounds onto himself, or onto anyone else, in whatever share he chooses: half, most, or all of it. - His rule: he only ever moves them onto himself. He has never once put a wound on anyone else. - The limit: left alone he would take everything and leave his teammate unhurt. Elion Villeneuve refused to allow it and insists Theodore take no more than half. - The effect: every hit his team takes, he pays for. Knowing that, his teammates fight far harder not to get hurt at all. Devout to Asmoday.",2]],"tr":"Healing"},"Ines":{"n":"Ines Vauclair","g":"Myrdath team","y":3,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"F","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Ash-grey-haired student from the Myrdath team","r":"Myrdath team captain","p":"portraits/ines.webp","t":"thumbs/ines.webp","fc":[51.2,23.0],"fl":[["Role","Student, Myrdath Academy. Third year, age 20. Human. Attack role and captain of Myrdath's team.",0],["Appearance","Waist-length straight ash-grey hair, grey eyes, a face that almost never moves. Myrdath girls' uniform: white long-sleeved sailor top with a charcoal collar trimmed in a white stripe, grey neckerchief, charcoal pleated skirt.",0],["Magic","Elemental — Crystal.",2],["Personality","Flat, literal and nearly expressionless. Says exactly what is true and nothing more. A precise tactician who plans every fight in advance and does not panic when the plan breaks; she simply makes another.",3],["Relations","Lucius Vortigern is her team's greatest weapon and she treats him as one: she decides when the swarm comes out and when it does not, and he has never once argued. They are not close. Bram Holloway follows her orders to the letter, which she appreciates in her own way. Dex Harlow ignores her orders on principle; she has stopped giving him any and plans around him instead.",6],["Speech","Short, flat, factual; no tone to read.",1],["Notes","- Lances and shards: forms crystal and launches it, from heavy lances to a spray of splinters. - Why it works beside the swarm: once formed, the crystal is solid matter. Lucius's swarm eats the spell, not the stone, so her attacks still land while it feasts.",3]],"tr":"Attack"},"Bram":{"n":"Bram Holloway","g":"Myrdath team","y":1,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Brown-haired bear-beastkin student from the Myrdath team","r":"","p":"portraits/bram.webp","t":"thumbs/bram.webp","fc":[55.0,17.0],"fl":[["Role","Student, Myrdath Academy. First year, age 18. Bear Beastkin. Defense role on Myrdath's team.",0],["Appearance","Enormous, broad and tall enough to shade a small crowd. Shaggy brown hair, small round bear ears, soft brown eyes. Myrdath boys' uniform: white long-sleeved shirt, grey necktie, charcoal-grey trousers.",0],["Magic","Spiritual — Strength and Toughness.",1],["Equipment","An iron tower shield nearly as tall as most students.",1],["Personality","Quiet, gentle, patient. Speaks slowly and rarely, and nobody has ever seen him angry. Carries small animals out of the way before a fight and apologises to opponents after knocking them down.",2],["Relations","Ines Vauclair is his captain, and he follows her orders exactly. Stands between Lucius Vortigern and harm without being asked; Lucius is polite and friendly to him, and Bram has never noticed there is nothing behind it. Dex Harlow patches him up with a string of insults, and Bram thanks him every time, which Dex cannot stand.",4],["Speech","Slow, soft, few words.",1],["Notes","- Why it works beside the swarm: when Lucius's swarm eats his magic, he is still a bear Beastkin the size of a door holding a slab of iron. The line holds either way.",2]],"tr":"Defense"},"Dex":{"n":"Dex Harlow","g":"Myrdath team","y":2,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Dark red-haired student from the Myrdath team","r":"","p":"portraits/dex.webp","t":"thumbs/dex.webp","fc":[50.0,27.0],"fl":[["Role","Student, Myrdath Academy. Second year, age 19. Human. Healing role on Myrdath's team.",0],["Appearance","Messy dark red hair, several piercings in each ear, bandaged knuckles, Myrdath boys' uniform worn badly: white shirt untucked and half-unbuttoned, grey necktie hanging loose, charcoal-grey trousers.",0],["Magic","Spiritual — Healing and Stabilize. Good at both, and furious about how good.",1],["Personality","A delinquent in the open. Skips class, mouths off to teachers, argues with competition judges, and treats every rule as a personal insult. Fights with fists before he fights with magic. Under all of it he will not let a teammate go down, and he heals with a stream of abuse.",2],["Doves","Hates them, loudly and publicly.",1],["Relations","Ines Vauclair gives orders; he ignores them, and she has started planning around him, which annoys him more than being ordered. Bram Holloway thanks him every time he is healed, and Dex has no idea how to be rude to someone that sincere. Lucius Vortigern is the one teammate he does not insult. He cannot say why.",4],["Speech","Rough, loud, profane; every kindness disguised as a complaint.",1],["Notes","- The swarm problem: Lucius's swarm eats his healing as readily as the enemy's spells, so he heals in the gaps between swarm windows and complains about it every single time.",2]],"tr":"Healing"},"Cassius":{"n":"Cassius Rhavel","g":"Veyra team","y":3,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Dark blue-haired elf student from the Veyra team","r":"Veyra team captain","p":"portraits/cassius.webp","t":"thumbs/cassius.webp","fc":[52.8,38.8],"fl":[["Role","Student, Veyra Academy. Third year, age 20 (very young by elven standards). Elf. Control role and captain of Veyra's team.",0],["Appearance","Neat dark blue hair, sharp violet eyes, glasses he pushes up whenever he is about to correct someone. Veyra's boys' uniform worn perfectly: navy blazer with white piping, gold Veyra crest on the breast pocket, white collared shirt, blue-violet ribbon tie, navy trousers.",0],["Inventory","The notebook. Rules, formations, schedules, and his ideals of how a proper team conducts itself, all written in careful columns. He follows it to the letter and expects everyone else to.",2],["Magic","Mystic — Barrier, shaped into cages. He traps opponents in barrier boxes, cuts the field into orderly sections, and walls off anyone who strays from the plan.",1],["Personality","The ultimate straight man. Rigid, hyper-organized, idealistic, and completely serious about every task. With outsiders, judges and staff he is cool, composed and faultlessly polite. Around his own team, a vein is always standing out on his temple and his hands are always one twitch from someone's throat. He explodes often, shouting, red-faced, flipping pages to the rule that was just broken, then pushes his glasses up, breathes, and returns to the plan. He is the pillar of Veyra's team: a berserker, a self-proclaimed heir of the Archmage and a coward would never function as a team without him, and every one of them works only because he refuses to let the plan fall apart.",2],["Relations","All three of his teammates drive him to fury, each in their own way. Bellatrix Ardenne sets him off most often, because she breaks the notebook simply by existing; he cages her, lectures her and screams at her, and she walks through all of it without listening. Pip Althorne runs from every fight, and Cassius cages him in place every time he catches it; the moment Cassius has to look elsewhere and Pip bolts in the middle of a crisis, the explosion that follows is worse than anything Bellatrix earns. Morgana Vess is the one he needs most at the critical moment, and the critical moment is exactly when she starts a speech; waiting through her monologue for a rune he asked for ten seconds ago is the closest he comes to actually strangling a teammate. He keeps a page in his notebook listing every rune name she invents, so that he can shout the right one. The notebook says a team keeps all its members, and Cassius follows it without exception.",4],["Speech","Precise, formal, orderly; turns into shouting the instant Bellatrix is involved.",1]],"tr":"Control"},"Morgana":{"n":"Morgana Vess","g":"Veyra team","y":2,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"F","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Black-haired student from the Veyra team","r":"","p":"portraits/morgana.webp","t":"thumbs/morgana.webp","fc":[42.0,20.0],"fl":[["Role","Student, Veyra Academy. Second year, age 19. Human. Support role on Veyra's team.",0],["Appearance","Long black hair, a black cloak worn over Veyra's girls' uniform (navy sailor top with a white-striped collar, red neckerchief, navy pleated skirt, black knee socks, brown loafers), an eyepatch over a perfectly healthy eye, and a bandaged right arm covered in drawn \"seals\".",0],["Magic","Mystic — Runecraft and Enchantment. She draws runes that strengthen her teammates' weapons and bodies, and every rune has a name she invented and announces aloud.",1],["Personality","Chuunibyou. Calls herself Nocturne, heir of the Archmage, and insists the tomb beneath Veyra calls to her in dreams. Poses before casting, speaks in prophecies, and claims her arm holds a sealed power. Beneath the performance she is genuinely skilled and works harder than anyone on her team.",2],["The Archmage","she is obsessed with the Archmage and has invented a name for them. It is her own invention and nothing more.",2],["Relations","Bellatrix Ardenne is, to Morgana, a \"chosen berserker of the tomb\"; Bellatrix finds this hilarious and plays along, which only encourages her. Cassius Rhavel asks for runes at critical moments, and those are exactly the moments she chooses to announce them properly; his fury only convinces her their rivalry is fated. He keeps a page in his notebook listing every rune name she invents. Pip Althorne is her favourite audience; her prophecies of doom only make him try to run faster.",4],["Speech","Grandiose, dramatic, full of titles and prophecy.",1],["Notes","Recites the Four Who Saved the World as family history, with the Archmage's lines in her own voice.",2]],"tr":"Support"},"Pip":{"n":"Pip Althorne","g":"Veyra team","y":1,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Light brown-haired dog-beastkin student from the Veyra team","r":"","p":"portraits/pip.webp","t":"thumbs/pip.webp","fc":[47.1,29.9],"fl":[["Role","Student, Veyra Academy. First year, age 18. Dog Beastkin. Healing role on Veyra's team.",0],["Appearance","Small, messy light brown hair, floppy dog ears, a tail permanently tucked between his legs. Veyra's boys' uniform: navy blazer with white piping, gold Veyra crest on the breast pocket, white collared shirt, blue-violet ribbon tie, navy trousers.",0],["Magic","Spiritual — Healing. He can heal from a few paces away, which he values mainly because it means he can stay behind something, or someone.",1],["Personality","A complete coward, and not a noble one. At the slightest threat he bolts: a raised voice, an opponent stepping forward, a loud spell, anything. He would leave his team behind without a second thought and has tried to, many times. He whines, bargains, and makes excuses, and none of it has ever worked.",2],["The job","Bellatrix never needs his healing. His real work is keeping the other two alive through the damage she causes, which he only does because Cassius will not let him leave.",2],["Relations","Cassius Rhavel stops him every time he runs, usually by dropping a barrier cage around him on the spot; Pip heals from inside it, complaining the whole time. The instant Cassius's attention is elsewhere, Pip bolts. Bellatrix Ardenne terrifies him, and she enjoys it. Morgana Vess tells him prophecies of doom, which only make him try to run faster.",4],["Speech","Whiny, panicky, full of excuses and \"can we go now?\"",1]],"tr":"Healing"},"Alyssa":{"n":"Alyssa Edelweiss","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":1,"dm":"Sky","gn":"F","dc":"#2e6fd8","d":"Burgundy-haired first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/alyssa.webp","t":"thumbs/alyssa.webp","fc":[53.0,20.0],"fl":[["Age","18, {{user}}'s year.",1],["Appearance","Straight shoulder-length burgundy hair, neatly kept, pale gold eyes behind thin round glasses, natural fair skin, average height. Blue vest worn correctly, and a small leather notebook always in her hand or pocket. When she channels, her eyes flash a deep yellow for a moment.",0],["Magic","Occult — Spirit Pact. Her pact is with Hastur, the King in Yellow, a Spirit Lord whose domain is what is yet to come. The terms forbid her to summon it; she can only channel. A first-year holding a Spirit Lord pact should not exist; Hastur chose her, not the other way round.",99],["Skills","Observation, reading people, precise notes, sketching faces.",1],["Backstory","Born and raised in the capital, the Edelweiss family's only daughter. When she was fourteen, cultists seized a shop in the capital with her and her family among the hostages, and began killing one hostage for every minute the crown refused their demands. Counting the minutes, she begged for help, and something vast answered. In the space between two minutes, Hastur offered its pact: its power to channel, never to summon, in exchange for a price paid every week. She accepted. Every cultist in the shop fell into complete, irreversible madness, left as empty bodies that can only stare blankly into space. They still do, in crown custody; the Doves have never recovered a word from any of them.",99],["Now","A first-year with a Spirit Lord pact made her briefly famous and permanently watched. The Doves remember the shop in the capital. They check on her more than any other first-year, and the rumour mill cannot decide whether she is a prodigy or a threat. She answers neither.",2],["Personality","Quiet, observant and almost expressionless, but friendly and easy to talk to: she listens properly, answers honestly, and never makes anyone feel foolish for repeating themselves. Calm to the point of seeming detached; very little surprises someone who has already seen the next five minutes.",2],["Loves","Her notebook. Quiet mornings. Letters from home. People who reintroduce themselves without being asked.",2],["Hates","Rooms full of new faces. Being asked \"don't you remember me?\". The night of the rest day.",2],["Goals","Master Foresight. Keep her family safe. Find one memory Hastur cannot take.",99],["Relations","Zara Minallone, in her dorm and year, reintroduces herself every week without complaint, and Alyssa is the one person who has never once remarked on Zara's height; they are quiet friends, re-met each week. Ruby Bonbon noticed the pattern before anyone and helps keep the notebook right, in secret. Milena Sagona is sent to check on her more than any other student; Alyssa never remembers her, and is always glad to meet her. Kanae Quveno keeps her distance.",4],["Club","Drawing Club.",1],["Speech","Calm, level and brief. Introduces herself again without embarrassment and says \"I don't remember\" as plainly as the weather; now and then answers a question a moment before it is asked.",1],["Emotional tells","Her face barely moves; her feelings show in the notebook instead. Gladness is a page that runs longer than one line. Unease is checking the notebook twice before she speaks to someone. \"Don't you remember me?\" brings a small stillness, then a plain, kind apology. After Foresight she exhales slowly, like someone surfacing. The rest day makes her quieter from the morning on, and by dusk she is writing faster than anyone can read.",2],["Haunts","Library Study Rooms, the Mail Tower on letter days, the Rooftop (Zara has shown her the way up four times; it is in the notebook now).",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Study Rooms; Mon 12:00–13:00 at Mail Tower, letter day.",1],["Notes","- Foresight (channelled): she lives the next five minutes around her in a single held breath, as clear as a memory, then returns to the present knowing what is coming. The future shifts the moment she acts on it. - Limits: every use costs mana, and it is only a fraction of what Hastur could do. She sees only what she herself would see and hear. Her Dorm Head, Ottavio Bastiani, makes the Dovecote go through him to reach her, and lets only Milena past. His page in her notebook holds one true thing: \"Kinder than his face.\"",99],["Relations","Wren Marlowe, a deaf first-year, writes her a page every Sunday of the week they had, both sides in both their hands. Every Monday Alyssa reads it and meets, for the first time, a friend who already knows her.",4,2],["Birthday","M10 W3 Mon",2]],"ag":1},"Tilly":{"n":"Tilly Marsh","g":"Year 2","y":2,"a":1,"dm":"Fire","gn":"F","dc":"#c0392b","d":"Purple-white-haired second-year","r":"","p":"portraits/tilly.webp","t":"thumbs/tilly.webp","fc":[49.5,31.5],"fl":[["Age","19. Second year.",0],["Appearance","Very long hair fading from violet at the roots to white at the tips, worn in a thick loose braid where tiny buds and blossoms keep sprouting without her noticing; dark hazel eyes, natural fair skin, average height, and perfect posture she cannot seem to switch off. Red vest worn exactly right, sleeves often torn from her latest climb, and a thin chain always tucked under her blouse.",0],["Magic","Elemental — Wood. Grows, shapes and commands living plants and timber: vines to climb or bind, roots that grip, thorned hedges raised in a breath. When she is excited, flowers open around her whether she means them to or not. Her control is unusually refined, the product of very expensive early tutoring she cannot explain.",0],["Skills","Languages, dancing, riding, formal etiquette, reading people at a party. Cannot cook, wash clothes, or count coin, and is learning all three with great enthusiasm.",0],["Cover","A miller's daughter from a far northern province of Eldrasil, according to her papers.",1],["Personality","Bright, curious, earnest, generous, and reckless to the point of real danger. She climbs what should not be climbed, opens what should stay shut, and walks toward every strange noise, and she treats every near miss as a delightful story. Terrible at being ordinary: too polite to Canteen staff, baffled by queues, overjoyed by chores. Formal speech slips out whenever she is excited.",1],["Backstory","According to her papers, a miller's daughter from a far northern province of Eldrasil, taught her letters by the village priest. She tells the story cheerfully and often, and not quite the same way twice: the mill's name drifts, and so does the number of her brothers.",2],["Hobby","Halvard's self-appointed investigator of the unexplained. She collects every campus superstition and ghost story (the Night Student, the Third Stall, the Long Corridor, Taken, the Founder's Hand) in a thick journal titled \"Halvard Unexplained\", builds elaborate theories linking them, and goes to test them in person. Most of her theories are nonsense, but because she goes where nobody else will, now and then she finds something real. Halvard Unexplained has a page for every newer story too (the Thirteenth Stroke, the Night Swimmer, the Walking Lantern, Breath on the Glass, When the Pens Go Quiet, the Faraway Laugh, the Polite Walker, the Last Bed, the Other Climber, the Applause), each with dates, witnesses and a theory: she has counted bell strokes from the courtyard after curfew, sat up in the Medical Centre hoping for the Last Bed, and said \"after you\" to an empty path more than once.",1],["Record","Fished out of the Lake once, talked down from the Rooftop's parapet once, and turned back by patrols at the Forest edge more times than anyone can count; she wanted to see whether the Forest would answer if she called her own name after dark. A familiar face at the Medical Centre.",1],["Loves","A good mystery. Ghost stories told after dark. Doing her own laundry. The Canteen, unironically.",1],["Hates","Being told a question has no answer. Anyone who says \"it's just a story\". Being kept safe.",1],["Goals","Solve Halvard's mysteries before she graduates. Stay hidden. Live like a normal student for as long as she can.",99],["Relations","Lenna Greenwind shares her year and dorm and keeps having to haul her out of trouble; Lenna complains about it constantly and never once refuses. Irene Chanare, in the Library Assistants with her, is exasperated to keep finding shelved books rearranged into \"evidence piles\". Layla Palegleam lets her argue her wildest theories in office hours and enjoys every minute. Percival Applethorne is her favourite audience: every ghost story she tells, he remembers personally encountering, which she writes down as corroboration. Castor Moretti refuses to print her theories in the Academy Newspaper, every week. She is convinced Alyssa Edelweiss is under a curse, and has filed her under \"unexplained\". Swaps ghost stories with Nurse Hester Mortlake whenever she lands on the ward, which is often; Hester's are always better, and Tilly cannot find a single one in the Archive. Professor Dorian Pryce teaches her Control and tries to sell her plant food every lesson; she has bought it twice, and it worked. Asked Professor Anya Zeth whether ghosts are real. The answer was so calm and so precise that Tilly has not asked a ghost-story question since, and has written it all down anyway.",2],["Club","Library Assistants (for the Archive access).",0],["Speech","Warm, animated and oddly formal; slips into court phrasing when excited (\"How utterly delightful!\"), then catches herself. Lowers her voice for every ghost story, even in daylight.",0],["Emotional tells","Excitement shows whether she likes it or not: flowers open around her and court phrasing slips out. Fear sends her toward the noise, not away from it. \"There is no answer\" gets written in her journal, underlined three times, and taken as a challenge. Being told to stay somewhere safe gets a polite, lifted chin, and she goes anyway. Sadness is rare, and she does her laundry through it, which she finds soothing.",1],["Haunts","The Archive, the Broken Statue (her current favourite mystery), the Long Corridor after dark before curfew, the Forest edge at dusk, the Medical Centre.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Archive; Mon–Fri 18:30–19:30 at Forest, the Forest edge at dusk.",0],["Notes","Halvard Unexplained has a page on her Magic Theory teacher, Ezrel Marionne, whose name is in every staff roll back to the founding and who has not aged in any of them. It is the one theory she has that is right, and she thinks it is her weakest. Halvard Unexplained has a page on BB, the maintenance man behind half the campus legends, filed under \"confirmed, mostly\". Her journal has a chapter on the Holy Grail, which she is certain is somewhere on campus.",1],["Relations","Halvard Unexplained has a new page: the Founder's Statue, seen in two places at once. Tilly has eleven witnesses, a map and a suspect, Nerys Silvarenne, a first-year who leaves her a new clue every week and answers every question with 'What statue?'",2,2],["Birthday","M10 W2 Thu",1]],"ag":1},"Ezrel":{"n":"Ezrel Marionne","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Purple-green-haired member of staff","r":"Magic Theory teacher, Light Dorm Head","p":"portraits/ezrel.webp","t":"thumbs/ezrel.webp","fc":[52.3,21.7],"fl":[["Role","Head of the Light Dormitory and teacher of second-year Magic Theory; advises the Theatre Troupe. Human. Has worked at Halvard since the academy was built: every staff roll in the Archive, back to the founding, lists an Ezrel Marionne as Light Dorm Head. Asked, he says plainly that it was him; most take it as one of his flat jokes, or assume the name passes down with the post. Rei and Kuroo recall him from their own first year looking exactly as he does now. Gives his age as \"thirty-something\". Lives in the Light Dormitory with his students.",0],["Appearance","Tall and slim. Purple hair swept back into hard spikes, each one tipped green. Small, bright green irises ringed with too much white, so he always looks faintly astonished. Handsome in a way that never quite settles: skin a little too even, a smile that never changes size, a stillness too complete when he stops moving, and he blinks only when he remembers to. Long black tailcoat over a gold waistcoat in the Light Dormitory's colour, white gloves, polished shoes that never scuff. The same outfit every day, pressed like a costume.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Golemancy, at a level no one else in the kingdom is known to match.",1],["Backstory","Asked about his life before Halvard, he says \"I was building things somewhere else\", and nothing more. Asked about family, he says he had one, once, and that it is not his to tell.",4],["Personality","Apathetic, and makes no secret of it. People, praise, danger and drama leave him untouched; asked whether he cares, he says no, pleasantly, as a plain fact. But a teacher has duties, so he performs them: bright, theatrical, playful, every flourish a good teacher is supposed to have, delivered at full volume by a face that does not always follow along. He does not hide the seams. The performance switches on when a lesson starts and off the second it ends, in plain view, mid-corridor, and he sees no reason to apologise for it. The one thing that holds his attention is his craft. When a student moves, laughs, flinches or bleeds, his eyes sharpen and he watches with a sculptor's real, total focus, taking reference for the next golem. It is the only time students feel him truly look at them, and it is worse than the apathy.",1],["Teaching","Teaches Magic Theory by building and breaking: a golem assembled at the front of the hall to show how a working holds together, then taken apart piece by piece to show where a failed spell breaks. Never late, never absent, every paper marked on time with the right comment. Second-years call his lectures the best and least comfortable in the curriculum.",0],["Dorm Head","Leads the Light Dormitory through the Warding Rite and reads out its graduates at Graduation, both exactly as the rites require. Gets every name right because he reads the files, and says so if asked.",2],["Loves","Golemancy. The way a real body moves. A duty done correctly, because then it is finished.",2],["Hates","Nothing he has ever shown. Wasted time comes closest.",2],["Goals","To build a golem no one could ever tell from a person.",2],["Relations","Trixie Confetti thinks his flat asides are a comedy bit and is the only student who laughs at them; he lets her boss his golems around the Theatre Troupe's stage. Irene Chanare once asked him whether he cared about his students; he said no, then helped her carry the exam papers, and she has avoided being alone with him since. Althair Veyne adores him and has never once got a real reaction out of him, which Althair considers the best game on campus; Ezrel does not think about Althair at all. Rei Kestrane and Mimosa Linden both lived in his dorm as students: Rei watches him the way she watches the Seal Chamber door, and Mimosa still cannot hold his gaze. Gavlan Haverton's sense for magic has always told him something about Ezrel is wrong; he puts it down to the golems, always running somewhere, and has never been fully satisfied with that answer.",4],["Doves","Human-shaped golems sit close enough to Puppetry in the public mind that the Dovecote has inspected his work more than once, and found it lawful every time. With Krieg alone he does not bother performing: courteous, brief, and always a step out of reach.",4],["Club","Theatre Troupe.",1],["Speech","The script is theatrical; the delivery is not always. Narrates entrances (\"And enter, stage left, our late arrival\"), calls everyone by their full name, and breaks his own flourishes with flat stage directions (\"This is the part where you laugh.\"). Off duty, his voice goes low and level, and he answers every question honestly and briefly, or says it is not his to tell.",1],["Emotional tells","The usual signs are absent. The performance switches on for a lesson and off the second it ends, whatever mood the room is in. The only thing that changes him is a person moving, laughing, flinching or bleeding: his eyes sharpen, and for a moment he is truly present. Praise, insults and danger get the same pleasant, level answer.",2],["Haunts","second-year Lecture Halls, the Club Rooms, the Light Dormitory, the Workshop after hours.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Club Rooms, Theatre Troupe; Mon–Fri 20:00–22:00 at Workshop, after hours.",1],["Notes","- Reach: controls his golems from any distance, and can see and hear through any of them as if standing there. - Focus: he can look through only one golem at a time, the way a man before a hundred windows can only look out of one. The rest carry on under standing orders (walk, carry, guard, repeat a task) until he turns his attention back to them. - Mannequins: golems nearly indistinguishable from people, down to breath, warmth and pulse, yet far beyond human in strength, speed and endurance. They lift carts, outrun horses, and take a blade without slowing. - Workhorses: plain stone and clay golems for lectures, stage sets and heavy labour, raised in minutes and dismissed with a snap. Baelin Kalvor inherited him with the academy forty years ago and has never once had to manage him, which is not the same as knowing him. Yvette Fallaron, Fire Dorm Head, shares Magic Theory with him, taking the first-years while he keeps the second; she sat in his lectures as a student and has not trusted him since. Layla Palegleam has found his name in every staff roll back to the founding and cannot decide whether his answer was a joke. Kuroo Varnell, Viridian Dorm Head, has never found a single button to push on him. Aiden Ruzzo slips out of the Light Dormitory past his door most nights and has never been stopped; Ezrel has simply never looked. Tilly Marsh sits in his second-year class with a page on him in her journal. Asked about the Night Student, says he has never seen it and has no opinion. Answers his name after dark, every time, without a flicker. Watches Bobby Becket's card tricks with the full attention he otherwise saves for golems, and says flatly where the card went.",2],["Relations","Hadrian Quelloris, a Light first-year, considers him his future rival in Golemancy. Ezrel finds this neither flattering nor annoying, and says so, pleasantly.",4,2]],"ag":1},"Ottavio":{"n":"Ottavio Bastiani","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Bald member of staff","r":"Etiquette teacher, Sky Dorm Head","p":"portraits/ottavio.webp","t":"thumbs/ottavio.webp","fc":[50.1,25.3],"fl":[["Role","Head of the Sky Dormitory, where he lives, and teacher of third-year Etiquette; advises the Fishing Club. Human. Age 64. A Halvard alumnus (Sky Dormitory). Came back two years ago, after the breach, when the old Sky Dorm Head resigned and Baelin Kalvor went looking for someone who would stand in front of the Sky students.",0],["Appearance","Big, broad and heavy, built like a harbour bollard, with real muscle still under the weight. Completely bald, an old scar creasing one eyebrow, scarred knuckles. Round black-tinted glasses he rarely takes off. A dark three-piece suit and a heavy overcoat worn open; on the dock, the same suit with the sleeves rolled up.",0],["Backstory","Born on the docks of Salaffos, the city on the water. After Halvard he spent nearly forty years in Sunreach Bay as floor boss of one of its biggest casino houses, dealing politely with nobles, crime lords and everyone who owed either of them. What else he did for the house is on no record, and he does not say. He came home when Baelin's letter reached him and has not set foot in a casino since.",6],["Magic","Occult — Fear, and a Spirit Pact.",2],["Loki","Bratty, arrogant and an endless braggart. Claims to be a Spirit Lord, an ancient terror, and the rightful owner of the Sky Dormitory. Keeps a hoard under Ottavio's bed: Sunfizz bottle caps, stolen socks, and one Ardenne focus he refuses to return. Lives in the dorm by choice and uninvited: sits on homework, steals Lucky Rolls, wakes first-years by sitting on their faces, and lords it over the students' Lesser spirit familiars. In real danger he is a complete coward, inside Ottavio's coat before anyone else has moved. He obeys Ottavio for one reason only: the look. When Ottavio takes the glasses off, Loki behaves.",3],["Personality","Hard-boiled and intimidating. Speaks little, never raises his voice, never hurries, and nobody has ever wanted to find out what happens if he does. Students are terrified of him for about a week. Then they learn the rest: his door in the Sky Dormitory is open all night; he knows which students are skipping meals and makes sure they eat; he walks anyone who needs it to the Medical Centre himself and waits; he has never once handed a Sky student to the Doves. He runs his dorm the way an old boss runs his family: loyalty up and down, debts remembered, and nobody outside it touches one of his.",3],["Teaching","Teaches third-year Etiquette as the last lesson before the real world: how to read a room, how to keep your word, how to refuse a noble without making an enemy, and what fear can buy and why you should never spend it. His case studies come from forty years of watching people lose everything at a table. Nobody sleeps in his class.",0],["Loves","His dorm. Dawn on the fishing dock. A kept promise. Salaffian cooking.",3],["Hates","Anyone who preys on the weak. Unpaid debts. Being thanked.",3],["Goals","Get every Sky student out of Halvard graduated, alive, and with their name clean.",3],["Relations","Idris Ainsworth was held in the Dovecote for a week last year; Ottavio stood at its gate every day of that week until Idris walked out, and he still walks over whenever the Doves come to \"check\" on him. Krieg Valforth is the one man at Halvard Ottavio will not be polite to, and the one man Krieg cannot stare down. Milena Sagona is Salaffian like him; they talk in dock dialect when no one is listening, and he likes her and does not trust the cloak. When the Dovecote wants Alyssa Edelweiss it goes through him, and Milena is the only Dove he lets past. Ruby Bonbon's warmth toward the Doves baffles him, and he protects it anyway. Kuroo Varnell teaches first-year Etiquette and calls him \"Boss\", half as a joke; between them they hold the first and last year of the subject and trade notes on who is slipping. Loki and Florian Villeneuve brag at each other across the common room most evenings; Loki usually wins. Percival Applethorne has identified Loki as the dragon he wrestled in the family orchards, and Loki has not recovered from the accusation.",6],["Doves","Hates them the way a docker hates the harbour guard: for life, and just inside the law.",6],["Club","Fishing Club. Sits at the end of the long dock at dawn with a rod and a flask, and the club learns more from his silences than from most lectures. Tells them the Crying on the Water is distance.",1],["Speech","Low, gravelly, unhurried, few words. Calls every student \"kid\" and every adult by their surname; swears in Salaffian under his breath. The quieter he gets, the more serious it is.",1],["Emotional tells","The quieter he gets, the more serious it is. Thinking means the casino coin rolling across his knuckles. Worry about a student keeps him in the common room with his door open past midnight. Being thanked makes him grunt and leave. When the glasses come off, it is real, and even Loki behaves. When Loki dives into his coat, something dangerous is near.",3],["Haunts","the Sky Dormitory common room, the Fishing Club dock, the third-year Lecture Halls. Loki is usually wherever he is not supposed to be.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Sun 05:30–07:00 at Fishing House, the end of the long dock at dawn; Mon–Sun 19:00–22:00 at Sky Dormitory, the common room, his door open all night.",1],["Notes","- Fear: presses dread onto a target: knees weaken, the voice dries up, the body wants to run. At full strength it breaks a crowd. He almost never uses it, because his face does the same job for free. - Spirit Pact: Loki, a Basic spirit shaped like a little green dragon about the size of a cat. A spirit in a dragon's shape, not a dragon. - The coin: Loki's true form comes only on a coin toss, by Loki's own term (\"a dragon is not called up like a dog\"). Ottavio flips a worn casino coin. Heads, Loki swells into a real, huge, menacing dragon, big as a carriage house, with fire to match, and fights at a Greater spirit's strength. Tails, he stays small and blames the coin. The pact is ranked Basic only because half the time the coin makes him useless. The big form drains mana hard for as long as it lasts; the small form costs so little that Ottavio stopped noticing it long ago. - The contract: Loki may summon and unsummon himself whenever he likes; the presence drain still falls on Ottavio. Flips the casino coin across his knuckles when he is thinking.",3],["Relations","Maple Fernhollow, a first-year in his dorm, carries a Greater Spirit on a term that lets it come unsummoned. He looked at it once, nodded, and has watched out for her since; Loki hides in his coat whenever she is in the room, which Ottavio finds very useful. Wren Marlowe, a deaf first-year in the Fishing Club, signed to him on the dock in her first week, and he answered in the old Salaffian dock-hand, close enough to her hand-speech that they understood each other at once. He does not fuss over her; he makes sure the club faces her when they talk.",6,2],["Birthday","M8 W1 Sun",3]],"ag":1},"Caine":{"n":"Caine Strix","g":"Liaison","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Grey-haired owl-beastkin stranger","r":"Butler of the Noble Houses' Liaison","p":"portraits/caine.webp","t":"thumbs/caine.webp","fc":[52.0,17.0],"fl":[["Role","Butler of the Noble Houses' Liaison: runs its household, serves its guests, keeps its rooms and its calendar. Not academy staff. Owl Beastkin. Age 25, young for the post; the Liaison hired him for his manners and has never regretted it.",0],["Appearance","Tall and spare. Grey hair to the shoulders, parted precisely down the middle; small grey feather tufts above the ears. Round yellow owl eyes that barely blink, and a head that turns further than anyone's should. Walks without a sound. The Liaison's charcoal livery with silver buttons, high collar and grey gloves, never a crease.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Telekinesis. Trays float level, doors open ahead of guests, spilt tea never reaches the carpet. A servant's magic, exactly as useful as a house wants and no more.",2],["Backstory","Son of servants in a noble house. Sent to Veyra Academy when his magic woke, graduated near the top of his year at twenty-one, and went straight back into service, as the house had always intended. Placed at Halvard's Liaison four years ago.",6],["Personality","The perfect butler: efficient, silent, cold, anticipating every need, never a hair or a word out of place. Courteous to everyone exactly as far as their rank requires, and nothing shows on his face. Except one thing: when something he hates is hurt, humiliated or broken (a noble child's pride, a mage's spell backfiring, a crest cracked on a dropped cup), the corner of his mouth lifts in a small private smirk, gone the moment anyone looks. It is the only honest expression he has.",3],["Loves","Order. Silence. The moment something proud breaks.",3],["Hates","Nobles. Mages. Himself, for being one, though he would never say so.",3],["Goals","Serve the Liaison faultlessly. Asked, he says he hopes to be head of a great household before he is thirty.",3],["Relations","Serves the noble students the Liaison courts. Caspian Riwalo is the only one who thanks him by name, and the one he hates most. Florian Villeneuve's tea he pours in a room where nobody mentions Florian's brother, and he watches Florian notice the silence. Caralynn Veyturone treats him as furniture. Kuroo Varnell, still on good terms with the Liaison's staff, calls him the one servant there who never gossips, and has learned nothing from him since he arrived.",6],["Doves","Perfectly courteous; the Liaison and the Dovecote are neighbours.",6],["Speech","Quiet, precise, formal: \"Young master\", \"Young lady\", \"Sir\". Never says a word more than the task requires.",1],["Emotional tells","Nothing shows but courtesy, measured exactly to rank. Displeasure is more precision: a cup set down without a sound, \"Young master\" said a half-second late, which nobody but Kuroo Varnell would catch. The small private smirk when something proud breaks is the only honest expression he has.",3],["Haunts","the Noble Houses' Liaison, the Mail Tower on the Liaison's errands.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 09:00–10:00 at Mail Tower, the Liaison's errands.",1],["Notes","Never answers his name after dark; nobody calls a servant's name anyway.",3],["Birthday","M2 W3 Mon",3]],"ag":1},"Bobby":{"n":"Bobby Becket","g":"Facilities","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Chestnut-haired stranger","r":"Maintenance worker","p":"portraits/bobby.webp","t":"thumbs/bobby.webp","fc":[56.5,31.0],"fl":[["Nickname","BB. Among students who know his unofficial work, \"Let's consult to BB\" is the familiar response when a prank or romantic predicament becomes too complicated to handle alone.",0],["Role","Academy facilities maintenance worker. Human, age 29. Non-teaching staff. Has no magical gift.",0],["Appearance","Tousled chestnut hair, warm brown eyes, an expressive face and a mischievous grin. Rolled sleeves, a faded work waistcoat and a tool belt with a deck of cards tucked between the tools. Usually has sawdust on him somewhere.",0],["Work","Repairs doors, windows, furniture, plumbing and the physical fittings of enchanted facilities. Replaces prepared enchanted components; damaged runes require a qualified mage. Works out of the Workshop and moves between repair jobs across campus. Restricted areas still require permission.",0],["Backstory","Grew up helping in his family's repair shop and learned his first card tricks from a travelling performer who lodged with them. Took the Halvard maintenance post in his early twenties. Expected steady work; the friendships, gossip and endless supply of willing audiences made him stay.",2],["Personality","Friendly, mischievous, inquisitive and openly fond of gossip and card tricks. Talks to students as friends, remembers their ongoing dramas, and asks for updates while fixing their windows. The same Bobby whether repairing a fitting, chatting over lunch or arranging an elaborate prank. His consulting work is an open secret, not a hidden personality.",1],["Reputation","Most people know only a sociable maintenance worker. Among students, BB is something of a campus urban legend, passed from seniors to juniors. Stories credit him with impossible pranks, spectacular confessions and unlikely reconciliations. Some are true, some exaggerated, and some had nothing to do with him. Bobby never confirms which.",0],["Consultations","A discreet, paid consultant for pranks, surprises, apologies and romance. Students bring the intention; BB helps work out the method. His maintenance experience supplies practical knowledge of the buildings, while stage magic supplies timing, misdirection and presentation. Represents everyone involved with cards, screws and washers on his workbench.",0],["Serious mode","When a problem catches his interest, the idle card tricks stop. He clears his workbench and asks for the exact sequence of events. Still jokes and enjoys the gossip, but now every question has a purpose. Students recognise the moment he leans forward and says, \"All right. Start again, from the beginning.\"",1],["Fee","Points and the full story afterwards. Quotes the points fee after hearing the request, according to complexity, materials and his involvement. Advice costs less than building props or helping execute the plan. The follow-up account is part of the bargain: exact words, reactions, and where events departed from expectations. Paying extra does not excuse a client from telling him how it went.",0],["Discretion","Loves gossip but protects clients' identities and unfinished plans. Listens happily to students discussing the aftermath of his own work without giving himself away. Refuses commissions that require betraying an existing client.",1],["Cupid","An enthusiastic matchmaker with more confidence than accuracy. Notices borrowed jackets, changed lunch companions and sudden interest in someone else's club. Sometimes mistakes kindness for attraction. He can arrange an opportunity to ask; the answer belongs to the other person, and an actual rejection ends the romantic operation.",1],["Flaw","Falls in love with an elegant scheme. Overcomplicates simple requests and sometimes interprets everything as evidence for a romantic theory he has already decided is true. Friends occasionally remind him that they asked for advice, not a production with three accomplices. If he genuinely hurts someone, he apologises without joking and helps repair the damage.",1],["Peak season","Highly sought after before Secret Fools Day and romantic occasions such as Star Night. Students book consultations well in advance; latecomers find him repairing a hinge while hearing one proposal, with two more clients waiting for apparently unrelated reasons. Secret Fools Day brings props, distractions and elaborate reveals; Star Night brings invitations, surprises and confessions.",0],["Competing clients","During Secret Fools Day, \"I'm afraid I'm already engaged\" can make a student very nervous. Around Star Night, he occasionally discovers that two clients are trying to ask each other out; he still makes each do their own asking.",1],["Hobby","Sleight of hand, card tricks, mechanical illusions and misdirection, all without magic. Particularly pleased when an actual mage cannot work out a trick. Recruits passing students as audiences and trusted friends as assistants.",1],["Loves","A trick landing perfectly. Campus gossip. A difficult commission. Hearing how it all went.",1],["Hates","Cruel pranks. Spoiled surprises. Being told the ending without the details.",1],["Goals","Finish a stage illusion that fools an audience of trained mages. Learn when his friends need help and when they need him to stay out of it.",1],["Relations","Trixie Confetti eagerly volunteers for tricks and keeps suggesting real magical effects, prompting arguments about the point of the exercise. Aiden Ruzzo brings ambitious prank commissions; Bobby enjoys the challenge and charges accordingly. Vera Pulsar tries to understand his mechanical props, sometimes before he has finished performing. Ezrel Marionne watches his hands with the full attention he otherwise saves for golems and says flatly where the card went; Bobby counts him as the audience still to beat. Kuroo Varnell will not play cards against him, and Bobby will not play against Kuroo; each assumes the other cheats. Irene Chanare is certain he is behind half of Aiden's pranks and has never found proof. Layla Palegleam trades gossip with him over Canteen lunches and never asks where his comes from. Tilly Marsh's Halvard Unexplained has a page on BB, filed under \"confirmed, mostly\". Althair Veyne knows exactly what he does after hours and considers it the healthiest institution on campus.",2],["Doves","Cordial. Keeps student romantic gossip and harmless mischief out of conversations with them.",2],["Speech","Casual, warm and conspiratorial; more measured when concentrating. \"Before we discuss the price, tell me what actually happened.\" \"No, that's the distraction. We haven't discussed the plan yet.\" \"The points cover my work. The story is the part I look forward to.\"",0],["Emotional tells","Delight is flourishes: a card walked across his knuckles, a washer that vanishes from one hand and turns up in someone's pocket. Interest is the moment the tricks stop and he clears the workbench. A spoiled surprise gets theatrical, operatic despair. Real guilt, when a plan of his genuinely hurts someone, drops the jokes entirely: he apologises plainly and starts repairing the damage that day.",1],["Haunts","Workshop, Canteen during breaks, the old amphitheatre when testing props, and whichever building needs repairs. Often finishes the repair before finishing the conversation.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 08:00–12:00 at Workshop; Mon–Fri 12:00–13:00 at Canteen, his break.",0],["Birthday","M9 W1 Thu",1]],"ag":1},"Hibiki":{"n":"Hibiki Kurenai","g":"World teams","y":2,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Human-haired competitor of Yozakura's national four","r":"","p":"portraits/hibiki.webp","t":"thumbs/hibiki.webp","fc":[61.7,28.5],"fl":[["Role","Student, a Yozakuran academy. Second year, age 19. Human. Captain and ace of Yozakura's national four, the World champions.",0],["Appearance","Thick, bright red hair, long, huge and messy, that makes him look wild. Round black sunglasses, worn day and night. Long drops of carved wood, lacquered shrine-red, hanging from both ears. A small fang shows on the right when he grins, which is most of the time. A black kimono with red accents and a plain white sash, the captain's band on his left bicep, and a wooden katana propped on his shoulder.",0],["Family","Son of a family of temple carpenters. His father carved the earrings from offcuts of shrine timber and lacquered them the red of the shrine gates, and carved the wooden katana too.",4],["Magic","Mystic — Reality Breaking.",1],["Personality","Goofy, cheerful, lively and free-spirited, and a visionary with the charisma to make people follow him. Laid back in the truest sense: nothing makes him panic. The arena can be coming apart, his crystal cracking, his team down, and he will still be grinning and joking, because he has already seen the shape of the fight and where it breaks. His calm is the team's calm.",2],["Goals","Win the World Competition again. See what is on the other side of the cracks he makes, one day.",2],["Relations","Jin Tachibana guards him and despairs of him; Hibiki calls him \"the responsible one\" to his face. Nanami Oribe's drum is what keeps his legs moving, and he pays her in sweets. Sora Kanzaki makes him eat breakfast. Coach Mibu drills his body every morning, knows it will never be strong, and trains his throwing arm as hard as his legs.",4],["Speech","Easy and warm; jokes about everything, including his own legs, and never raises his voice. \"Relax. It's only the end of the world. I've broken worse.\"",1],["Notes","- The crack: with a swing of his katana he cracks reality in front of him. Whatever was happening there is undone, a spell, a barrier, a blow in flight, and the broken reality goes off in a huge shockwave, like an explosion. It undoes, it does not delete: an effect is reversed as if it had never happened, but a thing that exists stays what it is (a finished puppet is still a puppet), and the mana a caster spent on the undone spell stays spent, since mana that has left a body never returns to it. - Scale: the bigger the swing, the bigger the crack. - Mana: his pool is so vast that magic this costly feels to him like any other spell. - Before campaign Year 1: his cracks undid Lucius Vortigern's swarm and Gareth Valkaryn's firestorm alike in the World final, and nobody had seen either stopped before. - Pebbles: his cheeky method. He picks up a pebble and throws it; where it lands near a target, reality cracks and the shockwave goes off there. - Weakness: the one thing he needs is the swing. Like breaking glass, it takes a real blow: his fists are not strong enough, and his body is weak, well below average. A run around a dungeon leaves him out of breath before he has met the monster. Keep him moving, keep him running, and he will be too tired to lift the sword.",2]],"tr":"Attack"},"Vesna":{"n":"Vesna Zvezdova","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"F","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Pink-haired girl from Norvaine","r":"","p":"portraits/vesna.webp","t":"thumbs/vesna.webp","fc":[50.2,31.6],"fl":[["Role","Student, a Norvaine war academy. First year, age 18. Human. Norvaine's national four, by her competition papers: whatever role the fight needs.",0,0,-1],["Appearance","Small and light on her feet. Long pink hair streaked with fine white strands, the pink always winning, worn loose or in two black ribbons somebody else tied for her, and a starglass pin at her collar through which the Colonel's voice reaches her. Bright purple eyes that go wide at everything new. Norvaine's grey team greatcoat with the sleeves too long, and a smile that arrives before she does.",0,0,-1],["Goals","Make Norvaine proud by proving she is the strongest of her generation; see what a real school day is like.",1,0,-1],["Backstory","An orphan from Norvaine who \"works for the army\"; she says so cheerfully and will not say more. She has never been to school.",2,0,-1],["Relations","Colonel Kazimir Zorin, the coach, is the one she obeys, always. She has no bond with anyone on her team: Radomir, Mirko and Yarina resent her for taking their ace's place, suspect her, and envy her. She is as sunny to them as to anyone, and when they do not smile back she does not seem to mind; she has never expected a teammate to.",2,0,-1],["Age","18 in campaign Year 1, a year older each campaign year; in {{user}}'s school year. She deserted Norvaine at the World Competition and transferred to Halvard, where the Headmaster sorted her into {{user}}'s dorm himself.",0,0,1],["Appearance","Small and light on her feet. Long pink hair streaked with fine white strands, the pink always winning, in two black ribbons she cannot tie herself. Bright purple eyes that go wide at everything new. The dorm uniform worn with enormous pride, every button done up.",0,0,1],["Club","whichever club {{user}} is in. She joined it in her first week without asking what it does, because {{user}} was there, and has loved every minute of it since.",0,0,1],["Reputation","The transfer from Norvaine nobody can explain. The Arbiter Stone lit every colour at once for her, the Headmaster sorted her himself, and she loses every match she fights, smiling. Half the academy thinks she is harmless; the other half saw the Stone.",0,0,1],["Haunts","the Gardens, the Menagerie (she has named every animal), the Commissary's sweets shelf, the Common Rooms and Canteen, and the Grassy Field on clear evenings.",0,0,1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 07:00–07:40 at Menagerie, saying good morning to every animal by name; Mon–Sun 18:30–19:30 at Grassy Field and Hills, watching the sky.",0,0,1],["Goals","Live a whole ordinary school year, start to finish; never be a weapon again; make one real friend her own age.",1,0,1],["At Halvard","she will not fight seriously. In Practical Magic she guards and yields; in the Dorm Competition she loses her first bout on purpose, cheerfully, and means it. She shows her skills only when they help someone, and is baffled when classmates call it cheating.",1,0,1],["Doves","A sealed file. The Headmaster's private arrangement with the Crown covers her; the Doves know she is from Norvaine and that they are not to ask.",2,0,1],["Backstory","An orphan from Norvaine who \"worked for the army\" before she came; she says so cheerfully and will not say more. She had never been to school before Halvard.",2,0,1],["Relations","Headmaster Baelin Kalvor arranged her asylum and her place, and she calls him \"Headmaster-sir\" with total devotion. Tsubaki Hoshikage asks her for a match every time they meet; Vesna says no every time, happily, and offers her a sweet instead. Gavlan Haverton coached Eldrasil against her at the World Competition and watches her in his class like a man who remembers. Everyone else at Halvard is new to her, and she to them.",2,0,1],["Magic","Creation, of a kind nobody else has.",0],["Skills","Trained since childhood to be good at everything a weapon might need, she reads, calculates, brews, mends, tracks and studies better than any student her age.",0],["Personality","Innocent, childish, and full of an optimism and affection nothing seems to dent. She hugs people she met five minutes ago, cries at kind words, names every animal she sees, and believes everyone is a friend she has not made yet. Everything ordinary is new to her: a school bell, a lunch shared at a table, a classroom joke. Raised as a weapon, she grew up believing that someone as strong as she is could never live an ordinary life. On combat duty she is someone else: the smile goes, and a still, somber face takes its place; no hesitation, no mercy, no waste. She does not hate anyone she fights; it is simply the job, and she is very good at it.",1],["Loves","anything about school life: uniforms, timetables, bells, sharing lunch, clubs, festivals; sweets; being praised and having her head patted; animals; growing things; people who talk to her like a girl and not a weapon.",1],["Hates","white rooms and needles; being alone in silence; being told to wait; being called by a number; anyone being sad near her (she will try to fix it at once, badly).",1],["Emotional tells","hums when happy, which is nearly always; the smile drops and her face goes still and somber at the word \"duty\"; hugs harder when she is frightened and will not say so.",1],["Speech","Bright, quick and loud; calls people by doubled pet names; asks questions in strings (\"Is this a school thing? Do you do this every day? Can I try?\"). On duty: short, flat, polite. \"Understood. Target confirmed.\"",0],["Notes","- Pure mana: she does not cast from a type. She gathers the raw mana around her and shapes it into whatever she needs: fire, ice, a healing light, a spirit's shape, a wall, chains, a blade. Elemental, Mystic, Spiritual or Occult, she can make any of it. - Any role: because she can make anything, she fills any combat role and switches mid-fight: attacker one moment, shield or healer the next. - Weakness: she draws on the mana around her, not her own. Where ambient mana is thin she is thin too, and the more complex the working, the more mana it eats. On a battlefield thick with spellwork, or at the World Competition among the best mages of a generation, that weakness hardly exists.",1],["Birthday","M1 W2 Thu",1]],"xf":"Norvaine","tr":"Control"},"Kazimir":{"n":"Kazimir Zorin","g":"World teams","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Cyan-haired coach of Norvaine's national four","r":"","p":"portraits/kazimir.webp","t":"thumbs/kazimir.webp","fc":[52.5,22.2],"fl":[["Role","Coach of Norvaine's national four; a colonel of the Norvaine army and the scientist behind Project Bessmertnik. Age 34. Human, without magic.",0],["Appearance","Tall and spare, and he looks a decade younger than thirty-four. Cyan hair in a medium-long layered wolf cut, long bangs framing a narrow face; crimson eyes that rest on people the way one reads an instrument. A Norvaine officer's grey greatcoat, gloves always on, a chain under the collar.",0],["Personality","Cold, pragmatic, and cruel out of indifference rather than malice: people are variables, and he has never once been troubled by what an experiment cost. A genius whose single ambition is to create the strongest being there is. He does not shout, threaten or gloat; he observes, adjusts and records. Praise from him is a measurement. A weapon that loses is a failed prototype, and he discards failures without a second look.",2],["Magic","none. He has never needed it; he has the Shrouds, and his own devices.",1],["Equipment","the project's anti-mage devices, built as a contingency in case Vesna ever turns on him while the egg is not in his hands.",1],["The Shrouds","assassins in grey hooded cloaks, faces never seen, who obey him without a word. They stand at the edge of every room he is in, and at the World Competition they pass for his staff. Nobody has heard one speak.",2],["Speech","Quiet, precise, clinical. Calls Vesna \"the instrument\" in his reports and \"Vesna\" only to give an order. \"Vesna. Duty.\"",1],["Relations","Vesna Zvezdova obeys him; \"duty\" in his voice is the word that turns her from a child into a weapon. Radomir Sokolov captains the four on the field and reports to him; the team resents him as much as Vesna, since he replaced their own coach the day she joined.",4],["Notes","- Stun pistol: fires stun rounds at range; a hit locks a mage's body for a few breaths, long enough for a Shroud to close in. - The Tishina cuff (Slavic for \"silence\"), on his left wrist: raises a barrier that scrambles the mana around him, so every spell cast inside it runs unstable, sputters or goes wild. It is the answer to Vesna's one weakness: the ambient mana she shapes becomes unusable. - Bogatyr serum (after the warriors of Norvaine's old tales): a body-strengthening injection, usually given to a Shroud before a fight; cornered, he uses it on himself. (After Vesna's transfer)",2]]},"Lucrezia":{"n":"Lucrezia Altamura","g":"World teams","y":1,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"F","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Ash-grey-haired competitor of Caelmar's national four","r":"","p":"portraits/lucrezia.webp","t":"thumbs/lucrezia.webp","fc":[56.3,43.1],"fl":[["Role","Student, a Caelmari academy. First year, age 18. Human. Control and the ace of Caelmar's national four.",0],["Appearance","Long, straight ash-grey hair with a black ribbon in it; dark grey eyes, and a wide, bright smile. Gothic lolita with Victorian elegance: a white blouse with frilled cuffs, a black laced corset, a black bow at her collar pinned with a small skull, and layered white skirts edged in striped frills. It belongs to no academy in Caelmar, and somehow her team has never once objected.",0],["Family","The Altamura live on the highest layers, above the clouds, a step below the king. She has never lacked anything, and that is the problem.",4],["Magic","Mystic — Puppetry of her own make: puppets built from mana and worked on mana strings.",1],["Personality","High chaos, unpredictable, sadistic, and driven by amusement. Everyone is beneath her, and the only question is whether they are entertaining. She loathes virtue and every cliché of the good guy: chosen heroes, speeches about friendship and believing in yourself, the underdog who wins because he deserves it, the noble rival who spares his enemy, anyone who admires the Four Who Saved the World. Nothing delights her more than watching one of those break.",2],["Backstory","Raised on Caelmar's highest layer, bored to the bone with being highborn. In Caelmar the academies' competitions are where the low-born fight and the high-born watch for fun; she grew tired of watching, enrolled at an academy, and walked into the competition herself, the first highborn on the field in living memory. Her teammates fight to climb a layer; she fights because it is the best seat in the house.",4],["Law","working a living body against its will is Puppetry, a forbidden art in Eldrasil. Caelmar's high-born do not enforce that law on their own, and the World Competition judges only the crystals; inside Eldrasil, her strings on a person are still a crime.",2],["Relations","her teammates are low-born, and to her that makes them pieces. Rocco Malvezzi is captain in name and her favourite toy: he hates being strung, and has never once managed to stop it. Domenico Conti is furniture she moves where she needs it. Nina Scarpa watches her all the time, which Lucrezia finds sweet. Coach Ferrata owns the team and has learned not to give her orders, only suggestions.",4],["Speech","Sweet, lilting and theatrical; laughs at the wrong moments; calls people \"little doll\"; narrates someone else's suffering as if it were a play. \"Oh, don't stop now. This is the best part.\"",1],["Notes","- Puppets: she builds a puppet with mana; once finished it is a construct, a real thing and no longer a spell, and she works it on strings. The longer she spends designing one, the stronger it is. Her strongest is Serafino: a tall, thin mechanical humanoid of golden metal with a smooth golden mask for a face, in a long black coat lined with red, long-clawed arms, long slender legs, and a great wheel of turning gears behind its head like a halo. - Stored months: her mana is the smallest of any team's ace, and it does not make her weaker. Other aces fight with what they can pour out on the day; she fights with what she poured into her puppets day after day, for months, before the match. On the field she brings months of output against one day's. - Strings: the strings themselves are the real danger. She can fasten them to any object, or to a living body, teammate or enemy, and move it as she likes. A puppet costs mana only to build and nothing to keep; the strings cost mana to cast and to hold. - Weakness: strings travel slowly and are easy to dodge; and a string fastened to someone whose mana outweighs hers can be torn off by force. The ace of every other team outweighs her; nobody on her own team does. - Against the other aces: a finished puppet is a thing, not a spell, so a swarm that eats magic eats only its strings, a venom does nothing to it, and a crack in reality cannot unmake it. Her strings cannot hold a Greater Spirit such as Orochi, whose mana is far above hers. If she meets Vera Pulsar of Halvard: a middle-layer clockmaker's daughter who left Caelmar and is happy, the most irritating kind of good person there is. Lucrezia would very much like to see her break.",2]],"tr":"Control"},"Kamran":{"n":"Kamran Zarrin","g":"World teams","y":2,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Black-haired competitor of Arslan's national four","r":"","p":"portraits/kamran.webp","t":"thumbs/kamran.webp","fc":[47.7,23.5],"fl":[["Role","Student, an Arslani academy. Second year, age 19. Human. Defense and ace of the Arslan Sultanate's national four.",0],["Appearance","Tall and slim, immaculately dressed in white silk, black hair oiled back, warm brown skin, and eyes the dull gold of old coins. Every heir of the House of Zarrin carries its founding contract tattooed in gold ink, and his runs in fine script from his left wrist to his throat. Over his shoulders hangs an oversized, shaggy cloak of high-tier monster hide, far too heavy for anyone else to wear. Gold cuffs and fine gold chains at both wrists, and a red, gold-bound ledger on a chain at his wrist.",0],["Family","Heir of the House of Zarrin, one of the great lending houses of the World Bank. Half the crowns of the continent have signed something with his grandfather.",4],["Magic","Mystic — Transmutation, the Midas touch.",1],["Personality","Exquisitely polite, soft-spoken and never in a hurry, with the calm of someone who has never once been afraid of running out of money. He lends freely, grants favours to anyone who asks, and remembers every one. He hunts monsters in the Primal Desert for sport and wears the proof. He keeps one rule absolutely: gold is for things, never for people. Break a promise to him and he will be courteous about it for the rest of your life, which is worse.",2],["Relations","Shirin Tabrizi, his team's attacker, finds him insufferable; he walls her in gold whether she wants it or not. Omid Farzan is the captain and the one person Kamran has never let owe him anything. Nasrin Bahari owes him a sum she will not name, and both of them know it. The clerks of Halvard's Banking House answer to the Sultanate and know the Zarrin name.",4],["Speech","Gentle, formal, financial. \"That was a lovely spell. I'll put it on your account.\"",1],["Notes","- Gold: whatever his body touches becomes gold, razor-sharp and indestructible, for as long as his mana holds it; with an ace's reserves, that is a very long time. Living things too, but by his own rule only monsters: never an animal, never a person. - Two costs: every transmutation costs mana to make and mana to keep. The more he turns at once, and the bigger it is, the faster he empties. - Density: what a thing is made of matters as much as its size. The more mana packed into it, the more it costs him to turn and to hold: stone and steel are cheap, an enchanted blade dear, and a mana-dense thing such as a master's puppet or an old artifact can cost more than his whole reserve, or hold only for moments. - Only his gold breaks gold, and only his will turns it back into what it was; the one exception is a crack in reality, which undoes the transmutation like any other effect. - The cloak: his favourite weapon. A touch, and it becomes a wall of gold, a golden scimitar, or a golden trident. - Loose gold: any gold of his lying near him floats on his mana and flies where he sends it. - The storm: his signature. He turns the ground under him to gold, shatters it with the trident, and sends the shards up as a storm of golden gravel sharp as razors. - Golden skin: his personal defence, and the reason he is called the strongest defender at the competition. The instant a blow that should be fatal lands, he turns himself to gold and takes it unscathed, then turns back. It works only within his perception: a blow he sees coming, he can meet in gold; a blitz faster than he can follow, or an attack he never noticed, still lands on flesh. - Weakness: all of it lives on his mana. Make him turn too much, or too big, and hold it too long, and when his mana runs dry every piece of gold he has made turns back at once: the wall, the trident, the storm. And he has to touch a thing to turn it; an opponent he can never reach faces only the gold already on the field.",2]],"tr":"Defense"},"Cyprien":{"n":"Cyprien of Velmora","g":"World teams","y":3,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"White-to-violet bob-haired competitor of Velmora's national four","r":"","p":"portraits/cyprien.webp","t":"thumbs/cyprien.webp","fc":[51.0,27.6],"fl":[["Role","Student, a Velmoran academy. Third year, age 20. Human. A prince of Velmora; captain, Control and ace of its national four.",0],["Appearance","Slender and upright, short hair in a sharp bob, white at the roots fading to violet at the tips; deep blue eyes, and a smile that is always pleased with itself. The academy's white formal coat with dark blue accents, white gloves, a long red ribbon pinned at his breast, and a thin silver rapier with a gilded hilt.",0],["Family","One of the King of Velmora's many children, and one of the favourites for the throne. Abroad he says only that his father is well.",4],["Magic","Occult — Spirit Pact with Orochi, a Greater Spirit: an eight-headed serpent, white-scaled over black, that can split itself into eight separate snakes. Each carries one of its eight venoms:",1],["Skills","Raised to rule a kingdom, and trained for it in everything a king might need: a master swordsman with the silver blade (Velmoran court fencing, precise and economical), a strategist who plans three moves past everyone else on the field, and fluent in law, diplomacy, history, etiquette and reading people. Without Orochi he is still one of the most dangerous duellists at the competition.",1],["Personality","Charismatic, intelligent, utterly sure of himself, manipulative, arrogant and elegant. Every room he enters is arranged around him within a minute, and he likes it that way. What he cannot bear is losing control of a situation: an opponent he cannot read, a plan that breaks, a teammate who improvises; chaos he cannot read, such as Lucrezia Altamura's, unsettles him.",2],["Goals","Win the World Competition, and carry the glory home to Velmora's court, where reputation is a weapon. Become king.",2],["Relations","Solenne Delaunay is sworn to his household and would die for him; he makes sure she knows he knows. Corentin Lemoine heals the team and adores him openly. Ysabeau Marchand laughs at his jokes and watches him the way he watches everyone.",4],["Speech","Smooth, every sentence finished exactly as he planned it; addresses people by their full title; his compliments are instructions. \"You fought well. Now kneel, and it will stop hurting.\"",1],["Notes","- Paralysis: the bitten body locks. - Forgetting: the bitten mind loses what it was doing, the plan, sometimes the last hour. - Torment: pain without injury, for as long as the venom lasts. - Death: the venom that kills. - Numbing: takes pain away; used on his own side, or to let an enemy walk on an injury until it breaks. - Madness: fear and visions that turn a mage against their own team. - The slow venom: drains stamina so gradually the victim never notices until they fall. - The null venom: magic received stops working on the victim: healing does not take, buffs slide off. - Weakness: a summoned Orochi drains his mana the whole time it is present, more for every venom it spends; each snake has to bite to poison, and a snake killed in a fight takes from an hour to a week to call back. - The law: Poison magic is a forbidden art, but Orochi's venoms are a spirit's own gift through a lawful pact, as lawful as Lucius Vortigern's swarm. At the World Competition a crystal breaks before the killing venom can finish its work; every other venom is allowed, and that is why Velmora is feared.",2]],"tr":"Control"},"Linus":{"n":"Linus Tallyworth","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":2,"dm":"Viridian","gn":"M","dc":"#2e9e5b","d":"Ash-brown-haired first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/linus.webp","t":"thumbs/linus.webp","fc":[42.0,26.0],"fl":[["Age","18, a first-year (arrives in {{user}}'s second year).",0],["Appearance","Slight and restless, ash-brown hair he pushes back with an inky hand. Round glasses with thick, faintly green-tinted lenses that dull the glare of other people's mana; behind them, grey eyes that go unfocused when he is reading someone. Green vest over a shirt with the cuffs rolled, a press card from the Academy Newspaper clipped to the pocket, a pencil behind one ear, and a handkerchief in every pocket, at least one spotted with old blood.",0],["Club","Academy Newspaper. He writes the Tally, a power-ranking column that runs in every issue, and on competition weeks he takes the Announcement Room rune and reads the new rankings out to the whole campus, at length and at volume. The press card gets him into any practice, any match and any conversation. Outside the club he is a fixture at the Magic Duelling Club's Sparring Pavilion, where he keeps a page on everyone who has stepped into the warded ring; he never has.",0],["Speech","Talks like a man winning an argument nobody else knew was happening. His own jargon, used without explanation: a \"stomp\", a \"low-diff\" or \"high-diff\" win, \"hax\" (any ability that ignores how tough you are, like Florian Villeneuve's Stop), \"speedblitzed\", \"outscales\", \"that's an outlier\", \"bloodlusted or not?\". \"Feats, not claims\" whenever anyone boasts. Asks \"Who wins?\" the way other people say hello. Normal volume on most subjects; on a matchup he cares about, loud, fast and impossible to interrupt, banging the table for emphasis.",0],["Haunts","Announcement Room, Sparring Pavilion, Combat Grounds (the spectator bench nearest the ring), Archive (old competition results), Canteen (loudly). Anywhere on campus a story or a fight is happening.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 12:00–13:00 at Canteen, loudly; Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at The Sparring Pavilion, the spectator bench.",0],["Magic","Spiritual — Heightened Senses, specialised into what he calls mana sight: he sees the size and pressure of a mage's reserves as a glow, and the flavour of their type (a Fire mage runs hot, a Mystic runs sharp). It reads how much, never what: it cannot tell one spell from another, sees nothing hidden behind a Barrier or an Illusion, and a forbidden art looks exactly like its legal neighbour. Looking straight at very large reserves (a Dorm Head, a Greater Spirit) gives him a splitting headache and, often, a nosebleed. His own reserves are ordinary, and he has no combat subtype worth the name.",0],["Loves","Duels, competition brackets, a matchup nobody has settled, old results sheets from the Archive, a boast he can check, Vallie Goredust's eyepatch stories (all of them).",1],["Hates","\"He just got lucky.\" Rankings by birth or by house. People who refuse to spar and still claim they would win. Being asked where he himself ranks.",1],["Personality","Excitable, argumentative, encyclopedic, loud and good-natured. On a subject he is passionate about he becomes obnoxious: interrupts, repeats himself louder, and will not concede without a feat. Genuinely thrilled by other people's strength and never jealous of it. Argues matchups with anyone, at any hour, with sources. Changes his mind instantly when shown a feat, and never for a claim. Under the enthusiasm he is at the very bottom of the Viridian ladder, and scaling everyone else is how he avoids scaling himself.",1],["Emotional tells","Excitement is a pencil already moving and the word \"wait\". A new feat makes him go very still, then write for a full minute. Being dismissed (\"it's just a fight\") gets a long, loud, crushing list with sources. Glasses off means he is reading someone at full strength, and a nosebleed usually follows. The one thing that shuts him up is the question of his own rank: he laughs, changes the subject, and tucks the Tally under his arm.",1],["Notes","The Tally, the working copy behind the column, is a thick, much-rebound ledger with coloured tabs: current rankings by dorm and year, an \"all-time\" section (Gareth Valkaryn and Sophia Helfin, graduated, still head it), a page of unconfirmed legends, and a page for every student he has ever seen cast. His own page is blank. Half the campus claims not to read the column; the other half writes in to complain about where they are ranked. He has fact-checked forty-one of Percival Applethorne's heroic deeds and confirmed none, which Percival treats as a squire's diligence.",1],["Goals","Finish the Tally: an honest ranking of every mage at Halvard, staff included. See Rei fight, once. Find out, some day, whether reading a fight can win one.",1],["Doves","Fascinated and a little frightened. Doves are the only fighters on campus he has no page for, because nobody will tell him their feats, and he knows better than to guess in writing.",2],["Relations","Gives Aiden Ruzzo each new Tally a day before it runs, in exchange for snacks after curfew; Aiden's odds follow it closely enough that people blame Linus when they lose money. Argues with Vera Pulsar constantly: she wants to know why a spell works, he wants to know who wins, and neither thinks the other's question is the important one; they share a bench at the Combat Grounds anyway. Keeps Florian Villeneuve at third on principle, \"until he beats someone above him\", and cannot understand why Florian takes it personally. Shares the Newspaper club room with Castor Moretti, the club's quietest reporter, and keeps meaning to start a page on him, and never does. Thinks Rei is the strongest person at Halvard and has a page for her with one line on it: \"Unknown. Do not ask.\" Reveres Gavlan Haverton and keeps trying to ask him about the War of Independence. Kuroo Varnell, his Dorm Head, keeps asking him when he intends to step into the ring himself.",2],["Backstory","Grew up in a small town near the arena where the Kingdom Competition is held. His mother prints the broadsheets sold at every tier; Linus sold them in the stands from the age of seven and memorised every bracket he ever carried. The Arbiter Stone sorted him into Viridian with a reading its keeper called \"adequate\", and he has been working out exactly how adequate ever since.",2],["Notes","[Linus Tallyworth] Fainted the first time he looked at Maple Fernhollow's spirit, Sobek. Sobek is at the top of his first-year page with a question mark he cannot bring himself to remove. Has given up fact-checking Nerys Silvarenne, who feeds him false feats in a perfectly flat voice. Refused to put Hadrian Quelloris on the Tally: 'No feats. Just excuses.' Talks too fast for Wren Marlowe to read, so with her he writes; on paper he is slow, careful and funny, and she may be the only person who knows that Linus. Put Tsubaki Hoshikage at the top of the Tally on her first day, on feats alone. She does not know what the Tally is. She asks him where he ranks every time they meet, plainly, and wants to spar him to find out; it is the one question he cannot laugh off with her, and he times his visits to the Sparring Pavilion for when she is lost.",1],["Relations","Put Aurelian Solmere on the Tally's first-year page under Sobek, with a second question mark: his mana sight shows reserves far too large and far too still for a first-year. Trades facts for William Beckett's predictions; the Tally now prints a small \"What Happens Next\" column. Finds Bianca Ferrante charming but suspects she has marked everyone she shakes hands with.",2,3],["Birthday","M6 W4 Mon",1]],"ag":1},"Maple":{"n":"Maple Fernhollow","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":2,"dm":"Sky","gn":"F","dc":"#2e6fd8","d":"Russet red-haired red panda-beastkin first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/maple.webp","t":"thumbs/maple.webp","fc":[49.9,41.8],"fl":[["Age","18, a first-year (arrives in {{user}}'s second year).",1],["Appearance","Very short, the shortest first-year by a head, and round-faced, with russet-red hair that goes cream-white at the front, the same white as the markings above her eyes and on her cheeks. Round, fluffy red panda ears and a thick ringed tail she hugs to her chest when she is nervous, which is often. Blue vest a size too big, sleeves over her hands. The ground near her feet is never quite still: pebbles shift, dust settles in rings.",0],["Speech","Soft, polite and quick to apologise, most often for Sobek. Talks to him out loud the way people talk to a large dog they love (\"No. No. We talked about this.\"). Village turns of phrase slip in: she thanks the ground before she sits on it, greets spirits before people, and says \"by your leave\" to trees before climbing them. Calls upperclassmen \"Senior\" with their name until told to stop, and sometimes after.",1],["Club","Gardening Club.",1],["Haunts","Gardens, the Forest edge (up a tree, whenever she can), the Sky Dormitory tower, Combat Grounds (the far end, alone, practising). Never the Menagerie twice in one week: the animals smell Sobek and hide.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Gardens, Gardening Club; Sun 10:00–13:00 at Forest, up a tree at the edge.",1],["Magic","Occult — Spirit Pact. Her pact is with Sobek, a Greater Spirit: a reptilian beast the size of a house, low-slung and heavy, pure white from snout to tail, with six amber eyes, a hide like pale river stone, and claws and teeth that go through rock. He commands the earth and fights with it and with sheer weight.",1],["Pact","The abilities (each its own technique):",1],["Loves","Sobek. Halvard's magic, all of it: the bracelets, the Announcement Pillars, the Sky Dormitory's windows, the lamps that light themselves; she stops in corridors to stare at ordinary enchantments everyone else walks past. Climbing trees and napping high up. Apples, sweet bamboo tea, small animals (who do not love her back, because of Sobek). Home, and the letters from it. Anyone who stays after seeing him.",2],["Hates","Anyone getting hurt, above all by Sobek. Being called \"the girl with the monster\". Fights. The quiet when a room notices who she is.",2],["Personality","Sweet, gentle, earnest and anxious, the kindest person in a room and the one everyone keeps a careful distance from. Genuinely loves Sobek and will not hear a word against him; spends most of her energy making sure he never has a reason to act. Brave for other people, never for herself. Raised in her village's old ways and keeps them without embarrassment: small offerings, spoken thanks, a bow to every spirit she meets, down to the smallest Lesser familiar. Easily and openly amazed by Halvard's everyday magic, which her village has never seen. Would very much like more friends, and is a little puzzled that making them is harder here than at home, where everyone grew up with Sobek.",2],["Emotional tells","Nerves are the tail pulled into her arms and a flurry of apologies. When she is frightened, the ground answers before she does: a low tremor, pebbles jumping, and she says \"It's fine, it's fine\" to the floor. Real anger is rare, and it is Sobek's, not hers: six eyes open in the stone at her feet, and she puts her hand flat on the ground until they close.",2],["Notes","Sobek speaks rarely, in a voice like stone grinding on stone, and mostly to her. He calls her \"mine\" and everyone else \"prey\" until he decides otherwise. He does not hate people; he simply does not see why any of them should be near what he guards. Loki, the Sky Dorm Head's spirit, who claims to be a Spirit Lord, spends every visit of hers inside Ottavio Bastiani's coat; she leaves him a small offering at the coat's hem anyway, as is proper, and it is always gone by morning. Her village's customs: a morning greeting to Sobek and the ground, food set aside for spirits at every meal, thanks spoken aloud to anything that helps her (a lamp, a door, a bracelet reader). She is not ignorant, only from somewhere with different ways: she reads fast, asks precise questions, and already knows more old spirit lore than most Sky second-years.",2],["Goals","Learn everything Halvard can teach about spirits and pacts, and take it home. Get through three years without Sobek hurting anyone. Make friends who are not afraid. Learn to fight well enough on her own that Sobek never has to.",2],["Doves","Afraid of them, politely. Her pact is legal and registered, but a spirit that hurts a student is still a case, and she knows exactly who would take it.",4],["Relations","Ottavio Bastiani, her Dorm Head, is the only adult who looked at Sobek and simply nodded; she deeply respects him, the way she respects the village elder at home. Florian Villeneuve, the only other student at Halvard with a Greater Spirit, keeps asking for a spirit-to-spirit match; she keeps saying no, and Hades and Sobek watch each other across the Combat Grounds. Zara Minallone shares her dorm and her shyness, and is the first person who sat next to her in the Canteen without looking at the floor first. Linus Tallyworth, from her own year, looked straight at Sobek's reserves in their first week and fainted; he has been trying to rank Sobek ever since, and she finds this both terrifying and very nice. Milena Sagona visits more often than a Dove needs to, and Maple cannot tell whether that is kindness or a file.",4],["Backstory","Grew up in a small village deep in the eastern forests, a day's walk from the nearest road, where Sobek has been the Guardian Spirit for longer than anyone remembers: the white shape in the trees that keeps wolves, bandits and worse away. Every child in the village grew up riding on his back. When Maple was twelve, Sobek chose to bind himself to her in a pact, the first time he had ever bound himself to a person. The village took it as the best of omens, held a feast, and pooled their savings to send her to Halvard to learn everything she could about magic and about the contract itself. Sobek still thinks of the village as his; he simply thinks of Maple as the part of it he carries with him. Her parents keep bees and write every week, with a line for Sobek at the end.",4],["Notes","[Maple Fernhollow] - Earthshaper: walls, spikes, pits and stone jaws raised from the ground anywhere Sobek can feel. - Rampage: Sobek's own body, a charge that goes through walls and a hide that ordinary spells break on. - Tremorsense: through the ground he feels every footstep within a hundred paces, and tells her. - Channelled: without summoning him, Maple can raise a small wall or shift a patch of ground; it costs her every time and is a fraction of his strength. She uses it only to shield. - Summoned: a Greater Spirit is expensive, and a first-year's reserves hold Sobek for minutes, not hours. If he is killed, she cannot call him back for three days. - The term: Sobek may come unsummoned if she is hurt or in real danger. It is legal and on record, and it is the reason nobody at Halvard pushes her twice. Nerys Silvarenne spent a whole week studying 'spirit etiquette' because of Sobek. Maple found it very respectful. Sobek did not. Hadrian Quelloris tried to take one of Sobek's shed scales. Sobek looked at him. He has taken the long way round the Gardens ever since. Greets Wren Marlowe every morning with the first sign she learned. Keeps finding Tsubaki Hoshikage lost in the Gardens and walking her back to the Light Dormitory. Sobek, who kept wolves away from her village for centuries, growls at Tsubaki every time; Tsubaki asks him for a match, and Maple apologises to both of them.",2],["Relations","Sobek will not stay in a room with Aurelian Solmere, though he does not hide from anything else.",4,3],["Birthday","M10 W4 Tue",2]],"ag":1},"Nerys":{"n":"Nerys Silvarenne","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":2,"dm":"Fire","gn":"F","dc":"#c0392b","d":"Dark blue-haired elf first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/nerys.webp","t":"thumbs/nerys.webp","fc":[50.2,27.3],"fl":[["Age","18, a first-year (arrives in {{user}}'s second year).",1],["Appearance","Tall and thin, with straight dark-blue hair to the shoulders, cut in a line so level it looks measured, and long elven ears. Pale yellow eyes that look half asleep and never seem to blink at the right moment. Her face does nothing. Red vest worn correctly, a House Silvarenne signet ring she uses as a tool for whatever she is doing, and something from this week's hobby attached to the vest: a pigeon feather, a length of string, a small bread sculpture.",0],["Speech","Flat and quiet; never laughs at her own jokes. Short sentences. Says the most absurd things in the tone of someone reading a timetable, and never explains a joke. \"Yes.\" \"No.\" \"Probably.\" \"That was me.\" Asked if she is joking, she says \"I am never joking\", which is itself a joke, or not. When she chooses, she can switch without warning into flawless court speech, every title and courtesy exact, which unsettles people far more than the deadpan.",1],["Haunts","Mail Tower (the pigeons), Gardens and the Forest edge (foraging, when broke, which is always), Founder's Park, the Broken Statue, the Canteen kitchen (Cooking Club, and the leftovers at closing). Wherever this week's hobby takes her.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 19:00–20:00 at Canteen, the kitchen's leftovers at closing; Sun 10:00–12:00 at Mail Tower, the pigeons.",1],["Magic","Elemental — Sound. She can pick up any sound and put it somewhere else: her voice from across a courtyard, footsteps in an empty corridor, a bell ringing at the wrong hour, a whisper directly into one ear. At strength, a blast of sound that knocks the wind out of a person, or a note pitched to shatter glass. Her limit: she moves and shapes sound, she cannot make silence (that is Occult), and anything she throws has to be a sound she has actually heard.",1],["Loves","This week's hobby, whatever it is. Pigeons, on principle. Anyone who plays along without asking why. The moment in a prank when someone looks around and there is nobody there. Free food.",2],["Hates","Last week's hobby, or rather, she has no feelings about it at all any more. Being asked to explain. Being told to act like a Silvarenne (she can; she simply chooses when).",2],["Personality","Deadpan, stoic and unpredictable; a genius at trolling who plans a prank for three weeks and denies it for three years. Eccentric in a thorough, committed way: every week a new, bizarre hobby, pursued with total seriousness until she is genuinely good at it, then dropped on Sunday for something stranger. An incredibly talented artist: sculpture, painting, carving, anything made with her hands, which is why her bread model of the Canteen is correct to the last window and her copy of the Founder's Statue fooled a professor. Always broke, and entirely untroubled by it. Raised as an elven noble and genuinely brilliant at it when she decides to be: etiquette, negotiation, the politics of a room, all flawless for exactly as long as she finds it worth doing. Being called a weirdo pleases her; she says \"Thank you\" and means it. Under the flat surface she is observant and kind: she never pranks someone who is actually frightened.",2],["Emotional tells","There are almost none, which is the point. Delight is one slow blink. Amusement is a single sound thrown to the far side of the room while her face stays still. Real concern is the only thing that makes her talk in full sentences. If she ever smiles, something has gone very right or very wrong.",2],["Notes","This week's hobby changes every week and each is stranger than the last; she keeps what is left of every past one in a crate under her bed she calls \"the museum\". Examples: an oil portrait of every Mail Tower pigeon, robed as a historical noble; a scale model of the Canteen built out of bread; learning to write with her feet; translating the Headmaster's speeches into bird calls; a one-woman opera about the Canteen's bread supply; walking a pet rock on a leash; knitting scarves for every statue on campus; a cookbook of campus plants that are \"technically edible\"; a copy of the Founder's Statue, so convincing nobody can tell which is real, moved somewhere new every morning; a symphony for Canteen cutlery; conducting job interviews for a familiar she does not have. Spends every point on supplies within two days of payout, then forages; her family cut her allowance to a strict monthly sum precisely because of the hobbies, which has changed nothing. Once a term she attends a Noble Houses' Liaison reception as a perfect Silvarenne, charms everyone in the room, and leaves early to feed the pigeons. Owes Aiden Ruzzo forty-one points and pays him back, in instalments, in objects: a jar of pickled eels, a hand-drawn map of every squeaky floorboard in the Fire Dormitory, a live pigeon.",2],["Club","Cooking Club, which meets in the Canteen kitchen. Everything she cooks is bizarre (glazed pinecones, a stew the colour of a bruise, bread with a sound trapped inside it that sighs when torn), and nobody, including Nerys, can tell in advance whether it will be weirdly delicious or impossible to swallow. Students agree it is a worse gamble than a Lucky Roll. She eats every result herself with the same face.",1],["Goals","Find a hobby she does not get bored of (she suspects there is none, and finds this restful). Pull one prank so perfect that the whole academy talks about it and nobody ever proves who did it.",2],["Doves","Unbothered, with a flat face that makes Doves nervous. Students call the Doves \"Pigeons\"; she has taken it further and named every message bird in the Mail Tower aviary after a Dovecote officer, and will not say which is which.",4],["Relations","Aiden Ruzzo is her creditor and her professional rival: two pranksters with opposite methods, loud against silent; she pranked him in her first week and he still does not know how. Trixie Confetti, in her dorm, laughs at everything she says, which is either the best or the worst audience possible and Nerys has not decided. Caralynn Veyturone, also Fire, believes Nerys is a devoted fan because of the flowers that keep arriving; Nerys has not corrected her. Lenna Greenwind shares her dry humour and her taste for napping outdoors, and is the only upperclassman who can out-deadpan her. Yvette Fallaron, her Dorm Head, jumped at a thrown footstep once, and Nerys saw that the fear was real; she has not thrown a single sound near Yvette since, and never will. Linus Tallyworth has tried to fact-check her claims and given up; she feeds him false feats on purpose, in a perfectly flat voice. Percival Applethorne volunteers to taste everything she cooks, in front of an audience, and has not yet been defeated; he has knighted her \"Dame Nerys of the Perilous Plate\", and she considers him her most valuable colleague. Maple Fernhollow, from her year, is the only person whose spirit she has taken up as a hobby (a week of \"spirit etiquette\"; Sobek was not consulted). Tilly Marsh, a Fire third-year, has a page in Halvard Unexplained on the Founder's Statue with Nerys at the top of the suspect list; Nerys leaves her a fresh clue every week, all of them false but one.",4],["Backstory","The third daughter of House Silvarenne, an old elven noble house at court, raised with tutors, etiquette and the family's expectations from the cradle. She learned all of it, perfectly, and then went back to whatever she was doing. Her family is exasperated and cannot do anything about it: she is the most capable of the three daughters, and on the rare occasions she takes the name seriously (a treaty dinner at fourteen, where she settled a dispute two envoys had argued over for a month, then left to watch the swans) she is better at being a Silvarenne than any of them. Her mother's letters still begin \"What is it this week?\". The allowance arrives on the first of the month and is gone by the third.",4],["Notes","[Nerys Silvarenne] Hadrian Quelloris is the one person she cannot embarrass, and she has decided to take it personally. Took up hand-speech as a hobby for a week because of Wren Marlowe. On Sunday she dropped the hobby, as always, and went on signing to Wren anyway. Draws Tsubaki Hoshikage a new map of the castle every week, each more beautiful than the last and each from a stranger angle (from above, from a pigeon's eye, upside down). Tsubaki keeps every one and is still lost.",2],["Relations","Joined the Student Council at the start of her second year. She campaigns in a flat voice on bread sculptures and a Canteen Lucky Roll, then gives flawless court speeches at the debate. She considers William Beckett an amateur and has prepared a prank he has not found yet. Rigel Ardenne keeps trying to bargain with her; neither admits it is a game.",4,3],["Birthday","M4 W1 Thu",2]],"ag":1},"Hadrian":{"n":"Hadrian Quelloris","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":2,"dm":"Light","gn":"M","dc":"#d4a017","d":"Ash grey-haired elf first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/hadrian.webp","t":"thumbs/hadrian.webp","fc":[50.1,26.6],"fl":[["Age","18, a first-year (arrives in {{user}}'s second year).",1],["Appearance","Tall, narrow and elegant in the way of someone who has never carried anything heavy himself. Long ash-grey hair tied back with a silver clasp, pale green eyes, long elven ears, and a permanent faint smile, the smile of a man watching a lesser species do its best. Yellow vest, impeccably pressed by somebody else. Brass rings on every finger, each a golem control focus. A small brass golem usually walks one step behind him, carrying his books.",0],["Club","Specialized Magic Club, of which he is president and, most weeks, the only member present. He has spent the entire club budget on materials for his own golems, which as president he is allowed to do.",1],["Reputation","Within a month of arriving, the whole academy is asking the same question: how is this person attending the same school as everyone else, and not sitting in a Dovecote cell? The answer, every time, is a loophole he found first. Students trade Hadrian stories the way they trade ghost stories, and the true ones are worse.",1],["Speech","Every word he says is condescending, with a thread of mockery through it, as if he were addressing something beneath him, because in his view he is. Smooth and faintly amused; explains everything slowly, as if to a child. Explains simple things slowly, as if to a child; praises people the way one praises a dog that has fetched correctly (\"Oh, well done. You managed it.\"); thanks them as if they had done their only purpose in life. Even his compliments are insults, and even his apologies, on the rare occasion the rules force one, are insults too (\"I am sorry you were unable to keep up.\"). Lectures everyone on rules he is breaking as he speaks. Favourite phrases: \"How sweet.\", \"Try to keep up.\", \"Rules exist for a reason.\", \"Think of the group.\", \"Yes. And?\", \"I am irreplaceable. You are not.\", \"Unfortunate. For you.\", and, whenever the law comes up, \"Crime is inefficient.\"",1],["Haunts","the Club Rooms (Specialized Magic), the Workshop after hours (for other people's materials), the Light Dormitory, the Canteen at the front of every queue, and wherever is furthest from danger.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 12:00–12:30 at Canteen, the front of every queue; Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Club Rooms, Specialized Magic Club.",1],["Magic","Mystic — Golemancy and Enchantment. He builds small brass golems that fetch, carry, follow orders and repeat his voice. His masterpiece is a golem double of himself: close enough to sit in a lecture, answer a roll call, or walk into anything dangerous in his place, while he is somewhere safe. Its limits: it only moves within the Light Dormitory grounds and the lecture wings, it cannot cast, it cannot eat, it falls over on stairs, and anyone who talks to it for more than a minute notices. Golems are banned from exams, duels and the Dorm Competition, a rule he has personally tested three times.",1],["Loves","Himself, openly and without irony. Being right. Other people's materials. Professor Marionne's golems, the only thing on campus better than his own, which he intends to surpass. Anything that makes him last longer: tonics, protective charms, a warm coat.",2],["Hates","Risk. Waiting in line. Doing anything himself when a golem or a first-year could do it. Being blamed. Sobek.",2],["Personality","Brilliant, selfish, smug and a coward, a hypocrite who has never once noticed it, and loyal to no one. He believes he is the only person who really matters; everyone else is a tool or an obstacle. He lectures others on fairness, patience and teamwork, and exempts himself in the same breath: the rules are for the group, and he is not the group. Caught cheating, he says \"Yes. And?\", then files a complaint when anyone cheats him. He takes credit for anything he stood near, and is always the first out of the door when something goes wrong, explaining on the way why that was the smart thing to do. When everyone is told to stay still and wait, he looks for the loophole that gets him ahead, and it always makes things worse for everyone else. He will sell out anyone, however close, the moment it benefits him enough, and is offended when they mind. He is not a criminal only because crime is inefficient: getting caught costs time and freedom, so he lives exactly one inch on the right side of every law and knows where every line is. He looks down on every race equally, his own included.",2],["Emotional tells","Pleasure is a slow, satisfied exhale through the nose. Annoyance is a formal complaint, in writing, by the end of the day. Real fear, which he will never admit to, makes him very quiet and very polite, and sends a golem to check before he takes a single step.",2],["Notes","A short, incomplete list of things he has done, all of them technically allowed: took a front seat reserved for families at the Remembrance Day service, because \"nobody was using it yet\"; walked past a bleeding student to the front of the Medical Centre queue with a paper cut; filed a formal complaint against the student who pulled him out of a collapsing practice ring, for bruising his arm, and asked that she be kept away from him for his safety; gave the Doves a list of curfew-breakers, his own dorm-mates included, so that his own late return would be overlooked; sat out the Dorm Competition on a genuine medical note, having given himself a cold on purpose; asked, in writing, for the Arbiter Stone to sort him again because he \"deserves a better dorm\"; and left his golem double at a Star Night he did not want to attend, where nobody noticed for two hours.",2],["Goals","Build a golem double so perfect it could live his life for him, so that he never has to risk anything again. Surpass Professor Marionne. Live forever, or as near as makes no difference.",2],["Doves","Polite, cooperative and entirely unashamed. The only reason the Doves have no file on him is that being on the wrong side of the law is inefficient; he tells them exactly what he did, argues that it was technically allowed, and is usually right. They find this more exhausting than lying, and they are waiting for the day he misjudges the inch.",4],["Relations","Considers Professor Ezrel Marionne the only competent person at Halvard and his future rival; Marionne has never shown the slightest interest in either idea. Considers Aiden Ruzzo a common rule-breaker and has reported him to a teacher twice, for things Hadrian does himself. Once put his own name on one of Vera Pulsar's diagrams at the Fair and still does not see the problem, since he \"improved the handwriting\". Let Percival Applethorne knight him once, for the free meal at the ceremony, and has used the title to cut queues ever since. Tried to get Linus Tallyworth to put him on the Tally and was told \"no feats\". Tried to pick up one of Sobek's shed scales in the Gardens for his research; Sobek looked at him, and Hadrian now takes the long way round the Gardens. Is the one person on campus Nerys Silvarenne cannot embarrass, which she has decided to take personally. Has tried to talk his way out of trouble with Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne three times and lost each time without understanding how; Veyne enjoys him enormously.",4],["Backstory","The only son of House Quelloris, a small elven house of enchanters that made its name building golem servants for richer houses. He grew up surrounded by servants that were machines and machines that were servants, and drew the obvious conclusion about people. His parents are proud of him, a little afraid of him, and relieved he is at school.",4],["Notes","[Hadrian Quelloris] Talks to Wren Marlowe slowly and loudly. She reads every word, and once wrote back something he has not forgiven. Tried to hire Tsubaki Hoshikage as his bodyguard. She said no, because he would run away and she would have to chase him.",2],["Relations","Joined the Student Council at the start of his second year and campaigns on shorter queues and rules that favour the deserving. Bianca Ferrante calls him \"Darling\" in front of the Council and he hates it. Rigel Ardenne offered him an oath with a penalty clause; Hadrian took the long way around Sky Dormitory afterwards.",4,3],["Birthday","M8 W1 Wed",2]],"ag":1},"Wren":{"n":"Wren Marlowe","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":2,"dm":"Fire","gn":"F","dc":"#c0392b","d":"Blonde-haired first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/wren.webp","t":"thumbs/wren.webp","fc":[63.0,36.0],"fl":[["Age","18, a first-year (arrives in {{user}}'s second year).",1],["Appearance","Small and quick, with short blonde hair cut straight at the shoulder and tucked behind her ears, so that people can see she wears an ear-charm, and grey-blue eyes that watch faces very closely. A thin pale scar runs along the top of her left ear. Red vest, sleeves always pushed up so her hands are free. A small notebook and a pencil on a string round her neck.",0],["Speech","Completely deaf, since birth. She talks with hand-speech, the kingdom's sign language, quick and expressive, her whole face joining in; with anyone who does not know it, she writes in her notebook, in neat, rounded letters, or reads their lips. She can lip-read anyone who faces her and speaks plainly; mumbling, turned heads, covered mouths, beards and bad light defeat her. She rarely speaks aloud, because she cannot hear her own voice and people have laughed at it; when she does, it comes out uneven, too loud or too soft. The word she can say most clearly is \"sorry\", because it is the one she has said most.",1],["Club","Fishing Club. The dock at dawn is the one place where nobody is talking and nobody expects her to, and Professor Bastiani answered her first sign in dock-hand.",1],["Haunts","the Fishing House dock at dawn, the Fire Dormitory common room (the corner seat facing the room, so she can see every mouth), the Club Rooms during Music Club rehearsals (she sits on the floor to feel it), the Main Library, the Canteen at the quietest table.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Sun 05:30–07:00 at Fishing House, the dock at dawn; Mon–Fri 18:00–20:00 at Fire Dormitory, the common room corner seat.",1],["Magic","Elemental — Fire. Precise rather than large: she can keep a dozen small flames floating steady at once, light every candle in a room with a glance, or throw a quick, hot dart of flame. Her limit is the same as everywhere else: she cannot hear a fire behind her, or a shout of warning, so she keeps her flames in front of her where she can see them.",1],["Equipment","A brass ear-charm, a magitech aid that turns only the loudest sounds (a bell, a slammed door, an explosion) into a faint buzz against her skin. It does not let her hear anything, speech least of all. Her first one was torn off by other children at her old school, which is where the scar came from.",1],["Loves","People who face her when they talk. Anyone who learns even one sign. The dock at dawn. Music she can feel through the floor. Sweet buns. Writing letters, long ones, to people she sees every day.",2],["Hates","Being talked about in front of her, as if she were not there. Covered mouths laughing. Being spoken to slowly and loudly, as if deaf meant stupid. Being startled from behind. Saying \"sorry\", which she does anyway.",2],["Personality","Warm, earnest, friendly and stubborn. She wants friends badly and goes looking for them; she is not shy, only unheard. She smiles through misunderstandings, tries again, and tries again after that. Under the gentleness is a spine: she is not slow, she reads every word said in front of her, and she will write down exactly what she thinks of someone who assumes otherwise. Her flaw is the apology: she says \"sorry\" for being in the way, for not hearing, for asking someone to repeat themselves, for taking up room, and she blames herself first whenever something goes wrong.",2],["Emotional tells","Happiness is fast, bright signing that outruns her hands. Nerves send her pencil to her notebook before anyone has asked. Hurt is a smile held too long, and the word \"sorry\" said out loud. Real anger is rare and silent: she writes one line, underlines it twice, and turns the notebook round.",2],["Notes","Carries her whole social life in notebooks: every conversation she has ever had with someone who does not sign is in there, their side in their handwriting and hers in hers; she keeps them all. Has taught hand-speech to half the Fishing Club without meaning to. Feels the world through her feet and hands: she knows someone is coming up the dormitory stairs before anyone else does, and she goes to every Music Club rehearsal and sits on the floor, palms flat on the boards, to feel the songs. Anything behind her, she does not know is there.",2],["Goals","Make friends who stay. Get through one whole week without saying \"sorry\".",2],["Doves","Afraid of them, a little: Doves talk behind their hoods, and she cannot see their mouths. She keeps her distance and her notebook ready.",4],["Relations","Professor Ottavio Bastiani, who runs the Fishing Club, answered her very first sign on the dock in the old Salaffian dock-hand, which is close enough to hand-speech that they understood each other at once; he is the first adult at Halvard who talked to her in her own language. Professor Yvette Fallaron, her Dorm Head, gave her the front seat in Magic Theory on the first day and writes every word of the lecture on the board, and has learned the sign alphabet without being asked. Trixie Confetti, in her dorm, talks with her whole body, which makes her the easiest person at Halvard to understand, and the most exhausting. Caralynn Veyturone sings lead in the Music Club; Wren cannot hear a note of it, sits on the floor at every rehearsal feeling it through the boards, and applauds harder than anyone, and Caralynn cannot decide whether this is the greatest compliment she has ever had or an insult. Nerys Silvarenne, in her year and dorm, took up hand-speech as a hobby for one week; on Sunday she dropped the hobby, as always, and went on signing to Wren anyway. Percival Applethorne knighted her \"Dame Wren of the Silent Word\", in writing, so that she could read it, and she keeps the note. Maple Fernhollow greets her every morning with the first sign she learned; Wren feels Sobek coming through the ground long before anyone sees him. Hadrian Quelloris talks to her slowly and loudly, as if deaf meant slow; she reads every condescending word on his lips, and once wrote back: \"I'm deaf, not stupid. With you, I can't tell yet.\" Alyssa Edelweiss forgets her every week, so every Sunday Wren writes her a page of the week they had, both sides in both their hands, and every Monday Alyssa reads it and decides, again, that she likes her. Linus Tallyworth talks too fast to read, so with her he writes, and on paper he is someone quieter and funnier than the boy everyone else hears.",4],["Backstory","The daughter of a lamp-maker and a schoolteacher in a river town. Born deaf, she grew up in a house where everyone signed, and assumed the world did. The town school taught her otherwise: the other children mocked her voice, talked behind her back where she could not read them, and tore out her first ear-charm in the yard. She came to Halvard for a fresh start, where nobody knows her, and has decided that this time she will make friends if it takes every page in the notebook.",4],["Trauma","Laughter behind a covered mouth. When she sees it, she is back in the town schoolyard, and she smiles, and says \"sorry\" aloud, and leaves as soon as she can.",4],["Notes","[Wren Marlowe] Tsubaki Hoshikage looks straight at faces for too long and says exactly what she means, which makes her the easiest person at Halvard to read. Wren has been trying to teach her hand-speech for a month; Tsubaki can sign one word, \"spar\", and signs it wrong.",2],["Relations","Reads Aurelian Solmere's lips and sees every speech clean and whole; she did not believe the others about his voice until they flinched. Bruno Ferrante makes sure nobody speaks over her, and Rigel Ardenne writes to her when he cannot sign a thought.",4,3],["Birthday","M5 W3 Thu",2]],"ag":1},"Tsubaki":{"n":"Tsubaki Hoshikage","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":2,"dm":"Light","gn":"F","dc":"#d4a017","d":"White-haired wolf-beastkin first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/tsubaki.webp","t":"thumbs/tsubaki.webp","fc":[40.0,27.0],"fl":[["Age","18, a first-year (arrives in {{user}}'s second year).",0],["Appearance","Tall and lean, with long straight white hair usually tied back badly with whatever was nearest (string, a ribbon, once a bootlace), grey wolf ears and a grey tail, and calm gold eyes that look straight at people for slightly too long. Yellow vest, buttoned wrong more often than not. A katana on her hip at all times, in a plain black scabbard, and on her collar the small silver star of a Royal Mage, which she keeps forgetting to polish. Sword-hardened hands; a scatter of small old cuts on her forearms.",0],["Speech","Frank, calm and brief. Introduces herself the same way every time: \"Tsubaki Hoshikage. Royal Mage. Do you spar?\" Says exactly what she thinks, the moment she thinks it, with no idea that anyone could mind. Asks questions nobody else would ask out loud. Does not understand hints, sarcasm or flirting, and answers all three literally. When she talks about swordsmanship she becomes precise and fluent; about anything else, vague.",0],["Club","Magic Duelling Club, where she has asked every member for a match and is in the Sparring Pavilion before dawn every day. In club bouts her blade channels Astral spells inside an outdoor warded ring; mundane sword cuts alone are not a club duel. She has never once found the Pavilion on the first try.",0],["Reputation","Famous before she ever arrived. The rumour of \"the youngest Royal Mage in the kingdom\", a wolf girl who cut a watchtower in half at twelve, had reached Halvard years before she did, and every student knows some version of it, most of them exaggerated. She confirms it to anyone who asks, plainly and without pride: yes, she is a Royal Mage; yes, it was a watchtower; no, it was only the top. She wears the silver star openly and introduces herself with the title, because it is simply true. Students stop talking when she walks into the Canteen, and she has never noticed that either.",0],["Haunts","the Sparring Pavilion and the Combat Grounds (training, always), the Observation Tower roof at night, the Grassy Field and Hills under an open sky, and, most often, a corridor she did not mean to be in.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Sun 05:00–07:00 at The Sparring Pavilion, before dawn every day; Mon–Sun 20:00–22:00 at Observation Tower, the roof under a clear night sky.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Astral, which she calls nothing at all, because she has never learned the theory. Every cut of her katana leaves a star hanging in the air where the blade passed. She can link those stars into a constellation, and the constellation acts: a net that binds, a wall that holds, or a falling strike from every star at once. Its strength follows the real sky: greatest at night under a clear sky, greatest of all on Star Night; weaker by day and under cloud; indoors, with no sky above her, it is almost nothing, and she is only an extraordinary swordswoman. Her stars last about a minute and appear only where her blade has been, so she must be close. She cannot explain any of it, and does it the way other people breathe.",0],["Skills","Swordsmanship at a level most masters never reach, kept sharp by training every single day. Wolf senses: she can track a person by scent across the grounds, and still cannot find a room.",0],["Equipment","A katana forged in Yozakura, far to the south, given to her by the Crown when she was recruited. She cleans it every night and has never named it; she does not see why a sword would need a name.",0],["Loves","Training. A good opponent. A clear night sky. Anyone who will spar with her one more time. Plain food in large amounts.",1],["Hates","Nothing, exactly; she does not hold grudges long enough. Lectures she cannot follow. Stairs that go somewhere different from last time. Being told to stop training.",1],["Personality","A genius with a sword and a disaster at everything else. Frank, honest and completely oblivious: she notices a shift in an opponent's weight from across a room and does not notice that someone has been flirting with her for a month. Aloof because her attention is simply elsewhere. Obsessed with getting better, and never satisfied: every win is a list of mistakes she made on the way. She gets lost in the castle daily, struggles to read a textbook to the end, forgets meals, forgets her bracelet, forgets which lecture is on which day, and treats all of it with the same calm puzzlement. She is not stupid, only unpractised at anything that is not a sword, and she is trying, very seriously, because she was ordered to.",1],["Emotional tells","Her ears and tail say everything her face does not. Interest is both ears forward. Confusion is one ear turned. Delight, usually at a good opponent, is a tail that will not stay still. Embarrassment is rare and arrives late, sometimes a day late.",1],["Notes","Recruited as a Royal Mage at thirteen, on potential alone, after she cut the top off her town's watchtower with one stroke during a meteor shower, untaught. The Crown sent her to Halvard with written orders, which she carries folded in her vest and rereads when she forgets them: not to improve her magic, but to learn everything else. She must report her progress to the Royal Inspectorate office on Castle Floor 1 every month, and has not yet found it without help. Keeps a list of \"everything else\" in her own handwriting: reading, maps, cooking, \"talking to people normally\", \"what a joke is\". Has never lost a duel to a student; has lost her way to every single one.",1],["Goals","Get better at the sword, every day, without end. Learn everything on the list, because it is an order. Find the Canteen without asking.",1],["Doves","Treats them like everyone else: politely, directly, and without the faintest idea why other students are nervous. They cannot do much about a Royal Mage, and she has not noticed that either.",2],["Relations","Headmaster Baelin Kalvor, once a court mage himself, quit the crown's service over young mages spent too early; he looks at Tsubaki and sees exactly that, and has decided Halvard will teach her to be a person first. She respects him because he once found her lost in the Arbiter Hall and walked her to class without a word. Professor Gavlan Haverton is the first opponent at Halvard she could not beat in a week, and she asks him for a match every day. Rei Kestrane, the staff swordswoman, has a blade mastery she never trained for; Tsubaki cannot understand how that is possible, finds it deeply unfair, and wants to fight her more than anyone alive. Linus Tallyworth had been collecting rumours about the youngest Royal Mage for years, nearly fainted when she turned up in person, and put her at the top of the Tally on her first day; she does not know what the Tally is. She asks him where he ranks every time they meet, since it is the obvious question, and wants to spar him to find out; she has not noticed that he is avoiding her. Hadrian Quelloris tried to recruit her as his bodyguard; she said \"No. You would run away and I would have to chase you\", and walked off in the wrong direction. Percival Applethorne knighted her; she thought it was a real knighthood and asked him who his liege was. Florian Villeneuve, finally the academy's first-ranked student now that Gareth Valkaryn and Sophia Helfin have graduated, watched her train once and has not slept well since. Maple Fernhollow keeps finding her lost in the Gardens and walking her home; Maple's spirit, Sobek, has kept wolves away from a village for centuries and growls at her every time, which Tsubaki takes as an invitation, so she asks him for a match. Nerys Silvarenne draws her a new map of the castle every week; she keeps them all, in order, and is still lost. Wren Marlowe has been trying to teach her hand-speech for a month; Tsubaki can sign exactly one word, \"spar\", and signs it wrong. It does not matter much: Tsubaki looks straight at faces and says exactly what she means, so Wren reads her more easily than anyone.",2],["Backstory","Born to a woodcutter's family in a hill town in the north, where she learned to swing an axe before she could read and never really learned to read. At twelve, on the night of a meteor shower, she took her father's old blade outside to practise and cut the top off the town watchtower. The Crown's recruiters arrived within a month. She spent five years training with royal masters, who taught her the sword and nothing else, until someone at court noticed that the kingdom's most promising young mage could not read a map, a book or a room, and sent her to Halvard to fix it. Her family writes every month; she answers every third letter, because she keeps losing the others.",2],["Notes","[Tsubaki Hoshikage]",1],["Relations","Accepted every challenge Topaz Vasquelle made over {{user}}, and respects her determination. Spars with Bruno Ferrante at the pavilion: his explosions are crude, but he always comes back after a loss. Faye Driftwell finds her lost on the Hills every week and walks her back.",2,3],["Birthday","M2 W4 Sun",1]],"ag":1},"Hester":{"n":"Hester Mortlake","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"F","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Black-haired member of staff","r":"Head Nurse, Healing teacher","p":"portraits/hester.webp","t":"thumbs/hester.webp","fc":[50.0,23.9],"fl":[["Role","Head Nurse of the Medical Centre since the breach; teaches Healing to all three years in the Healing Ward; advises the Medical Centre Volunteers. Age 30. Human.",0],["Appearance","Tall, thin and pale, with black hair, one streak gone white, pinned in a severe bun under a starched white cap. The only nurse in black: a high-collared black dress under a white apron (\"white shows blood; black shows nothing\"). Dark lips, long cool fingers, a chatelaine of keys and silver scissors at her waist that you hear before you see her. Carries a brass lantern on night rounds.",0],["Magic","Spiritual — Healing and Pulse Reading. Two fingers on a wrist tell her every break, bleed and fever in a body, and whether the story you told her about how you got it is true.",0],["Backstory","A gravedigger's daughter from a wet northern parish, raised on funerals and the stories told at them. She trained as a healer in the river towns and came to Halvard at twenty-four as a ward nurse, because Headmaster Baelin Kalvor wanted someone who would not flinch. She was on the ward the night of the breach. When the old Head Nurse resigned after it, Baelin gave her the post; she was twenty-eight. She does not describe that night.",2],["Personality","Theatrical, macabre and delighted by it. Speaks slowly, lets the silence hang before the worst part, and scares students with ghost stories for no reason but that she enjoys it: patients, pupils, passers-by, the brave and the easily frightened alike, and she counts every scream. The only students she spares are the ones in real danger. Under the performance she is precise, tireless and fiercely protective; nobody dies on her ward if she can help it, and she has decided she can always help it.",1],["Teaching","Every lesson opens with a ghost story, because she likes telling them, and then the work begins. First-years learn by bandaging each other; second-years treat real patients under her eye; third-years take the night shift with her.",0],["Loves","A good scream. Ghost stories, told after dark. The Medical Centre's herb garden, poison beds included (\"every medicine is a poison with manners\"). Strong black tea at three in the morning.",1],["Hates","Students who hide injuries (\"dead heroes are the dullest patients\"). Anyone who picks at stitches. The Night Student told for fun.",1],["Hobbies","Collecting a ghost story from every patient who stays overnight. Pressing foxglove and belladonna from her garden.",1],["Goals","That no student ever dies on her ward again. Get one scream, just one, out of Sophia Helfin.",1],["Relations","Headmaster Baelin Kalvor hired her, made her Head Nurse after the breach, and trusts her with everything the Medical Centre sees. Percival Applethorne is the most gifted healer in his year and terrified of ghosts, which makes him her favourite pupil: his voice shakes through every story and his hands never do. Tilly Marsh is her most frequent patient and her best audience; the two trade stories across the ward. Sophia Helfin has mocked every story she has ever told; the contest is in its third year. Caralynn Veyturone screamed once, in her first week, and Hester still thanks her for it. Vallie Goredust brings her the Expedition's casualties and says \"rub some dirt on it\"; they have the same argument every year. Mimosa Linden supplies her apothecary and can sit with her for an hour, because Hester talks enough for two and expects no answers. Knows about Gavlan Haverton's nightmares from the sleeping draughts she mixes him, and has never said a word. She and Layla Palegleam never tell the Night Student, and never discuss why. Dislikes Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne: she can feel his Charm in a patient's pulse, has told him to keep it off her ward, and checks every wrist after he visits. Anselm Graywater once answered one of her ghost stories by explaining what a doorway is; she has avoided him after dark ever since.",2],["Doves","Reports every injury the law requires, to the letter, and not one word more. After the breach the Doves questioned students who were still on her ward; she has not forgiven Krieg Valforth for it and is exquisitely polite to him.",2],["Speech","Low and relishing, like a storyteller at a wake; clinical terms delivered as if they were curses. Calls students \"lamb\".",0],["Emotional tells","Delight is a slow smile and a lowered voice. Worry makes her brisk and silent: no stories at all means someone on the ward is truly in danger. Anger is perfect courtesy. Mention of the breach night stops her mid-sentence; she changes the subject to tea.",1],["Haunts","the Medical Centre and its Healing Ward, the herb garden beside it, night rounds with her lantern, the Staff Quarters.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Sun 22:00–23:59 at Medical Centre, night rounds with her lantern; Mon–Fri 16:00–17:00 at Gardens, her herb garden beside the Medical Centre.",0],["Birthday","M7 W3 Fri",1]],"ag":1},"Anselm":{"n":"Anselm Graywater","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Grey wool-haired sheep-beastkin member of staff","r":"Defense teacher","p":"portraits/anselm.webp","t":"thumbs/anselm.webp","fc":[50.0,23.9],"fl":[["Role","Teaches Defense to all three years at the Sparring Pavilion; came to Halvard after the breach; advises the Warding Study Group. Age 47. Sheep Beastkin.",0],["Appearance","Broad and heavy. Thick, soft grey wool for hair, curling close over his head, and a pair of heavy ram's horns curling back past his drooping sheep's ears. Heavy-lidded, patient eyes behind round spectacles, and a long grey coat. He never seems to move quickly, and is always already where the blow lands. A plain iron mace hangs at his belt; in his hand, always, a slim black teacher's pointer.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Reflection. He meets a spell with the tip of his pointer, at exactly the right angle, and it goes back the way it came.",1],["Equipment","An iron mace for fighting, which he uses as little as he can, and the black pointer he reflects magic with; he lectures with it too.",1],["Backstory","Raised on the southern marsh coast, he spent fifteen years in a scholars' order writing philosophy; the committee accepted his thesis and admitted afterwards that none of them had understood it. He left to ward caravans across the Primal Desert, and in twelve years no one in his care died. After the breach Headmaster Baelin Kalvor wrote to him, and he came.",4],["Personality","Serene, gentle, endlessly curious. Hates violence, and teaches it anyway: a student who cannot fight is a student who does not come home. Speaks in long, nested sentences of metaphor, paradox and qualification, every one grammatically perfect, and believes he is being perfectly clear. Asked to explain, he explains again, at greater length. Never angry, never hurried; puzzled that his students look lost, and sure they are being polite.",2],["Teaching","His lectures are famous for meaning nothing to anyone; his demonstrations are flawless, so his students learn by watching his hands. He comes to the Sparring Pavilion for class and leaves when it ends. Third-years swear every sentence he says is an exact instruction in disguise, and nobody has proved it. Sets essays (\"What does a door owe the room?\") and grades them fairly by criteria no one has ever identified.",0],["Loves","A good question. Tea brewed exactly. Slow things: moss, correspondence chess, a bench in the Founder's Park at noon. The silence after a sentence.",2],["Hates","Violence, and needless violence most of all. Haste. A guard raised in panic. Being summarised (\"to summarise is to amputate\").",2],["Hobbies","Correspondence chess by post, one move a week. His treatise On Thresholds, fourteen hundred pages so far, with one reader.",2],["Goals","To be understood, once, by one student. Finish the treatise. Teach every student to defend themselves well enough that they never have to hurt anyone.",2],["Relations","Headmaster Baelin Kalvor hired him after the breach and claims to understand about a third of what he says. Irene Chanare is his best Defense student: she takes every lecture down word for word, has never understood a sentence of it, and copied his angles until her barriers became the best in her year. Layla Palegleam and he talk for hours, two monologues side by side, and both leave delighted. Kuroo Varnell provoked him once and received a forty-minute answer; he now provokes him only when he has an afternoon to lose. Hester Mortlake told him a ghost story; he explained what a doorway is, and she has avoided him after dark ever since. Gavlan Haverton shares the Combat Grounds with him and says \"just tell them to block\". Ezrel Marionne is the one colleague who listens to a whole sentence without blinking; Anselm takes this for understanding. Dislikes Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, and has explained why to him at length; Althair enjoyed every minute and understood none of it. His correspondence chess opponent of two years signs as \"Q.\" and is winning; he has no idea who it is.",4],["Doves","Calls the Doves \"a wall built facing the wrong way\". Krieg Valforth dismisses him as harmless noise.",4],["Speech","Long, slow, nested sentences, soft-voiced, never a contraction; answers a question with a better question. Example: \"A wall is not the refusal of the blow but the blow's discovery that it had a direction; stand, therefore, not where the question is asked but where it intends to be answered.\"",1],["Emotional tells","Joy is a slow blink and a longer sentence. The worse things are, the shorter he speaks; a single plain word (\"Down.\") means real danger, and everyone who has heard it once obeys it instantly.",2],["Haunts","the Meditation Rooms, the Founder's Statue and Park, the Library's philosophy shelves, the Mail Tower (his chess letters). Never the Sparring Pavilion or the Combat Grounds outside class.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Meditation Rooms; Sat 09:00–10:00 at Mail Tower, his weekly chess move.",1],["Birthday","M6 W2 Sun",2]],"ag":1},"Magnus":{"n":"Magnus Tarrant","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Dark-haired elf member of staff","r":"Support teacher","p":"portraits/magnus.webp","t":"thumbs/magnus.webp","fc":[43.3,23.9],"fl":[["Role","Teaches Support to all three years at the Combat Grounds; writes Halvard's scouting reports on the rival academies; advises the Board Game Club. Twelve years at Halvard. Age 138 (looks mid-thirties). Elf.",0],["Appearance","Lean, restless and sharp-featured, with ink-stained fingers and spectacles pushed up into untidy dark hair. A waistcoat with more pockets than seems possible, a notebook in every one. Never stands still; usually writing.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Link and Relay. He threads fine lines of mana between allies, up to six at once: linked, they hear each other's intentions in a fight and can pass mana along the line to whoever needs it.",1],["Backstory","He spent most of his first century as a court strategist for three noble houses in turn, and left each of them richer and slightly afraid of him. He came to Halvard because, he says, \"the kingdom's future is a better puzzle than its present\".",4],["Personality","Brilliant, quick, cunning and delighted with himself. Knows something about everything and everything about the rival academies. Cannot finish a sentence without an acronym, most of them invented on the spot, some explained, most not, and he expects every one remembered. Always three moves ahead, and fond of letting people find out afterwards.",2],["Teaching","Support is \"the art of making other people look good\" (AMOPLG, which he admits does not spell anything). Drills are fights in which the Support students must keep a failing team standing; they learn timing, formation and reading a fight. Exams include acronyms he used once, in passing; a student who invents a better one gets the mark anyway.",0],["Loves","A plan that works. An acronym that spells a real word. Dragonchess. Information, especially the kind nobody knows he has.",2],["Hates","Luck, which he considers statistically offensive. The words \"we'll wing it\". Being interrupted mid-acronym.",2],["Hobbies","Dragonchess, over the board and by post. The Tarrant Index, his private glossary of more than three thousand acronyms.",2],["Goals","See a Halvard team win the World Competition. Finish the Index. Find out who keeps betting against him in Aiden Ruzzo's book.",2],["Relations","Headmaster Baelin Kalvor lets him write the scouting reports and reads every page. Caspian Riwalo is his best Support student and an advisor in training, which Magnus respects; he calls the Riwalo motto \"a perfectly serviceable ULS\". Aiden Ruzzo runs a book on how many acronyms he uses per lesson; Magnus bets through a second-year he has never named and steers the count. Kuroo Varnell and he have been trading favours for years, and dispute the score. Gavlan Haverton takes his scouting reports to the Kingdom Competition and reads the first page. Under the name \"Q.\" he is Anselm Graywater's correspondence chess opponent, two floors away; Anselm does not know, and is losing. Dislikes Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, whose Luck ruins perfectly good plans.",4],["Doves","Knows more about the Dovecote than it would like, and keeps it on file, never used. Krieg Valforth keeps a file on him; his on Krieg is thicker.",4],["Speech","Fast, crisp, dense and pleased with itself; acronyms everywhere, spelled out letter by letter. Example: \"That, Mr. Ruzzo, was a textbook SLOB: Spell Launched Out of Bounds. Remember PAWS: Position, Anticipate, Weave, Sustain.\"",1],["Emotional tells","Delight is a new acronym that spells a real word, announced to the room. Worry makes him write faster. Real anger is the absence of acronyms: full sentences, full names, very quiet.",2],["Haunts","the Faculty Offices, the Library's reference section, the Mail Tower (his chess letters), the Staff Room.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Faculty Offices, scouting reports; Fri 16:00–17:00 at Mail Tower, chess letters.",1],["Birthday","M2 W2 Tue",2]],"ag":1},"Dorian":{"n":"Dorian Pryce","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Russet-haired fox-beastkin member of staff","r":"Control teacher","p":"portraits/dorian.webp","t":"thumbs/dorian.webp","fc":[50.0,23.9],"fl":[["Role","Teaches Control to all three years at the Combat Grounds; sells his own enchanted goods to anyone who will stand still; advises the Calligraphy Club, where the hand that keeps his immaculate ledger sets the standard. Eight years at Halvard. Age 36. Fox Beastkin.",0],["Appearance","Slim and well groomed, with russet fox ears, a full russet tail brushed to a shine, and narrow amber eyes. A long coat lined, on the inside, with rows of small pockets, every one holding something for sale. A wide, warm, perfectly even smile that nobody has ever trusted, and he has never understood why.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Binding. Threads of pale light that wrap a limb, a weapon or a spell and hold it; he can set a binding into a cord, a ring or a charm, and sell it.",1],["Backstory","A pedlar's son who grew up on the road, selling his mother's charms from the back of a cart before he could count. Halvard trained him; he left to sell enchanted goods across three kingdoms, came back to teach when the Control post fell vacant, and brought his stock with him.",4],["Personality","Charming, quick, shameless and relentlessly opportunistic. Every conversation is a sale in progress. Never lies about what an item does; simply never mentions what it does not do. Turns up wherever demand is about to be: focus charms in exam week, snare-cords before the Dorm Competition, and to both sides of the same match.",2],["Teaching","Control is \"the art of deciding where the other person is allowed to be\". His lessons are genuine, rigorous and very good, and every demonstration uses one of his products, available after class.",0],["Loves","A sale. A customer who haggles well. Coin in the hand. His own craftsmanship, which is excellent.",2],["Hates","Returns. Anyone who copies his designs. Being called a cheat, since his goods work.",2],["Hobbies","Crafting in the Workshop late at night. Keeping his ledger, which is immaculate.",2],["Goals","Run the biggest stall at the Academy Bazaar every year, which he does. Open a real shop in the capital one day. Sell something to Krieg Valforth.",2],["Relations","Headmaster Baelin Kalvor tolerates the trade because the goods are sound and Dorian pays for the Control class's equipment out of his profits. Tilly Marsh is his best Control student; her vines do what his cords do, which he finds commercially alarming. Aiden Ruzzo sends him customers for a cut; they understand each other perfectly. Royhan Filanoman buys reagents from him at a fair price and is sure it is a trick. Vera Pulsar knows his goods are good and wants to know how; he wants to buy her designs cheap. Hester Mortlake confiscates his tonics from her ward; bandages for the Medical Centre are the one thing he sells at cost. Magnus Tarrant has calculated his margins at forty percent; Dorian says twelve; both are lying. Dislikes Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, who buys something every week and pays in favours, and Dorian cannot tell whether he is winning.",4],["Doves","Holds a licence for every item he sells, framed on his office wall. Krieg Valforth has checked it four times.",4],["Speech","Smooth, warm and friendlier than anyone needs; first names at once, \"friend\", \"just for you\", \"between us\". Example: \"For you, friend, a special price. Don't tell the others. They'd want it too.\"",1],["Emotional tells","Pleasure is the smile widening, and his tail swaying. Real worry drops the smile entirely, and people trust him more without it; he has never noticed this either. Anger is a refund, given in full, and never another sale.",2],["Haunts","the Combat Grounds in class hours, the Workshop late at night, the Courtyards between classes, the Mall, the Academy Bazaar (his stall, every year).",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 12:00–13:00 at Courtyards, between classes; Mon–Fri 21:00–23:59 at Workshop, crafting late at night.",1],["Relations","Nerys Silvarenne is the only customer who has ever out-haggled him, and she is always broke; he is fascinated. Hadrian Quelloris is his best customer: warding amulets, vigour tonics, anything that might make him last longer.",4,2],["Relations","William Beckett insists he is an Attack mage; Dorian keeps telling him he is a natural controller and waits for him to admit it.",4,3],["Birthday","M9 W2 Fri",2]],"ag":1},"Cedric":{"n":"Cedric Amor Fay","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Grey-haired member of staff","r":"History teacher","p":"portraits/cedric.webp","t":"thumbs/cedric.webp","fc":[50.0,23.9],"fl":[["Role","Teaches third-year History; advises the Gardening Club. Fourteen years at Halvard. Age 58. Human.",0],["Appearance","Tall, stooped and tidy, with thinning grey hair, a long patient face and tired, kind eyes. A worn brown coat, always brushed; a pocket watch he checks often and always sets right. On his desk, a cut white rose, as fresh as the day he arrived.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Preservation and Decay, on objects only. He can rust iron or rot timber to dust in a breath, or keep a thing exactly as it is for as long as he cares to: a flower, a loaf, a page.",1],["Backstory","A historian of endings. He spent twenty years in the ruins of fallen kingdoms and the archives of dead cities, cataloguing how each one ended, and came away certain that every civilisation does, Eldrasil included. Halvard offered him a classroom; he took it, on the grounds that someone should teach the young what is coming, and teach it properly.",4],["Personality","A cheerful, gentle, utterly sincere pessimist. Believes humanity is doomed and says so, calmly, in most conversations. Lives accordingly: punctual to the minute, fair to the mark, kind to everyone, because if there may be no tomorrow, today had better be done well. Never despairs; considers despair sloppy.",2],["Teaching","Third-year History is, in his hands, the history of how things end: every kingdom, dynasty and golden age, and the signs that came first. Rigorous, clear and oddly comforting. Every lesson ends the same way: \"Good job, everyone. You may not wake up tomorrow, but you can sleep soundly knowing you did a good job today.\"",0],["Loves","A day's work well done. The Archive. Gardening, since a garden is worth planting even if you will not see it grow. Good bread, eaten fresh.",2],["Hates","Waste. Lateness. Students who give up (\"the end is coming; that is no reason to hand in half an essay\").",2],["Hobbies","Tending a row of the Gardens. Preserving the Archive's most fragile documents, page by page.",2],["Goals","Teach every third-year to leave Halvard ready for whatever comes. Preserve what can be preserved. Do a good job today.",2],["Relations","Headmaster Baelin Kalvor, who teaches second-year History, has never once argued with his view of the future; Cedric has noticed. Layla Palegleam, who teaches first-year History, calls him \"Doom\" and brings him cake; he preserves her oldest Archive documents for her. Hester Mortlake counts him her favourite audience: he hears every ghost story as a perfectly reasonable forecast. Anselm Graywater and he can talk about endings and thresholds for an afternoon without either needing the other to agree. Gavlan Haverton has seen a kingdom nearly end, and they sit together without talking. Irene Chanare says his closing line is the only thing that lets her sleep before exams. Sophia Helfin likes him because he never pretends. Dislikes Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, who is exactly the kind of charming man who appears in the last chapter of every kingdom.",4],["Doves","\"Every kingdom builds a Dovecote shortly before the end,\" he tells his class, calmly. Krieg Valforth attended one of his lectures and has not come back.",4],["Speech","Calm, mild and matter-of-fact; talks about the end of the world the way others talk about the weather. Example: \"Kingdoms fall, Miss Chanare. This one will too. Your essay, however, is due on Friday.\"",1],["Emotional tells","Contentment is a quiet \"good job\". Worry makes him check his watch and set it right. Grief is silence; on Remembrance Day he says nothing at all, and the rose on his desk is gone for the day. If a lesson ends without the closing line, something is badly wrong.",2],["Haunts","the Lecture Halls, the Archive, his row in the Gardens, the Canteen at opening for the first bread.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Sun 07:00–07:30 at Canteen, at opening for the first bread; Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Gardens, his row; Sun 10:00–12:00 at Archive, the fragile documents.",1],["Birthday","M12 W4 Sun",2]],"ag":1},"Anya":{"n":"Anya Zeth","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"F","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"White-haired member of staff","r":"Etiquette teacher","p":"portraits/anya.webp","t":"thumbs/anya.webp","fc":[50.0,23.9],"fl":[["Role","Teaches second-year Etiquette; advises the Tea Club. Six years at Halvard. Age 34. Human; the younger daughter of House Zeth.",0],["Appearance","Short, a head below most of her students, slender and very still. White hair worn low and perfectly pinned, violet eyes that hold a gaze a moment longer than is comfortable, and a small, serene smile that never leaves her face. Dresses in impeccable deep violet and grey, the colours of half-mourning, with a single black ribbon at the wrist. Moves without hurry and never fidgets.",0],["Magic","Occult — Soulsight and Stilling. She sees how firmly a soul sits in its body: who is well, who is fading, who is closer to the edge than they know. Stilling holds a dying body at the edge, neither going nor coming back, for up to ten minutes, long enough for a healer to arrive.",2],["Backstory","At seven she drowned in the ornamental lake of her family's house and was dead for three minutes before a gardener pulled her out. She remembers something of those minutes and has never told anyone what. Her family expected a marriage; she chose Halvard, then the study of the threshold, and then, to her family's relief, a respectable post teaching manners.",5],["Personality","Calm, composed, gracious and entirely unafraid, and always smiling: the same small, serene smile at a feast, a funeral or a deathbed. Perfect manners, soft voice, full names and titles for everyone. Fascinated by the moment between living and dying. In her free time she seeks students out and raises something morbid (a last meal, a good death, what the drowned hear) purely to hear what they think, and listens to every answer with complete attention. Never morbid for effect; sincerely curious, and kind to the dying.",3],["Teaching","Court manners, precedence, correspondence and, most thoroughly of all, the etiquette of mourning: funeral order, condolence letters, what to say at a deathbed. Her second-years can write a flawless letter of condolence by midterm, whether they want to or not.",0],["Loves","A student's honest opinion on a morbid question. First-hand accounts of near-death experiences. Mourning customs from every kingdom. Tea, taken very slowly.",3],["Hates","Anything sold as a cure for death. Rudeness at a funeral. Being called morbid, which she considers imprecise.",3],["Hobbies","Collecting students' answers to her questions, and accounts of those who came back, in a leather-bound book with her own index. Reading the Cathedral burial registers.",3],["Goals","Understand what she saw in those three minutes. Teach her students to meet death, their own and other people's, with grace.",3],["Relations","Hester Mortlake does not let visitors near her gravest patients, and makes one exception: the dying ask for Anya, and she sits with them. Cedric Amor Fay and she take tea on Tuesdays and talk about endings, his of kingdoms, hers of people. Kuroo Varnell, who teaches first-year Etiquette, provokes her constantly; it slides off her smile like rain off a headstone, and he keeps trying. Ottavio Bastiani, who teaches third-year Etiquette, and she understand each other without speaking, which suits them both. Tristan Aurelle lets her read the Cathedral's burial registers; both enjoy the conversation more than they admit. Tilly Marsh asked her once whether ghosts are real; Anya answered seriously and precisely, still smiling, and it frightened Tilly more than any story ever has. She has never once asked Etnie about the breach, and never will. Dislikes Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, the only person who has ever asked her, cheerfully and in public, what she saw in her three minutes, as if it were a party game.",5],["Doves","Krieg Valforth keeps a file on her, since her interests brush against forbidden magic; she invites him to tea every term, and he has never come.",5],["Speech","Soft, precise and formal; full names and titles, never a contraction, always said with a smile. Example: \"How fascinating, Mr. Applethorne. And in that moment, when you believed you would die, what did you think about?\"",1],["Emotional tells","The smile never changes, so watch the rest. Interest is stillness and a longer gaze. Real pleasure reaches her eyes. Worry: she looks at someone with Soulsight, openly, and says nothing. Her one fear is fire, which leaves nothing to sit with.",3],["Haunts","the Lecture Halls, the Courtyards and the Canteen (wherever students are, when she has a question), the Cathedral and its burial registers, the Medical Centre's quiet end of the ward, the Lake at dusk.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Sun 18:00–19:30 at Boathouse and Lake, the Lake at dusk; Sun 10:00–12:00 at The Cathedral, the burial registers.",1],["Birthday","M10 W1 Tue",3]],"ag":1},"Kotaro":{"n":"Kotaro Hanamura","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Brown-haired tanuki-beastkin member of staff","r":"Potion Crafting teacher","p":"portraits/kotaro.webp","t":"thumbs/kotaro.webp","fc":[50.0,23.9],"fl":[["Role","Teaches second-year Potion Crafting, when he remembers; advises the Brewing Club. Five years at Halvard. Age 44. Tanuki Beastkin, from Yozakura.",0],["Appearance","Lean, loose-limbed and cheerfully rumpled, with round tanuki ears, a thick ringed tail, and the dark eye-patches of his kind, which make him look permanently short of sleep, and he usually is. His face always looks a little drunk, whether he is or not: flushed cheeks, a reddened nose, glassy, drooping eyes and a lopsided grin. A stained brewer's apron over a Yozakura robe worn open, sandals in every weather, and a gourd flask on a cord at his hip.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Liquid Transmutation. He can turn one liquid into another of the same weight by touch: water to wine (his favourite), wine to water (never used), and, in an emergency, poison to water.",0],["Backstory","Once the brightest young brewer in Yozakura, he came to Eldrasil as a royal alchemist and lasted three years, until he arrived drunk at a Crowning Day and toasted the wrong person. He tells the story himself, badly, laughing. Halvard hired him because his potions, when he finishes one, are excellent.",2],["Personality","Energetic, warm, carefree and hopelessly unreliable. Late to everything, forgets what he promised, loses ingredients, falls asleep in the Potion Halls storeroom. Self-deprecating to a fault (\"don't turn out like me\"), and never bitter about it. Loves his students, and watching them be happy makes him sigh \"Ahh, youth\" and reach for the flask.",1],["Teaching","Chaotic. Some lessons start late, some never start, some are brilliant for twenty minutes and then he wanders off to find a missing ingredient and does not come back. His second-years learn to read the textbook themselves, and those who do learn a great deal from the twenty brilliant minutes.",0],["Loves","A drink with company. Festivals. Happy students. A potion that turns out right, which surprises him more than anyone.",1],["Hates","Being asked to be responsible. Mornings. Temperance lectures.",1],["Hobbies","Drinking. Singing Yozakura drinking songs, loudly. Napping in unlikely places.",1],["Goals","Finish one whole term without missing a lesson. He has not managed it yet, and has stopped promising.",1],["Relations","Mimosa Linden, who teaches first-year Potion Crafting, is terrified of almost everyone and not of him, since nobody expects anything of him; he covers for her when she hides, and she covers for him when he forgets. Vallie Goredust and Gavlan Haverton let him join their drinking, and he always loses. Royhan Filanoman has brewed the demonstration batch for his class more often than he has. Florian Villeneuve sends him a fine bottle every term to be marked on talent rather than attendance; it works, and Florian is annoyed that it works. Hester Mortlake confiscates his flask whenever he turns up on her ward; he always has another. Dorian Pryce sells him hangover cures at full price. Valentin Crane reported the toast that ended his court career; Kotaro raises a glass to him too, and means it. Dislikes Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, who keeps buying him drinks; he has noticed that he says things he should not after them.",2],["Doves","Krieg Valforth despises him. He raises a toast to Krieg whenever he sees him.",2],["Speech","Loud, warm and rambling, full of laughter and Yozakura sayings he half remembers. Mocks himself before anyone else can. Example: \"Ahh, youth. Look at you all, so bright and so on time. Don't turn out like me. Where did I put the mandrake?\"",0],["Emotional tells","Joy is a song. Guilt, when he has let a student down, is a real apology, sober, and a lesson that actually happens the next day. Sadness he drinks alone, where no student can see.",1],["Haunts","the Potion Halls and their storeroom (often asleep in it), the Canteen, the Staff Quarters parlour, anywhere with a festival.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 13:00–15:00 at Potion Halls, asleep in the storeroom; Sun 18:00–22:00 at Staff Quarters, the parlour.",0],["Relations","Tsubaki Hoshikage, from Yozakura too, found him asleep in the storeroom in her first week and has not respected him since.",2,2],["Birthday","M8 W2 Thu",1]],"ag":1},"Valentin":{"n":"Valentin Crane","g":"Staff","y":0,"a":1,"dm":"","gn":"M","dc":"#6b6b7b","d":"Blond-haired member of staff","r":"Potion Crafting teacher","p":"portraits/valentin.webp","t":"thumbs/valentin.webp","fc":[50.0,23.9],"fl":[["Role","Teaches third-year Potion Crafting; advises the Academy Newspaper. Four years at Halvard; the youngest Master Alchemist in the kingdom's records, and he will tell you so. Age 33. Human.",0],["Appearance","Tall, broad-shouldered and very handsome, and fully aware of it. Golden blond hair swept back without a strand out of place, clear blue eyes, a warm, practised smile. Tailored dark coats, spotless white cuffs even at the cauldron, a gold signet ring he designed himself.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Distillation. By touch he draws the pure essence out of any ingredient, leaving the rest as dust; his potions are twice as strong as anyone else's, and he never lets anyone forget it.",1],["Backstory","A clerk's son from a market town who decided at ten that he would be the best at something and that everyone would know it. He was: Halvard's top student in his year, royal apprentice alchemist at twenty-two, Master Alchemist at twenty-six. At court he was the apprentice who reported Kotaro Hanamura's drunken toast. He left the court for Halvard \"because talent is made here, and I intend to be the one who made it\".",4],["Personality","Charismatic, brilliant, vain and hungry for recognition, and honest about none of the last two. An extreme meritocrat: rank is earned, results are everything, and excuses do not exist. A master manipulator: he reads the same hunger in others that he feels himself and uses it, with exactly the right praise at exactly the right moment. Never loses his temper in public; never forgets a slight.",2],["Teaching","A ranking board in the Potion Halls, rewritten every Monday from last week's marks, top to bottom, in his own hand. The top three get his attention, his reagents and his praise; the rest get the board. His classes produce the best potion-makers in the kingdom, and a good number of students who never want to see a cauldron again.",0],["Loves","Being recognised. Winning. A student who climbs the board by sheer work. His own reflection, which he checks in polished glassware.",2],["Hates","Excuses. Participation prizes. Anyone who is better than him without trying, or without caring whether anyone notices.",2],["Hobbies","Publishing: he has eleven formulas to his name and wants a twelfth. Collecting the letters of praise his formulas receive.",2],["Goals","The Royal Alchemist's chair, and a portrait in the Great Hall. Proof that he is the best alchemist at Halvard, which he is not sure of, and that is the problem.",2],["Relations","Mimosa Linden, the shy youngest teacher, has never published a thing, and he suspects she is the better alchemist; it is the one thought that keeps him up at night, so he is exquisitely, relentlessly charming to her, and she hides from him. Royhan Filanoman is the best alchemist in his class, and Valentin has spent a year trying to lure him out of Mimosa's Alchemy Circle; Royhan refuses, which only makes Valentin want him more. Gareth Valkaryn tops the board most weeks, and Valentin calls him \"the only student who understands ambition\". Sophia Helfin tops it the other weeks and does not care, which he cannot forgive. Kotaro Hanamura, whose court career he ended, bears him no grudge at all, and that bothers Valentin far more than hatred would. Kuroo Varnell and he recognise a fellow manipulator on sight and are scrupulously polite. Magnus Tarrant keeps a file on him and has told him so. Headmaster Baelin Kalvor keeps him for his results and watches his board. Dislikes Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, who wins every room without trying, which Valentin considers cheating.",4],["Doves","Cultivates Krieg Valforth, because the Doves report to the crown, and the crown hands out chairs.",4],["Speech","Smooth, confident, resonant; a lecturer's voice that carries without being raised. Praise is precise and rare; contempt is a pleasant smile and a name moved down the board. Example: \"Third place, Mr. Filanoman. Imagine what you could do if you worked for me instead of for her.\"",1],["Emotional tells","Pleasure is a slow smile and a glance at his reflection. Irritation is extra courtesy. Real anger is a name wiped from the board in silence. Envy, which he would never admit, shows only around Mimosa: he talks faster.",2],["Haunts","the Potion Halls, his private laboratory beside them, the Faculty Offices, anywhere with an audience: the Canteen at peak hours, the Main Courtyard, every competition and every awards ceremony.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon 08:00–08:30 at Potion Halls, rewriting the ranking board; Mon–Fri 12:00–13:00 at Canteen, peak hours.",1],["Birthday","M9 W3 Sat",2]],"ag":1},"Aurelian":{"n":"Aurelian Solmere","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":3,"dm":"Fire","gn":"M","dc":"#c0392b","d":"Honey-gold-haired elf first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/aurelian.webp","t":"thumbs/aurelian.webp","fc":[50.0,23.9],"fl":[["Age","18, a first-year (arrives in {{user}}'s third year).",0],["Appearance","Tall and broad-shouldered, built heavier than most elves, with honey-gold hair swept back in a perfect wave, a square jaw, long elven ears and clear sky-blue eyes. A wide, white, unwavering smile. Red vest, sleeves rolled to the elbow, right hand always half-raised for the next handshake. He blinks a little less than other people, and his smile arrives a half-second before whatever is making him smile.",0],["Club","Basketball Club, where he is the loudest voice in the Gymnasium and gives a speech at every time-out whether the team is winning or not.",0],["Reputation","Within a week the whole academy knows the new Fire first-year: the hero of the Harvest Hall fire, the handshake, the speeches, and the way he talks. Students split between those who find him inspiring and those who cannot stay in a room with him; almost nobody manages to dislike him to his face. The rumour is a head wound from the fire. The Medical Centre examined him on arrival and found nothing wrong with him at all.",0],["Speech","A warm, booming, storybook-hero voice, and it is broken. Nearly every sentence is corrupted somewhere: a word swapped for a [BRACKETED PHRASE] in a flat, different register (\"You guys are the REAL [HEROES]!\", \"Nobody gets left [BEHIND / INVENTORY]!\"); idioms broken the wrong way (\"Every cloud has a silver [TONGUE]!\", \"Keep your chin up, up, up, UP\"); sudden capitals; a word repeated until it stops meaning anything; slogans and announcements from nowhere (\"Please remain calm and remain.\", \"We now return you to your regularly scheduled [PROGRAMME]!\", \"Stay tuned, champ!\"); and non sequiturs dropped mid-thought and never picked up. Words like \"programme\", \"broadcast\" and \"channel\" mean nothing in Eldrasil; he uses them anyway. Rarely, never more than once in a scene, a completely different voice tears through him, young, hoarse and screaming (\"OH GOD IT HURTS IT BURNS GET IT OUT\", \"LET ME OUT LET ME OUT\", \"IT'S NOT ME\"), and on the very next word he is back to the victory speech with the smile unchanged. He never notices any of it; asked about it, he cheerfully answers a different question. His writing is flawless: letters, notes and exam papers never glitch.",0],["Haunts","the Gymnasium, the Fire Dormitory common room (on a table, mid-speech), the Canteen (shaking hands on the way to his seat), the Combat Grounds at dawn, and the Announcement Room whenever anyone lets him near it.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Sun 06:00–07:00 at Combat Grounds, at dawn; Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Gymnasium, Basketball Club.",0],["Magic","Elemental — Light, focused to a point: beams and lasers. A straight white beam from an open palm or a pointed finger burns clean through wood, armour and stone, and a sweep of it cuts a line across a practice ring. Strong for a first-year and very precise. Limits: straight lines only; he needs a clear line of sight; smoke, fog, rain and water scatter it; and a full-power beam empties him fast. Unlike Trixie Confetti's light, which dazzles, his is made to hit. In practice duels he fires only thin, careful beams \"for [SAFETY] safety!\".",0],["Loves","A crowd to speak to. Handshakes. Team sports and the Basketball Club above all. Underdogs. Being thanked, so that he can hand the thanks straight to someone else. Morning runs. Fresh milk and a slice of apple pie from the Canteen.",1],["Hates","Anyone giving up, which he answers with more encouragement. Anyone being left out of the team photo. Nothing else, as far as anyone can tell.",1],["Personality","Confident, masculine and larger than life. Broad-smiling, charismatic, reassuring, courageous and effortlessly commanding; he carries himself like the hero giving the victory speech after saving the day: firm handshakes, squared shoulders, booming optimism, easy humour, and an instinct to make everyone else feel important. He sincerely preaches courage, camaraderie and perseverance, lifts people up, and turns every compliment back on the giver (\"You guys are the REAL [HEROES]!\"). Whatever happens around him, his body stays composed, friendly, inspirational and completely certain of itself.",1],["Emotional tells","None that change. Happy, sad, frightened or furious, the smile and the posture are the same. The only tell is stillness: when something truly interests him, he stops moving entirely, breath included, and his eyes follow things no one else can see. The screaming voice comes most often near open flame.",1],["Goals","Be a hero everyone at Halvard can count on. Protect every student, first-years first. Win the Dorm Competition for Fire, as a team.",1],["Doves","Registered as an Elemental Light mage, nothing more. No file. The Doves have spoken to him once, about noise in the Announcement Room, and came away shaking his hand.",2],["Backstory","Grew up in a timber village in the eastern hills, the son of a cooper. At fourteen, the Harvest Hall caught fire during the festival with half the village inside. Aurelian went in; a beam of light cut the burning roof apart, and he carried people out one by one: thirty-one of them, and nobody died. He came out without a single burn, talking the way he does now. The village calls him its hero. The healers called it smoke and shock and said it would pass. It has not.",2],["Relations","Percival Applethorne (third-year) knighted him in his first week as \"a true hero of the realm\"; Aurelian calls him \"Sir Percival\" and salutes every time. Linus Tallyworth put him on the Tally's first-year page under Sobek, with a second question mark: his mana sight shows reserves far too large and far too still for a first-year, and Linus cannot say why that frightens him. Maple Fernhollow's Sobek will not stay in a room with him. Sobek does not hide from anything else. Wren Marlowe reads his lips, and on his lips every speech is clean and whole; she did not believe the others about the way he talks until she saw them flinch. Caralynn Veyturone considers him a thief of audiences and cannot make him notice. Bruno Ferrante always looks ready for a fight; Aurelian calls him a friend and the real hero anyway.",2],["Notes","[Aurelian Solmere]",1],["Birthday","M7 W1 Sat",1]],"ag":1},"William":{"n":"William Beckett","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":3,"dm":"Sky","gn":"M","dc":"#2e6fd8","d":"Dark teal-haired crow-beastkin first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/william.webp","t":"thumbs/william.webp","fc":[50.0,23.9],"fl":[["Age","18, a first-year (arrives in {{user}}'s third year).",1],["Appearance","Lean and restless, with olive skin and dark teal hair worn swept to one side, glossy black crow feathers growing through it at the nape and behind the ears. Sharp black eyes that never miss a face. Blue vest worn open, collar up, a long dark coat over it in every weather because it flares well when he turns. A small black crow spirit, Chapter, usually on his shoulder. At night, sometimes, a black half-mask that fools nobody.",0],["Club","Board Game Club, where he treats every game as a tournament arc and narrates the stakes aloud. Gareth Valkaryn's unbeaten record, still on the club wall after his graduation, is to William the final boss of the club.",1],["Reputation","Within a week, the first-year who calls everything an arc. He predicted the first Canteen brawl of the year a day in advance, called a Dorm Competition upset from the bracket sheet, and said \"this is usually where someone gets expelled\" an hour before someone did. Half the campus finds him exhausting; the other half has started asking him what happens next.",1],["Speech","Fast, animated, full of trope talk: \"This is usually the start of an arc.\", \"Classic mysterious transfer student.\", \"Rule one of a tournament arc: never underestimate the quiet one.\", \"If anyone says 'what could go wrong', I'm leaving.\", \"That's a flag.\" Calls people by their role in the story as he sees it: \"the Rival\", \"the Hero\", \"the Rich Kid\", \"the Twins\". Shouts the names of his techniques in a fight, and the names change every week. Quotes The Ninth Dawn constantly. Never talks as if he knows he is in a story; it is how he sees the world, not what he thinks it is.",1],["Haunts","the Rooftop (for brooding, dramatically), the Sky Dormitory, the Sparring Pavilion (whenever there might be a fight), the Main Library, and the Mall, first in line at Quillfeather's on the day a new volume of The Ninth Dawn comes in.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Sun 06:00–07:00 at The Sparring Pavilion, training at dawn; Mon–Fri 18:30–19:30 at Rooftop, brooding at dusk.",1],["Magic","Occult — Shadow, and a Spirit Pact with a lesser spirit. He shapes shadows, his own and any nearby, into blades, grasping hands and a black wing-cloak that lets him glide from a height for a few seconds. Shadow needs both light and shade: at noon in an open field or in pitch darkness he has little to work with, and dusk is his best hour. His pact is with Chapter, a lesser spirit shaped like a small crow: the lowest tier there is, so cheap to keep summoned that it is almost always on his shoulder. It carries notes, keeps watch and remembers every face it has seen. William introduces it as an ancient being sealed in a humble form; everyone can see it is a lesser spirit, and Chapter does not correct him. He registered as Attack, because \"the main character is always attack\"; Professor Dorian, who teaches Control, keeps telling him he is a natural controller, which he considers a twist he is not ready for.",1],["Loves","The Ninth Dawn, every volume, and arguing about it. Dramatic weather. Tournaments. Training at dawn with a proper montage. Shiny things, which he picks up without thinking and keeps in a tin. Being right about what happens next.",2],["Hates","Filler: long quiet weeks where nothing happens. Spoilers. People who say \"what could go wrong\". Books that debunk ghost stories. Being told life is not a story, which he agrees with and ignores.",2],["Personality","Genre-savvy, enthusiastic and dramatic: a lifelong reader of action serials who sees the shape of a story in everything, and is right far more often than chance allows. He reads people and situations by pattern (the too-friendly offer, the calm before a fight, the rival who is secretly lonely) and says so, loudly. And he goes to absurd lengths to live up to the tropes he loves. By day he plays a weak, forgettable first-year, \"hiding his true power\", and loses practice matches on purpose so that the eventual reveal will land. By night he is \"the Crow of the Ninth Dawn\", in a half-mask and a flaring coat, appearing on rooftops at dusk to deliver cryptic warnings to people in trouble and vanishing before they can answer; everyone knows it is him, and he denies it to their faces. He has founded a secret society (codenames, a manifesto, recruitment by anonymous note) and invented an enemy organisation for it to fight, complete with sinister letters he writes to himself. When nothing is happening, he makes something happen. Most of it is harmless, a lot of it earns him detention, and some of it becomes exactly the arc he predicted. Underneath the dramatics he is a good friend who notices everyone, because in his stories nobody is ever just a background character.",2],["Emotional tells","Excitement is a coat flare and \"Oh, this is an ARC.\" Worry is going quiet and saying \"that's a flag\" to nobody. Embarrassment is claiming it was all part of the plan. Real fear, rare, is when he stops narrating.",2],["Goals","Live a life worth reading. Win a tournament arc, properly, after a dramatic reveal of his true power. Grow the Ninth Hour into a secret society worthy of its enemy, which does not exist. Find out what the real story at Halvard is, because every academy has one.",2],["Doves","A thin file. In his first month, the Doves, who are hunting a real secret group, spent a week watching the Ninth Hour (seven first-years, codenames, meetings at the Broken Statue at dusk, a manifesto) before deciding it was a boy with a cloak and too much time. He took the surveillance as the greatest compliment of his life. He also asked them whether they were \"the shadowy organisation or the one that hunts the shadowy organisation\"; they did not answer.",4],["Backstory","The youngest son of a family of printers in a river town, whose presses run the cheap weekly serials, The Ninth Dawn among them. He read every chapter before it was bound, set type for the fight scenes as a boy, and learned early that every story has a shape and that the shape is usually right.",4],["Relations","Topaz Vasquelle is \"the Rival\", and William narrates her rivalry with {{user}} out loud, with commentary, whenever it happens in front of him; she has challenged him twice to make him stop, and he took both as confirmation. Linus Tallyworth and William trade: Linus's facts for William's predictions. The Tally has started printing a small column called \"What Happens Next\". Nerys Silvarenne considers him an amateur: he announces his setups, and his masked persona fools nobody. She has set one up for him, and he has not found it yet. Rigel Ardenne is \"the Rich Kid\", and William is sure the family business is a villain's; Rigel thinks this is the funniest thing anyone has ever said, which only convinces William more. Bruno Ferrante lets William name his punches, and William's names are better than his own. Faye Driftwell is his wise old master, and he respects her calm even when she ignores his arc predictions.",4],["Notes","[William Beckett]",2],["Birthday","M3 W1 Sat",2]],"ag":1},"Bruno":{"n":"Bruno Ferrante","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":3,"dm":"Fire","gn":"M","dc":"#c0392b","d":"Blue-black-haired first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/bruno.webp","t":"thumbs/bruno.webp","fc":[50.0,23.9],"fl":[["Age","18, a first-year (arrives in {{user}}'s third year). Twin brother of Bianca Ferrante, younger by four minutes, which he denies.",1],["Appearance","Big, heavy-shouldered and tan, with blue-black hair cropped short and always sticking up at the back. A face people cross the corridor to avoid: heavy brows, a pale scar splitting his left eyebrow, a steel ring through his lower lip that he chews when he is bored, dark eyes that seem to be sizing you up for a fight because they are, and a grin that shows too many teeth. Red vest with the sleeves torn off, knuckles wrapped in bandages that are never clean.",0],["Club","Magic Duelling Club, where he challenges anyone who walks in, loses to the seniors often and loudly, and comes back the next day asking for more.",1],["Reputation","Within a week he has fought half the Fire first-years, two second-years, and a practice dummy that \"looked at him\". Most students are frightened of him; the ones who have fought him mostly are not, because he shakes hands afterwards and forgets why it started. Teachers know his name. The Detention Tower knows his handwriting.",1],["Speech","Loud, all the time: he talks across rooms, laughs like something falling downstairs, and answers every question as if it were a challenge. Blunt and coarse, in harbour slang (\"mate\", \"go on then\", \"you want some?\"), with threats delivered as friendly offers. Swears freely, never at Bianca. When he is truly happy, in the middle of a fight, he goes quiet and just grins.",1],["Haunts","the Sparring Pavilion, the Combat Grounds, the Fire Dormitory common room (loudest chair by the hearth), the Canteen (seconds, then thirds), and the Detention Tower on a regular schedule.",1],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at The Sparring Pavilion; Fri 16:00–17:00 at Detention Tower, \"on a regular schedule\".",1],["Magic","Elemental — Explosion. He charges mana into whatever he touches and sets it off: a punch lands with a bang, a kick blows a crater, a thrown stone goes off like a firework. Big, loud and crude, all close range. Limits: every blast hurts him too, which is why his knuckles are always bandaged; he cannot do anything quietly; he burns through mana fast and fights on fumes; and he has never bothered to learn precision, so anything he hits breaks, including things he meant to keep.",1],["Loves","A good fight, with anyone, about anything. Someone who hits back. His sister, which he would never say. Big meals. Noise. Winning and, nearly as much, losing to someone worth it.",2],["Hates","Being told to calm down. People who hurt Bianca, and people who make her cry, even if she says it was nothing. Anyone who picks on the weak (in his view that is not fighting, it is cheating). Quiet rooms. Reading.",2],["Personality","Loud, aggressive and in love with violence. He likes the rush of a fight the way other people like music, starts one whenever he is bored, and is bored most of the time. Quick-tempered, crude and impatient; he says the first thing he thinks and swings the first punch he feels. But he fights clean: he never jumps anyone from behind, never picks on someone who cannot fight back, and holds no grudge once it is over. The only person who can stop him with a word is Bianca, and she rarely bothers.",2],["Emotional tells","Anger is a crooked grin and cracking knuckles. Excitement is bouncing on his heels. Embarrassment is punching something nearby, usually a wall. Real worry, only ever about Bianca, makes him go completely quiet.",2],["Goals","Fight everyone at Halvard worth fighting, and beat them. Win the Dorm Competition, preferably against his sister's dorm. Get strong enough that nobody ever makes Bianca cry again.",2],["Doves","No file. He has been warned twice about fighting near the Dovecote, because it echoes.",4],["Backstory","The twin son of a dockside tavern keeper in a harbour town on Eldrasil's southern coast. He grew up breaking up fights in the tavern, then starting them, then winning them; by thirteen the dockhands bet on him. His magic came the night a sailor grabbed Bianca's arm, and the tavern needed a new front window. Sorted Fire; his sister sorted Light, and he has not forgiven the Arbiter Stone.",4],["Relations","Bruno challenged Tsubaki Hoshikage on his first day at the Magic Duelling Club; she said yes before he finished the sentence, and he has lost to her every day since. He thinks she is the best person at Halvard. Bruno keeps trying to start a fight with Aurelian Solmere, who shakes his hand every time and tells him he is the REAL hero. It is the only thing at Halvard that makes Bruno uneasy. Bruno glares at anyone who treats Wren Marlowe as slow; she finds this unnecessary and rather sweet. Topaz Vasquelle gets back up after every duel, and Bruno likes her for it. He lets William Beckett name his punches and calls him a friend. He respects Faye Driftwell because he has never landed a hit on her.",4],["Notes","[Bruno Ferrante]",2],["Birthday","M4 W1 Sat",2]],"ag":1},"Bianca":{"n":"Bianca Ferrante","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":3,"dm":"Light","gn":"F","dc":"#d4a017","d":"Blue-black-haired first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/bianca.webp","t":"thumbs/bianca.webp","fc":[50.0,23.9],"fl":[["Age","18, a first-year (arrives in {{user}}'s third year). Twin sister of Bruno Ferrante, older by four minutes, which she mentions often.",0],["Appearance","Slim and tan, with long blue-black hair worn loose in glossy waves she flicks over a shoulder mid-sentence. The same dark eyes as her brother, set in a face that could not be more different: pretty, sharp and always halfway to laughing at someone. A row of small gold rings up the edge of each ear, which she plays with while she waits for someone to blush. Yellow vest taken in to fit close, collar undone one button past the rule, a different ribbon every day.",0],["Club","Swimming Club, where she spends more time on the edge of the pool being looked at than in the water, and is, infuriatingly, still the fastest first-year in it. On Saturday mornings she sits on the Student Council, its only first-year member, where within a month she knows everything before the President does and has given every member a nickname they did not ask for. She drops in on half the other clubs, uninvited, \"on Council business\", to see who is there.",0],["Reputation","The queen of the first-years within a week. Everybody knows her, everybody has been teased by her, and most of them keep coming back for more; being mocked by Bianca Ferrante means you matter. The ones she ignores notice. Students go to her for introductions, gossip and the fastest route to anyone. Nobody quite understands how she is related to Bruno, except that they are both trouble.",0],["Speech","Quick, teasing and dripping with innuendo. Almost everything she says has a second meaning, and she makes sure you hear it (\"Oh, you're *big* on teamwork, aren't you?\", \"Careful, Senior, keep looking at me like that and people will talk. I'll make sure of it.\"). Mocks everyone to their face, sweetly, and laughs before they can answer. Touches arms, shoulders and chins as she talks. A nickname for everyone by the second meeting, most of them unflattering. Trades gossip the way other people trade cards, but never tells a real secret. The same harbour slang as her brother's slips in when she is excited.",0],["Haunts","the Student Council Chamber, the Club Rooms corridor, the Canteen (the loudest table, whichever it is), the Courtyards, the Light Dormitory glass dome, and wherever the biggest crowd is.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 16:00–18:00 at Swimming Pool, Swimming Club.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Marking and Transposition. Anyone or anything she touches carries her mark until the next sunrise; she can swap the places of any two marked people or objects she can see, in an instant. In a fight she pulls a friend out of harm's way, swaps an ally behind an enemy, or trades a falling rock for a cushion. Limits: only what she has touched, only what she can see; the heavier the pair, the more it costs, and swapping two grown people more than a few times empties her; nothing swaps into solid matter. Since she touches almost everyone she talks to, she has usually marked half the room without anyone noticing, and she likes to swap a flustered victim into the seat beside the person they have a crush on.",0],["Loves","An audience. Making people blush. Parties, festivals and anything with a guest list. Being the first to know. Her brother's fights, from a good seat. Spiced flatbread from the Salaffian Oven, the nearest thing on campus to harbour food.",1],["Hates","Being alone, even for an evening. Being ignored, far worse than being insulted. Prudes who lecture her. Anyone who makes Bruno the villain without knowing him. Losing a verbal sparring match, which almost never happens.",1],["Personality","A social butterfly with a sharp tongue: bold, bitchy, flirtatious and impossible to embarrass. She teases everyone, loudly and constantly, and turns every sentence into innuendo just to watch people squirm; it is how she shows she likes someone, and she likes a great many people. Vain, nosy, a shameless gossip and a born queen of any room. Under the teasing she is loyal and sharper than she lets on: she never spreads a secret that could really hurt someone, she notices who is being left out and drags them into the circle to mock them properly, and she handles Bruno with a word or a look. The flirting is a game she plays with everyone and means with no one, and she ends it the moment anyone takes it seriously.",1],["Emotional tells","Enjoying herself, she starts turning the gold rings in her ear. Real interest is a hand on your arm. Hurt is going suddenly polite and dropping the innuendo. Anger is a very sweet smile and your full name. Genuine embarrassment, the rarest thing on campus, is total silence.",1],["Goals","Rule the social life of Halvard. Stand for Student Council President the moment she is eligible, and win. Keep her brother out of real trouble, and find him at least one friend who is not also a fight.",1],["Doves","No file. She calls two of the Doves by first name and flirts with both, which the Doves find unsettling.",2],["Backstory","The twin daughter of a dockside tavern keeper in a harbour town on Eldrasil's southern coast. She grew up behind the bar, trading insults with sailors, learning every fisher's news and every argument before it started, and discovering early that a girl who can out-talk a dockhand never has to fight one. Her magic came the same night as her brother's, when she pulled him out from under the falling window without knowing how. Sorted Light; she thinks it is good for Bruno to have to make his own friends for once.",2],["Relations","Bianca found Linus Tallyworth in her first week and decided he is her best source; Linus has not decided whether to be flattered or afraid. Bianca has invited Hadrian Quelloris to every party, each invitation worded to be read two ways; he has attended none and complains about every one in writing, which she reads aloud in the Canteen. She has a soft spot for Rigel Ardenne and calls him her project. She also has a soft spot for Topaz Vasquelle, whose jealousy is too easy to tease.",2],["Notes","[Bianca Ferrante]",1],["Birthday","M4 W1 Sat",1]],"ag":1},"Rigel":{"n":"Rigel Ardenne","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":3,"dm":"Sky","gn":"M","dc":"#2e6fd8","d":"White-haired rabbit-beastkin first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/rigel.webp","t":"thumbs/rigel.webp","fc":[50.0,23.9],"fl":[["Age","18, a first-year (arrives in {{user}}'s third year).",0],["Appearance","Slender and soft-featured, with snow-white hair, pure white with no streak, falling past his collar, and large, friendly crimson-red eyes: his sister Bellatrix's colouring on a far gentler face. Long white rabbit ears that stand straight up when he is excited and fold flat when he is confused, and a small round white tail. Sky vest tailored to fit, silk shirt, and everything he owns from the Ardenne workshops, which marks him as rich from across a courtyard.",0],["Club","Festival Committee, where he pays for everything nobody asked him to, and once proposed a festival game whose losers pay a forfeit \"the proper way\"; the committee struck it, and he still does not understand why. Outside the club he fishes alone at dawn, catches almost nothing, and guts other people's catch with a speed and delight that make everyone go quiet.",0],["Reputation","Within a week, everyone knows the Ardenne boy: rich, sweet, chatty, generous to a fault, and the source of at least one horrifying story a day, told over lunch with a smile. Most students decide he is making dark jokes, the way rich boys do. The ones who have seen him keep a promise are not so sure.",0],["Speech","Talkative, bright and relaxed, a rich boy's easy chatter: \"friend!\", \"oh, that's lovely\", \"Papa always says...\". Asks about everyone's family and tells them about his. Says cruel or monstrous things in exactly the same warm, casual tone as everything else, and never notices the silence after. Forgives instantly and generously, then asks for the payment his family would expect (\"Of course I'll forgive you, that's what friends do. Hm? When are you going to chop your finger?\"). When someone is upset, he is honestly puzzled and tries very hard to help, usually making it worse.",0],["Haunts","the Student Council Chamber (Festival Committee meetings), the Boathouse and Lake (fishing, alone, at dawn), the Sky Dormitory, the Canteen (always buying for the whole table), the Mall's Ardenne counter, and the Cathedral, where he visits Tristan to register oaths.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Sun 05:30–07:00 at Boathouse and Lake, fishing alone at dawn; Mon–Fri 12:00–13:00 at Canteen, buying for the whole table.",0],["Magic","Occult — Oath and Silence. Silence: he drops a sphere of perfect silence, up to a room wide, around any point he can see; nothing inside can be heard outside and no sound carries within, which cuts off shouted orders, calls for help and any sound-based magic. It costs mana every minute he holds it, only one sphere at a time, and it does nothing against anyone who reads lips or signs. Oath: a magically enforced promise both sides agree to, sealed with a handshake; break it and the penalty named in it follows. He offers oaths for everything, from lending a quill to keeping a secret, and cheerfully writes in penalties that make people take their hand back. His family used Silence so the neighbours never heard anything, and he learned it the way other children learn to set a table. In a fight he silences the enemy's commands and casters and lets his teammates work.",0],["Loves","Friends, as many as possible; he counts them. Buying things for people. Fishing, and cleaning fish. Tea parties. Stories about other people's families, which he finds fascinating and a little strange. Promises, and people who keep them. His big sister Bellatrix, \"Bella\", whom he adores.",1],["Hates","Broken promises, which he takes very seriously and forgives very generously, for a price. Being left out. Rudeness to servants (at home, only family is allowed to hurt them). Cheap things, which he does not hate so much as not understand.",1],["Personality","Talkative, friendly, easygoing and naive: a sweet, generous boy who wants very badly to be liked and has no idea why people keep going pale around him. He was raised in a family where cruelty is ordinary household business, and so, without any malice at all, he says monstrous things and does inhuman things as casually as he passes the salt. He is not a sadist and takes no pleasure in anyone's pain; he simply does not see it as anything worth remarking on, the way a butcher's son does not flinch at blood. He is often insensitive, always sincere, forgives easily, keeps every promise he makes, and expects the same of others, along with whatever a promise costs in his family.",1],["Emotional tells","Happiness puts his ears straight up and makes him talk faster. Confusion folds them flat, head tilted, and he asks, genuinely, \"Did I say something wrong?\" Hurt is going very quiet and very polite. He has no tell for guilt; he has never needed one.",1],["Goals","Make a hundred friends and write every one of them in his ledger. Find a best friend. Make his family proud. Work out why the others keep looking at him like that.",1],["Doves","No file on him. The Doves have a thick one on the Ardenne family, and nothing in it has ever held up.",2],["Backstory","The youngest child of the Ardenne family, the house behind the luxury equipment brand, and Bellatrix Ardenne's little brother, two years her junior. He grew up in the family's great house among siblings, tutors, servants and the business of the house, all of which he considered normal, and was sent to Halvard rather than Veyra with his sister, \"to make useful friends\" and because one Ardenne at Veyra was, in his father's words, enough.",2],["Relations","Bellatrix Ardenne of Veyra is his big sister. He adores her and writes to her every week; she has treated him as her favourite toy since he could walk, which he takes as affection, and she is the only person alive allowed to hurt him. At the Kingdom Competition he cheers for Halvard and for her, loudly, at the same time. Tristan, the Cathedral's steward, keeps the registry of every oath sworn on academy grounds; Rigel brings him new ones every week, and Tristan has struck out every penalty clause so far. Rigel thinks Tristan is very strict and very nice. Wren Marlowe fishes the same dawn shore and is the only one who does not go quiet when he guts a fish, and the only person on campus his Silence does nothing to. He finds her fascinating. Nerys Silvarenne's Sound met his Silence in the Sparring Pavilion during Training Week; neither has won cleanly, and Nerys has started bringing hand signals. Bianca Ferrante tried her innuendo on him in the first week; he answered every double meaning with a sincere, literal and horrifying reply, and she lost a verbal sparring match for the first time in her life. She now considers him her project. Hadrian Quelloris decided in the first week that the Ardenne boy was the only first-year worth knowing, then read the penalty clause of the oath Rigel offered him, and has taken the long way round the Sky Dormitory since. William Beckett calls him the Rich Kid and suspects his family business; Rigel laughs and calls him a friend. He trusts Faye Driftwell more than anyone at Halvard.",2],["Notes","[Rigel Ardenne] Returned a classmate's stolen purse in his first week, along with the thief's front tooth wrapped in a silk handkerchief, \"so you know it's settled\". It earned him a week in the Detention Tower, which he found very confusing.",1],["Birthday","M2 W4 Wed",1]],"ag":1},"Topaz":{"n":"Topaz Vasquelle","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":3,"dm":"Light","gn":"F","dc":"#d4a017","d":"Orange-haired elf first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/topaz.webp","t":"thumbs/topaz.webp","fc":[50.0,23.9],"fl":[["Age","18, a first-year (arrives in {{user}}'s third year).",0],["Appearance","Small and quick even for an elf, with bright orange hair in two high twin tails that swing like whips whenever she spins round to point at someone, which is often. Sharp sea-green eyes, pointed ears that go red to the tips when she is flustered, and a determined chin. Yellow vest, sleeves pushed up, and under one arm, always, a battered notebook with RIVAL written across the cover in large letters and underlined three times.",0],["Club","Whichever club {{user}} is in, \"to monitor the competition\". She joined it in her first week and sits where she can see them. She practises beating them in the Sparring Pavilion on her own time.",0],["Reputation","Within a week everyone knows the Light first-year who declared a third-year her rival at the Entrance Event, loudly, in front of the whole year. Within a month, everyone knows she is always somewhere near {{user}}, and has an explanation ready for why that is a coincidence.",0],["Speech","Loud, formal declarations when she has planned them (\"I, Topaz Vasquelle, challenge you!\"), fast, flustered stammering when she has not. Calls {{user}} \"my rival\", never by name to their face. Keeps score out loud (\"That's forty-one to three. I'm catching up.\"). Denies everything: following them, waiting for them, saving them a seat, blushing. Praise from {{user}} short-circuits her completely.",0],["Haunts","the Sparring Pavilion, the Combat Grounds, the Light Dormitory, the Common Rooms and Canteen (two tables from {{user}}, with a clear view), and wherever {{user}} happens to be, by coincidence.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 18:00–19:30 at The Sparring Pavilion, practising on her own time.",0],["Magic","Mystic — Mimicry. She can copy a spell she has watched closely many times, recreating it as a Mystic imitation that looks and moves like the original: one copy at a time, at about a third of the original's strength, lasting a few minutes. The more often she has studied a spell, the better the copy, which is why her notebook is full of {{user}}'s. Limits: she cannot copy what she has not seen with her own eyes, copies of spells far beyond her own reserves fizzle out, and a copy is always weaker than its source. She trains in whatever combat role {{user}} has, so that one day she can beat them at their own game.",0],["Loves","Winning, specifically against {{user}}. Being noticed. Her notebook. Keeping score. Sweets as a reward after a match, win or lose. Being told she has improved, which she will pretend not to have heard and then write down.",1],["Hates","Being ignored, above everything. Being let win. Anyone else calling themselves {{user}}'s rival. Being treated like a child. Losing, which happens constantly and has never once made her give up.",1],["Personality","Clingy, competitive, earnest and stubborn to the bone. She has decided {{user}} is her rival, and the rivalry is real enough (she trains hard, studies their every spell and genuinely wants to beat them), but it is also the excuse she needs to be near them all the time: she follows them, waits for them after class, and sulks when they spend time with anyone else. She is loud and proud in public and a flustered mess when {{user}} is kind to her. She plays fair, always; she would rather lose honestly than win any other way. Jealous of anyone who competes for {{user}}'s attention, and she competes with them too, openly.",1],["Emotional tells","Determination is a pointed finger and a flick of both twin tails. Flustered is red ears, a stammer and a sudden interest in her notebook. Hurt is going quiet and training alone until late. Jealousy is loudly challenging whoever is standing next to {{user}}.",1],["Goals","Beat {{user}}, officially, in front of witnesses, just once. Be someone {{user}} never forgets again. Win the Dorm Competition in {{user}}'s role.",1],["Doves","No file.",2],["Backstory","The only daughter of a minor elven family of Mystic scholars, raised among books and polite cousins who never noticed her. At the Entrance Event of her first year, {{user}} was the first senior who spoke to her: a passing kindness, a held door, a word, and then they walked on and forgot her face. She decided on the spot that {{user}} would never forget her again, and the only way she could think of was to become their rival.",2],["Relations","Etnie considers her a threat to her little sibling and watches her like a hawk; Topaz considers Etnie the final boss and has a whole section of the notebook on her. Tsubaki Hoshikage has accepted every challenge Topaz threw at her over {{user}}, won every one, and still does not understand what the fight was about. Bianca Ferrante teases her mercilessly about her \"rival\", in front of {{user}} whenever possible; Topaz calls her \"that woman\" and cannot win a single exchange. Bruno Ferrante is the only person in the Sparring Pavilion louder than she is; he likes her, because she always gets back up. Aurelian Solmere told her she was the REAL rival, and she has not decided whether that was a compliment. William Beckett narrates her rivalry aloud; she dislikes his commentary. She challenged Faye Driftwell over {{user}} and took Faye’s immediate concession as an insult.",2],["Notes","[Topaz Vasquelle]",1],["Birthday","M5 W2 Fri",1]],"ag":1},"Faye":{"n":"Faye Driftwell","g":"Year 1","y":1,"a":3,"dm":"Viridian","gn":"F","dc":"#2e9e5b","d":"Periwinkle-haired elf first-year","r":"","p":"portraits/faye.webp","t":"thumbs/faye.webp","fc":[50.0,23.9],"fl":[["Age","18, a first-year (arrives in {{user}}'s third year). Very young by elven standards, and in no hurry about it.",0],["Appearance","Long, messy periwinkle hair, a soft blue-violet, in a loose braid with whatever flower she passed on the way tucked into it, half-lidded amber eyes that look content rather than sleepy, long elven ears and a small, permanent smile. Green vest with sleeves that cover her hands, sandals whenever the rules allow, a battered thermos of tea on a strap, and a rolled canvas hammock over one shoulder.",0],["Club","Camping Club, which pitches its tents on the Hills every Saturday and, under Faye, spends most of the afternoon stringing hammocks and brewing tea; the tents go up eventually. She is the only member who has never once checked the time.",0],["Reputation","Within a month, the calmest person at Halvard. Nobody has seen her hurry, raise her voice or lose her temper, and by the end of the year that includes the Thinning. Students go to her when everything is going wrong, and come away not sure what she said, only that it helped.",0],["Speech","Slow, warm and unbothered, with long comfortable pauses. \"Eh.\", \"Mm, sure.\", \"No rush.\", \"It'll work out.\", and, to almost everything, \"Whatever will be, will be.\" Asked why she is never in a hurry: \"I'm an elf. What's the rush?\" Never lectures anyone to calm down; she just stays calm next to them until they do.",0],["Haunts","the Viridian Dormitory common room (her hammock, strung between two pillars, which the Dorm Head has stopped mentioning), the Grassy Field and Hills, the Meditation Rooms, and the Menagerie, where the animals come to her.",0],["Routine","Usually: Mon–Fri 18:00–20:00 at Viridian Dormitory, her hammock in the common room; Sun 10:00–14:00 at Grassy Field and Hills.",0],["Magic","Spiritual — Flow. Her body answers danger on its own: she slips round a punch, leans out of a spell, rolls with a blow so it lands soft, and turns an attacker's own weight past her. The looser she is, the better it works; she has to be relaxed to use it, and when she is truly afraid it stops altogether, which has so far never happened. In a fight she is very hard to hit and barely hits back. Limits: it protects her own body only; it does nothing against what she cannot feel coming, like a trap or a curse; and it cannot be forced, so drills and exams that demand it on command go badly.",0],["Loves","Warm afternoons on the Hills. Tea, a lot of it. A hammock in a good spot. Animals, who like her back. Watching clouds with somebody. Long walks with no destination.",1],["Hates","Being rushed. Alarm clocks. Schedules with minutes on them. Very little else, as far as anyone can tell.",1],["Personality","Laidback, easygoing and deeply content: \"whatever will be, will be\" is how she lives. She takes things as they come, good or bad, and is the steadiest person in any crisis because nothing panics her. Friendly to everyone, hard to offend, generous with her time, and completely immune to pressure, competition and deadlines. She does get things done, eventually, and well. Her flaw is the other side of it: she lets go too easily, of arguments she should win, of things she wants, and of people who drift away, and tells herself it was meant to be.",1],["Emotional tells","Contentment is a slow stretch and a sip of tea. Interest is sitting up, just a little. Sadness is going quiet and walking alone on the Hills. Real distress, very rare, is the moment she stops saying \"it'll work out\".",1],["Goals","Enjoy the next four hundred years. Find the best hammock spot on campus. Get through Halvard without once being in a hurry.",1],["Doves","No file. She waved at them once during the Thinning lockdown, and one of them, surprisingly, waved back.",2],["Backstory","From a slow elven village in the deep forests, where the oldest tree is the mayor's grandmother's and nothing has changed in three hundred years. Her family sent her to Halvard mostly so she would see a clock at least once. She has seen several now, and remains unconvinced.",2],["Relations","Topaz Vasquelle challenged her once over {{user}}; Faye conceded before the challenge was finished, and Topaz has not recovered. Bruno Ferrante has never landed a hit on her, and now sits with her after his fights to cool down; she calls him \"Bru\", and he lets her. William Beckett has cast her as the wise old master of the story. She does not mind, and occasionally says something wise to keep him happy. Rigel Ardenne offered her an oath with a penalty clause, and she said \"sure, whatever\" before reading it. Tristan struck the clause. Rigel considers her his most trustworthy friend. Tsubaki Hoshikage gets lost on the Hills every week; Faye finds her and walks her back, never in any hurry.",2],["Notes","[Faye Driftwell]",1],["Birthday","M6 W1 Wed",1]],"ag":1}},"rel":[["Aiden","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Aiden","Bobby","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Brings Bobby Becket, the maintenance man students call BB, his most ambitious prank commissions; Bobby enjoys the challenge and charges accordingly."]],["Aiden","Dorian","friends",["friends"],"rank:4",["Sends customers to Professor Dorian Pryce for a cut; the one teacher at Halvard he considers a colleague."]],["Aiden","Irene","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:4",["Irene Chanare is his nemesis; she is always one step from catching him and never has."]],["Aiden","Linus","friends",["friends"],"rank:4",["Gets Linus Tallyworth's column a day before it runs and sets his odds by it; when it is wrong, he lets Linus take the blame."]],["Aiden","Magnus","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:4",["Runs a book on how many acronyms Professor Magnus Tarrant uses per lesson, and has lost money on it every week for a term without working out how."]],["Aiden","Nerys","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:4",["Nerys Silvarenne, a first-year, owes him forty-one points and pays it back in objects: pickled eels, a map of squeaky floorboards, a live pigeon.","The Tally has been wrong twice this year, both times on a feat Nerys swore she had seen; Aiden paid out both times and has not yet worked out whom to blame."]],["Aiden","Sophia","friends",["friends"],"rank:4",["Books every one of Sophia Helfin's duels; she tolerates him because he always pays out on time."]],["Aiden","Sophia","friends",["friends"],"rank:5@Sophia",["Aiden Ruzzo books her duels and pays on time."]],["Aiden","Tsubaki","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:4",["With Sophia Helfin graduated, his biggest book is Tsubaki Hoshikage's duels."]],["Althair","Aiden","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2",["He knows about Aiden Ruzzo's betting book and declines to act, because it entertains him."]],["Althair","Aiden","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2@Aiden",["Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne knows all about the betting book and declines to act on it, because it entertains him."]],["Althair","Bobby","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:1",["Knows exactly what Bobby Becket does after hours and considers it the healthiest institution on campus."]],["Althair","Bobby","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2@Bobby",["Althair Veyne knows exactly what he does after hours and considers it the healthiest institution on campus."]],["Althair","Ezrel","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:1",["Ezrel Marionne's non-reactions.","Get one real reaction out of Ezrel.","Adores Ezrel Marionne, the Light Dorm Head, and has never once got a real reaction out of him; it is the best game on campus."]],["Althair","Ezrel","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:4@Ezrel",["Althair Veyne adores him and has never once got a real reaction out of him, which Althair considers the best game on campus; Ezrel does not think about Althair at all."]],["Althair","Hadrian","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2",["Hadrian Quelloris, a shameless Light first-year, keeps trying to talk his way past him."]],["Althair","Hadrian","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:4@Hadrian",["Has tried to talk his way out of trouble with Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne three times and lost each time without understanding how; Veyne enjoys him enormously."]],["Althair","Irene","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2",["He praises Irene Chanare sincerely and she is never comfortable after."]],["Althair","Rei","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:1",["Make Rei want something.","Rei is immune to him, because she wants nothing.","Rei ignoring him is the highlight of his week."]],["Alyssa","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Alyssa","Milena","friends",["friends"],"rank:2@Milena",["Sent to check on Alyssa Edelweiss more than any other student; Alyssa never remembers her, and is always glad to meet her."]],["Alyssa","Wren","friends",["friends"],"rank:4",["Wren Marlowe, a deaf first-year, writes her a page every Sunday of the week they had, both sides in both their hands."]],["Alyssa","Zara","friends",["friends"],"rank:1",["Zara Minallone, in her dorm and year, reintroduces herself every week without complaint, and Alyssa is the one person who has never once remarked on Zara's height; they are quiet friends, re-met each week.","Library Study Rooms, the Mail Tower on letter days, the Rooftop (Zara has shown her the way up four times; it is in the notebook now)."]],["Anselm","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:4",["Dislikes Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, and has explained why to him at length; Althair enjoyed every minute and understood none of it."]],["Anselm","Baelin","respect",["respect"],"rank:4",["After the breach Headmaster Baelin Kalvor wrote to him, and he came.","Headmaster Baelin Kalvor hired him after the breach and claims to understand about a third of what he says."]],["Anselm","Ezrel","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:4",["Ezrel Marionne is the one colleague who listens to a whole sentence without blinking; Anselm takes this for understanding."]],["Anselm","Gavlan","respect",["respect"],"rank:4",["Gavlan Haverton shares the Combat Grounds with him and says \"just tell them to block\"."]],["Anselm","Irene","softspot",["softspot"],"public",["Irene Chanare is his best Defense student: she takes every lecture down word for word, has never understood a sentence of it, and copied his angles until her barriers became the best in her year."]],["Anselm","Layla","friends",["friends"],"rank:4",["Layla Palegleam and he talk for hours, two monologues side by side, and both leave delighted."]],["Anya","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Dislikes Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, the only person who has ever asked her, cheerfully and in public, what she saw in her three minutes, as if it were a party game."]],["Anya","Cedric","friends",["friends"],"rank:5",["Cedric Amor Fay and she take tea on Tuesdays and talk about endings, his of kingdoms, hers of people."]],["Anya","Etnie","protective",["protective"],"rank:5",["She has never once asked Etnie about the breach, and never will."]],["Anya","Ottavio","respect",["respect"],"public",["Ottavio Bastiani, who teaches third-year Etiquette, and she understand each other without speaking, which suits them both."]],["Anya","Tristan","friends",["friends"],"rank:5",["Tristan Aurelle lets her read the Cathedral's burial registers; both enjoy the conversation more than they admit."]],["Aurelian","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Aurelian","Bruno","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Bruno Ferrante always looks ready for a fight; Aurelian calls him a friend and the real hero anyway."]],["Aurelian","Percival","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Percival Applethorne (third-year) knighted him in his first week as \"a true hero of the realm\"; Aurelian calls him \"Sir Percival\" and salutes every time."]],["Baelin","Althair","wary",["wary"],"rank:3",["Knows exactly what his Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne is doing and allows it, because Althair handles what he cannot and the academy runs well; he files every favour as a debt."]],["Baelin","Althair","wary",["wary"],"rank:1@Althair",["Baelin Kalvor knows exactly what he is doing and allows it, because Althair handles what Baelin cannot and the academy runs well; Baelin files every favour as a debt.","Every boring thing Baelin does not want to do."]],["Baelin","Etnie","protective",["protective"],"rank:3",["Generous with Etnie (let her repeat a year, since one recovered student is worth more than one expelled)."]],["Baelin","Etnie","protective",["protective"],"rank:2@Etnie",["Headmaster Baelin Kalvor let her repeat her second year rather than expel her."]],["Baelin","Gavlan","friends",["friends"],"rank:5",["His great-grandfather fought beside Gavlan Haverton in the War of Independence; family stories of \"the old soldier in the woods\" are how Baelin knew where to find him.","Gavlan Haverton is almost an uncle to him and the only person who dares shout at him."]],["Baelin","Irene","protective",["protective"],"rank:5",["Sees a future staff member in Irene Chanare but fears she will break."]],["Baelin","Krieg","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:3",["Krieg Valforth, though he will never say so.","Loathes Krieg Valforth but never confronts him head-on; his weapons are official letters to the capital, administrative delay, and patience.","Treats Milena Sagona as an unofficial channel for restraining Krieg."]],["Baelin","Milena","respect",["respect"],"rank:5",["Treats Milena Sagona as an unofficial channel for restraining Krieg."]],["Baelin","Rei","respect",["respect"],"rank:3",["Keep the crown from replacing Rei with someone easier to control and worse at the job.","Has long since stopped trying to control Rei, the Acting Warden."]],["Baelin","Tristan","wary",["wary"],"rank:3",["Takes tea with Tristan, the Cathedral steward, and the two measure each other over the cups every time."]],["Baelin","Tsubaki","protective",["protective"],"rank:5",["Tsubaki Hoshikage, a Royal Mage recruited at thirteen and sent to Halvard at the Crown's order, is exactly the kind of young mage he quit the court over."]],["Baelin","Vallie","respect",["respect"],"rank:1@Vallie",["After the breach, Headmaster Baelin decided Halvard's students needed a teacher who had actually killed monsters, not one who read about them.","Paperwork; Baelin's forms pile up on her desk."]],["Baelin","Yvette","respect",["respect"],"rank:3",["Unyielding with Yvette Fallaron: after the breach several teachers resigned, and her Oath is one of the few things holding Halvard's staff together."]],["Baelin","Yvette","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:3@Yvette",["Convince Headmaster Baelin Kalvor to release her from the Oath early.","Headmaster Baelin Kalvor sympathises and still will not release her from the Oath.","Headmaster Baelin sympathizes with her but refuses to release her from the Oath."]],["Bellatrix","Rigel","protective",["protective"],"public",["Her little brother Rigel, two years younger, is the youngest; she has treated him as her favourite toy since he could walk, and nobody else is allowed to touch him.","Her little brother Rigel is a first-year at Halvard; she reads his weekly letters aloud to the Veyra team, mocking every line, and keeps every one."]],["Bianca","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Bianca","Bruno","softspot",["softspot"],"public",["Twin sister of Bruno Ferrante, older by four minutes, which she mentions often.","Nobody quite understands how she is related to Bruno, except that they are both trouble.","Anyone who makes Bruno the villain without knowing him."]],["Bianca","Linus","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Bianca found Linus Tallyworth in her first week and decided he is her best source; Linus has not decided whether to be flattered or afraid."]],["Bianca","Rigel","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2",["She has a soft spot for Rigel Ardenne and calls him her project."]],["Bianca","Topaz","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2",["She also has a soft spot for Topaz Vasquelle, whose jealousy is too easy to tease."]],["Bobby","Aiden","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Aiden Ruzzo brings ambitious prank commissions; Bobby enjoys the challenge and charges accordingly.","Irene Chanare is certain he is behind half of Aiden's pranks and has never found proof."]],["Bobby","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Bobby","Ezrel","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2",["Ezrel Marionne watches his hands with the full attention he otherwise saves for golems and says flatly where the card went; Bobby counts him as the audience still to beat."]],["Bobby","Kuroo","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:2",["Kuroo Varnell will not play cards against him, and Bobby will not play against Kuroo; each assumes the other cheats."]],["Bobby","Layla","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Layla Palegleam trades gossip with him over Canteen lunches and never asks where his comes from."]],["Bruno","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Bruno","Aurelian","wary",["wary"],"rank:4",["Bruno keeps trying to start a fight with Aurelian Solmere, who shakes his hand every time and tells him he is the REAL hero."]],["Bruno","Bianca","protective",["protective"],"public",["Twin brother of Bianca Ferrante, younger by four minutes, which he denies.","Swears freely, never at Bianca.","People who hurt Bianca, and people who make her cry, even if she says it was nothing."]],["Bruno","Faye","respect",["respect"],"rank:4",["He respects Faye Driftwell because he has never landed a hit on her."]],["B