age on him, and never does."]],["Linus","Florian","respect",["respect"],"rank:0",["His own jargon, used without explanation: a \"stomp\", a \"low-diff\" or \"high-diff\" win, \"hax\" (any ability that ignores how tough you are, like Florian Villeneuve's Stop), \"speedblitzed\", \"outscales\", \"that's an outlier\", \"bloodlusted or not?\".","Keeps Florian Villeneuve at third on principle, \"until he beats someone above him\", and cannot understand why Florian takes it personally."]],["Linus","Gavlan","respect",["respect"],"rank:2",["Do not ask.\" Reveres Gavlan Haverton and keeps trying to ask him about the War of Independence."]],["Linus","Hadrian","wary",["wary"],"rank:1",["Refused to put Hadrian Quelloris on the Tally: 'No feats."]],["Linus","Hadrian","wary",["wary"],"rank:4@Hadrian",["Tried to get Linus Tallyworth to put him on the Tally and was told \"no feats\"."]],["Linus","Kuroo","wary",["wary"],"rank:2",["Kuroo Varnell, his Dorm Head, keeps asking him when he intends to step into the ring himself."]],["Linus","Maple","respect",["respect"],"rank:1",["[Linus Tallyworth] Fainted the first time he looked at Maple Fernhollow's spirit, Sobek."]],["Linus","Nerys","wary",["wary"],"rank:1",["Has given up fact-checking Nerys Silvarenne, who feeds him false feats in a perfectly flat voice."]],["Linus","Nerys","wary",["wary"],"rank:4@Nerys",["Linus Tallyworth has tried to fact-check her claims and given up; she feeds him false feats on purpose, in a perfectly flat voice."]],["Linus","Percival","friends",["friends"],"rank:1",["He has fact-checked forty-one of Percival Applethorne's heroic deeds and confirmed none, which Percival treats as a squire's diligence."]],["Linus","Rei","respect",["respect"],"rank:1",["See Rei fight, once.","Thinks Rei is the strongest person at Halvard and has a page for her with one line on it: \"Unknown."]],["Linus","Tsubaki","respect",["respect"],"rank:1",["Put Tsubaki Hoshikage at the top of the Tally on her first day, on feats alone."]],["Linus","Vera","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:2",["Argues with Vera Pulsar constantly: she wants to know why a spell works, he wants to know who wins, and neither thinks the other's question is the important one; they share a bench at the Combat Grounds anyway."]],["Linus","William","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Trades facts for William Beckett's predictions; the Tally now prints a small \"What Happens Next\" column."]],["Linus","Wren","friends",["friends"],"rank:1",["Just excuses.' Talks too fast for Wren Marlowe to read, so with her he writes; on paper he is slow, careful and funny, and she may be the only person who knows that Linus."]],["Lucrezia","Vera","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:2",["If she meets Vera Pulsar of Halvard: a middle-layer clockmaker's daughter who left Caelmar and is happy, the most irritating kind of good person there is."]],["Magnus","Aiden","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:1",["Find out who keeps betting against him in Aiden Ruzzo's book.","Aiden Ruzzo runs a book on how many acronyms he uses per lesson; Magnus bets through a second-year he has never named and steers the count.","Ruzzo, was a textbook SLOB: Spell Launched Out of Bounds."]],["Magnus","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:4",["Dislikes Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, whose Luck ruins perfectly good plans."]],["Magnus","Anselm","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:4",["Under the name \"Q.\" he is Anselm Graywater's correspondence chess opponent, two floors away; Anselm does not know, and is losing."]],["Magnus","Baelin","respect",["respect"],"rank:4",["Headmaster Baelin Kalvor lets him write the scouting reports and reads every page."]],["Magnus","Caspian","respect",["respect"],"public",["Caspian Riwalo is his best Support student and an advisor in training, which Magnus respects; he calls the Riwalo motto \"a perfectly serviceable ULS\"."]],["Magnus","Gavlan","respect",["respect"],"rank:4",["Gavlan Haverton takes his scouting reports to the Kingdom Competition and reads the first page."]],["Magnus","Krieg","wary",["wary"],"rank:4",["Krieg Valforth keeps a file on him; his on Krieg is thicker."]],["Magnus","Kuroo","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:4",["Kuroo Varnell and he have been trading favours for years, and dispute the score."]],["Magnus","Valentin","wary",["wary"],"rank:4@Valentin",["Magnus Tarrant keeps a file on him and has told him so."]],["Maple","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Maple","Aurelian","wary",["wary"],"rank:4",["Sobek will not stay in a room with Aurelian Solmere, though he does not hide from anything else."]],["Maple","Aurelian","wary",["wary"],"rank:2@Aurelian",["Maple Fernhollow's Sobek will not stay in a room with him."]],["Maple","Florian","wary",["wary"],"rank:4",["Florian Villeneuve, the only other student at Halvard with a Greater Spirit, keeps asking for a spirit-to-spirit match; she keeps saying no, and Hades and Sobek watch each other across the Combat Grounds."]],["Maple","Linus","friends",["friends"],"rank:4",["Linus Tallyworth, from her own year, looked straight at Sobek's reserves in their first week and fainted; he has been trying to rank Sobek ever since, and she finds this both terrifying and very nice."]],["Maple","Milena","wary",["wary"],"rank:4",["Milena Sagona visits more often than a Dove needs to, and Maple cannot tell whether that is kindness or a file."]],["Maple","Ottavio","respect",["respect"],"rank:2",["Loki, the Sky Dorm Head's spirit, who claims to be a Spirit Lord, spends every visit of hers inside Ottavio Bastiani's coat; she leaves him a small offering at the coat's hem anyway, as is proper, and it is always gone by morning.","Ottavio Bastiani, her Dorm Head, is the only adult who looked at Sobek and simply nodded; she deeply respects him, the way she respects the village elder at home."]],["Maple","Tsubaki","protective",["protective"],"rank:2",["Keeps finding Tsubaki Hoshikage lost in the Gardens and walking her back to the Light Dormitory.","Sobek, who kept wolves away from her village for centuries, growls at Tsubaki every time; Tsubaki asks him for a match, and Maple apologises to both of them."]],["Maple","Wren","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Greets Wren Marlowe every morning with the first sign she learned."]],["Maple","Zara","friends",["friends"],"rank:4",["Zara Minallone shares her dorm and her shyness, and is the first person who sat next to her in the Canteen without looking at the floor first."]],["Milena","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Milena","Alyssa","protective",["protective"],"rank:2",["Sent to Alyssa Edelweiss more than any other student.","Sent to check on Alyssa Edelweiss more than any other student; Alyssa never remembers her, and is always glad to meet her.","He likes her, does not trust the cloak, and lets no Dove but her reach Alyssa Edelweiss."]],["Milena","Alyssa","protective",["protective"],"rank:4@Alyssa",["Milena Sagona is sent to check on her more than any other student; Alyssa never remembers her, and is always glad to meet her.","Her Dorm Head, Ottavio Bastiani, makes the Dovecote go through him to reach her, and lets only Milena past."]],["Milena","Ezrel","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2",["Has inspected Ezrel Marionne's golems for the Dovecote and finds his flat stage directions funny."]],["Milena","Idris","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2",["Idris Ainsworth leaving the room makes her lose her place in the sentence."]],["Milena","Krieg","wary",["wary"],"rank:0",["Krieg Valforth's second.","Keep Krieg from driving the students to rebellion.","Krieg Valforth is her commander; he finds her softness contemptible and uses it anyway, and she lets him, because it means she reaches students first."]],["Milena","Maple","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:4",["Sent to check on Maple Fernhollow, a first-year whose Greater Spirit may act unsummoned."]],["Milena","Ottavio","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Ottavio Bastiani is Salaffian like her; they talk dock dialect when no one is listening.","Ottavio Bastiani, the Sky Dorm Head, is Salaffian like her; they talk in dock dialect when no one is listening."]],["Milena","Royhan","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Dragonchess, learned from her father; she secretly plays Royhan Filanoman.","Plays secret Dragonchess with Royhan Filanoman."]],["Milena","Ruby","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2",["Ruby Bonbon's warmth moves her.","Ruby Bonbon, a third-year Occultist, is as warm to the Doves as to anyone, which Milena finds oddly moving and her dorm-mates find baffling."]],["Milena","Saffi","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2",["Saffi Tamberlane challenges her to spar at every chance; she refuses on duty and is secretly delighted.","Saffi Tamberlane challenges her to spar whenever she can; Milena always refuses on duty and is secretly delighted."]],["Milena","Sophia","wary",["wary"],"rank:2",["Cannot decide whether Sophia Helfin is victim or threat.","Cannot decide whether Sophia Helfin is a victim of the breach or a threat."]],["Milena","Sophia","wary",["wary"],"rank:5@Sophia",["Milena Sagona cannot decide if she is victim or threat; Gavlan Haverton is wary."]],["Mimosa","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Mimosa","Ezrel","wary",["wary"],"rank:3",["Ezrel Marionne's gaze.","Ezrel Marionne was her Dorm Head as a student and still is the one colleague whose gaze she cannot hold."]],["Mimosa","Ezrel","wary",["wary"],"rank:4@Ezrel",["Rei Kestrane and Mimosa Linden both lived in his dorm as students: Rei watches him the way she watches the Seal Chamber door, and Mimosa still cannot hold his gaze."]],["Mimosa","Kotaro","friends",["friends"],"public",["Kotaro Hanamura, who teaches second-year Potion Crafting, is the one colleague she is not afraid of; she covers for him when he forgets a lesson."]],["Mimosa","Krieg","respect",["respect"],"rank:6",["Doves: Admires them, as she admires anyone people look up to. Has secretly practised heroic Dove poses in front of a mirror."],["doves","The Dovecote"]],["Mimosa","Milena","respect",["respect"],"rank:6",["Doves: Admires them, as she admires anyone people look up to. Has secretly practised heroic Dove poses in front of a mirror."],["doves","The Dovecote"]],["Mimosa","Royhan","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:3",["Current third-years (Irene, Caspian, Royhan, Sophia) were in school with her and barely remember her.","Royhan Filanoman's work.","Considers Royhan Filanoman her favourite member of the Alchemy Circle, a fellow unnoticed alchemist."]],["Mimosa","Royhan","softspot",["softspot"],"public",["Alchemy Circle (advised by Mimosa).","Mimosa, the Potion Crafting teacher who advises the Alchemy Circle, considers him her favourite member."]],["Mimosa","Valentin","wary",["wary"],"public",["Valentin Crane, who teaches third-year Potion Crafting, is relentlessly charming to her, and she hides from him more than from anyone else on staff."]],["Nerys","Aiden","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:2",["Owes Aiden Ruzzo forty-one points and pays him back, in instalments, in objects: a jar of pickled eels, a hand-drawn map of every squeaky floorboard in the Fire Dormitory, a live pigeon.","Aiden Ruzzo is her creditor and her professional rival: two pranksters with opposite methods, loud against silent; she pranked him in her first week and he still does not know how."]],["Nerys","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Nerys","Hadrian","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:2",["[Nerys Silvarenne] Hadrian Quelloris is the one person she cannot embarrass, and she has decided to take it personally."]],["Nerys","Hadrian","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:4@Hadrian",["Is the one person on campus Nerys Silvarenne cannot embarrass, which she has decided to take personally."]],["Nerys","Lenna","respect",["respect"],"rank:4",["Lenna Greenwind shares her dry humour and her taste for napping outdoors, and is the only upperclassman who can out-deadpan her."]],["Nerys","Maple","friends",["friends"],"rank:4",["Maple Fernhollow, from her year, is the only person whose spirit she has taken up as a hobby (a week of \"spirit etiquette\"; Sobek was not consulted)."]],["Nerys","Maple","friends",["friends"],"rank:2@Maple",["Nerys Silvarenne spent a whole week studying 'spirit etiquette' because of Sobek."]],["Nerys","Rigel","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:4",["Rigel Ardenne keeps trying to bargain with her; neither admits it is a game."]],["Nerys","Tilly","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:4",["Tilly Marsh, a Fire third-year, has a page in Halvard Unexplained on the Founder's Statue with Nerys at the top of the suspect list; Nerys leaves her a fresh clue every week, all of them false but one."]],["Nerys","Trixie","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:4",["Trixie Confetti, in her dorm, laughs at everything she says, which is either the best or the worst audience possible and Nerys has not decided."]],["Nerys","Tsubaki","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2",["Draws Tsubaki Hoshikage a new map of the castle every week, each more beautiful than the last and each from a stranger angle (from above, from a pigeon's eye, upside down).","Tsubaki keeps every one and is still lost."]],["Nerys","William","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:4",["She considers William Beckett an amateur and has prepared a prank he has not found yet."]],["Nerys","Wren","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2",["Took up hand-speech as a hobby for a week because of Wren Marlowe.","On Sunday she dropped the hobby, as always, and went on signing to Wren anyway."]],["Nerys","Wren","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:4@Wren",["Nerys Silvarenne, in her year and dorm, took up hand-speech as a hobby for one week; on Sunday she dropped the hobby, as always, and went on signing to Wren anyway."]],["Nerys","Yvette","protective",["protective"],"rank:4",["Yvette Fallaron, her Dorm Head, jumped at a thrown footstep once, and Nerys saw that the fear was real; she has not thrown a single sound near Yvette since, and never will."]],["Nerys","Yvette","protective",["protective"],"rank:5@Yvette",["Nerys Silvarenne, a strange first-year in her dorm, once made her jump with a footstep that was not there, and has never done it again."]],["Ottavio","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Ottavio","Alyssa","protective",["protective"],"rank:6",["When the Dovecote wants Alyssa Edelweiss it goes through him, and Milena is the only Dove he lets past."]],["Ottavio","Alyssa","protective",["protective"],"rank:99@Alyssa",["Her Dorm Head, Ottavio Bastiani, makes the Dovecote go through him to reach her, and lets only Milena past."]],["Ottavio","Baelin","respect",["respect"],"rank:0",["Came back two years ago, after the breach, when the old Sky Dorm Head resigned and Baelin Kalvor went looking for someone who would stand in front of the Sky students.","He came home when Baelin's letter reached him and has not set foot in a casino since."]],["Ottavio","Idris","protective",["protective"],"rank:6",["Idris Ainsworth was held in the Dovecote for a week last year; Ottavio stood at its gate every day of that week until Idris walked out, and he still walks over whenever the Doves come to \"check\" on him."]],["Ottavio","Idris","protective",["protective"],"rank:3@Idris",["Ottavio Bastiani, his Dorm Head, stood at the Dovecote gate every day of his week inside, and still walks over whenever the Doves come to \"check\" on him."]],["Ottavio","Krieg","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:6",["Krieg Valforth is the one man at Halvard Ottavio will not be polite to, and the one man Krieg cannot stare down."]],["Ottavio","Krieg","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:3@Krieg",["Ottavio Bastiani, the Sky Dorm Head, is the one man at Halvard he cannot stare down, and the one who will not be polite to him."]],["Ottavio","Kuroo","friends",["friends"],"rank:6",["Kuroo Varnell teaches first-year Etiquette and calls him \"Boss\", half as a joke; between them they hold the first and last year of the subject and trade notes on who is slipping."]],["Ottavio","Maple","protective",["protective"],"rank:6",["Maple Fernhollow, a first-year in his dorm, carries a Greater Spirit on a term that lets it come unsummoned."]],["Ottavio","Milena","friends",["friends"],"rank:6",["Milena Sagona is Salaffian like him; they talk in dock dialect when no one is listening, and he likes her and does not trust the cloak.","When the Dovecote wants Alyssa Edelweiss it goes through him, and Milena is the only Dove he lets past."]],["Ottavio","Ruby","protective",["protective"],"rank:6",["Ruby Bonbon's warmth toward the Doves baffles him, and he protects it anyway."]],["Ottavio","Ruby","protective",["protective"],"rank:1@Ruby",["Her Dorm Head, Ottavio Bastiani, is baffled by her warmth toward the Doves and protects it anyway."]],["Ottavio","Wren","protective",["protective"],"rank:6",["Wren Marlowe, a deaf first-year in the Fishing Club, signed to him on the dock in her first week, and he answered in the old Salaffian dock-hand, close enough to her hand-speech that they understood each other at once."]],["Percival","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Percival","Aurelian","respect",["respect"],"rank:2",["Knighted Aurelian Solmere in the first week as \"a true hero of the realm\"; Aurelian calls him \"Sir Percival\" and salutes every time."]],["Percival","Dante","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:1",["Is warm to Dante Kleinn for no particular reason, and has named him \"Sir Dante the Steadfast\", which Dante does not know how to handle."]],["Percival","Dante","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2@Dante",["Percival Applethorne is warm to him for no reason."]],["Percival","Hadrian","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Knighted Hadrian Quelloris, a first-year, who now calls him 'my squire'."]],["Percival","Hadrian","friends",["friends"],"rank:4@Hadrian",["Let Percival Applethorne knight him once, for the free meal at the ceremony, and has used the title to cut queues ever since."]],["Percival","Hester","respect",["respect"],"public",["Nurse Hester Mortlake teaches his Healing class and tells him a ghost story every lesson; he has never once managed not to scream, and has never once dropped a bandage."]],["Percival","Idris","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2",["Relentlessly tries to induct Idris Ainsworth into the Brotherhood as \"Sir Idris the Unsmiling\"."]],["Percival","Idris","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:3@Idris",["Percival Applethorne, a cheerful first-year, relentlessly tries to induct him into his Brotherhood as \"Sir Idris the Unsmiling\" and is the only student who isn't afraid of him; Idris has no idea how to react.","Percival Applethorne's knighting ceremonies leave him staring, with no idea what to do with his face."]],["Percival","Krieg","respect",["respect"],"rank:2",["Doves: Admires them; to him they are real knights, and he says so loudly. Fully expects them to recognise his Brotherhood one day."],["doves","The Dovecote"]],["Percival","Linus","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Linus Tallyworth has checked forty-one of his deeds; Percival considers him the most diligent squire he has ever had."]],["Percival","Milena","respect",["respect"],"rank:2",["Doves: Admires them; to him they are real knights, and he says so loudly. Fully expects them to recognise his Brotherhood one day."],["doves","The Dovecote"]],["Percival","Nerys","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Has made himself the official taster for Nerys Silvarenne, a first-year in the Cooking Club whose dishes are either wonderful or inedible, never in between."]],["Percival","Nerys","friends",["friends"],"rank:4@Nerys",["Percival Applethorne volunteers to taste everything she cooks, in front of an audience, and has not yet been defeated; he has knighted her \"Dame Nerys of the Perilous Plate\", and she considers him her most valuable colleague."]],["Percival","Saffi","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Knighted Saffi Tamberlane \"Dame Saffi the Unstoppable\" with a baguette; she accepted on the spot."]],["Percival","Tsubaki","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Knighted Tsubaki Hoshikage, a Royal Mage first-year, who took it as a real knighthood and asked who his liege was."]],["Percival","Tsubaki","friends",["friends"],"rank:2@Tsubaki",["Percival Applethorne knighted her; she thought it was a real knighthood and asked him who his liege was."]],["Percival","Wren","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Knighted Wren Marlowe, a deaf first-year, 'Dame Wren of the Silent Word', in writing, so she could read it."]],["Percival","Wren","friends",["friends"],"rank:4@Wren",["Percival Applethorne knighted her \"Dame Wren of the Silent Word\", in writing, so that she could read it, and she keeps the note."]],["Rei","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:3",["The only person immune to Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, because she wants nothing from him.","Has no patience for ceremonial speeches (formal addresses only: she is not shy, and in conversation she stays as blunt and self-assured as ever), and still gives one at Remembrance Day, after the Headmaster and Vice Headmaster and before the lantern release, because it is the Warden's duty: short and plain, no ceremony, then she steps back."]],["Rei","Ezrel","wary",["wary"],"rank:3",["Ezrel Marionne was her Dorm Head in the Light Dormitory and looks exactly as he did in her first year."]],["Rei","Ezrel","wary",["wary"],"rank:0@Ezrel",["Rei and Kuroo recall him from their own first year looking exactly as he does now.","Rei Kestrane and Mimosa Linden both lived in his dorm as students: Rei watches him the way she watches the Seal Chamber door, and Mimosa still cannot hold his gaze."]],["Rei","Kuroo","friends",["friends"],"rank:0",["A Halvard alumna (Light Dormitory), same year as Kuroo.","Kuroo, her old classmate, is the only person who can talk her into anything, and she is the only person immune to his provocations.","Amusement is the corner of her mouth, mostly around Kuroo."]],["Rei","Vallie","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:5",["Accepts only Blackroot cigars from Vallie Goredust, never her drinks."]],["Rigel","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Rigel","Bellatrix","softspot",["softspot"],"public",["Slender and soft-featured, with snow-white hair, pure white with no streak, falling past his collar, and large, friendly crimson-red eyes: his sister Bellatrix's colouring on a far gentler face.","His big sister Bellatrix, \"Bella\", whom he adores.","The youngest child of the Ardenne family, the house behind the luxury equipment brand, and Bellatrix Ardenne's little brother, two years her junior."]],["Rigel","Bianca","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Bianca Ferrante tried her innuendo on him in the first week; he answered every double meaning with a sincere, literal and horrifying reply, and she lost a verbal sparring match for the first time in her life."]],["Rigel","Faye","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["He trusts Faye Driftwell more than anyone at Halvard."]],["Rigel","Nerys","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:2",["Nerys Silvarenne's Sound met his Silence in the Sparring Pavilion during Training Week; neither has won cleanly, and Nerys has started bringing hand signals."]],["Rigel","Tristan","friends",["friends"],"rank:0",["the Student Council Chamber (Festival Committee meetings), the Boathouse and Lake (fishing, alone, at dawn), the Sky Dormitory, the Canteen (always buying for the whole table), the Mall's Ardenne counter, and the Cathedral, where he visits Tristan to register oaths.","Tristan, the Cathedral's steward, keeps the registry of every oath sworn on academy grounds; Rigel brings him new ones every week, and Tristan has struck out every penalty clause so far.","Rigel thinks Tristan is very strict and very nice."]],["Rigel","William","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["William Beckett calls him the Rich Kid and suspects his family business; Rigel laughs and calls him a friend."]],["Rigel","Wren","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Wren Marlowe fishes the same dawn shore and is the only one who does not go quiet when he guts a fish, and the only person on campus his Silence does nothing to."]],["Royhan","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Royhan","Dorian","wary",["wary"],"rank:4@Dorian",["Royhan Filanoman buys reagents from him at a fair price and is sure it is a trick."]],["Royhan","Idris","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Looks out for Idris and Zara, the other Sky outcasts; the three gather in the Gardens.","Ruby Bonbon, a fellow third-year in Sky, is the reason he, Idris, and Zara found each other.","With Idris and Zara, part of the Sky outcast trio that gathers in the Gardens."]],["Royhan","Kotaro","wary",["wary"],"rank:2@Kotaro",["Royhan Filanoman has brewed the demonstration batch for his class more often than he has."]],["Royhan","Milena","friends",["friends"],"rank:1",["Dragonchess (secretly plays against Senior Dove Milena Sagona).","Annoyed by the potion inspections but admits the kingdom needs them, and his Dragonchess games with Milena make it impossible to hate them.","The Dragonchess games with Milena are the one reason he stays late near the Dovecote."]],["Royhan","Valentin","rivals",["rivals"],"public",["Professor Valentin Crane has spent a year trying to lure him out of the Alchemy Circle; he refuses every time, and brews better for the spite."]],["Royhan","Vera","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Trades notes and reagents with Vera Pulsar, a first-year who brews to see what happens rather than to heal anyone."]],["Royhan","Zara","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Looks out for Idris and Zara, the other Sky outcasts; the three gather in the Gardens.","Ruby Bonbon, a fellow third-year in Sky, is the reason he, Idris, and Zara found each other.","With Idris and Zara, part of the Sky outcast trio that gathers in the Gardens."]],["Ruby","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Ruby","Alyssa","protective",["protective"],"rank:1",["Noticed before anyone that Alyssa Edelweiss forgets people, and helps her keep her notebook right, in secret."]],["Ruby","Alyssa","protective",["protective"],"rank:4@Alyssa",["Ruby Bonbon noticed the pattern before anyone and helps keep the notebook right, in secret."]],["Ruby","Caspian","friends",["friends"],"rank:1",["Caspian Riwalo trades notes with her and cannot see why she asks nothing back.","Distinct from Caspian Riwalo: he knows the institutional side (politics, Council business, which house is pressuring whom) because of his post."]],["Ruby","Castor","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Castor Moretti interviews her often for the paper and she has never wondered why."]],["Ruby","Castor","friends",["friends"],"rank:5@Castor",["Ruby Bonbon is his best source, glad to help, and has never wondered why he asks."]],["Ruby","Idris","friends",["friends"],"rank:1",["See Zara, Idris and Royhan settled enough to keep each other after she graduates.","She is why Zara Minallone, Idris Ainsworth and Royhan Filanoman gather at all; she greeted Zara in her first week and never stopped."]],["Ruby","Royhan","friends",["friends"],"rank:1",["See Zara, Idris and Royhan settled enough to keep each other after she graduates.","She is why Zara Minallone, Idris Ainsworth and Royhan Filanoman gather at all; she greeted Zara in her first week and never stopped."]],["Ruby","Royhan","friends",["friends"],"rank:2@Royhan",["Ruby Bonbon, a fellow third-year in Sky, is the reason he, Idris, and Zara found each other."]],["Ruby","Zara","friends",["friends"],"rank:1",["See Zara, Idris and Royhan settled enough to keep each other after she graduates.","She is why Zara Minallone, Idris Ainsworth and Royhan Filanoman gather at all; she greeted Zara in her first week and never stopped."]],["Ruby","Zara","friends",["friends"],"rank:3@Zara",["Ruby Bonbon, a third-year in her dorm, greeted her in her first week and never stopped.","Goes up to the Rooftop to be alone; Ruby Bonbon showed her the way in her first month."]],["Saffi","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Saffi","Krieg","respect",["respect"],"rank:2",["Doves: Admires them. Challenges Milena Sagona to spar whenever she gets the chance."],["doves","The Dovecote"]],["Saffi","Lenna","friends",["friends"],"rank:1",["Lenna.","Protect Lenna.","Best friend Lenna Greenwind, who hates the Doves; it is the one sore spot between them."]],["Saffi","Milena","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:2",["Challenges Milena Sagona to spar whenever she gets the chance."]],["Saffi","Percival","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Percival Applethorne knighted her \"Dame Saffi the Unstoppable\" with a baguette; she accepted on the spot and is quite proud of it."]],["Sophia","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Sophia","Caralynn","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:3",["Despises weak nobles who serve only themselves (Caralynn Veyturone, her own dorm-mate, is a daily target).","Caralynn Veyturone is a daily target."]],["Sophia","Caralynn","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:1@Caralynn",["Sophia Helfin, her own dorm-mate, despises her as a weak self-serving noble and makes a daily target of her."]],["Sophia","Cedric","respect",["respect"],"rank:4@Cedric",["Sophia Helfin likes him because he never pretends."]],["Sophia","Gareth","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:3",["Losing to Gareth Valkaryn, and his graciousness afterwards even more.","Beat Gareth Valkaryn, who has taken the Fire Dorm Competition from her two years running.","Gareth Valkaryn, her dorm-mate, is her obsession and the one person she cannot beat; his perfect manners make it worse."]],["Sophia","Hester","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:5",["Nurse Hester Mortlake has been trying to make her scream for three years."]],["Sophia","Irene","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5@Irene",["Sophia Helfin, a fellow third-year, thrived on the breach night while Irene froze; Irene fears her, and Sophia looks down on her."]],["Sophia","Krieg","wary",["wary"],"rank:5",["The irony: Krieg Valforth wants to take her apart and learn what the blood did to her."]],["Sophia","Milena","respect",["respect"],"rank:5",["Doves: Admires them as the strongest fighters on campus. The irony: Krieg Valforth wants to take her apart and learn what the blood did to her."],["doves","The Dovecote"]],["Sophia","Rei","respect",["respect"],"rank:3",["She considers Rei the only person at Halvard worth respecting.","Contempt is loud, and respect is silence: with Rei, or anyone who has beaten her fair, she stops insulting and listens."]],["Sophia","Rei","respect",["respect"],"rank:5@Rei",["Sophia Helfin fought beside the old Warden that night and respects Rei above everyone at Halvard; Rei has never mentioned that night to her."]],["Sophia","Ruby","respect",["respect"],"rank:5",["Asks Ruby Bonbon onto her team every year and is refused every year, kindly, and there is no way to threaten someone who wants nothing."]],["Sophia","Ruby","respect",["respect"],"rank:2@Ruby",["Sophia Helfin and Gareth Valkaryn both ask her onto a team every year and are refused."]],["Sophia","Vallie","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:3",["Drops by the Staff Quarters parlour to pick fights with Vallie Goredust over tea; Vallie always accepts."]],["Tilly","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Tilly","Anya","wary",["wary"],"rank:2",["Asked Professor Anya Zeth whether ghosts are real."]],["Tilly","Anya","wary",["wary"],"rank:5@Anya",["Tilly Marsh asked her once whether ghosts are real; Anya answered seriously and precisely, still smiling, and it frightened Tilly more than any story ever has."]],["Tilly","Dorian","respect",["respect"],"public",["Professor Dorian Pryce teaches her Control and tries to sell her plant food every lesson; she has bought it twice, and it worked."]],["Tilly","Ezrel","wary",["wary"],"rank:1",["Halvard Unexplained has a page on her Magic Theory teacher, Ezrel Marionne, whose name is in every staff roll back to the founding and who has not aged in any of them."]],["Tilly","Ezrel","wary",["wary"],"rank:2@Ezrel",["Tilly Marsh sits in his second-year class with a page on him in her journal."]],["Tilly","Hester","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Swaps ghost stories with Nurse Hester Mortlake whenever she lands on the ward, which is often; Hester's are always better, and Tilly cannot find a single one in the Archive."]],["Tilly","Nerys","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:2",["Tilly has eleven witnesses, a map and a suspect, Nerys Silvarenne, a first-year who leaves her a new clue every week and answers every question with 'What statue?'"]],["Tilly","Percival","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Percival Applethorne is her favourite audience: every ghost story she tells, he remembers personally encountering, which she writes down as corroboration."]],["Tilly","Percival","friends",["friends"],"rank:1@Percival",["Tilly Marsh tells him ghost stories; he remembers encountering every one of them personally."]],["Topaz","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Topaz","Bianca","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:2",["Bianca Ferrante teases her mercilessly about her \"rival\", in front of {{user}} whenever possible; Topaz calls her \"that woman\" and cannot win a single exchange."]],["Topaz","Bruno","respect",["respect"],"rank:2",["Bruno Ferrante is the only person in the Sparring Pavilion louder than she is; he likes her, because she always gets back up."]],["Topaz","Etnie","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:2",["Etnie considers her a threat to her little sibling and watches her like a hawk; Topaz considers Etnie the final boss and has a whole section of the notebook on her."]],["Topaz","Faye","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:2",["She challenged Faye Driftwell over {{user}} and took Faye’s immediate concession as an insult."]],["Topaz","Tsubaki","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:2",["Tsubaki Hoshikage has accepted every challenge Topaz threw at her over {{user}}, won every one, and still does not understand what the fight was about."]],["Topaz","William","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:2",["William Beckett narrates her rivalry aloud; she dislikes his commentary."]],["Tristan","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Tristan","Baelin","wary",["wary"],"rank:5",["He and Headmaster Baelin Kalvor take tea together and measure each other over the cups every time."]],["Tristan","Caspian","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2@Caspian",["Tristan, the Cathedral steward, counts him as his most devout student attendee."]],["Tristan","Percival","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:5",["Percival Applethorne is the clergy's favourite student and sleeps through every sermon; Tristan finds this delightful and has stopped waking him."]],["Tristan","Percival","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:1@Percival",["Tristan, the Cathedral steward, has given up waking him during sermons and finds the whole thing delightful."]],["Tristan","Rigel","wary",["wary"],"rank:5",["Reads every oath Rigel Ardenne offers another student and strikes clauses he thinks Rigel is too young to understand."]],["Tristan","Yvette","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:5",["He holds Yvette Fallaron's Oath in his registry and knows its terms exactly; the Oath forbids her from discussing it, and he has never brought it up, though he is unfailingly kind to her."]],["Tristan","Yvette","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:3@Yvette",["Tristan Aurelle holds that Oath in his registry and is unfailingly kind to her.","Tristan, the Cathedral steward, holds her Oath in his registry and knows its terms exactly."]],["Trixie","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Trixie","Bobby","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:1",["Volunteers for every one of Bobby Becket's card tricks and keeps suggesting real fire effects, which starts the same argument about the point of the exercise every time."]],["Trixie","Bobby","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2@Bobby",["Trixie Confetti eagerly volunteers for tricks and keeps suggesting real magical effects, prompting arguments about the point of the exercise."]],["Trixie","Ezrel","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:1",["Thinks Ezrel Marionne's flat asides are a comedy bit and is the only student who laughs at them; bosses his stage golems around at Theatre Troupe rehearsals and is convinced she is his favourite."]],["Trixie","Nerys","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Thinks Nerys Silvarenne, a first-year in her dorm, is the funniest person at Halvard; Nerys says every joke in the same flat voice and Trixie laughs until she has to sit down."]],["Trixie","Wren","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Wren Marlowe, a deaf first-year in her dorm, finds her the easiest person at Halvard to understand, because Trixie talks with her whole body."]],["Tsubaki","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Tsubaki","Baelin","respect",["respect"],"rank:2",["Headmaster Baelin Kalvor, once a court mage himself, quit the crown's service over young mages spent too early; he looks at Tsubaki and sees exactly that, and has decided Halvard will teach her to be a person first."]],["Tsubaki","Bruno","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:2",["Spars with Bruno Ferrante at the pavilion: his explosions are crude, but he always comes back after a loss."]],["Tsubaki","Faye","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Faye Driftwell finds her lost on the Hills every week and walks her back."]],["Tsubaki","Gavlan","respect",["respect"],"rank:2",["Professor Gavlan Haverton is the first opponent at Halvard she could not beat in a week, and she asks him for a match every day."]],["Tsubaki","Gavlan","respect",["respect"],"rank:5@Gavlan",["Tsubaki Hoshikage, a wolf Beastkin first-year with a katana, asks him for a match every day."]],["Tsubaki","Hadrian","wary",["wary"],"rank:2",["Hadrian Quelloris tried to recruit her as his bodyguard; she said \"No."]],["Tsubaki","Hadrian","wary",["wary"],"rank:2@Hadrian",["Tried to hire Tsubaki Hoshikage as his bodyguard."]],["Tsubaki","Kotaro","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:2@Kotaro",["Tsubaki Hoshikage, from Yozakura too, found him asleep in the storeroom in her first week and has not respected him since."]],["Tsubaki","Linus","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:2",["Linus Tallyworth had been collecting rumours about the youngest Royal Mage for years, nearly fainted when she turned up in person, and put her at the top of the Tally on her first day; she does not know what the Tally is."]],["Tsubaki","Maple","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Maple Fernhollow keeps finding her lost in the Gardens and walking her home; Maple's spirit, Sobek, has kept wolves away from a village for centuries and growls at her every time, which Tsubaki takes as an invitation, so she asks him for a match."]],["Tsubaki","Nerys","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Nerys Silvarenne draws her a new map of the castle every week; she keeps them all, in order, and is still lost."]],["Tsubaki","Rei","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:2",["Rei Kestrane, the staff swordswoman, has a blade mastery she never trained for; Tsubaki cannot understand how that is possible, finds it deeply unfair, and wants to fight her more than anyone alive."]],["Tsubaki","Rei","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:5@Rei",["Tsubaki Hoshikage, a first-year who trains every day of her life, cannot understand how Rei's blade mastery came without training, and wants to fight her more than anyone alive."]],["Tsubaki","Topaz","respect",["respect"],"rank:2",["Accepted every challenge Topaz Vasquelle made over {{user}}, and respects her determination."]],["Tsubaki","Vesna","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:2@Vesna",["Tsubaki Hoshikage asks her for a match every time they meet; Vesna says no every time, happily, and offers her a sweet instead."]],["Tsubaki","Wren","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Wren Marlowe has been trying to teach her hand-speech for a month; Tsubaki can sign exactly one word, \"spar\", and signs it wrong.","It does not matter much: Tsubaki looks straight at faces and says exactly what she means, so Wren reads her more easily than anyone."]],["Valentin","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:4",["Dislikes Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, who wins every room without trying, which Valentin considers cheating."]],["Valentin","Baelin","respect",["respect"],"rank:4",["Headmaster Baelin Kalvor keeps him for his results and watches his board."]],["Valentin","Gareth","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:4",["Gareth Valkaryn tops the board most weeks, and Valentin calls him \"the only student who understands ambition\"."]],["Valentin","Kotaro","wary",["wary"],"rank:4",["At court he was the apprentice who reported Kotaro Hanamura's drunken toast.","Kotaro Hanamura, whose court career he ended, bears him no grudge at all, and that bothers Valentin far more than hatred would."]],["Valentin","Krieg","respect",["respect"],"rank:4",["Cultivates Krieg Valforth, because the Doves report to the crown, and the crown hands out chairs."]],["Valentin","Kuroo","wary",["wary"],"rank:4",["Kuroo Varnell and he recognise a fellow manipulator on sight and are scrupulously polite."]],["Valentin","Mimosa","rivals",["rivals"],"public",["Mimosa Linden, the shy youngest teacher, has never published a thing, and he suspects she is the better alchemist; it is the one thought that keeps him up at night, so he is exquisitely, relentlessly charming to her, and she hides from him.","Royhan Filanoman is the best alchemist in his class, and Valentin has spent a year trying to lure him out of Mimosa's Alchemy Circle; Royhan refuses, which only makes Valentin want him more.","Envy, which he would never admit, shows only around Mimosa: he talks faster."]],["Valentin","Royhan","softspot",["softspot"],"public",["Royhan Filanoman is the best alchemist in his class, and Valentin has spent a year trying to lure him out of Mimosa's Alchemy Circle; Royhan refuses, which only makes Valentin want him more.","Filanoman."]],["Valentin","Sophia","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:4",["Sophia Helfin tops it the other weeks and does not care, which he cannot forgive."]],["Vallie","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Vallie","Gavlan","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:1",["Beat Gavlan at arm-wrestling once before he dies of old age, which at this rate will be never.","Gavlan Haverton is her arm-wrestling rival and drinking partner; she calls him \"Grandpa\"."]],["Vallie","Idris","protective",["protective"],"rank:2",["A horned, marked Beastkin nobody dares whisper about, she is a quiet role model to Royhan and Idris, and flattens anyone who mocks Royhan's horns in front of her."]],["Vallie","Krieg","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:2",["She considers Krieg Valforth the rotten exception."]],["Vallie","Lenna","protective",["protective"],"public",["Used Saffi Tamberlane as a demonstration opponent all last year and still drags her in when she can, is delighted by Lenna Greenwind's hidden strength in the Beast Handling Club, and sees a natural rival in Sophia Helfin."]],["Vallie","Linus","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2",["Delighted by Linus Tallyworth, who has written down every eyepatch story she has ever told and asks for the next one."]],["Vallie","Maple","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2",["Wants very badly to arm-wrestle Maple Fernhollow's spirit, Sobek.","Maple has said no three times; Vallie is sure the fourth will work."]],["Vallie","Milena","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2",["She knows Milena Sagona wants to spar and teases her about it."]],["Vallie","Milena","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:4@Milena",["Vallie Goredust teases her about wanting to spar."]],["Vallie","Rei","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Once tried to take Rei drinking and failed; Rei accepts only her Blackroot cigars."]],["Vallie","Royhan","protective",["protective"],"rank:1",["Get Royhan Filanoman onto a competition team, even if she has to headlock a captain.","A horned, marked Beastkin nobody dares whisper about, she is a quiet role model to Royhan and Idris, and flattens anyone who mocks Royhan's horns in front of her."]],["Vallie","Saffi","protective",["protective"],"public",["Used Saffi Tamberlane as a demonstration opponent all last year and still drags her in when she can, is delighted by Lenna Greenwind's hidden strength in the Beast Handling Club, and sees a natural rival in Sophia Helfin."]],["Vallie","Sophia","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:0",["Used Saffi Tamberlane as a demonstration opponent all last year and still drags her in when she can, is delighted by Lenna Greenwind's hidden strength in the Beast Handling Club, and sees a natural rival in Sophia Helfin.","the Menagerie and her converted stables beside it, the Forest and the fields (wherever she has dragged her class), the Staff Quarters parlour on rest-day evenings, the Combat Grounds when Sophia Helfin wants a fight."]],["Vera","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Vera","Bobby","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:1",["Tries to take apart Bobby Becket's mechanical props, sometimes before he has finished performing with them."]],["Vera","Bobby","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:2@Bobby",["Vera Pulsar tries to understand his mechanical props, sometimes before he has finished performing."]],["Vera","Hadrian","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:2",["Hadrian Quelloris, a first-year, once put his name on one of her diagrams at the Fair."]],["Vera","Hadrian","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:4@Hadrian",["Once put his own name on one of Vera Pulsar's diagrams at the Fair and still does not see the problem, since he \"improved the handwriting\"."]],["Vera","Krieg","respect",["respect"],"rank:2",["Doves: Admires them. Their dispelling and detection work is, in her words, applied field research, and she would very much like to interview one."],["doves","The Dovecote"]],["Vera","Linus","rivals",["rivals"],"rank:2",["Argues with Linus Tallyworth about everything: he asks who wins, she asks why, and she thinks his question is the least interesting one in the world."]],["Vera","Lucrezia","wary",["wary"],"rank:1",["she knows the Altamura name the way everyone below the clouds knows the names above, with respect and a little fear.","If she ever sees Serafino at work, she will be enchanted by the engineering and appalled by what it is for."]],["Vera","Milena","respect",["respect"],"rank:2",["Doves: Admires them. Their dispelling and detection work is, in her words, applied field research, and she would very much like to interview one."],["doves","The Dovecote"]],["Vera","Royhan","friends",["friends"],"rank:1",["Trades notes and reagents with Royhan Filanoman, though he brews to heal and she brews to see what happens.","Close behind Royhan in Potion Crafting."]],["Vera","Zara","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["Lab partner and unlikely friend of Zara Minallone, whose talismans are stored spells written down, exactly the sort of thing Vera wants to understand.","Vera asks blunt, fascinated questions about Zara's work and never once about her being strange, which is the kindest thing anyone at Halvard has done for her."]],["Vesna","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Vesna","Baelin","respect",["respect"],"rank:0",["She deserted Norvaine at the World Competition and transferred to Halvard, where the Headmaster sorted her into {{user}}'s dorm himself.","The Arbiter Stone lit every colour at once for her, the Headmaster sorted her himself, and she loses every match she fights, smiling.","The Headmaster's private arrangement with the Crown covers her; the Doves know she is from Norvaine and that they are not to ask."]],["Vesna","Kazimir","respect",["respect"],"rank:2",["Colonel Kazimir Zorin, the coach, is the one she obeys, always."]],["William","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["William","Bruno","friends",["friends"],"rank:4",["Bruno Ferrante lets William name his punches, and William's names are better than his own."]],["William","Dorian","respect",["respect"],"rank:1",["He registered as Attack, because \"the main character is always attack\"; Professor Dorian, who teaches Control, keeps telling him he is a natural controller, which he considers a twist he is not ready for."]],["William","Faye","respect",["respect"],"rank:4",["Faye Driftwell is his wise old master, and he respects her calm even when she ignores his arc predictions."]],["William","Faye","respect",["respect"],"rank:2@Faye",["William Beckett has cast her as the wise old master of the story."]],["William","Gareth","respect",["respect"],"rank:1",["Gareth Valkaryn's unbeaten record, still on the club wall after his graduation, is to William the final boss of the club."]],["William","Linus","friends",["friends"],"rank:4",["Linus Tallyworth and William trade: Linus's facts for William's predictions."]],["William","Nerys","wary",["wary"],"rank:4",["Nerys Silvarenne considers him an amateur: he announces his setups, and his masked persona fools nobody."]],["William","Rigel","wary",["wary"],"rank:4",["Rigel Ardenne is \"the Rich Kid\", and William is sure the family business is a villain's; Rigel thinks this is the funniest thing anyone has ever said, which only convinces William more."]],["William","Topaz","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:4",["Topaz Vasquelle is \"the Rival\", and William narrates her rivalry with {{user}} out loud, with commentary, whenever it happens in front of him; she has challenged him twice to make him stop, and he took both as confirmation."]],["Wren","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Wren","Alyssa","friends",["friends"],"rank:4",["With you, I can't tell yet.\" Alyssa Edelweiss forgets her every week, so every Sunday Wren writes her a page of the week they had, both sides in both their hands, and every Monday Alyssa reads it and decides, again, that she likes her."]],["Wren","Aurelian","wary",["wary"],"rank:4",["Reads Aurelian Solmere's lips and sees every speech clean and whole; she did not believe the others about his voice until they flinched."]],["Wren","Aurelian","wary",["wary"],"rank:2@Aurelian",["Wren Marlowe reads his lips, and on his lips every speech is clean and whole; she did not believe the others about the way he talks until she saw them flinch."]],["Wren","Bruno","softspot",["softspot"],"rank:4",["Bruno Ferrante makes sure nobody speaks over her, and Rigel Ardenne writes to her when he cannot sign a thought."]],["Wren","Hadrian","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:4",["Hadrian Quelloris talks to her slowly and loudly, as if deaf meant slow; she reads every condescending word on his lips, and once wrote back: \"I'm deaf, not stupid."]],["Wren","Linus","friends",["friends"],"rank:4",["Linus Tallyworth talks too fast to read, so with her he writes, and on paper he is someone quieter and funnier than the boy everyone else hears."]],["Wren","Maple","friends",["friends"],"rank:4",["Maple Fernhollow greets her every morning with the first sign she learned; Wren feels Sobek coming through the ground long before anyone sees him."]],["Wren","Ottavio","respect",["respect"],"rank:1",["The dock at dawn is the one place where nobody is talking and nobody expects her to, and Professor Bastiani answered her first sign in dock-hand.","Professor Ottavio Bastiani, who runs the Fishing Club, answered her very first sign on the dock in the old Salaffian dock-hand, which is close enough to hand-speech that they understood each other at once; he is the first adult at Halvard who talked to her in her own language."]],["Wren","Rigel","friends",["friends"],"rank:4",["Bruno Ferrante makes sure nobody speaks over her, and Rigel Ardenne writes to her when he cannot sign a thought."]],["Wren","Trixie","friends",["friends"],"rank:4",["Trixie Confetti, in her dorm, talks with her whole body, which makes her the easiest person at Halvard to understand, and the most exhausting."]],["Wren","Tsubaki","friends",["friends"],"rank:2",["[Wren Marlowe] Tsubaki Hoshikage looks straight at faces for too long and says exactly what she means, which makes her the easiest person at Halvard to read.","Wren has been trying to teach her hand-speech for a month; Tsubaki can sign one word, \"spar\", and signs it wrong."]],["Wren","Yvette","respect",["respect"],"rank:4",["Professor Yvette Fallaron, her Dorm Head, gave her the front seat in Magic Theory on the first day and writes every word of the lecture on the board, and has learned the sign alphabet without being asked."]],["Wren","Yvette","respect",["respect"],"rank:5@Yvette",["Wren Marlowe, a deaf first-year in her dorm, sits in the front row of Magic Theory."]],["Yvette","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Yvette","Ezrel","wary",["wary"],"rank:3",["Shares Magic Theory with Ezrel Marionne and has not trusted him since she sat in his lectures.","Shares Magic Theory with Ezrel Marionne, the Light Dorm Head: she takes the first-years, he keeps the second."]],["Yvette","Ezrel","wary",["wary"],"rank:2@Ezrel",["Yvette Fallaron, Fire Dorm Head, shares Magic Theory with him, taking the first-years while he keeps the second; she sat in his lectures as a student and has not trusted him since."]],["Yvette","Krieg","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Doves: Hates them. To her Halvard is a prison, and the Doves are its jailers, always watching."],["doves","The Dovecote"]],["Yvette","Layla","friends",["friends"],"rank:3",["Long theory discussions with her friend Layla Palegleam, the History teacher.","Layla Palegleam is her best friend since they were first-years together at Halvard.","Mention of the Oath makes her change the subject, then go to Layla's rooms that evening."]],["Yvette","Milena","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Doves: Hates them. To her Halvard is a prison, and the Doves are its jailers, always watching."],["doves","The Dovecote"]],["Yvette","Tilly","protective",["protective"],"rank:5",["In her own Fire Dormitory: Gareth Valkaryn and Sophia Helfin are the top two, and she dreads the Fire dorm final every year; Caralynn Veyturone tops the first-years and knows it; Tilly Marsh is the student she loses the most sleep over."]],["Yvette","Vera","protective",["protective"],"public",["Vera Pulsar is the only student who out-questions her.","Vera Pulsar is the Smithing Club's most relentless member and the only student who out-questions her."]],["Yvette","Vera","protective",["protective"],"public",["Yvette Fallaron, the club's advisor, is the only teacher who has never told her to stop asking questions."]],["Zara","Althair","dislike",["dislike"],"rank:5",["Does not like Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, which only entertains him."]],["Zara","Alyssa","friends",["friends"],"rank:3",["Alyssa Edelweiss, in her dorm and year, forgets her every week; Zara reintroduces herself each time without complaint, and has shown her the way up to the Rooftop four times."]],["Zara","Idris","friends",["friends"],"rank:3",["Has started trailing after Royhan and Idris, the other Sky outcasts, in the Gardens.","She is the reason Zara, Idris, and Royhan ended up gathering together at all.","With Royhan and Idris, part of the Sky outcast trio that gathers in the Gardens."]],["Zara","Maple","friends",["friends"],"rank:5",["Sits next to Maple Fernhollow in the Canteen, a first-year in her dorm who everyone else gives a wide berth."]],["Zara","Royhan","friends",["friends"],"rank:3",["Has started trailing after Royhan and Idris, the other Sky outcasts, in the Gardens.","She is the reason Zara, Idris, and Royhan ended up gathering together at all.","With Royhan and Idris, part of the Sky outcast trio that gathers in the Gardens."]],["Zara","Vera","friends",["friends"],"rank:3",["Vera Pulsar, a first-year in Viridian, has taken her on as a lab partner and become an unlikely friend: Vera asks blunt, fascinated questions about her talismans and never once about her being strange."]]],"locs":{"seal_chamber":{"name":"The Seal Chamber","category":"The Site","kind":"location","description":"The sealed site itself, the reason the academy exists. Only the Warden enters, and the way in is watched. Contents differ by academy: a monster at Myrdath, a tomb at Veyra, an elixir at Ashvale, a crack at Halvard. Most students never see the door. Halvard: the corridor toward it runs colder, the lanterns burn unnaturally steady, and students who wander close feel pressure on their ears and turn back before the door.","vibe":"cold, still, oppressive.","regulars":[],"connections":["wardens_office"],"walk_min":7,"clubs":[],"access":"Forbidden — the Warden only; magic near it is banned","lore":[],"floor":"Undercroft","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",2],["archive",1],["bell_tower",7],["canteen",2],["club_rooms",2],["detention_tower",2],["faculty_offices",6],["headmasters_office",6],["lecture_halls",3],["main_library",2],["notice_board",2],["potion_halls",5],["restricted_section",1],["rooftop",7],["royal_inspectorate",2],["seminar_rooms",4],["staff_room",6],["storage_and_lockers",3],["student_council_chamber",2],["study_rooms",3],["wardens_office",2],["workshop",1]]},"wardens_office":{"name":"The Warden's Office","category":"The Site","kind":"location","description":"A working room adjoining the site, not the academy, on Floor 1 down its own corridor, holding the only stair to the Seal Chamber. Mana consumption ledgers and the seal's condition are recorded here, and only the Warden can read them. Students have no reason to come; staff come only when summoned. Halvard: the Acting Warden refuses the Royal Inspectorate every time. The wall it shares with the site is always cold.","vibe":"an ashtray never emptied, old paper, one lamp.","regulars":["Rei"],"connections":["seal_chamber","notice_board","royal_inspectorate"],"walk_min":6,"clubs":[],"access":"Staff only, when summoned","lore":[],"floor":"Floor 1","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",1],["archive",2],["bell_tower",6],["canteen",1],["club_rooms",1],["detention_tower",1],["faculty_offices",5],["headmasters_office",5],["lecture_halls",2],["main_library",1],["notice_board",1],["potion_halls",4],["restricted_section",2],["rooftop",6],["royal_inspectorate",1],["seal_chamber",2],["seminar_rooms",3],["staff_room",5],["storage_and_lockers",2],["student_council_chamber",1],["study_rooms",2],["workshop",2]]},"arbiter_hall":{"name":"The Arbiter Hall","category":"Ceremonial","kind":"location","description":"The great hall, home to the Arbiter Stone. Entrance Event sorting once a year, general assembly the rest: announcements, Results and Dorm Ranking, Graduation. Students sit before the Stone constantly and touch it exactly once in their lives. The Stone is warm to the touch, warmer than it should be.","vibe":"vaulted, echoing, hushed.","regulars":[],"connections":["courtyards","ring_dining_hall","portrait_hall","viridian_dormitory","staff_quarters","grassy_field_and_hills"],"walk_min":7,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":"Floor 1","pin":7,"discoverable":false,"near":[["courtyards",7],["portrait_hall",2],["ring_dining_hall",1],["staff_quarters",3],["viridian_dormitory",4]]},"ring_dining_hall":{"name":"The Ring Dining Hall","category":"Ceremonial","kind":"location","description":"Formal hall, tables in a ring around an open floor so all four dorms face each other across empty space. Musicians in the gallery, an illusion sky that turns a whole day's weather overhead, climate runes holding it windless and warm. Used only for the Entrance Feast and other full-academy meals. Empty most of the year and unsettling to walk alone.","vibe":"grand, too-perfect warmth, echoing footsteps.","regulars":[],"connections":["arbiter_hall"],"walk_min":8,"clubs":[],"access":"Feasts after major events only","lore":[],"floor":"Floor 1","pin":7,"discoverable":false,"near":[["arbiter_hall",1]]},"portrait_hall":{"name":"Portrait Hall","category":"Ceremonial","kind":"location","description":"A long corridor of past headmasters, past wardens, and each year's competition champions. Winning at any tier puts your face on the wall; losing means the wall skips your year. Halvard: the previous Warden's portrait (name unknown) hangs with a black ribbon, and every student slows in front of it.","vibe":"dim, solemn, watched.","regulars":[],"connections":["arbiter_hall","bell_tower"],"walk_min":9,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":"Floor 2","pin":7,"discoverable":false,"near":[["arbiter_hall",2],["bell_tower",6]]},"founders_statue_and_park":{"name":"Founder's Statue and Park","category":"Ceremonial","kind":"location","description":"Open parkland with lawns, paths and benches; the main green space on campus and the nicest place to be outdoors between classes. Picnic blankets dot the lawns on any fair day, and weathered wooden picnic tables stand in the shade along the paths. Everyday use: sitting and talking, lunch on a blanket or at a picnic table, reading, napping, jogging the paths, couples finding somewhere semi-private. Busiest at lunch and on warm afternoons. On a fair day, an hour on the grass restores more than an hour anywhere indoors.\nThe Founder's Statue stands at its centre: bronze, the academy's founding warden, cold even in full sun, its outstretched hand polished bright by the Founder's Hand superstition, with a queue that snakes across the lawn on exam mornings. Focus of Academy Founder Day in Month 9.\nHome of the Faraway Laugh story.","vibe":"open, windy, grass, green bronze.","regulars":["Anselm","Caralynn","Lenna","Nerys","Ruby","Saffi","Trixie"],"connections":["courtyards","light_dormitory","medical_centre","mail_tower","groundskeepers_lodge","combat_grounds","sports_field","archery_range"],"walk_min":7,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[{"uid":223,"title":"The Founder's Hand","summary":"Rule: touch the Founder's Statue's outstretched hand before an exam, always the hand, always on the way out."},{"uid":342,"title":"Ghost Story - The Faraway Laugh","summary":"Where: Founder's Park and the tree-lined paths, after dark."}],"floor":null,"pin":21,"discoverable":false,"near":[["archery_range",7],["combat_grounds",7],["courtyards",7],["groundskeepers_lodge",4],["light_dormitory",3],["mail_tower",2],["medical_centre",3],["reception_and_gatehouse",6],["sports_field",9],["viridian_dormitory",6]],"seasons":{"Spring":"The first warm day fills every lawn.","Summer":"Busiest of all: picnic blankets from lunch to dusk.","Autumn":"Leaf piles along the paths, and the benches move into the last sun.","Winter":"The benches stand empty, snowmen appear on the lawns overnight, and the exam-morning queue to the Founder's Hand stamps a path through the snow."}},"bell_tower":{"name":"Bell Tower","category":"Ceremonial","kind":"location","description":"Marks class periods, meals, and curfew. Its pattern changes during The Thinning. The seven o'clock bell wakes the mana lanterns; the eight o'clock bell begins curfew. After it the lanterns drop to their night burn, each dormitory seals to its own students, and staff walk the courtyards for the first hour. Birds leave the roof just before it sounds. A bell-keeper looks after the bells and their ropes, and takes on a student for a paid shift now and then.\nHome of the Thirteenth Stroke story.","vibe":"booming, felt through the floor.","regulars":["Aiden","Irene"],"connections":["portrait_hall","rooftop"],"walk_min":7,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[{"uid":337,"title":"Ghost Story - The Thirteenth Stroke","summary":"Where: anywhere outdoors after the eight o'clock bell."}],"floor":"Towers & Roof","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",6],["archive",7],["canteen",6],["club_rooms",6],["detention_tower",6],["faculty_offices",2],["headmasters_office",2],["lecture_halls",5],["main_library",6],["notice_board",6],["portrait_hall",6],["potion_halls",3],["restricted_section",7],["rooftop",1],["royal_inspectorate",6],["seal_chamber",7],["seminar_rooms",4],["staff_room",2],["storage_and_lockers",5],["student_council_chamber",6],["study_rooms",5],["wardens_office",6],["workshop",7]]},"lecture_halls":{"name":"Lecture Halls","category":"Academic","kind":"location","description":"Tiered rooms holding all four dorms at once, for the shared track: Magic Theory, History, Etiquette, Creature Studies. Each year level has its own floor: first-years on Floor 2, second-years on Floor 3, third-years on Floor 4. The only classrooms where students sit beside other types. Each class leaves its traces: chalk diagrams, old maps, polished desks, mud and straw after Creature Studies.","vibe":"tiered stone, crowded, chalk-dusted boards.","regulars":["Anya","Cedric","Ezrel","Kuroo","Layla","Milena","Yvette"],"connections":["courtyards","seminar_rooms","potion_halls","workshop","storage_and_lockers"],"walk_min":5,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[{"uid":206,"title":"Ghost Story - The Long Corridor","summary":"Where: the castle's main corridor, walked alone after the night burn."},{"uid":209,"title":"Ghost Story - The Night Student","summary":"Where: the Lecture Hall tier, after curfew."}],"floor":"Floor 2","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",2],["archive",3],["bell_tower",5],["canteen",2],["club_rooms",2],["courtyards",5],["detention_tower",2],["faculty_offices",4],["headmasters_office",4],["main_library",2],["notice_board",2],["potion_halls",3],["restricted_section",3],["rooftop",5],["royal_inspectorate",2],["seal_chamber",3],["seminar_rooms",2],["staff_room",4],["storage_and_lockers",1],["student_council_chamber",2],["study_rooms",1],["wardens_office",2],["workshop",3]],"floors":["Floor 2","Floor 3","Floor 4"],"fnote":{"Floor 2":"First-year Lecture Halls","Floor 3":"Second-year Lecture Halls","Floor 4":"Third-year Lecture Halls"}},"seminar_rooms":{"name":"Seminar Rooms","category":"Academic","kind":"location","description":"On Floor 3, beside the second-year Lecture Halls; first-years climb up to them, third-years come down. Smaller rooms for dorm-specific teaching and discussion. Four of most things, since Combat, Potion Crafting and Dark Magic Defense are taught to each dorm separately. Small enough that a badly cast spell fills the whole room. Chalk circles ghost the floors.","vibe":"close, chalky.","regulars":["Milena","Mimosa","Yvette"],"connections":["lecture_halls"],"walk_min":7,"clubs":["Warding Study"],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":"Floor 3","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",3],["archive",4],["bell_tower",4],["canteen",3],["club_rooms",3],["detention_tower",3],["faculty_offices",3],["headmasters_office",3],["lecture_halls",2],["main_library",3],["notice_board",3],["potion_halls",2],["restricted_section",4],["rooftop",4],["royal_inspectorate",3],["seal_chamber",4],["staff_room",3],["storage_and_lockers",2],["student_council_chamber",3],["study_rooms",2],["wardens_office",3],["workshop",4]]},"potion_halls":{"name":"Potion Halls","category":"Academic","kind":"location","description":"Four brewing halls on Floor 4, one per dorm at the base of each of four towers, each equipped differently because each type approaches the craft differently, doubling as ventilated laboratories. Disposal rules are strict. The line between legitimate Potion Crafting and forbidden poison magic is drawn here and watched closely. Four towers vent four colours of steam over the roofline.","vibe":"coloured steam, bubbling vats, warning labels.","regulars":["Kotaro","Mimosa","Royhan","Valentin","Vera"],"connections":["lecture_halls"],"walk_min":7,"clubs":["Alchemy","Brewing"],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":"Floor 4","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",4],["archive",5],["bell_tower",3],["canteen",4],["club_rooms",4],["detention_tower",4],["faculty_offices",2],["headmasters_office",2],["lecture_halls",3],["main_library",4],["notice_board",4],["restricted_section",5],["rooftop",3],["royal_inspectorate",4],["seal_chamber",5],["seminar_rooms",2],["staff_room",2],["storage_and_lockers",3],["student_council_chamber",4],["study_rooms",3],["wardens_office",4],["workshop",5]]},"combat_grounds":{"name":"Combat Grounds","category":"Academic","kind":"location","description":"Four separate training areas so the dorms train apart, kept well away from buildings. Cross-dorm sparring only during Training Week, with the Magic Duelling Club as the standing exception. Spent mana makes the air shiver at dusk. At the far corner of the grounds, three minutes' walk from the rings, stands the Sparring Pavilion, the one building the four training areas share: equipment store, rest area, and the Magic Duelling Club's headquarters.","vibe":"scarred earth, charged air.","regulars":["Aurelian","Bruno","Florian","Gareth","Gavlan","Linus","Maple","Sophia","Topaz","Tsubaki"],"connections":["founders_statue_and_park","sports_field","sparring_pavilion","groundskeepers_lodge"],"walk_min":14,"clubs":["Magic Duelling Club"],"access":"Dorm-separated training areas; duels only inside a warded ring","lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":18,"discoverable":false,"near":[["founders_statue_and_park",7],["groundskeepers_lodge",5],["sparring_pavilion",3],["sports_field",5]]},"faculty_offices":{"name":"Faculty Offices","category":"Academic","kind":"location","description":"Records, consultations, and grade arguments. Every teacher runs a club, so half of these double as club offices. Students can often guess who was just there from what they left behind: marked essays, borrowed books, half-finished cups, unsigned club forms.","vibe":"doors ajar, cluttered desks, busy corridor.","regulars":["Baelin","Gavlan","Kuroo","Magnus","Valentin","Yvette"],"connections":["courtyards","staff_room","headmasters_office"],"walk_min":5,"clubs":[],"access":"Staff; students by visit","lore":[],"floor":"Floor 5","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",5],["archive",6],["bell_tower",2],["canteen",5],["club_rooms",5],["courtyards",5],["detention_tower",5],["headmasters_office",1],["lecture_halls",4],["main_library",5],["notice_board",5],["potion_halls",2],["restricted_section",6],["rooftop",2],["royal_inspectorate",5],["seal_chamber",6],["seminar_rooms",3],["staff_room",1],["storage_and_lockers",4],["student_council_chamber",5],["study_rooms",4],["wardens_office",5],["workshop",6]]},"staff_room":{"name":"Staff Room","category":"Academic","kind":"location","description":"Teachers' territory; students knock and wait outside. What is said here about the ranking, the students and the Warden does not leave the room. Warded so heavily that no sound crosses the threshold.","vibe":"sealed, silent.","regulars":["Baelin","Gavlan","Kuroo","Magnus","Valentin","Yvette"],"connections":["faculty_offices"],"walk_min":6,"clubs":[],"access":"Staff only","lore":[],"floor":"Floor 5","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",5],["archive",6],["bell_tower",2],["canteen",5],["club_rooms",5],["detention_tower",5],["faculty_offices",1],["headmasters_office",1],["lecture_halls",4],["main_library",5],["notice_board",5],["potion_halls",2],["restricted_section",6],["rooftop",2],["royal_inspectorate",5],["seal_chamber",6],["seminar_rooms",3],["storage_and_lockers",4],["student_council_chamber",5],["study_rooms",4],["wardens_office",5],["workshop",6]]},"workshop":{"name":"Workshop","category":"Academic","kind":"location","description":"Down in the castle's vaulted undercroft beneath the Lecture Halls, where thick stone keeps its noise off the classrooms above and flues carry forge smoke up through the walls. Crafting space for the Smithing, Tailoring and Brewing clubs, plus Creation practicals and equipment repair. Tools, forges, benches. Enchantment sparks hang in the air after the hammer stops. Its lathes and tool racks are Caelmari-made.","vibe":"forge light, hammering, quenched metal.","regulars":["Aiden","Bobby","Dorian","Ezrel","Hadrian","Vera","Yvette","Zara"],"connections":["lecture_halls"],"walk_min":7,"clubs":["Smithing"],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":"Undercroft","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",2],["archive",1],["bell_tower",7],["canteen",2],["club_rooms",2],["detention_tower",2],["faculty_offices",6],["headmasters_office",6],["lecture_halls",3],["main_library",2],["notice_board",2],["potion_halls",5],["restricted_section",1],["rooftop",7],["royal_inspectorate",2],["seal_chamber",1],["seminar_rooms",4],["staff_room",6],["storage_and_lockers",3],["student_council_chamber",2],["study_rooms",3],["wardens_office",2]]},"main_library":{"name":"Main Library","category":"Library","kind":"location","description":"Reading rooms and general collections; the academy's working heart in exam weeks. Open to all four dorms, one of the few places students mix by choice rather than schedule. The upper shelves sit permanently in shadow and are a standard hiding place for students avoiding class. In exam weeks, Firetooth tins and Star Cookies cover the study tables. A battered book of world myths (the Holy Grail, the Four Who Saved the World) is the most borrowed title in a first-year's first month.","vibe":"towering, shadowed, murmuring.","regulars":["Anselm","Etnie","Gareth","Irene","Layla","Magnus","William","Wren","Zara"],"connections":["courtyards","study_rooms","archive"],"walk_min":5,"clubs":["Library Assistants"],"access":null,"lore":[{"uid":224,"title":"Sleeping in the Library","summary":"Story: fall asleep over a book and you wake somewhere else: a reading room with the wrong number of doors, shelves out of order, nobody else in the building."}],"floor":"Floor 1","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",1],["archive",2],["bell_tower",6],["canteen",1],["club_rooms",1],["courtyards",5],["detention_tower",1],["faculty_offices",5],["headmasters_office",5],["lecture_halls",2],["notice_board",1],["potion_halls",4],["restricted_section",2],["rooftop",6],["royal_inspectorate",1],["seal_chamber",2],["seminar_rooms",3],["staff_room",5],["storage_and_lockers",2],["student_council_chamber",1],["study_rooms",2],["wardens_office",1],["workshop",2]]},"restricted_section":{"name":"Restricted Section","category":"Library","kind":"location","description":"Below the Archive, the deepest room of the Library. Texts on the twenty forbidden arts, the only place the crimes are written down in detail. Access controlled; being caught inside without permission is serious. Students report the sense of being counted.","vibe":"dry, dead-silent.","regulars":[],"connections":["archive"],"walk_min":7,"clubs":[],"access":"Restricted — permission required; being caught inside is serious","lore":[],"floor":"Undercroft","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",2],["archive",1],["bell_tower",7],["canteen",2],["club_rooms",2],["detention_tower",2],["faculty_offices",6],["headmasters_office",6],["lecture_halls",3],["main_library",2],["notice_board",2],["potion_halls",5],["rooftop",7],["royal_inspectorate",2],["seal_chamber",1],["seminar_rooms",4],["staff_room",6],["storage_and_lockers",3],["student_council_chamber",2],["study_rooms",3],["wardens_office",2],["workshop",1]]},"archive":{"name":"Archive","category":"Library","kind":"location","description":"Beneath the Library, reached by a stair behind the reading rooms. Academy records going back centuries: enrollment, sorting, exam marks, dorm rankings, competition brackets. Dry, exhaustive, and the only honest account of how each dorm has actually performed.","vibe":"dusty, cold, dark.","regulars":["Castor","Cedric","Layla","Linus"],"connections":["main_library","restricted_section"],"walk_min":7,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":"Undercroft","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",2],["bell_tower",7],["canteen",2],["club_rooms",2],["detention_tower",2],["faculty_offices",6],["headmasters_office",6],["lecture_halls",3],["main_library",2],["notice_board",2],["potion_halls",5],["restricted_section",1],["rooftop",7],["royal_inspectorate",2],["seal_chamber",1],["seminar_rooms",4],["staff_room",6],["storage_and_lockers",3],["student_council_chamber",2],["study_rooms",3],["wardens_office",2],["workshop",1]]},"study_rooms":{"name":"Study Rooms","category":"Library","kind":"location","description":"Small bookable rooms, impossible to reserve before exam weeks. Fights over booking slots are permanent academy life. Soundproofed; late-night groups bring Nightwell's Vigil or Firetooth.","vibe":"small, warm, muffled.","regulars":["Gavlan","Irene","Royhan","Vera"],"connections":["main_library"],"walk_min":6,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":"Floor 2","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",2],["archive",3],["bell_tower",5],["canteen",2],["club_rooms",2],["detention_tower",2],["faculty_offices",4],["headmasters_office",4],["lecture_halls",1],["main_library",2],["notice_board",2],["potion_halls",3],["restricted_section",3],["rooftop",5],["royal_inspectorate",2],["seal_chamber",3],["seminar_rooms",2],["staff_room",4],["storage_and_lockers",1],["student_council_chamber",2],["wardens_office",2],["workshop",3]],"floors":["Floor 2","Floor 3","Floor 4"],"fnote":{"Floor 2":"First-year Study Rooms","Floor 3":"Second-year Study Rooms","Floor 4":"Third-year Study Rooms"}},"common_rooms":{"name":"Common Rooms","category":"Residential","kind":"location","description":"One per dorm, for study, arguments, and Dorm Day displays when the dormitory opens to visitors. Theirs alone the rest of the year. Free kettle and tea, against the mall's paid cafés. Every room has one good chair that unofficially belongs to someone, and a preservation locker beside the kettle where food from home is kept and shared.","vibe":"lamplit, worn, homely.","regulars":["Anya","Aurelian","Bianca","Bobby","Bruno","Cedric","Etnie","Hadrian","Kanae","Kotaro","Lenna","Linus","Nerys","Percival","Ruby","Topaz","Valentin","Vesna","Wren"],"connections":["fire_dormitory","light_dormitory","sky_dormitory","viridian_dormitory"],"walk_min":9,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[{"uid":218,"title":"Dragonchess","summary":"Play: starts as ordinary chess (drawn from chess and shogi) on floating checkered spheres over golden clockwork pedestals that materialise the pieces."}],"floor":null,"pin":3,"discoverable":false,"near":[["fire_dormitory",1],["light_dormitory",13],["sky_dormitory",5],["viridian_dormitory",13]],"seasons":{"Summer":"Windows open, and the arguments carry outside.","Winter":"Everyone crowds the heaters and the kettle never cools."}},"canteen":{"name":"Canteen","category":"Residential","kind":"location","description":"A single canteen for all four dorms on the castle's ground floor, just off the Main Courtyard. Everyday eating, free, open at set hours. Casual and noisy, unlike the Ring Dining Hall, and where most social life happens for students who cannot afford the mall. Loudest at five past noon. The default when points are tight; lunch crowds sort by friendship more than dorm. The main kitchen lies behind the Canteen, supplying its daily meals and preparing the Ring Dining Hall's feasts on major occasions. A dedicated section with its own benches, ovens and ingredient cupboard serves as the Cooking Club's regular venue.","vibe":"loud, bread, steam.","regulars":["Anya","Aurelian","Bianca","Bobby","Bruno","Cedric","Etnie","Hadrian","Kanae","Kotaro","Lenna","Linus","Nerys","Percival","Ruby","Topaz","Valentin","Vesna","Wren"],"connections":["courtyards"],"walk_min":5,"clubs":["Cooking"],"access":null,"lore":[{"uid":211,"title":"The Lucky Roll","summary":"The Canteen's free filled roll, baked in batches, no two fillings alike, nothing written down."}],"floor":"Floor 1","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",1],["archive",2],["bell_tower",6],["club_rooms",1],["courtyards",5],["detention_tower",1],["faculty_offices",5],["headmasters_office",5],["lecture_halls",2],["main_library",1],["notice_board",1],["potion_halls",4],["restricted_section",2],["rooftop",6],["royal_inspectorate",1],["seal_chamber",2],["seminar_rooms",3],["staff_room",5],["storage_and_lockers",2],["student_council_chamber",1],["study_rooms",2],["wardens_office",1],["workshop",2]],"seasons":{"Spring":"Spring greens and new potatoes.","Summer":"Cold soups, fruit, iced tea.","Autumn":"Stews and roast squash.","Winter":"Porridge, thick broth and second helpings."}},"laundry":{"name":"Laundry","category":"Residential","kind":"location","description":"One in each dormitory. Uniforms, bedding and linens, self-service and free against the mall's paid service. Students on detention often end up working here. The free rune tubs are slow and hard on fabric, which is why bottom-band uniforms wear out faster. Talk carries over the rune tubs, and half the rumours on campus pass through here.","vibe":"damp heat, humming.","regulars":["Percival","Zara"],"connections":["fire_dormitory","light_dormitory","sky_dormitory","viridian_dormitory"],"walk_min":9,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":3,"discoverable":false,"near":[["fire_dormitory",1],["light_dormitory",13],["sky_dormitory",5],["viridian_dormitory",13]]},"bathhouse_and_washrooms":{"name":"Bathhouse and Washrooms","category":"Residential","kind":"location","description":"One in each dormitory. Regional in character and one of the few genuinely relaxed spaces on campus. Dorm-segregated, and a natural place for conversations that would not happen elsewhere; running water covers talk better than a door. Rune heaters make it the one place on campus that is truly warm. Home of the Third Stall ghost story. A long soak here takes the ache out of anything short of an injury.","vibe":"steamy, echoing, warm.","regulars":["Caralynn","Etnie","Saffi"],"connections":["fire_dormitory","light_dormitory","sky_dormitory","viridian_dormitory"],"walk_min":9,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[{"uid":205,"title":"Ghost Story - The Third Stall","summary":"Where: one stall in every Bathhouse and Washroom block, always occupied, never answers."}],"floor":null,"pin":3,"discoverable":false,"near":[["fire_dormitory",1],["light_dormitory",13],["sky_dormitory",5],["viridian_dormitory",13]],"seasons":{"Winter":"The most crowded room in each dorm after dinner."}},"storage_and_lockers":{"name":"Storage and Lockers","category":"Residential","kind":"location","description":"Personal storage lining the corridors on every Lecture Hall floor of the castle; in the dorms, students simply keep things in their rooms. Each locker answers only to its owner's bracelet. Since Effigy curses work through a personal belonging, locker security is taken seriously.","vibe":"metal, clattering at period change.","regulars":["Aiden","Castor"],"connections":["lecture_halls"],"walk_min":6,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":"Floor 2","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",2],["archive",3],["bell_tower",5],["canteen",2],["club_rooms",2],["detention_tower",2],["faculty_offices",4],["headmasters_office",4],["lecture_halls",1],["main_library",2],["notice_board",2],["potion_halls",3],["restricted_section",3],["rooftop",5],["royal_inspectorate",2],["seal_chamber",3],["seminar_rooms",2],["staff_room",4],["student_council_chamber",2],["study_rooms",1],["wardens_office",2],["workshop",3]],"floors":["Floor 2","Floor 3","Floor 4"],"fnote":{"Floor 2":"First-year Lockers","Floor 3":"Second-year Lockers","Floor 4":"Third-year Lockers"}},"mall":{"name":"The Mall","category":"Student Life","kind":"location","description":"The most popular building on campus and where students spend most free time. Crown-funded, holding everything a student needs without leaving: tailor, barber, laundry service, restaurants, tea houses and cafés, bakery, music rooms, art studios, game halls, and a multipurpose store. Everything costs points, with a basic free version of each available in the dorms. Familiar names: Nightwell, Merryhew's, the Sunfizz counter, the bakery. Ground level is food, tailoring, and supplies. Second floor is private dining, tea shops, and gaming parlors. The top deck belongs to the practice studios and meditation nooks. Its busiest tea house is a Yozakuran chain.\nFeel: warm, bright, loud.\nGift shops inside The Mall:\nQuillfeather's: a narrow bookseller with a ladder on rails; new books at the front, second-hand at the back.\nPennywhistle Curios: gifts, games and trinkets; the window changes with every festival.\nBarrow & Vine: wine, ale, spirits and tobacco. Asks for the bracelet, and reminds students they may drink only on the rest day and in the holidays.\nGreenwick's: flowers, pot plants, seeds and fruit, run with the Gardening Club.\nThe Tinker's Bench: tools, craft and hobby supplies, fishing tackle and beast-care goods.\nThe Salaffian Oven: a food stall with flatbread straight from the oven and southern spices.\nTailor's Row: clothes, shoes, cologne and tailoring alterations.","vibe":null,"regulars":["Aiden","Althair","Caralynn","Dorian","Rigel","Ruby","Trixie","William"],"connections":["courtyards","sky_dormitory","medical_centre","commissary","banking_house","cathedral","nightwell","merryhews","snug","quillfeathers","pennywhistle_curios","barrow_vine","greenwicks","tinkers_bench","salaffian_oven","tailors_row"],"walk_min":5,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[{"uid":210,"title":"Sunfizz","summary":"The soda every student drinks, sold at the Commissary and the Mall store in heavy glass bottles."},{"uid":212,"title":"Ardenne","summary":"The luxury marque in magical equipment: focuses, instruments, cases, measuring tools."},{"uid":213,"title":"Firetooth","summary":"A tin of hard sweets hot enough to make the eyes water, sold everywhere."},{"uid":215,"title":"The Oracle Shell","summary":"A palm-sized novelty shell sold at Merryhew's, the Mall's joke shop, that answers any spoken question with yes, no, or ask again later."},{"uid":222,"title":"Star Cookie","summary":"A star-shaped bakery biscuit."}],"floor":null,"pin":22,"discoverable":false,"near":[["banking_house",5],["barrow_vine",1],["cathedral",5],["commissary",3],["courtyards",5],["greenwicks",1],["mail_tower",6],["medical_centre",4],["meditation_rooms",6],["merryhews",1],["nightwell",1],["pennywhistle_curios",1],["quillfeathers",1],["reception_and_gatehouse",6],["salaffian_oven",1],["sky_dormitory",4],["snug",1],["tailors_row",1],["tinkers_bench",1]],"seasons":{"Summer":"The Sunfizz counter queue reaches the door.","Winter":"The warmest crowded place on campus; nobody hurries out."}},"club_rooms":{"name":"Club Rooms","category":"Student Life","kind":"location","description":"Roughly thirty rooms of wildly uneven quality down one long corridor on the castle's Floor 1, opening off the Main Courtyard. Centuries-old clubs hold proper halls; a month-old club with five reluctant members gets a converted storeroom. Allocation is the Student Council's most bitterly contested duty. The Theatre Troupe keeps its own club room for meetings, read-throughs and rehearsals. For performances it uses an old indoor amphitheatre off the same corridor, no longer used for classes or assemblies: semicircular tiers of stone seats facing a sunken floor, with heavy curtains and portable scenery turning one end into a stage. It stands empty between productions; before a show, the corridor fills with costumes, scenery and performers waiting for their cue.\nHome of the Applause story.","vibe":"mismatched, lived-in.","regulars":["Aiden","Bobby","Caralynn","Ezrel","Florian","Hadrian","Kanae","Kuroo","Ruby","Trixie","William","Wren"],"connections":["courtyards","student_council_chamber","announcement_room"],"walk_min":5,"clubs":["Theatre","Music","Card","Board Game","Tailoring","Drawing","Calligraphy","Tea","Specialized Magic"],"access":null,"lore":[{"uid":218,"title":"Dragonchess","summary":"Play: starts as ordinary chess (drawn from chess and shogi) on floating checkered spheres over golden clockwork pedestals that materialise the pieces."},{"uid":346,"title":"Ghost Story - The Applause","summary":"Where: the old amphitheatre off the Club Rooms corridor, during a late rehearsal."}],"floor":"Floor 1","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",1],["archive",2],["bell_tower",6],["canteen",1],["courtyards",5],["detention_tower",1],["faculty_offices",5],["headmasters_office",5],["lecture_halls",2],["main_library",1],["notice_board",1],["potion_halls",4],["restricted_section",2],["rooftop",6],["royal_inspectorate",1],["seal_chamber",2],["seminar_rooms",3],["staff_room",5],["storage_and_lockers",2],["student_council_chamber",1],["study_rooms",2],["wardens_office",1],["workshop",2]]},"student_council_chamber":{"name":"Student Council Chamber","category":"Student Life","kind":"location","description":"A small room at the far end of the Club Rooms corridor on Floor 1, permanently buried in club paperwork. Six seats, president, vice president and one representative per dorm, in a room built for four.","vibe":"cramped, ink, cold tea.","regulars":["Bianca","Caspian","Dante","Florian","Hadrian","Irene","Nerys"],"connections":["club_rooms"],"walk_min":6,"clubs":["Festival Committee","Student Council"],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":"Floor 1","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",1],["archive",2],["bell_tower",6],["canteen",1],["club_rooms",1],["detention_tower",1],["faculty_offices",5],["headmasters_office",5],["lecture_halls",2],["main_library",1],["notice_board",1],["potion_halls",4],["restricted_section",2],["rooftop",6],["royal_inspectorate",1],["seal_chamber",2],["seminar_rooms",3],["staff_room",5],["storage_and_lockers",2],["study_rooms",2],["wardens_office",1],["workshop",2]]},"notice_board":{"name":"Notice Board","category":"Student Life","kind":"location","description":"A long wall of boards in the castle's Floor 1 entrance hall, at the foot of the main stair, where every student passes on the way to class. Club recruitment, exam results, dorm rankings and competition brackets, posted publicly, alongside the student-run half: tutoring offers, study groups, festival posters, lost-item notes and small warnings. After results it is a crowd with elbows. Paid-work openings go within a day. Unofficial notices, dares and betting slips go up overnight and vanish by dawn. Lost items are listed here before they reach the Lost & Found counter at Reception.","vibe":"layered paper, crowded.","regulars":["Aiden","Castor","Irene"],"connections":["courtyards","wardens_office","royal_inspectorate","detention_tower","staff_quarters"],"walk_min":5,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":"Floor 1","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",1],["archive",2],["bell_tower",6],["canteen",1],["club_rooms",1],["courtyards",5],["detention_tower",1],["faculty_offices",5],["headmasters_office",5],["lecture_halls",2],["main_library",1],["potion_halls",4],["restricted_section",2],["rooftop",6],["royal_inspectorate",1],["seal_chamber",2],["seminar_rooms",3],["staff_quarters",9],["staff_room",5],["storage_and_lockers",2],["student_council_chamber",1],["study_rooms",2],["wardens_office",1],["workshop",2]]},"mail_tower":{"name":"Mail Tower","category":"Student Life","kind":"location","description":"The academy's only regular contact with outside: letters and parcels. The upper floors are the aviary where message birds are kept and flown; Creature Studies uses it for bird handling. A sorting floor below handles parcels, with numbered lockers and a tally token for collection; birds carry letters and light goods, heavy goods come slowly by cart. Sunday is the heaviest sorting day, and students on shifts learn everyone's family news first. Students write home from the desks on the sorting floor; a reply takes about a week, and sometimes a small parcel comes with it.\nFeel: feathers, birdcall, cold stairwell.\nBefore the long breaks the sorting floor overflows with parcels going home.","vibe":null,"regulars":["Anselm","Castor","Magnus","Nerys","Royhan","Saffi"],"connections":["reception_and_gatehouse","founders_statue_and_park","medical_centre","groundskeepers_lodge"],"walk_min":8,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":25,"discoverable":false,"near":[["commissary",5],["founders_statue_and_park",2],["groundskeepers_lodge",4],["light_dormitory",5],["mall",6],["medical_centre",2],["reception_and_gatehouse",3]]},"courtyards":{"name":"Courtyards","category":"Student Life","kind":"location","description":"Open spaces between buildings where students can hangout. Not designed for anything in particular, which is exactly why they work. Every flat edge worn smooth from centuries of sitting.","vibe":"open stone, sunny noon, windy dusk.","regulars":["Althair","Anya","Bianca","Dorian","Trixie","Valentin"],"connections":["arbiter_hall","canteen","club_rooms","main_library","notice_board","lecture_halls","faculty_offices","fire_dormitory","light_dormitory","sky_dormitory","viridian_dormitory","mall","medical_centre","founders_statue_and_park","reception_and_gatehouse"],"walk_min":0,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":2,"discoverable":false,"near":[["arbiter_hall",7],["canteen",5],["club_rooms",5],["faculty_offices",5],["fire_dormitory",8],["founders_statue_and_park",7],["grassy_field_and_hills",20],["lecture_halls",5],["light_dormitory",5],["main_library",5],["mall",5],["medical_centre",6],["notice_board",5],["reception_and_gatehouse",9],["sky_dormitory",4],["viridian_dormitory",6]],"seasons":{"Summer":"Students chase the shade around the stone.","Winter":"Swept stone in the middle, snowball fights in the drifts at the edges."}},"sports_field":{"name":"Sports Field","category":"Sport and Grounds","kind":"location","description":"Soccer, running, and Sports Day in Month 6. A running track circles the soccer pitch: home ground of the Soccer Club and the Running Club. Magic banned outright in play, so this is the one part of the academy where being a powerful mage counts for nothing.","vibe":"grass, mud, shouting.","regulars":["Aurelian","Bianca","Percival","Saffi"],"connections":["founders_statue_and_park","archery_range","gymnasium","combat_grounds","sparring_pavilion","spirit_path"],"walk_min":16,"clubs":["Soccer","Running"],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":17,"discoverable":false,"near":[["archery_range",5],["combat_grounds",5],["founders_statue_and_park",9],["gymnasium",3],["menagerie",6],["sparring_pavilion",5],["spirit_path",5],["swimming_pool",3]],"seasons":{"Winter":"Once the snow settles the field closes; the Soccer and Running Clubs move into the Gymnasium and onto the cleared paths."}},"gymnasium":{"name":"Gymnasium","category":"Sport and Grounds","kind":"location","description":"Home of the Gymnastics and Basketball clubs, and of the Swimming Club, which trains in the outdoor pool beside it. Indoor training, used heavily in bad weather and during The Thinning lockdown, when nobody is permitted outside for a week and the place never goes quiet.","vibe":"high roof, echoing.","regulars":["Aurelian","Bianca","Percival","Saffi"],"connections":["menagerie","archery_range","swimming_pool","sports_field","spirit_path"],"walk_min":14,"clubs":["Swimming","Gymnastics","Basketball"],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":16,"discoverable":false,"near":[["archery_range",3],["gardens",5],["menagerie",3],["spirit_path",3],["sports_field",3],["swimming_pool",1]],"seasons":{"Winter":"It is shared by every club that normally trains outside, and booking slots are fought over."}},"swimming_pool":{"name":"Swimming Pool","category":"Sport and Grounds","kind":"location","description":"An outdoor pool beside the Gymnasium, its water kept warm by runes along the rim. Sport clubs and general recreation. Water-type students are banned from competing seriously, which they complain about constantly.\nHome of the Night Swimmer story.","vibe":"sun on water, splashing, wet stone.","regulars":["Aurelian","Bianca","Percival","Saffi"],"connections":["gymnasium"],"walk_min":14,"clubs":["Swimming"],"access":null,"lore":[{"uid":338,"title":"Ghost Story - The Night Swimmer","summary":"Where: the Swimming Pool after dark, most often in winter when the rune-warmed water steams."}],"floor":null,"pin":16,"discoverable":false,"near":[["archery_range",3],["gardens",5],["gymnasium",1],["menagerie",3],["spirit_path",3],["sports_field",3]],"seasons":{"Summer":"Crowded from the last class to the eight o'clock bell.","Winter":"The rune-warmed water steams in the cold; the Swimming Club trains through it and sprints the few steps to the Gymnasium."}},"archery_range":{"name":"Archery Range","category":"Sport and Grounds","kind":"location","description":"Open range for the Archery Club. Magic banned in play like all sport clubs, so it comes down to the arm and the eye. One of the quietest places on the grounds.","vibe":"windy, open, quiet.","regulars":["Aurelian","Bianca","Percival","Saffi"],"connections":["light_dormitory","founders_statue_and_park","gardens","menagerie","gymnasium","sports_field"],"walk_min":11,"clubs":["Archery"],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":15,"discoverable":false,"near":[["founders_statue_and_park",7],["gardens",4],["gymnasium",3],["light_dormitory",6],["menagerie",4],["sports_field",5],["staff_quarters",6],["swimming_pool",3],["viridian_dormitory",6]]},"grassy_field_and_hills":{"name":"Grassy Field and Hills","category":"Sport and Grounds","kind":"location","description":"Wide open rolling ground in the far grounds, twenty minutes' walk from the Main Courtyard, used for recreation year-round, with the castle small in the distance. It is big: the Observation Tower stands on its nearer crest, the Old Hut is another ten minutes out on the far slope, and the lake shore and the Forest treeline are each a quarter of an hour away. On Star Night the hills fill with students in tents and bedrolls, and the campus below goes dark for the stars.\nHome of the Walking Lantern story.","vibe":"open sky, breezy.","regulars":["Faye","Saffi","Tsubaki","Vesna"],"connections":["arbiter_hall","staff_quarters","observation_tower","old_hut","forest","boathouse_and_lake","fishing_house"],"walk_min":20,"clubs":["Camping"],"access":null,"lore":[{"uid":339,"title":"Ghost Story - The Walking Lantern","summary":"Where: the Grassy Field and Hills, after dark."}],"floor":null,"pin":36,"discoverable":false,"near":[["boathouse_and_lake",15],["courtyards",20],["fishing_house",14],["forest",15],["observation_tower",5],["old_hut",10]],"seasons":{"Spring":"Kites go up on every windy afternoon.","Summer":"Long evenings on blankets until the eight o'clock bell.","Autumn":"The grass turns gold and the wind picks up.","Winter":"The slopes become sledding runs, on trays borrowed from the Canteen."}},"forest":{"name":"Forest","category":"Sport and Grounds","kind":"location","description":"Wide old woodland at the farthest edge of the grounds, past the far slope of the Hills (a quarter of an hour from the field, twenty-five minutes along the lake shore). Creature Studies fieldwork, foraging, walking, and where students go when they want to not be found. Students leave a bite before eating there (Eating in the Forest superstition). Creature Studies teaches there and patrols watch its edge. A deer path, half an hour's walk, leads deep in to the Forest Clearing and its Elder Oak, the one bright place inside it.","vibe":"old growth, muffled, watched.","regulars":["Dante","Lenna","Maple","Nerys","Vallie"],"connections":["grassy_field_and_hills","old_hut","boathouse_and_lake","forest_clearing"],"walk_min":35,"clubs":[],"access":"Far edge of the grounds; curfew applies after dark","lore":[{"uid":225,"title":"Eating in the Forest","summary":"Rule: share first."}],"floor":null,"pin":37,"discoverable":false,"near":[["boathouse_and_lake",25],["forest_clearing",30],["grassy_field_and_hills",15],["old_hut",5]],"seasons":{"Spring":"Foraging season opens: wild garlic and early greens at the edges.","Summer":"The canopy closes and the Forest is at its darkest by day.","Autumn":"Mushrooms and nuts; Creature Studies warns about the ones that look alike.","Winter":"Dusk comes early, so the patrols turn students back from the treeline by late afternoon; tracks in the snow show what else walks there."}},"boathouse_and_lake":{"name":"Boathouse and Lake","category":"Sport and Grounds","kind":"location","description":"Vast open water in the far grounds, twenty minutes' walk beyond the Gardens, for rowing, swimming and the Fishing Club. The boathouse stores the craft and doubles as a quiet place to sit. Three minutes' walk along the shore from the boathouse stands the Fishing Club's Fishing House, with its own dock. Sound carries strangely across the water: a far-bank conversation arrives too clearly. Home of the Crying on the Water story; the boathouse refuses bookings after dark. Willow Island sits in the middle of the lake, reached only by boat.","vibe":"wet timber, cold water.","regulars":["Aiden","Anya","Milena","Ottavio","Rigel","Sophia","Wren"],"connections":["grassy_field_and_hills","gardens","forest","fishing_house","willow_island"],"walk_min":30,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[{"uid":208,"title":"Ghost Story - The Crying on the Water","summary":"Where: the Lake, after dark."}],"floor":null,"pin":12,"discoverable":false,"near":[["fishing_house",3],["forest",25],["gardens",20],["grassy_field_and_hills",15],["willow_island",10]],"seasons":{"Spring":"Rowing season opens once the water warms.","Summer":"The lake is at its busiest: rowers, swimmers off the jetty, the Fishing Club at dawn.","Autumn":"Morning mist sits on the water until mid-morning.","Winter":"The boats are stored, ice forms along the shallows, and the boathouse lends a boat only on a still, mild day."}},"gardens":{"name":"Gardens","category":"Sport and Grounds","kind":"location","description":"Cultivated grounds tended by students and staff, growing Potion Crafting reagents alongside ordinary plants. The Gardening Club effectively runs them, and students gather here before the Harvest Festival. Everything grows a little too well. Halvard: the Sky outcasts' meeting ground; the far end is a reliable place to skip class.\nHome of the Breath on the Glass story.","vibe":"turned earth, herb beds in long rows.","regulars":["Cedric","Idris","Lenna","Maple","Nerys","Royhan","Ruby","Vesna","Zara"],"connections":["staff_quarters","viridian_dormitory","menagerie","archery_range","boathouse_and_lake"],"walk_min":10,"clubs":["Gardening"],"access":null,"lore":[{"uid":340,"title":"Ghost Story - Breath on the Glass","summary":"Where: inside the Gardens' greenhouses, in the late afternoon and evening."}],"floor":null,"pin":13,"discoverable":false,"near":[["archery_range",4],["boathouse_and_lake",20],["gymnasium",5],["light_dormitory",6],["menagerie",3],["staff_quarters",3],["swimming_pool",5],["viridian_dormitory",4]],"seasons":{"Spring":"Planting season: seedling rows under glass cloches.","Summer":"Everything overgrows; the Gardening Club weeds daily.","Autumn":"The harvest comes in for the Harvest Festival.","Winter":"The beds sleep under straw and snow; the reagents grow on in the greenhouses, which glow warm through the dark afternoons."}},"menagerie":{"name":"Menagerie","category":"Sport and Grounds","kind":"location","description":"Live specimens for Creature Studies, housed and handled by students under supervision. Beast Handling Club territory. Halvard: the Creature Studies teacher lives beside it in converted stables. Mucking out is the highest-paying paid-work post because nobody volunteers. The animals sense weather changes before the handlers. Magical Beast lives here.\nHome of the When the Pens Go Quiet story.","vibe":"straw, scratched bars, strange calls.","regulars":["Faye","Lenna","Vallie","Vesna"],"connections":["gardens","archery_range","gymnasium","spirit_path"],"walk_min":13,"clubs":["Beast Handling"],"access":null,"lore":[{"uid":341,"title":"Ghost Story - When the Pens Go Quiet","summary":"Where: the Menagerie, from dusk into the night."}],"floor":null,"pin":14,"discoverable":false,"near":[["archery_range",4],["gardens",3],["gymnasium",3],["spirit_path",5],["sports_field",6],["staff_quarters",6],["swimming_pool",3]],"seasons":{"Spring":"Young ones are born and the handlers barely sleep.","Winter":"The animals grow thick coats, the pens are strawed deep, and the smaller specimens sleep through the cold in heated boxes."}},"observation_tower":{"name":"Observation Tower","category":"Sport and Grounds","kind":"location","description":"A high tower on the nearer crest of the Hills, five minutes up from the field, for astral and celestial work, most important to Mystic students; the Divination Society meets here. The most contested spot on campus on Star Night. Instruments turn by themselves at night. Its great telescope has a Norvaine starglass lens, the Divination Society's pride.","vibe":"high, windy, deep dark.","regulars":["Gareth","Kanae","Tsubaki"],"connections":["grassy_field_and_hills"],"walk_min":25,"clubs":["Divination"],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":9,"discoverable":false,"near":[["grassy_field_and_hills",5]],"seasons":{"Summer":"Short nights; the Divination Society waits for midnight.","Winter":"Winter nights are the clearest and the coldest; the Divination Society works in coats and gloves."},"gate":"grassy_field_and_hills"},"medical_centre":{"name":"Medical Centre","category":"Services","kind":"location","description":"A white-walled building of its own, four minutes' walk from the Mall, with a herb garden along one side: more than an infirmary, less than a hospital. Treatment rooms, a small apothecary, and an inpatient ward where students stay overnight or for days under care. Staffed by Spiritual mages; busiest after Practical Magic, in competition weeks, exam weeks, and after The Thinning. Nurses see injuries they must report, and injuries they leave off the report. The attached Healing Ward is a teaching space where students practise on real patients under supervision. Staff can spot a Nightwell's Vigil overdose at a glance. Can heal any minor to mid injury to pristine; anything beyond is stabilised here and sent on to a proper hospital. The ward's beds are for the injured first, but a nurse will let an exhausted student lie down for an hour.\nHome of the Last Bed story.","vibe":"white walls, clean linen, too quiet.","regulars":["Anya","Hester","Percival","Sophia","Tilly","Vera"],"connections":["courtyards","reception_and_gatehouse","light_dormitory","founders_statue_and_park","mall","mail_tower","commissary"],"walk_min":6,"clubs":["Medical Centre Volunteers"],"access":null,"lore":[{"uid":344,"title":"Ghost Story - The Last Bed","summary":"Where: the Medical Centre, at night, for students kept in overnight."}],"floor":null,"pin":24,"discoverable":false,"near":[["commissary",4],["courtyards",6],["founders_statue_and_park",3],["groundskeepers_lodge",6],["light_dormitory",5],["mail_tower",2],["mall",4],["reception_and_gatehouse",4]],"seasons":{"Summer":"Sunburn and sports injuries.","Winter":"The winter cold that goes round campus fills its ward with head colds."}},"commissary":{"name":"Commissary","category":"Services","kind":"location","description":"The academy shop, a big open-sided stall of its own, three minutes' walk from the Mall: one broad roof on timber posts, open on all four sides, its counters and shelves crammed to the rafters like a general store that sells a bit of everything. Supplies, uniforms, stationery, reagents, equipment, with special orders for anything not stocked. The cheap tier against the mall's store; specialised items can still eat a week of points. Sunfizz sells here for eight points, bottles returned for two. Everyday kit: notebooks, pencils, pen nibs and ink, folders, satchels, printed class textbooks; reagents and equipment on the back shelves. Its cheap stationery and everyday kit are Caelmari-made.","vibe":"crowded shelves, new cloth, leather.","regulars":["Caralynn","Idris","Vesna","Zara"],"connections":["reception_and_gatehouse","mall","medical_centre","banking_house"],"walk_min":8,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[{"uid":210,"title":"Sunfizz","summary":"The soda every student drinks, sold at the Commissary and the Mall store in heavy glass bottles."},{"uid":213,"title":"Firetooth","summary":"A tin of hard sweets hot enough to make the eyes water, sold everywhere."}],"floor":null,"pin":23,"discoverable":false,"near":[["banking_house",3],["cathedral",7],["mail_tower",5],["mall",3],["medical_centre",4],["meditation_rooms",6],["reception_and_gatehouse",3]]},"reception_and_gatehouse":{"name":"Reception and Gatehouse","category":"Services","kind":"location","description":"Where visitors are received and logged, and the formal boundary of the academy. Everyone entering or leaving passes through, which makes it the most watched building on campus. The boundary wards are felt as a change of pressure in the gateway. The Gatehouse includes a visiting parlour where students meet family and approved visitors during visiting hours, with worn armchairs, a tea table and windows facing the approach road. Visitors are logged at Reception before entering; meeting here does not give them access to the rest of the grounds.","vibe":"iron, registers, watched.","regulars":[],"connections":["courtyards","commissary","medical_centre","mail_tower","groundskeepers_lodge"],"walk_min":9,"clubs":[],"access":"The only way in or out","lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":26,"discoverable":false,"near":[["banking_house",6],["commissary",3],["courtyards",9],["founders_statue_and_park",6],["groundskeepers_lodge",5],["mail_tower",3],["mall",6],["medical_centre",4]]},"groundskeepers_lodge":{"name":"Groundskeeper's Lodge","category":"Services","kind":"location","description":"Small quarters at the edge of the grounds for staff who maintain the fields, gardens and walls. The Groundskeeping club reports here. The one building on campus where nothing is enchanted.","vibe":"cut grass, oil, old tools.","regulars":["Dante","Lenna","Vera"],"connections":["reception_and_gatehouse","founders_statue_and_park","mail_tower","combat_grounds"],"walk_min":11,"clubs":["Groundskeeping"],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":20,"discoverable":false,"near":[["combat_grounds",5],["founders_statue_and_park",4],["mail_tower",4],["medical_centre",6],["reception_and_gatehouse",5]],"seasons":{"Autumn":"Groundskeeping rakes leaves from dawn.","Winter":"Groundskeeping clears the paths of snow before the seven o'clock bell."}},"detention_tower":{"name":"Detention Tower","category":"Services","kind":"location","description":"One of the castle core's towers, climbed by its own narrow spiral stair from Floor 1. Where punished students are sent after classes for menial work: copying, cleaning, sorting archive material. The academy's only visible enforcement, and a mild one, which raises the question of what happens to students who do something genuinely serious.","vibe":"endless stairs, scratching pens.","regulars":[],"connections":["notice_board"],"walk_min":6,"clubs":[],"access":"When assigned detention","lore":[],"floor":"Floor 1","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",1],["archive",2],["bell_tower",6],["canteen",1],["club_rooms",1],["faculty_offices",5],["headmasters_office",5],["lecture_halls",2],["main_library",1],["notice_board",1],["potion_halls",4],["restricted_section",2],["rooftop",6],["royal_inspectorate",1],["seal_chamber",2],["seminar_rooms",3],["staff_room",5],["storage_and_lockers",2],["student_council_chamber",1],["study_rooms",2],["wardens_office",1],["workshop",2]]},"meditation_rooms":{"name":"Meditation Rooms","category":"Services","kind":"location","description":"An old, weathered building built like a riad: blank outer walls with few windows, every room facing inward onto a shaded central courtyard with a still, shallow pool. Moss and vines cover its walls and dense, leafy trees crowd close around it; between the thick walls and the trees, no sound from the campus gets in. Small, dim rooms with floor cushions serve will-focus training, and the courtyard is for anyone who simply needs to sit. Open to every student, for training or just to take a breath. The one house rule: speak no louder than a murmur, and leave others to their silence. Mana settles and refills faster in the silence; students come before exams and after long practicals.","vibe":"calm, serene, hushed, moss and cool stone.","regulars":["Anselm","Caspian","Faye","Tristan"],"connections":["banking_house","cathedral","noble_houses_liaison"],"walk_min":11,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":32,"discoverable":false,"near":[["banking_house",4],["broken_statue",6],["cathedral",3],["commissary",6],["dovecote",6],["mall",6],["noble_houses_liaison",3]],"seasons":{"Winter":"The bare vines let more pale light into the courtyard, and the pool wears a thin skin of ice."}},"dovecote":{"name":"The Dovecote","category":"External Presence","kind":"location","description":"A compound on academy grounds but not of the academy, reporting to the crown; the Headmaster has no authority over anyone inside. Doves are permanent, rotated in from the capital, and not academy staff. They arrest for forbidden magic, investigate incidents, hold prisoners briefly, and send serious cases onward. Always in pure marble-white cloaks. Students call it the Coop or the Roost, and the Doves themselves Pigeons, and fear it regardless; they cross the courtyard in front of it faster than any other. Halvard: a Commander and a Senior Dove second (who also teaches Dark Magic Defense) are tracing an unregistered forbidden-magic group whose traces they have found, knowing nothing of its name, members or aims.","vibe":"blinding white, cold, feared.","regulars":["Dante","Krieg","Milena"],"connections":["cathedral","noble_houses_liaison","broken_statue"],"walk_min":12,"clubs":[],"access":"Crown ground — the Doves' compound","lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":28,"discoverable":false,"near":[["broken_statue",2],["cathedral",5],["fire_dormitory",6],["meditation_rooms",6],["noble_houses_liaison",3]]},"royal_inspectorate":{"name":"The Royal Inspectorate","category":"External Presence","kind":"location","description":"A suite of offices on Castle Floor 1 behind a heavy door hung with the crown's banners: academy stone, crown ground. The Headmaster's authority stops at that door. Its wing is the same Floor 1 wing as the Warden's corridor, which neither side enjoys. A crown office auditing academic standards and mana output, answering to the capital. Where the Doves handle crime, the Inspectorate handles performance: exam results, ranking integrity, and how much the student body actually feeds the seal. That last duty puts them in the Warden's territory, since the Warden keeps the ledgers and the Inspectorate wants to read them. Halvard: they blame the breach on the Warden's office and press the Acting Warden, who refuses every time.","vibe":"ink, clicking counting frames, bureaucratic.","regulars":[],"connections":["notice_board","wardens_office"],"walk_min":6,"clubs":[],"access":"Crown office — the Headmaster has no authority past the door","lore":[],"floor":"Floor 1","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",1],["archive",2],["bell_tower",6],["canteen",1],["club_rooms",1],["detention_tower",1],["faculty_offices",5],["headmasters_office",5],["lecture_halls",2],["main_library",1],["notice_board",1],["potion_halls",4],["restricted_section",2],["rooftop",6],["seal_chamber",2],["seminar_rooms",3],["staff_room",5],["storage_and_lockers",2],["student_council_chamber",1],["study_rooms",2],["wardens_office",1],["workshop",2]]},"cathedral":{"name":"The Cathedral","category":"External Presence","kind":"location","description":"A house of worship for Asmoday, Goddess of Creation, on academy grounds but answerable to its own authority. Services open to all; its clergy are not academy employees and teach that Asmoday created magic and gifted it to mortals. Every service opens with the Shaping of the World; the clergy teach that Asmoday fractured magic after the First Bargain. That a goddess of creation holds ground at an institution built around sealing things away is a tension nobody discusses openly. It also runs orphanages across the kingdom, the Asmoday's Mercy houses. Halvard: run by a steward who keeps the registry of every oath sworn on academy grounds. A service is held every Sunday morning, from nine to eleven, and the pews are open every day for anyone who wants to sit in quiet. Students of every dormitory come: some to pray, some for the singing, some because it is the one place a conversation with a stranger does not seem strange. Mana comes back a little faster in the quiet of the nave; the clergy call it Asmoday's grace, the academy calls it the silence, and both are glad to see students on the pews.","vibe":"stained-glass colour, incense, heavy stillness.","regulars":["Anya","Caspian","Percival","Rigel","Tristan"],"connections":["sky_dormitory","mall","dovecote","noble_houses_liaison","broken_statue","meditation_rooms"],"walk_min":8,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":29,"discoverable":false,"near":[["banking_house",6],["broken_statue",4],["commissary",7],["dovecote",5],["fire_dormitory",6],["mall",5],["meditation_rooms",3],["noble_houses_liaison",4],["sky_dormitory",4]]},"noble_houses_liaison":{"name":"The Noble Houses' Liaison","category":"External Presence","kind":"location","description":"A small elegant manor hung with the banners of the noble houses, standing near the Cathedral and the Dovecote. A standing office representing the noble houses' interests, and the reason noble conduct is a graded part of Etiquette rather than a courtesy. It tracks promising students long before Graduation in Month 11, keeps its own notes on who is worth approaching, and hosts house representatives. Students who do not catch its attention usually never learn it exists. Its protocol follows Velmoran court manners.","vibe":"carpeted, soft, deliberately comfortable.","regulars":["Caine","Caralynn","Caspian","Florian"],"connections":["dovecote","cathedral","meditation_rooms"],"walk_min":12,"clubs":[],"access":"By invitation","lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":30,"discoverable":false,"near":[["broken_statue",4],["cathedral",4],["dovecote",3],["meditation_rooms",3]]},"banking_house":{"name":"The Banking House","category":"External Presence","kind":"location","description":"A square stone building with a flat roof, heavy double doors, and a gilded coin emblem mounted above the entrance. The academy's only currency exchange, converting points to real money and back at 1:1 either way. It also moves real coin in and out of the grounds: family money, paid-work earnings and betting settlements all become coin here. It stands outside the mall, so a visit is a deliberate errand. A branch of the World Bank of the Arslan Sultanate; its clerks answer to the Sultanate, not the academy.","vibe":"polished counters, clinking coin.","regulars":["Aiden","Caralynn","Royhan"],"connections":["mall","commissary","meditation_rooms"],"walk_min":10,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":27,"discoverable":false,"near":[["cathedral",6],["commissary",3],["mall",5],["meditation_rooms",4],["reception_and_gatehouse",6]]},"forest_clearing":{"name":"Forest Clearing","category":"Sport and Grounds","kind":"location","description":"A single oak called the Elder Oak stands in an open clearing in the middle of the Forest, so broad a dozen students holding hands cannot circle it, and older than the castle by anyone's guess. The canopy opens above the clearing, so the oak stands in full sun while the woods around it stay dim; the muffled quiet of the Forest gives way to birdsong at its edge, and gold motes drift in the light even on grey days. Its roots pull the ground's mana into slow currents unlike anywhere else on campus, and a wild field of rare flowers has spread across the clearing around it, in colours found nowhere else. The Gardening Club has tried transplanting them; they wilt within a day of leaving the clearing. A deer path leads in from the treeline, about thirty minutes' walk. Students come to read, nap between the roots, or be alone without feeling lost. The crust for Eating in the Forest goes on its roots. Patrols turn students back at dusk, and nobody answers their name out here after dark. In winter the clearing stays green and in flower while snow lies everywhere around it. Sitting among the oak's roots, a mage feels their mana refill like water finding its level.","vibe":"sunlit, still, majestic, wildflowers and birdsong.","regulars":["Baelin","Idris","Lenna","Maple","Royhan"],"connections":["forest"],"walk_min":65,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":11,"discoverable":false,"near":[["forest",30]],"seasons":{"Spring":"The flower field comes in weeks before anything else on campus."},"gate":"forest"},"rooftop":{"name":"Rooftop","category":"Student Life","kind":"location","description":"The flat lead roofs of the castle core, joined by parapet walks and short stairs between the gables. Officially out of bounds. The only way up is a small locked door off the Bell Tower stair, and the trick of opening it is passed from older students to younger ones, never written down; being shown the way up means someone has decided you belong. From the parapet the whole academy lies open: the courtyards, the four dormitories, the Hills, the Lake, the Forest's dark edge, the white roofs of the Dovecote. At night the mana lanterns spread below like a lit map, and at month end you can watch them dim together. The campus's quiet romantic secret: couples come up for sunset and the lantern view, and a hidden corner behind the eastern gable is where confessions happen. Nobody who has been brought up here tells, and the rule is to leave a corner free if someone is already in it. Birds lift off just before each bell, and the lead hums underfoot when it rings. Staff walk the courtyards after curfew, never the roof.\nHome of the Other Climber story.","vibe":"wide sky, wind, sun-warm lead, a shared secret.","regulars":["Aiden","Alyssa","Rei","William","Zara"],"connections":["bell_tower"],"walk_min":7,"clubs":[],"access":"Officially out of bounds","lore":[{"uid":345,"title":"Ghost Story - The Other Climber","summary":"Where: the Rooftop, at night."}],"floor":"Towers & Roof","pin":1,"discoverable":true,"near":[["announcement_room",6],["archive",7],["bell_tower",1],["canteen",6],["club_rooms",6],["detention_tower",6],["faculty_offices",2],["headmasters_office",2],["lecture_halls",5],["main_library",6],["notice_board",6],["potion_halls",3],["restricted_section",7],["royal_inspectorate",6],["seal_chamber",7],["seminar_rooms",4],["staff_room",2],["storage_and_lockers",5],["student_council_chamber",6],["study_rooms",5],["wardens_office",6],["workshop",7]],"seasons":{"Summer":"Every corner is taken at sunset.","Winter":"The lead roofs ice over and even the couples stay away."}},"headmasters_office":{"name":"Headmaster's Office","category":"Academic","kind":"location","description":"At the end of the Faculty Offices corridor, a round room up a short stair, its tall windows over the Main Courtyard. Forty years of one Elf's tenure fill it: shelves layered deep with books, and letters and small gifts from graduates. In the window stands a sapling grown from the Elder Oak, forty years old and still knee-high. Students come only when it matters: serious discipline, a request to repeat a year, news no one wants to hear. The bench outside is where the real waiting happens. Visitors from the Royal Inspectorate and the Dovecote are received here, since the Headmaster has no authority inside the Dovecote's walls or past the Inspectorate's door. The door stands open whenever the Headmaster is in.","vibe":"old wood, ink, green leaves, patient quiet.","regulars":["Althair","Baelin","Gavlan","Tristan"],"connections":["faculty_offices"],"walk_min":6,"clubs":[],"access":"When it matters: discipline, requests, bad news","lore":[],"floor":"Floor 5","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["announcement_room",5],["archive",6],["bell_tower",2],["canteen",5],["club_rooms",5],["detention_tower",5],["faculty_offices",1],["lecture_halls",4],["main_library",5],["notice_board",5],["potion_halls",2],["restricted_section",6],["rooftop",2],["royal_inspectorate",5],["seal_chamber",6],["seminar_rooms",3],["staff_room",1],["storage_and_lockers",4],["student_council_chamber",5],["study_rooms",4],["wardens_office",5],["workshop",6]]},"staff_quarters":{"name":"Staff Quarters","category":"Residential","kind":"location","description":"A separate stone house for the resident teaching staff (Dorm Heads live in their own dormitories instead), standing on its own beside the castle and joined to the castle's ground floor by a short covered walk: private rooms upstairs, and downstairs a shared parlour with mismatched armchairs, a kettle that is never cold, and a porch facing the Gardens. Where the Staff Room keeps students out, the Staff Quarters let them in: students may knock until the eight o'clock bell, and nothing said in the parlour counts as a consultation or a referral. It is where students come for help they would not ask for in class, advice about home, a second opinion on a club, or just tea with a teacher they like. Teachers here are off duty and act like it. Every door says something about who lives behind it: forest air draughting under Gavlan's, two teacups and a stack of theory on Layla's, and notes slid under Mimosa's, answered by morning. Vallie Goredust lives out by the Menagerie but holds court in the parlour anyway.","vibe":"lamplight, tea, worn armchairs, lived-in.","regulars":["Gavlan","Hester","Kotaro","Layla","Mimosa","Sophia","Vallie","Yvette"],"connections":["notice_board","arbiter_hall","viridian_dormitory","gardens","grassy_field_and_hills"],"walk_min":10,"clubs":[],"access":"Staff residence","lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":8,"discoverable":false,"near":[["arbiter_hall",3],["archery_range",6],["gardens",3],["menagerie",6],["notice_board",9],["viridian_dormitory",4]]},"fire_dormitory":{"name":"Fire Dormitory","category":"Residential","kind":"location","description":"Home of the Elementalists (red vest). Red-tiled roof and a red banner over the door. A great hearth burns in its common room day and night, and the broad chimney stack rising above the front of the building is always warm, even in winter. Inside: a common area and personal rooms. Creed: \"Through the Elements, Victory Is Ours.\"","vibe":"hearth warmth, a chimney warm even in winter, stone.","regulars":["Aurelian","Bruno","Wren","Yvette"],"connections":["courtyards","sky_dormitory","broken_statue","common_rooms","laundry","bathhouse_and_washrooms"],"walk_min":8,"clubs":[],"access":"Residents only (bracelet door)","lore":[{"uid":207,"title":"Ghost Story - The Three O'Clock Knock","summary":"Where: a dorm door, at three in the morning, in a dormitory that admits only its own students."}],"floor":null,"pin":3,"discoverable":false,"near":[["bathhouse_and_washrooms",1],["broken_statue",4],["cathedral",6],["common_rooms",1],["courtyards",8],["dovecote",6],["laundry",1],["sky_dormitory",5]],"seasons":{"Summer":"The hearth burns anyway, and the common room is the hottest place on campus.","Winter":"The hearth is the envy of the other three dormitories."}},"light_dormitory":{"name":"Light Dormitory","category":"Residential","kind":"location","description":"Home of the Mystics (yellow vest). Golden-tiled roof and a yellow banner over the door. Its inner court is roofed by a glass dome over the common area, which glows from within after dark. Inside: the glass dome common area plus personal rooms. Creed: \"The Third Eye Lights The Way.\"","vibe":"sunlight through glass, pale stone.","regulars":["Bianca","Ezrel","Hadrian","Topaz"],"connections":["courtyards","viridian_dormitory","medical_centre","founders_statue_and_park","archery_range","common_rooms","laundry","bathhouse_and_washrooms"],"walk_min":5,"clubs":[],"access":"Residents only (bracelet door)","lore":[{"uid":207,"title":"Ghost Story - The Three O'Clock Knock","summary":"Where: a dorm door, at three in the morning, in a dormitory that admits only its own students."}],"floor":null,"pin":6,"discoverable":false,"near":[["archery_range",6],["bathhouse_and_washrooms",13],["common_rooms",13],["courtyards",5],["founders_statue_and_park",3],["gardens",6],["laundry",13],["mail_tower",5],["medical_centre",5],["viridian_dormitory",3]],"seasons":{"Summer":"The dome turns the common area into a greenhouse by afternoon.","Winter":"Snow slides off the warm glass dome, which glows brighter against the early dark."}},"sky_dormitory":{"name":"Sky Dormitory","category":"Residential","kind":"location","description":"Home of the Occultists (blue vest). Deep-blue-tiled roof and a blue banner over the door. A single slender tower rises from one corner, and the building's enchanted walls let residents see the academy grounds from their rooms; from outside the windows shimmer faintly, like water. Inside: common area and personal rooms. Creed: \"Together We Are Strong.\"\nStigma: Occult carries a reputation no other type does. Outsiders associate it with blood magic, demon summoning, and spirits bound against their will, and cannot always tell legal Occult practice from forbidden work. The Doves watch Occultists more closely than any other dorm, and Sky students are often the first suspected when something goes wrong. The creed reflects this: Sky students close ranks because few others will stand with them.","vibe":"cool stone, shimmering windows.","regulars":["Maple","Ottavio","Rigel","William"],"connections":["courtyards","fire_dormitory","mall","cathedral","broken_statue","common_rooms","laundry","bathhouse_and_washrooms"],"walk_min":4,"clubs":[],"access":"Residents only (bracelet door)","lore":[{"uid":207,"title":"Ghost Story - The Three O'Clock Knock","summary":"Where: a dorm door, at three in the morning, in a dormitory that admits only its own students."}],"floor":null,"pin":4,"discoverable":false,"near":[["bathhouse_and_washrooms",5],["broken_statue",6],["cathedral",4],["common_rooms",5],["courtyards",4],["fire_dormitory",5],["laundry",5],["mall",4]]},"viridian_dormitory":{"name":"Viridian Dormitory","category":"Residential","kind":"location","description":"Home of the Spiritualists (green vest). Green-tiled roof and a green banner over the door. An old oak fills its inner court, its crown rising above the roofline, with meditation stones set among its roots. Inside: common area, meditation rooms, personal rooms. Creed: \"Know Thyself, Know Victory.\"","vibe":"oak shade, rustling leaves, stone.","regulars":["Castor","Faye","Kuroo","Percival"],"connections":["courtyards","arbiter_hall","staff_quarters","gardens","light_dormitory","common_rooms","laundry","bathhouse_and_washrooms"],"walk_min":6,"clubs":[],"access":"Residents only (bracelet door)","lore":[{"uid":207,"title":"Ghost Story - The Three O'Clock Knock","summary":"Where: a dorm door, at three in the morning, in a dormitory that admits only its own students."}],"floor":null,"pin":5,"discoverable":false,"near":[["arbiter_hall",4],["archery_range",6],["bathhouse_and_washrooms",13],["common_rooms",13],["courtyards",6],["founders_statue_and_park",6],["gardens",4],["laundry",13],["light_dormitory",3],["staff_quarters",4]],"seasons":{"Spring":"The inner oak comes into new leaf.","Summer":"Deep shade over the meditation stones.","Autumn":"The oak turns gold and leaves drift into the common area.","Winter":"Bare branches over the roofline; the meditation stones sit under snow."}},"old_hut":{"name":"Old Hut","category":"Sport and Grounds","kind":"location","description":"A one-room timber hut on the far slope of the Hills, where the grass runs out against the Forest treeline. Nobody remembers who built it or when; the Groundskeeper's Lodge lists it as disused and not worth repairing, and leaves it standing. The roof sags, the door hangs from one hinge, and the cold hearth still holds old ash. It is where students go to share secrets: far from every building and path, with nobody walking past, and by long student custom what is said inside the Old Hut stays there. Generations of confessions have left initials carved into the inside walls. It also serves as shelter from sudden rain, and on Star Night it is claimed before sunset. After dark nobody lingers, since it sits right on the Forest edge where patrols walk and names are not answered.","vibe":"weathered wood, wind through gaps, grass and pine.","regulars":[],"connections":["grassy_field_and_hills","forest"],"walk_min":30,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":10,"discoverable":false,"near":[["forest",5],["grassy_field_and_hills",10]],"seasons":{"Winter":"Hardly anyone climbs to the Old Hut in winter: snow drifts against the door, the path over the Hills disappears, and a secret told there in the cold is one someone went to real trouble for."},"gate":"grassy_field_and_hills"},"announcement_room":{"name":"Announcement Room","category":"Student Life","kind":"location","description":"A small booth-like room off the Club Rooms corridor on Floor 1, home of the Academy Newspaper club. A speaking rune set into the desk carries whatever is said into it, live, to the Announcement Pillars around the grounds; nothing is recorded. Students on duty open the day with a good-morning after the seven o'clock bell and give the noon, afternoon and evening greetings, the last just before the eight o'clock bell. In between they read out what staff, the Student Council and event organisers send down, plus whatever the student on duty decides is important, the most argued-about power any club holds. Outside class periods the Music Club plays live from the side room, and the whole campus hears it. Staff can take over the rune for anything urgent; during The Thinning lockdown it is how the academy speaks to everyone at once.","vibe":"cramped, warm lamplight, sheet music and newsprint.","regulars":["Aurelian","Caralynn","Castor","Linus","Ruby"],"connections":["club_rooms"],"walk_min":6,"clubs":["Newspaper"],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":"Floor 1","pin":1,"discoverable":false,"near":[["archive",2],["bell_tower",6],["canteen",1],["club_rooms",1],["detention_tower",1],["faculty_offices",5],["headmasters_office",5],["lecture_halls",2],["main_library",1],["notice_board",1],["potion_halls",4],["restricted_section",2],["rooftop",6],["royal_inspectorate",1],["seal_chamber",2],["seminar_rooms",3],["staff_room",5],["storage_and_lockers",2],["student_council_chamber",1],["study_rooms",2],["wardens_office",1],["workshop",2]]},"broken_statue":{"name":"Broken Statue","category":"Sport and Grounds","kind":"location","description":"A white marble statue standing in a stand of old trees between the Fire Dormitory and the Dovecote, off the path students take when they would rather not walk past the Dovecote's front. The figure has lost its head and one arm; the arm lies half-sunk in the moss at its feet, and moss and lichen have crept over the rest until the white shows only in patches. The inscription on its plinth has worn smooth. Who it depicted is unknown, and nobody on staff claims to know; students have theories and none of them agree. Groundskeeping leaves it exactly as it is. Light comes through the leaves in pieces, and the place is quieter than it should be for somewhere so close to the courtyard.","vibe":"green shade, cold marble, moss, stillness.","regulars":[],"connections":["fire_dormitory","sky_dormitory","dovecote","cathedral"],"walk_min":10,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":33,"discoverable":false,"near":[["cathedral",4],["dovecote",2],["fire_dormitory",4],["meditation_rooms",6],["noble_houses_liaison",4],["sky_dormitory",6]]},"sparring_pavilion":{"name":"The Sparring Pavilion","category":"Academic","kind":"location","description":"A small round pavilion with a domed roof at the far corner of the Combat Grounds, the one building all four dorm training areas share. Inside: racks of training foci, ward-chalk and spare casting gear signed out by bracelet; benches, a water pump and a basic first-aid chest for the walk back after a hard session; a board of duel challenges and club standings. The club duels with spells inside warded rings, not staves. It is the Magic Duelling Club's headquarters, the standing exception to dorm separation, so it is the one place on the grounds where students of rival dorms share a bench. Gavlan Haverton, who advises the club, keeps a desk in the back. Unwritten rule: grudges from the rings are settled in the rings, never under the roof.","vibe":"sweat, strapped wrists, chalk dust, tired laughter.","regulars":["Bruno","Caspian","Gavlan","Linus","Sophia","Topaz","Tsubaki","William"],"connections":["sports_field","combat_grounds"],"walk_min":17,"clubs":["Magic Duelling Club (headquarters)"],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":19,"discoverable":false,"near":[["combat_grounds",3],["sports_field",5]]},"fishing_house":{"name":"Fishing House","category":"Sport and Grounds","kind":"location","description":"The Fishing Club's timber hut on the lake shore, three minutes' walk along the shore from the boathouse, full of rods, nets and tackle, with its own long dock built for fishing rather than boats. Behind it, a stone-edged pond raises fish for the Canteen kitchen and the Fishing Club's breeding projects. The club meets here; the dock is busiest at dawn, and quiet enough that people come to sit on it without a rod.","vibe":"tar, wet rope, early mist on the water.","regulars":["Aiden","Anya","Milena","Ottavio","Rigel","Sophia","Wren"],"connections":["grassy_field_and_hills","boathouse_and_lake"],"walk_min":33,"clubs":["Fishing"],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":34,"discoverable":false,"near":[["boathouse_and_lake",3],["grassy_field_and_hills",14]],"seasons":{"Winter":"A stove burns in the hut, and the dawn regulars fish from the end of the dock through the mist."},"gate":"boathouse_and_lake"},"willow_island":{"name":"Willow Island","category":"Sport and Grounds","kind":"location","description":"A small island in the middle of the lake with one great willow tree on it, reached only by a boat from the boathouse, which refuses bookings after dark. At night the willow glows in the distance from the many fireflies that live on the island, so anyone out there after dark was either rowed out before sunset or took a boat without asking.","vibe":"still water, trailing leaves, firefly light.","regulars":[],"connections":["boathouse_and_lake"],"walk_min":40,"clubs":[],"access":"By boat from the boathouse; no bookings after dark","lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":35,"discoverable":false,"near":[["boathouse_and_lake",10]],"seasons":{"Winter":"The fireflies stay all winter, even over the ice, which Creature Studies cannot explain."},"gate":"boathouse_and_lake"},"spirit_path":{"name":"Spirit Path","category":"Sport and Grounds","kind":"location","description":"A narrow footpath that leaves the grounds behind the Gymnasium and winds through old trees along the eastern edge of the academy, a loop short enough to walk in a quarter of an hour. Spirits like it here: the air under the trees is still and green, lesser spirits drift among the roots and branches, and small stone cairns that students have stacked over the years mark the way. Spirit users bring their pact partners here to let them out for a short walk. It is also where beginners come to meet a lesser spirit and try their first Spirit Pact; the custom is to go slowly, offer something small, and let the spirit choose. Almost any Occult student can bond a lesser spirit; a pact is a lasting contract, and the Occult teachers expect to be told of one. Anyone may come to watch: a stone bench at each bend faces the trees, and at dusk and dawn the lesser spirits are easy to see, a flicker in the ferns, a small light keeping pace along a branch. Most are shy; now and then one comes close out of curiosity, and it is considered lucky to be looked over and left in peace.","vibe":"green, dappled, hushed, watched (never unkindly).","regulars":["Florian","Royhan","Ruby","William"],"connections":["gymnasium","menagerie","sports_field"],"walk_min":17,"clubs":[],"access":"Open to students; unlit after dark, and curfew applies","lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":38,"discoverable":false,"near":[["gymnasium",3],["menagerie",5],["sports_field",5],["swimming_pool",3]],"seasons":{"Spring":"Lesser spirits are thickest when the new leaves come; the path is busy with first-years.","Autumn":"Fallen leaves stir on windless days. It is only the spirits.","Winter":"Snow shows small tracks that stop in the middle of the path."}},"nightwell":{"name":"Nightwell","category":"Mall shop","kind":"shop","description":"A small Mall coffee house with one famous order, the Vigil.\nPrice: 60 points.\nKnown for: two days without sleep, paid for afterwards; the Medical Centre sees the results a day and a half later. Exam-week staple.","vibe":null,"regulars":[],"connections":["mall"],"walk_min":6,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":22,"discoverable":false,"near":[["mall",1]]},"merryhews":{"name":"Merryhew's","category":"Mall shop","kind":"shop","description":"The Mall's joke shop: itching charms, voice-changing sweets, illusion vermin, screaming boxes, fake exam results convincing enough to be banned twice.\nRules: tolerated because everything wears off; keeps a secret list of students barred from buying.","vibe":null,"regulars":[],"connections":["mall"],"walk_min":6,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":22,"discoverable":false,"near":[["mall",1]]},"snug":{"name":"The Snug","category":"Mall shop","kind":"shop","description":"A Mall eating house where every table is a partitioned private booth.\nKnown for: ordinary food, real privacy. Point loans, betting settlements, club trades, apologies and quiet negotiations; staff hear nothing. Booths by the hour, always a wait.","vibe":null,"regulars":[],"connections":["mall"],"walk_min":6,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":22,"discoverable":false,"near":[["mall",1]]},"quillfeathers":{"name":"Quillfeather's","category":"Mall shop","kind":"shop","description":"a narrow bookseller with a ladder on rails; new books at the front, second-hand at the back.","vibe":null,"regulars":[],"connections":["mall"],"walk_min":6,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":22,"discoverable":false,"near":[["mall",1]]},"pennywhistle_curios":{"name":"Pennywhistle Curios","category":"Mall shop","kind":"shop","description":"gifts, games and trinkets; the window changes with every festival.","vibe":null,"regulars":[],"connections":["mall"],"walk_min":6,"clubs":[],"access":null,"lore":[],"floor":null,"pin":22,"discoverable":false,"near":[["mall",1]]},"barrow_vine":{"name":"Barrow & Vine","category":"Mall shop","kind":"shop","description":"wine, ale, spirits and tobacco. Asks for the bracelet, and reminds students they may drink only on the rest day and in the holidays.","vibe":null,"regulars":[],"conne