"Nerys":1,"Ottavio":1,"Percival":0,"Rei":1,"Rigel":0,"Royhan":1,"Ruby":0,"Saffi":0,"Sophia":1,"Tilly":0,"Topaz":0,"Tristan":1,"Trixie":0,"Tsubaki":0,"Valentin":1,"Vallie":0,"Vera":0,"Vesna":0,"William":1,"Wren":1,"Yvette":1,"Zara":1}},"areas":{"forest":{"area":"Grand Vast Forest","map":"map/grand_vast_forest.webp","unit":"h","arrive":"base_camp","start":"base_camp","reveal":"near","paths":true,"offGo":"Only during the Expedition","offText":"You are not in the forest now. The map shows what you found on your Expedition.","legs":[["base_camp","wildwood_west",2],["base_camp","wildwood_north",2],["base_camp","wildwood_east",2],["wildwood_west","wildwood_north",2.5],["wildwood_north","wildwood_east",2.5],["wildwood_west","blightbriar",3],["wildwood_north","gloaming",3.5],["wildwood_east","falls",4],["blightbriar","gloaming",2.5],["blightbriar","cave",5],["gloaming","falls",3.5],["gloaming","cave",4],["gloaming","old_heart",5],["falls","terraces",1.5],["terraces","old_heart",4],["cave","old_heart",5]],"modes":{},"pins":[{"id":"base_camp","name":"Base Camp","x":50,"y":80},{"id":"wildwood_north","name":"Wildwood (north)","x":50,"y":57},{"id":"wildwood_west","name":"Wildwood (west)","x":28,"y":76},{"id":"wildwood_east","name":"Wildwood (east)","x":70,"y":75},{"id":"blightbriar","name":"Blightbriar","x":18,"y":48},{"id":"gloaming","name":"The Gloaming","x":48,"y":43},{"id":"falls","name":"Silverstair Falls","x":83,"y":45},{"id":"terraces","name":"Jade Terraces","x":83,"y":23},{"id":"cave","name":"Grand Cave Network","x":15,"y":22},{"id":"old_heart","name":"The Old Heart","x":50,"y":9}],"places":[{"id":"base_camp","name":"Base Camp","pin":"base_camp","vibe":"Woodsmoke, wet canvas, nervous laughter, the ships creaking overhead","desc":"A wide meadow at the forest's southern edge where the three academy airships ride at anchor; the Expedition's start and end. Tents in three rings, one per year level, around a central fire and Vallie's command tent with the bracelet reading board; a marking table where catches are logged and caged; watch posts at the corners. On its edge stands the Huntsmen's Lodge, a timber lodge the hunting companies share: smokehouse, weighing hook, and a counter selling rope, bait, salves, lamp oil and cloth spore masks for coin. Company hunters pass through and size up the students. Every way out of camp leads into the Wildwood: west, north or east.","go":"Base Camp"},{"id":"wildwood_north","name":"Wildwood (north)","pin":"wildwood_north","vibe":"Birdsong that stops when something bigger moves","desc":"The ordinary rainforest that fills everything between the named places: broadleaf giants on buttress roots, palms and tree ferns underneath, vines hanging to the ground, deer paths, deadfall, muddy hollows churned by boar, the odd clearing where a storm took the trees down. It is ordinary only by this forest's standards. Three stretches of it are named on the map, west, north and east of Base Camp; they are the same forest, only in different directions. Vallie tells every group about ironback boars before they leave camp.","go":"Wildwood (north)"},{"id":"wildwood_west","name":"Wildwood (west)","pin":"wildwood_west","vibe":"Birdsong that stops when something bigger moves","desc":"The ordinary rainforest that fills everything between the named places: broadleaf giants on buttress roots, palms and tree ferns underneath, vines hanging to the ground, deer paths, deadfall, muddy hollows churned by boar, the odd clearing where a storm took the trees down. It is ordinary only by this forest's standards. Three stretches of it are named on the map, west, north and east of Base Camp; they are the same forest, only in different directions. Vallie tells every group about ironback boars before they leave camp.","go":"Wildwood (west)"},{"id":"wildwood_east","name":"Wildwood (east)","pin":"wildwood_east","vibe":"Birdsong that stops when something bigger moves","desc":"The ordinary rainforest that fills everything between the named places: broadleaf giants on buttress roots, palms and tree ferns underneath, vines hanging to the ground, deer paths, deadfall, muddy hollows churned by boar, the odd clearing where a storm took the trees down. It is ordinary only by this forest's standards. Three stretches of it are named on the map, west, north and east of Base Camp; they are the same forest, only in different directions. Vallie tells every group about ironback boars before they leave camp.","go":"Wildwood (east)"},{"id":"blightbriar","name":"Blightbriar","pin":"blightbriar","vibe":"Sweet rot, itching skin, everything faintly moving","desc":"A stretch of the forest gone wrong: thorn thickets with poisoned barbs, fungus in shelves and bulbs and towers, and puffs of spore that hang in the air and burn the throat. Walking it without a face cloth leaves anyone coughing and drained. The danger here is mostly the plants.","go":"Blightbriar"},{"id":"gloaming","name":"The Gloaming","pin":"gloaming","vibe":"Green dark, damp, the sense that nobody has stood here in years","desc":"The oldest, thickest stand of the rainforest: trunks wider than towers, moss and hanging vines over everything, a canopy so dense that noon looks like dusk and pale fungi give the only light. Few people come here, and it feels it: no trails, no cut wood, no sound of anyone. Hunting companies do not take work in the Gloaming.","go":"the Gloaming"},{"id":"falls","name":"Silverstair Falls","pin":"falls","vibe":"Roar of water, soaked to the skin, rainbows","desc":"The Silverrun river drops over a wide cliff in a dozen broad tiers, each with its own plunge pool; spray hangs over the whole stair, rainbows by day and mist by morning. Climbing the stair to the Jade Terraces takes an hour and a half and wet hands.","go":"Silverstair Falls"},{"id":"terraces","name":"Jade Terraces","pin":"terraces","vibe":"Colour, stillness, steam on cold mornings","desc":"Above the falls, a valley of stepped pools rimmed in pale gold stone, hundreds of them, each a different blue or green. The springs that feed the pools run cold, the one cool place in the forest. Animal-shaped stones stand in some of the pools; they are not carvings.","go":"Jade Terraces"},{"id":"cave","name":"Grand Cave Network","pin":"cave","vibe":"Cold breath from below, dripping, an echo that answers late","desc":"A mouth in a cliff wall at the forest's north-west, wide enough to fly an airship into, opening onto caves said to run as far as the forest itself; nobody has mapped the end. Groups often pitch their tents just inside the mouth, dry and out of the wind. Staff chalk a line across the first chamber: no group goes past it. Warm air rises from somewhere below.","go":"Grand Cave Network"},{"id":"old_heart","name":"The Old Heart","pin":"old_heart","vibe":"Silver light, absolute quiet, the sense of being allowed in","desc":"A single giant tree at the northern edge of the Expedition country, its trunk wider than the Main Courtyard, rising far above the canopy and seen from anywhere in the southern forest. Past it the deep forest begins, unmapped and weeks across. The protected beasts live around it; harming one is a crime the Doves investigate. No student goes, and no hunting company takes work there. Rumour says poachers do.","go":"the Old Heart"}]},"avalon":{"area":"Avalon","map":"map/avalon.webp","unit":"min","arrive":"skyport","start":"square","offGo":"Only while in Avalon","offText":"You are not in Avalon now. The map shows the city as you saw it.","legs":[["square","gate",25],["square","lantern",35],["square","arena",40],["square","oldtown",75],["square","garden",75],["square","castle",45],["gate","lantern",40],["lantern","oldtown",50],["oldtown","garden",50],["garden","arena",45],["arena","gate",35],["gate","meadow",30],["arena","undercroft",5]],"modes":{"carriage":{"fare":10,"name":"hire carriage"}},"pins":[{"id":"castle","name":"Eldrasil Castle","x":50,"y":31,"locked":true},{"id":"square","name":"Crown Square","x":50,"y":57},{"id":"gate","name":"Great Gate","x":50,"y":83},{"id":"lantern","name":"Lantern Quarter","x":24,"y":56},{"id":"oldtown","name":"Old Town","x":32,"y":23},{"id":"garden","name":"Garden of Avalon","x":67,"y":27},{"id":"arena","name":"Arena Quarter","x":78,"y":56},{"id":"meadow","name":"Kingsmeadow","x":50,"y":96,"kc":1},{"id":"undercroft","name":"The Undercroft","x":88,"y":64,"kc":2}],"places":[{"id":"eldrasil_castle","name":"Eldrasil Castle","pin":"castle","in":10,"locked":true,"desc":"The royal seat at the top of the hill, white towers higher than anything in the city but the Great Spire, deep blue and gold banners on every tower. The King lives and rules here. The royal road climbs to it from Crown Square through the Noble Ring.","go":"Eldrasil Castle"},{"id":"noble_ring","name":"Noble Ring","pin":"castle","in":5,"locked":true,"desc":"The townhouses of the noble families on the terraces around the castle: gardens behind white walls, quiet streets, private guards at the gates. The Noble Houses' Liaison keeps its offices here.","go":"the Noble Ring"},{"id":"crown_square","name":"Crown Square","pin":"square","in":0,"desc":"The great square at the foot of the castle hill, where Crown Avenue ends and every avenue of the city meets the Crown Ring. The parade finishes here on Crowning Day, the Royal Mages at its head, and the King speaks from the dais on the White Line; the Herald Spires carry the speech to the whole city. Fountains, a column to the War of Independence, food stalls on holidays.","vibe":"The heart of the kingdom, in white stone and blue banners.","go":"Crown Square"},{"id":"grand_cathedral","name":"Grand Cathedral","pin":"square","in":5,"desc":"The house of Asmoday for the whole kingdom, white and immense, its nave open to anyone. Every cathedral in Eldrasil, Halvard's included, answers to it. Sermons on the hour on holy days; the registry of oaths sworn in the capital is kept in its undercroft.","go":"the Grand Cathedral"},{"id":"chancery","name":"The Chancery","pin":"square","in":5,"desc":"The crown's offices in one long white building around a courtyard: ministries, courts, the Royal Inspectorate's headquarters, the royal archive. Open to the public in its front halls for petitions; nobody goes in for fun.","go":"the Chancery"},{"id":"high_dovecote","name":"High Dovecote","pin":"square","in":5,"desc":"The headquarters of the Doves, a white tower with a walled courtyard of grey uniforms. The public may stand at its gate; nobody walks in. Mages in academy uniform are noticed here.","go":"the High Dovecote"},{"id":"royal_bank","name":"Royal Bank","pin":"square","in":5,"desc":"The kingdom's bank behind a long white colonnade, where Halvard's Banking House sends its ledgers. Coin changed, accounts opened, loans signed. The Arslan World Bank keeps an office in the same street.","go":"the Royal Bank"},{"id":"skyport","name":"Skyport","pin":"gate","in":5,"desc":"Airship masts and a paved landing field just outside the Great Gate, the main gate in the south wall, with the customs hall and the passenger halls inside it. Every academy trip lands and musters here.","vibe":"Masts, balloon envelopes and the whole city rising in front of you.","go":"the Skyport"},{"id":"gilded_arcade","name":"Gilded Arcade","pin":"gate","in":5,"desc":"Two glass-roofed shopping arcades either side of Crown Avenue, just inside the Great Gate. Ardenne's flagship store, the original Merryhew's, Firetooth's own sweet shop, cafés, tailors and jewellers. Expensive, polished, and the first thing most visitors see.","go":"the Gilded Arcade"},{"id":"lantern_market","name":"Lantern Market","pin":"lantern","in":5,"desc":"Avalon's biggest market: covered streets and a glass market hall hung with paper lanterns that are lit at dusk. Food from every province, cheap clothes, charms, imported goods, street performers, pickpockets.","vibe":"Lanterns, awnings, shouting, frying, and your purse to watch.","go":"the Lantern Market"},{"id":"spellwright_row","name":"Spellwright Row","pin":"lantern","in":10,"desc":"The street of the magic trades. Staff and wand makers, component sellers, enchanters, rune engravers, spellbook dealers, a shop for duelling gear. Stock the academy Mall never carries, at capital prices; every shop holds a Doves licence on the wall.","go":"Spellwright Row"},{"id":"old_town","name":"Old Town","pin":"oldtown","in":5,"desc":"The one grey quarter: narrow crooked lanes of grey stone from before independence, taverns, old bookshops, fortune tellers, the cheapest food in the city. Easy to get lost in. Everyone in Avalon has heard that somewhere in Old Town a door leads down into the Rookery, the city's underbelly; nobody respectable admits to knowing which one.","vibe":"Grey stone, crooked lanes, and doors nobody talks about.","go":"Old Town"},{"id":"rookery","name":"The Rookery","pin":"oldtown","in":10,"hidden":true,"desc":"Avalon's underbelly, a warren of old cellars, cisterns and smugglers' tunnels beneath Old Town, older than the white city above it. Its people call themselves rooks, a joke at the Doves' expense. A black market (stolen goods, contraband, unlicensed components, forged papers), gambling dens, a fighting pit where unlawful duels are fought for coin, and brokers who sell information to anyone. Lantern-lit, crowded, polite in its own way: rooks do not rob guests who behave, and they never forget a face that brings the Watch. Students are forbidden to go there.","go":"the Rookery"},{"id":"skywheel_fair","name":"Skywheel Fair","pin":"oldtown","in":5,"desc":"A permanent fairground on the old parade ground at the edge of Old Town. Its giant wheel, turned by magitech, gives the second-best view in Avalon after the Great Spire and is the city's favourite place for a date; around it, games of skill with prizes, sweet stalls, a carousel and fortune booths. Busiest on holidays and at dusk, when the wheel lights up.","vibe":"Music, sugar, and the city tilting below the wheel.","go":"the Skywheel Fair"},{"id":"great_spire","name":"The Great Spire","pin":"oldtown","in":10,"desc":"The tallest of the seven Herald Spires and the oldest, a slender white tower inside the north wall with a public viewing gallery near the top (a small fee in coin; a long stair or the lift). From the gallery the whole white city lies in its rings.","go":"the Great Spire"},{"id":"garden_of_avalon","name":"Garden of Avalon","pin":"garden","in":5,"desc":"The city's great public garden: lawns, flower terraces, a long reflecting pool and shaded walks, busiest on holidays. At its centre stands the Archmage, the largest statue in Eldrasil: a figure in white stone, taller than the trees, staff raised over four seals cut into the ground around the plinth. The face under the hood is smooth and the plinth carries no name, because no record keeps either; visitors argue about it.","vibe":"Flowers, still water, and a hero with no face.","go":"the Garden of Avalon"},{"id":"grand_theatre","name":"Grand Theatre","pin":"garden","in":10,"desc":"The domed white opera house of the capital beside the garden. Opera, plays and concerts; on Crowning Day a cheap afternoon matinee for the holiday crowd.","go":"the Grand Theatre"},{"id":"royal_arena","name":"Royal Arena","pin":"arena","in":5,"desc":"The open-air stadium of the kingdom, white stone tiers round a sand floor, warded for magic duels; the Kingdom Competition is fought here. Great scrying crystals hang above the tiers and show the crowd the rounds fought away from the sand; beneath the sand lies the Undercroft. On other days: tournaments, races, shows.","vibe":"Ten thousand seats and the sand where reputations are made.","go":"the Royal Arena"},{"id":"whitestone_hotel","name":"Whitestone Hotel","pin":"arena","in":5,"desc":"The grand hotel beside the arena where the four academies' Kingdom Competition teams stay. Doormen, a lobby that never sleeps, a courtyard fountain, and a dining room where rival teams pretend not to look at each other.","go":"the Whitestone Hotel"},{"id":"judges_pavilion","name":"Judges' Pavilion","pin":"meadow","in":5,"kc":1,"desc":"A white pavilion with the royal blue and gold on its poles where the Kingsmeadow road meets the grass: the competition panel's table, the four academies' banners, a healer's tent beside it. Round one starts here at dawn, and here at sunset the judges take one Kingsbloom from each team.","go":"the Judges' Pavilion"},{"id":"long_meadow","name":"Long Meadow","pin":"meadow","in":10,"kc":1,"desc":"Waist-high grass rolling away from the pavilion in long waves, a few lone oaks, larks going up wherever someone walks. Everything moving out here can be seen from far off.","go":"the Long Meadow"},{"id":"willow_brook","name":"Willow Brook","pin":"meadow","in":10,"kc":1,"desc":"A clear stream winding under old willows, stepping stones at the shallows and a footbridge of three planks; the banks are soft and keep footprints.","go":"the Willow Brook"},{"id":"old_orchard","name":"Old Orchard","pin":"meadow","in":10,"kc":1,"desc":"Rows of old apple and pear trees from a royal estate long gone, gone half wild, windfalls in the grass and a collapsed press house at the end of the rows.","go":"the Old Orchard"},{"id":"bramble_hollow","name":"Bramble Hollow","pin":"meadow","in":15,"kc":1,"desc":"A sunken hollow choked with bramble and blackthorn, narrow tracks through it that badgers made and nobody else can walk upright; the best place in the Kingsmeadow to wait unseen.","go":"the Bramble Hollow"},{"id":"standing_stones","name":"Standing Stones","pin":"meadow","in":15,"kc":1,"desc":"A ring of eleven grey standing stones on a low rise, older than the kingdom; the panel's wards hum faintly between them, and the grass inside the ring is short and dry.","go":"the Standing Stones"},{"id":"reed_marsh","name":"Reed Marsh","pin":"meadow","in":15,"kc":1,"desc":"Reed beds taller than a person around pools of black water, duckboards laid by the panel along one line only; off them, it is wet to the knee and loud with every step.","go":"the Reed Marsh"},{"id":"beacon_hill","name":"Beacon Hill","pin":"meadow","in":15,"kc":1,"desc":"The highest ground in the Kingsmeadow, crowned by an old beacon basket on a stone post; from the top the whole field shows, and so does whoever stands on it.","go":"the Beacon Hill"},{"id":"undercroft_gates","name":"Undercroft Gates","pin":"undercroft","in":5,"kc":2,"desc":"A long vaulted hall at the foot of the stairs under the arena, warded lamps in brackets, and three iron gates into the Undercroft, one for each team still in. A board of ten sigils by the stairs lights a room's sigil in the colour of the team that holds it.","go":"the Undercroft Gates"},{"id":"undercroft_room_1","name":"Undercroft Room 1","pin":"undercroft","in":5,"kc":2,"desc":"The Pillar Hall: a low hall of squat pillars close enough to touch, lamplight broken into stripes between them.","go":"the Undercroft Room 1"},{"id":"undercroft_room_2","name":"Undercroft Room 2","pin":"undercroft","in":5,"kc":2,"desc":"The Cistern: a flooded vault with a stone walkway round its edge and still black water in the middle.","go":"the Undercroft Room 2"},{"id":"undercroft_room_3","name":"Undercroft Room 3","pin":"undercroft","in":5,"kc":2,"desc":"The old Armoury: empty weapon racks on every wall, a broken portcullis half down across the far arch.","go":"the Undercroft Room 3"},{"id":"undercroft_room_4","name":"Undercroft Room 4","pin":"undercroft","in":10,"kc":2,"desc":"The sunken Chapel: three steps down to a stone floor, a plain altar, niches in the walls where candles once stood.","go":"the Undercroft Room 4"},{"id":"undercroft_room_5","name":"Undercroft Room 5","pin":"undercroft","in":10,"kc":2,"desc":"The Gallery: a narrow balcony room above a drop into darkness, a rail on one side, the wards glowing along the edge.","go":"the Undercroft Room 5"},{"id":"undercroft_room_6","name":"Undercroft Room 6","pin":"undercroft","in":10,"kc":2,"desc":"The Kennels: a row of barred stalls where the arena's beasts were kept between shows, straw still on the floor.","go":"the Undercroft Room 6"},{"id":"undercroft_room_7","name":"Undercroft Room 7","pin":"undercroft","in":10,"kc":2,"desc":"The Furnace room: a great cold furnace with an iron door, flues climbing into the dark, soot on every surface.","go":"the Undercroft Room 7"},{"id":"undercroft_room_8","name":"Undercroft Room 8","pin":"undercroft","in":15,"kc":2,"desc":"The Vault: a round room behind a door a hand thick, shelves cut into the stone, the air dry and still.","go":"the Undercroft Room 8"},{"id":"undercroft_room_9","name":"Undercroft Room 9","pin":"undercroft","in":15,"kc":2,"desc":"The Pit: a sand-floored fighting pit older than the arena above it, tiers of rough stone around it where a few hundred once watched.","go":"the Undercroft Room 9"},{"id":"undercroft_room_10","name":"Undercroft Room 10","pin":"undercroft","in":15,"kc":2,"desc":"The Deep Hall: the lowest and largest room, a vault so high the lamps do not reach its roof, and every sound comes back twice.","go":"the Undercroft Room 10"}]},"sunreach":{"area":"Sunreach Bay","maps":{"day":"map/sunreach_day.webp","night":"map/sunreach_night.webp"},"night":{"from":"18:00","to":"06:00"},"unit":"min","arrive":"skydock","start":"strand","offGo":"Only while in Sunreach Bay","offText":"You are not in Sunreach Bay now. The map shows the city as you saw it.","legs":[["skydock","wharf",10],["skydock","strand",15],["skydock","cliffs",30],["wharf","strand",15],["wharf","crossing",15],["strand","sunpier",10],["strand","crossing",10],["sunpier","casino",15],["crossing","casino",15],["crossing","terraces",15],["casino","lagoon",20],["terraces","cliffs",35],["terraces","lagoon",35],["wharf","sea",60,"tour"]],"modes":{"carriage":{"fare":6,"name":"carriage"},"boat":{"fare":8,"name":"water taxi"},"tour":{"fare":15,"from":"the Sea Dock"}},"pins":[{"id":"skydock","name":"Skydock","x":14,"y":68,"shore":true},{"id":"wharf","name":"Fisherman's Wharf","x":25,"y":50,"shore":true},{"id":"strand","name":"Coral Strand","x":44,"y":44,"shore":true},{"id":"sunpier","name":"Sunpier","x":64,"y":56,"shore":true},{"id":"crossing","name":"Sunreach Crossing","x":51,"y":31},{"id":"casino","name":"Casino Row","x":81,"y":37,"shore":true},{"id":"terraces","name":"Cliffside Terraces","x":60,"y":16},{"id":"lagoon","name":"Turquoise Lagoon","x":84,"y":77,"shore":true},{"id":"cliffs","name":"West Cliffs","x":8,"y":35,"shore":true},{"id":"sea","sea":true,"name":"Open Sea","x":45,"y":87}],"places":[{"id":"skydock","name":"Skydock","pin":"skydock","in":5,"vibe":"salt wind, gulls, ropes creaking","vibe_night":"warm wind, distant music","desc":"A broad walled stone platform on the bay's south-west headland, where airships rest in wooden cradles beside their mooring masts, with a customs shed where a single bored Yozakuran clerk stamps everything. Every arrival and departure musters here. A switchback cliff road climbs from it along the west headland to the Lighthouse.","desc_night":"The masts and the platform are lit like a row of lanterns, lamps mark the cliff road all the way up to the Lighthouse, and the city's glow fills the whole bay below.","go":"the Skydock"},{"id":"fish_market","name":"Fish Market","pin":"wharf","in":5,"vibe":"smoke, salt, shouting","vibe_night":"steam, sizzle, red light","desc":"The city's seafood heart on the wharf: a long open hall where the morning catch is sold off ice and cooked on the spot, and the streets around it given over to grills, steamers and noodle stalls. Skewered prawns, grilled octopus, crab in chilli, coconut rice in leaf parcels, shaved ice in fruit syrup. Cheap by Sunreach standards, loud, and the best food on the island.","desc_night":"Red paper lanterns and rune-lit signs over a hundred steaming stalls, low wooden stools in the street, and the cooks still shouting until three in the morning.","go":"the Fish Market"},{"id":"sea_dock","name":"Sea Dock","pin":"wharf","in":5,"vibe":"tar, nets, gulls","vibe_night":"lamps on water, wet planks","desc":"The working dock beside the Fish Market where the fishing fleet ties up and the tour boats leave for the open sea: whale and dolphin tours in the morning, deep-sea fishing at noon, a dusk cruise at sunset. Nets drying, crates of ice, crews calling the next departure.","desc_night":"The fishing boats come in under their lamps and unload straight into the market.","go":"the Sea Dock"},{"id":"the_hanabira","name":"The Hanabira","pin":"strand","in":5,"vibe":"cool wood, quiet water, polite bows","vibe_night":"lantern light, steam, distant city noise","desc":"Halvard's hotel for the Trip: a long white Yozakuran beachfront hotel of five storeys with paper lanterns on every balcony, a lobby of pale wood and koi pools, a garden of flowering trees, and a hot spring bath on the roof. Postcards at the front desk.","desc_night":"The lanterns glow on every balcony, and from the rooftop bath the whole lit city is laid out across the bay.","go":"the Hanabira"},{"id":"coral_beach","name":"Coral Beach","pin":"strand","in":5,"vibe":"hot sand, bright, waves","vibe_night":"drums, firelight, warm sand","desc":"The white beach in front of the hotels, a long curve of fine sand and gentle surf, striped umbrellas, rented loungers and beach volleyball nets. Lifeguards in red until sunset; half the people on it are some shade of sunburnt.","desc_night":"Beach clubs open under coloured rune lamps, fire dancers spin on the sand to drums, and the lit skyline doubles itself in the wet sand at the water's edge.","go":"the Coral Beach"},{"id":"sunpier","name":"Sunpier","pin":"sunpier","in":5,"vibe":"screams, sugar, sea spray","vibe_night":"lights, screams, black water","desc":"An amusement pier running far out over the bay: a carousel, games of skill with stuffed prizes, a hall of mirrors, ice cream and Sunfizz stands, caricature artists, and the Gull Run, a little wooden roller coaster that swings out over the water. Sunreach's family side at its loudest.","desc_night":"The pier is outlined in rune lamps from end to end, fortune tellers set up between the games, and the Gull Run goes out over black water.","go":"the Sunpier"},{"id":"tidehouse_aquarium","name":"Tidehouse Aquarium","pin":"sunpier","in":5,"vibe":"blue, cool, hushed","vibe_night":"violet glow, whispers","desc":"A domed glass aquarium at the pier's root: a walk-through tunnel under a tank of reef fish, rays and a slow old sea turtle everyone names. Quiet, cool and dim, the best place on the island to escape the heat.","desc_night":"Open late with the tank lit violet by rune lamps and jellyfish glowing in the dark; a favourite date.","go":"the Tidehouse Aquarium"},{"id":"sunreach_crossing","name":"Sunreach Crossing","pin":"crossing","in":5,"vibe":"crowds, bright paint, movement","vibe_night":"colour, footsteps, a sea of faces","desc":"The heart of the city, a vast crossroads where six streets meet under walls of huge painted banners (suns, waves, swirls of colour) and shopfronts: fashion boutiques, fruit-juice bars, game halls, a stand of horse carriages, and a clock tower everybody uses as a meeting point, where the Skyrail starts up the hill. By day it is busy and colourful.","desc_night":"Every banner glows under rune lamps and every shop sign burns in rune-lit glass; when the crossing keepers drop their flags, a thousand people cross at once in every direction. Street fashion, buskers, portrait sketchers, game halls open all night, and the noise never drops.","go":"the Sunreach Crossing"},{"id":"velvet_lanes","name":"Velvet Lanes","pin":"crossing","in":5,"vibe":"shuttered, narrow, stale smoke","vibe_night":"rune-glow, smoke, whispers, too close","desc":"A tangle of narrow alleys behind the Crossing, packed with tiny bars of six seats each, stacked two and three storeys high and reached by steep outside stairs; singing rooms with a hired lute player, smoky grills, fortune tellers, a night market selling anything (charms, forged papers, potions no apothecary at home would stock), and further in the pleasure houses behind silk curtains. Shuttered and sleepy by day.","desc_night":"The brightest, densest, loudest few streets in the world: every sign competes in rune-lit glass, touts call from every door, and a group can lose each other in ten steps.","go":"the Velvet Lanes"},{"id":"golden_tide","name":"The Golden Tide","pin":"casino","in":5,"vibe":"cool air, chips clicking, gold","vibe_night":"fountains, roar of the tables, gold and red","desc":"The biggest casino resort on the island, a domed tower of gold and blue glass with a great golden sea serpent coiled up its whole front, and a round lake of fountains at its feet: dice, cards and the great wheel on a floor of nobles, crime lords and tourists, and house dealers who never smile. It does not check a bracelet or ask an age. By day it is half-asleep: cleaners, gamblers who never went to bed, and cool air at the doors.","desc_night":"Every hour the house's water mages throw the lake into fountains higher than the tower in time to an orchestra on the terrace, the tables are full to the walls, and the doors swallow the whole street.","go":"the Golden Tide"},{"id":"plaza_dourada","name":"Plaza Dourada","pin":"casino","in":5,"vibe":"pastel, mosaic, sweet pastry","vibe_night":"gold light, old stone, the casinos' glow","desc":"An old colonial square beside the casinos, from the days before the island sold itself to pleasure: pastel arcaded buildings, a wave-patterned black-and-white mosaic pavement, a fountain, and pastry shops selling custard tarts and almond cookies. Quiet and charming by day.","desc_night":"The square is ringed by the casino towers' light and filled with tourists drifting in from the tables; the pastry shops stay open and the fountain is lit gold.","go":"the Plaza Dourada"},{"id":"the_terraces","name":"The Terraces","pin":"terraces","in":5,"vibe":"stairs, spice, laundry lines, shade","vibe_night":"chilli steam, gold light, a long way down","desc":"The island's own town, built up the steep hillside behind the city in layers: streets stacked on streets, stairways, alley markets and houses on tall timber stilts clinging to the cliff, so that the ground floor of one street is the roof of the next; old stone aqueducts arch across the ravines between the hills. Spice stalls, woven hats, shell jewellery, fruit nobody can name, aloe salve, and cafés where the locals play dominoes. Cheaper and friendlier than anywhere on the beach.","desc_night":"The whole hillside lights up layer by layer, the stilt houses glowing gold over the city like a stacked lantern; hot-pot restaurants spill onto every landing.","go":"the Terraces"},{"id":"skyrail","name":"Skyrail","pin":"terraces","in":5,"vibe":"rattling, windy, a view","vibe_night":"vertigo, light everywhere below","desc":"Little red cable cars drawn by rune-engines on a long cable from the clock tower at the Crossing up over the stilt houses to the summit by the Old Fort, passing through a station built right into a house halfway up. Everyone takes the same sketch of it.","desc_night":"The cabins glow as they swing up over the lit terraces, and the whole city opens out below.","go":"the Skyrail"},{"id":"old_fort","name":"Old Fort","pin":"terraces","in":5,"vibe":"wind, quiet, old stone","vibe_night":"dark, stars, the city humming below","desc":"A ruined sea fort at the top of the hill: crumbling walls, rusted cannons and goats; the best view of the whole bay, and on a clear day of the open sea.","desc_night":"Dark and quiet above the glowing city; the one place in Sunreach where the stars show.","go":"the Old Fort"},{"id":"the_lagoon","name":"The Lagoon","pin":"lagoon","in":5,"vibe":"turquoise, warm water, laughter","vibe_night":"small lights, black water, slow music","desc":"A shallow lagoon of startling turquoise behind the reef on the eastern headland, warm as a bath, with floating rafts, rented paddle boats, and a beach bar on stilts over the water with thatched huts on its jetties, serving coconut drinks.","desc_night":"The rafts are strung with rune lamps and the beach bar plays slow music; the water is black and still.","go":"the Lagoon"},{"id":"reef_gardens","name":"Reef Gardens","pin":"lagoon","in":5,"vibe":"colour, salt, sunlight through water","vibe_night":"dark, faint glow","desc":"The coral reef at the lagoon's mouth: glass-bottom boats on the hour, snorkels for hire, and pearl divers who show off for coins. The colours are like nothing in Eldrasil.","desc_night":"The boats stop; the reef's edge glows faintly where the plankton stirs.","go":"the Reef Gardens"},{"id":"shell_cove","name":"Shell Cove","pin":"lagoon","in":5,"vibe":"secret, pink sand, quiet","vibe_night":"moonlight, waves, alone together","desc":"A small hidden cove at the tip of the eastern headland, beyond the rocks at the lagoon's far end and reached by a path through the palms: pink shell sand, a single crooked palm leaning over the water, and nobody else.","desc_night":"Moonlight on the shells and the city's glow on the far side of the bay.","go":"the Shell Cove"},{"id":"the_lighthouse","name":"The Lighthouse","pin":"cliffs","in":5,"vibe":"wind, white paint, endless sea","vibe_night":"the beam, the dark sea","desc":"A tall white lighthouse at the top of the west headland, reached by the switchback cliff road from the Skydock; open to climb by day for a coin. The keeper is a retired Norvaine sailor who tells storm stories to anyone who listens.","desc_night":"The beam sweeps the sea and the lit city both; the keeper lets nobody up after dark.","go":"the Lighthouse"},{"id":"sunset_cliffs","name":"Sunset Cliffs","pin":"cliffs","in":5,"vibe":"gold light, height, held breath","vibe_night":"wind, dark, surf below","desc":"The cliffs below the lighthouse where the whole island comes to watch the sun go down into the sea. Locals and the brave dive from the lower ledges into deep clear water; the Trip's most famous confessions happen here at dusk.","desc_night":"The crowd goes back to the city; the cliffs are dark and windy.","go":"the Sunset Cliffs"},{"id":"glowtide_grotto","name":"Glowtide Grotto","pin":"cliffs","in":5,"vibe":"blue-green glow, echo, cool stone, glittering water","vibe_night":"glow, stillness, the sea breathing outside","desc":"A sea cave in the cliff foot. A boatman rows visitors in through a low arch at the water line and along a winding tunnel where the water glows blue wherever an oar touches it, until the tunnel opens into a great cavern. There the boat ties up on a broad shore of smooth rock that can be walked on all the way round. In the middle lies a still round pool whose water glitters like scattered stars, and high above, the whole ceiling is covered in glowing plants, hanging moss and vines that shed a soft blue-green light over everything. Voices echo; nobody talks loudly for long. Boatmen charge a few coins and wait as long as you like.","desc_night":"Outside it is dark, inside it is exactly the same, only quieter; the boatmen charge double after dark.","go":"the Glowtide Grotto"},{"id":"open_sea","name":"Open Sea","pin":"sea","in":5,"vibe":"blue on blue, sun, deep swell","vibe_night":"dark swell, a glowing horizon","desc":"The deep water beyond the bay, an hour out by tour boat from the Sea Dock: morning tours to watch whales and dolphins, deep-sea fishing with the crew's rods, and a slow dusk cruise. The island shrinks to a line, then to nothing. Sailors here say the Leviathan has always lived somewhere under these waters and that, once in a lifetime, it lets itself be seen.","desc_night":"Only the dusk cruise is out; the city glows on the horizon like a jewel.","go":"the open sea"}]},"hanakaze":{"area":"Hanakaze","map":"map/yozakura.webp","unit":"min","arrive":"hanakaze_skyport","start":"park","offGo":"Only while in Hanakaze","offText":"You are not in Hanakaze now. The map shows the city as you saw it.","legs":[["skyport","avenue",15],["skyport","ring",20],["avenue","park",10],["avenue","oldquarter",20],["park","temple",10],["park","palace",15],["park","ring",15],["park","oldquarter",20],["temple","palace",10],["temple","shrine",15],["temple","ring",15],["ring","shrine",20],["oldquarter","springs",20],["ring","bamboo",40,"tour"],["ring","shiroyama",25,"tour"]],"modes":{"team":{"name":"team carriage","from":"the Thousand Lantern Inn"}},"pins":[{"id":"skyport","name":"Hanakaze Skyport","x":69,"y":83},{"id":"avenue","name":"Victors' Avenue","x":50,"y":71},{"id":"park","name":"Sakura Park","x":50,"y":52},{"id":"temple","name":"Thunder Gate","x":60,"y":35},{"id":"palace","name":"Castle Hill","x":50,"y":17},{"id":"shrine","name":"Shrine Hill","x":73,"y":19},{"id":"ring","name":"The Crowning Ring","x":76,"y":52},{"id":"oldquarter","name":"Old Quarter","x":20,"y":60},{"id":"springs","name":"Hell Valley","x":6,"y":44},{"id":"bamboo","name":"The Bamboo Sea","x":17,"y":14,"kc":1},{"id":"shiroyama","name":"Old Castle Shiroyama","x":91,"y":26,"kc":2}],"places":[{"id":"hanakaze_skyport","name":"Hanakaze Skyport","pin":"skyport","in":5,"desc":"The hub of Yozakura's airship lines: red mooring towers in a row along the bay, liners coming and going all day, and clerks who bow before they stamp.","vibe":"Red towers, white balloons, and a clerk bowing before every stamp.","go":"Hanakaze Skyport"},{"id":"red_tower_arcade","name":"Red Tower Arcade","pin":"skyport","in":5,"desc":"A covered arcade beneath the mooring towers, where Yozakura's great service companies keep their flagship counters: the hotel chain behind The Hanabira at Sunreach, the airship lines, the bathhouse houses. Boxed winter sweets, folding umbrellas, lucky charms for the flight home.","go":"Red Tower Arcade"},{"id":"challenge_crossing","name":"The Challenge Crossing","pin":"avenue","in":0,"desc":"The great five-way crossing on Victors' Avenue, the main street from the castle hill, lined with snow-laden sakura and a stone lantern for every Alpha. When the bell rings, the crowd crosses in every direction at once; on the clerks' platform in the middle, anyone may challenge anyone to a fair contest, from duels to eating matches, and a Tournament Office clerk records the result. A Yozakuran never refuses.","vibe":"A bell, a thousand people moving at once, and someone always shouting a challenge.","go":"the Challenge Crossing"},{"id":"eternal_sakura","name":"The Eternal Sakura","pin":"park","in":0,"desc":"A giant sakura at the heart of the city, wider than a house and older than the throne, in full bloom all year round. In winter its pink petals fall onto the snow beneath it, and the whole city comes to stand under it at least once. Nobody knows why it never stops flowering; Yozakurans say it will bloom as long as Yozakura has an Alpha.","vibe":"Pink petals falling on white snow, and the whole crowd gone quiet.","go":"the Eternal Sakura"},{"id":"snow_festival_park","name":"Snow Festival Park","pin":"park","in":5,"desc":"The long park around the Eternal Sakura, given over this week to the snow festival: towering snow sculptures of past Alphas and champions, ice slides for children and students alike, and a sculpture of every competing team's ace, unveiled at the opening banquet.","go":"Snow Festival Park"},{"id":"golden_pavilion","name":"The Golden Pavilion","pin":"park","in":10,"desc":"A gilded pavilion on a still pond at the park's far end, its golden roof white with snow and doubled in the water: the most painted view in Yozakura.","go":"the Golden Pavilion"},{"id":"thunder_gate_temple","name":"Thunder Gate Temple","pin":"temple","in":0,"desc":"The city's oldest temple behind a great red gate hung with one enormous paper lantern, guarded by carved thunder and wind gods. Fortune slips tied to every branch, a five-storey pagoda in the courtyard, and the narrow approach street before it selling grilled rice crackers, sweet bean cakes and fox masks.","vibe":"Incense, grilled rice crackers, and fortune slips fluttering on every branch.","go":"Thunder Gate Temple"},{"id":"hall_of_victors","name":"The Hall of Victors","pin":"palace","in":5,"desc":"The Alpha's great hall on the castle hill, where the opening and closing banquets are held. The name of every Alpha is carved into its pillars, the newest still bright; the government's offices and the Tournament Office fill the wooden wings below it.","vibe":"Every Alpha's name carved in the pillars, the newest still bright.","go":"the Hall of Victors"},{"id":"alphas_residence","name":"The Alpha's Residence","pin":"palace","in":10,"locked":true,"desc":"Behind the Hall, closed to every guest. Whoever holds the throne lives here until someone takes it from them.","go":"the Alpha's Residence"},{"id":"fox_gates","name":"The Fox Gates","pin":"shrine","in":5,"desc":"A mountain path through thousands of red gates, one after another, climbing through the snow; stone foxes guard every turn, and Yozakurans leave offerings for luck before a fight.","vibe":"A red tunnel through the snow, and a stone fox at every turn.","go":"the Fox Gates"},{"id":"cliff_temple","name":"The Cliff Temple","pin":"shrine","in":10,"desc":"A wooden temple built out over a ravine on great timber stilts, its veranda the city's best view: the bay, the rooftops white with snow, the pink crown of the Eternal Sakura, and Mount Hakuho on the horizon.","go":"the Cliff Temple"},{"id":"crowning_ring","name":"The Crowning Ring","pin":"ring","in":5,"desc":"The arena where the Alpha is crowned by tournament: a stone ring under open sky, tiered galleries for thirty thousand, and great starglass scrying crystals that carry the final to every capital.","vibe":"Thirty thousand seats around a ring of bare stone.","go":"the Crowning Ring"},{"id":"thousand_lantern_inn","name":"The Thousand Lantern Inn","pin":"ring","in":5,"desc":"A vast wooden inn beside the Ring, of the same company that runs The Hanabira, where every team lodges, one wing each. Paper screens, polished corridors, staff who remember every guest's name, hot springs in a walled garden under snow-laden sakura, and a dining hall where six nations eat breakfast within earshot of each other.","vibe":"Paper screens, polished corridors, and six nations at breakfast within earshot.","go":"the Thousand Lantern Inn"},{"id":"hundred_alleys","name":"The Hundred Alleys","pin":"oldquarter","in":0,"desc":"A knot of lanes so narrow two people cannot pass, packed with a hundred tiny stalls that seat six at most: noodle broth simmered since dawn, skewers over charcoal, sake by the cup, smoke and laughter spilling into the snow. Every stall owner knows every regular.","vibe":"Broth simmered since dawn, charcoal smoke, and laughter spilling into the snow.","go":"the Hundred Alleys"},{"id":"glass_canal","name":"The Glass Canal","pin":"oldquarter","in":5,"desc":"An old canal lined with stone warehouses turned into glass-blowing workshops and music-box shops, where visitors can blow their own glass; at night in winter, hundreds of candles in snow lanterns light the path along the water.","go":"the Glass Canal"},{"id":"forge_street","name":"Forge Street","pin":"oldquarter","in":5,"desc":"The katana smiths' street: the ring of hammers from dawn, blades cooling in snow-fed troughs, and swords far more visitors admire than can afford. The smiths test a buyer's hand before they sell, and register every blade they make.","go":"Forge Street"},{"id":"mask_theatre","name":"The Mask Theatre","pin":"oldquarter","in":10,"desc":"Yozakura's great stage: painted faces, roaring actors, revolving sets and a crowd that shouts the famous lines along with the cast.","go":"the Mask Theatre"},{"id":"the_warrens","name":"The Warrens","pin":"oldquarter","in":10,"hidden":true,"desc":"Hanakaze's underbelly, a warren of old flood tunnels, sake cellars and smugglers' passages beneath the Hundred Alleys, older than the castle on the hill. Its people call themselves ronin, the masterless, a joke at the Alpha's expense. A black market (stolen goods, unregistered blades from smiths who will not sign them, forged Tournament Office records, contraband components), gambling dens that take bets on every challenge in the city, the Cellar Ring where fights are held that are anything but fair (no rules, no clerks, bets in cash), and brokers who sell information to anyone. Lantern-lit, crowded and polite in its own way: ronin do not rob guests who bow properly, and they never forget a face that brings the Alpha's Watch. Students are forbidden to go there.","go":"the Warrens"},{"id":"hell_valley_springs","name":"Hell Valley Springs","pin":"springs","in":5,"desc":"A steaming volcanic valley on the city's edge, sulphur vents hissing between the rocks and carved demon statues on the path, with bathhouses below fed by its waters. Yozakurans settle arguments here, in silence, by who leaves the hottest pool last.","vibe":"Sulphur steam, hissing vents, and grim old men in the hottest pool.","go":"Hell Valley Springs"},{"id":"bamboo_sea","name":"The Bamboo Sea","pin":"bamboo","in":0,"kc":1,"desc":"A vast bamboo forest beyond the city, its stalks bowed under snow, ringed for the competition by a barrier that closes in all day.","go":"the Bamboo Sea"},{"id":"old_castle_shiroyama","name":"Old Castle Shiroyama","pin":"shiroyama","in":0,"kc":2,"desc":"A ruined white hill castle from the age of warring lords, stone walls and gates still standing; its two ward stones are the Siege's targets.","go":"Old Castle Shiroyama"}]},"airship":{"area":"Airship","kind":"cards","legs":[],"pins":[],"modes":{},"places":[{"id":"promenade_deck","name":"Promenade Deck","vibe":"The glassed gallery around the bow: the view, benches, teachers strolling.","desc":"The glassed gallery that wraps the airship's bow and runs down both sides: brass rails, padded benches under the windows, and nothing between the passengers and the sky but the glass. The bow end is the best view on the ship and the first place every student runs to at boarding; by the second hour it is the quietest. The glass is cold to the touch at height and the deck hums faintly underfoot. Yozakuran stewards walk it with tea on the long flights. The teachers stroll here too, which makes it the safest place on board to be seen talking to someone and the worst place to say anything private. Past the bow, a door marked in Yozakuran and Common leads to the bridge: crew only.","go":"the Promenade Deck"},{"id":"common_room","name":"Common Room","vibe":"Low tables and cushions, the canteen counter, a small bar and a stage.","desc":"The ship's heart, midships: a long low room of lacquered wood with low tables and floor cushions in the Yozakuran style. At one end, a canteen counter where the stewards serve set meals included in the fare and tea that never runs out; beside it a small bar of polished dark wood, drinks and sweets for coin. The bar keeps the academy's rule: students drink only on the rest day and in the holidays, and the stewards check the bracelet first. In the far corner, a small raised stage with a lamp rail: usually a crew musician plays, but anyone can chalk their name on the board beside it and take a turn (a song, a trick, a little spellwork, a duel of rhymes), and the teachers borrow it for announcements. A shelf of worn board games and card decks. Every year level and dorm ends up here; it is where rivalries carry on in lowered voices and seating plans fall apart by the second hour. The crew counts passengers here at boarding. A hatch behind the counter leads down to the galley: crew only.","go":"the Common Room"},{"id":"cabin_deck","name":"Cabin Deck","vibe":"One cabin to each group of four; the washrooms and hot bathing stalls at the end.","desc":"A narrow corridor of numbered doors, one cabin to each group of four: two bunks stacked on each side, a round porthole, four lockers and a fold-down table. Thin walls; everyone hears the cabin next door laugh. At the far end are the washrooms and the bathing stalls, hot water piped from the engines, a Yozakuran touch every student remembers. On long flights it is where people sleep, sulk, study or hide. At the aft end a steep ladder goes down to the Cargo Hold. The forward end, past a curtain, holds the teachers' cabins: knock or don't go. Nothing aboard records or sends anything.","go":"the Cabin Deck"},{"id":"cargo_hold","name":"Cargo Hold","vibe":"Crates, luggage and gear below; cold, loud, and the most private place aboard.","desc":"The bottom of the ship, down a steep ladder from the aft end of the Cabin Deck: a long dim hold of crates in cargo nets, racks of luggage and gear strapped to the ribs of the hull. Cold, and the loudest place aboard: the engines' hum comes up through the floor. Passengers may come down for their luggage. A Yozakuran quartermaster keeps the hold and grumbles at everyone who does, but sends no one away. The teachers rarely come down, which makes it the most private place on the ship and the reason couples, plotters and the seasick end up here. What it carries changes with the route: tents, cookfires and camp gear on the way to the forest, the same gear and muddier on the way home; the academy's banners and spare uniforms on the way to Avalon; on the way back from Sunreach, more luggage than left Halvard, and the crates of what the teachers confiscated. A door at the bow end of the hold leads to the engine room: crew only.","go":"the Cargo Hold"}]}},"wind":{"groups":{"fed":[1,0.75],"scattered":[1.5,2],"unaffected":[1,1],"fights":[1.25,1.5]},"subtypes":{"Wind":"fed","Storm":"fed","Mist":"scattered","Smoke":"scattered","Ash":"scattered","Sand":"scattered","Steam":"scattered","Sound":"scattered","Reinforcement":"unaffected","Mending":"unaffected","Phasing":"unaffected","Resizing":"unaffected"},"default":"fights"},"rom1":{"Etnie":{"field":"Loves","note":"Loves you above everything, and is wholly convinced she is your big sister."},"Kanae":{"secret":"plan|love|goal|feeling|obsess|reading|true","note":"Loves you, and has planned for a long time to keep you for herself."}},"mastery":{"arcana_co