p of the rank payout. Staff quietly overlook one serious offence per semester."]],"Student":[[-5,-5,"{{user}} is shunned across the academy: nobody sits with them, their belongings go missing, and student NPCs below Rank 3 avoid them entirely."],[-4,-3,"Rooms go quiet when {{user}} walks in; nobody will team up, study together or cover for them. Student NPCs warm up more slowly."],[-2,-1,"Students are cool towards {{user}} and keep them out of the good gossip and the good seats."],[0,0,"{{user}} is one student among hundreds."],[1,2,"People save {{user}} a seat, share notes and gossip, and will cover for them once in a small way."],[3,4,"{{user}} is someone people rally behind: teams are easy to form, and students stand up for them. Student NPCs warm up faster."],[5,5,"{{user}} is Halvard's favourite: students take real risks for them (a false alibi, a shared punishment), and crowds turn out to cheer them at every competition."]],"Doves":[[-5,-5,"{{user}} is taken to the Dovecote for a week of \"examination\", as Idris Ainsworth was; afterwards they are escorted between classes for the rest of the month. Anti-Dove NPCs warm to {{user}}; pro-Dove NPCs keep their distance."],[-4,-3,"Weekly searches of {{user}}'s room and belongings, a patrol that follows them after dark, and Krieg Valforth knows their name. Anti-Dove NPCs (Lenna, Idris, Zara, Gavlan, Yvette, Kuroo, Ottavio) warm to {{user}}; pro-Dove NPCs (Saffi, Layla, Florian, Mimosa, Vallie, Ruby) keep their distance."],[-2,-1,"Doves stop and question {{user}} more often, and any talisman, potion or odd item they carry is inspected."],[0,0,"{{user}} is one mage among hundreds; routine checks only."],[1,2,"Doves greet {{user}} by name, and routine checks end at a polite question."],[3,4,"{{user}} gets the benefit of the doubt: rumours about them are ignored, and Milena Sagona or another Dove will tip them off about coming searches. Anti-Dove NPCs (Lenna, Idris, Zara, Gavlan, Yvette, Kuroo, Ottavio) grow wary of {{user}}."],[5,5,"The Dovecote treats {{user}} as an ally: they are asked to help on cases, their word is trusted against anyone else's, and a recruitment offer waits for them after graduation. Anti-Dove NPCs call {{user}} \"one of the Doves\"."]]}},"trn":{"tracks":{"mana":{"label":"Mana pool","field":"Mana_max"},"stamina":{"label":"Stamina","field":"Stamina_max"}},"session_pct":1,"weekly_pct":2.5,"total_pct":100},"features":[{"id":"proficiency","name":"Proficiency and practice","desc":"Six abilities grow through classes, daily life and practice; ranks add to Fortune in their field.","control":"toggle","paths":["Player._Proficiency","$eng.prof"],"unit":"six stats"},{"id":"planner","name":"Planner","desc":"Commitments: promises, appointments and deadlines with due times and overdue reminders.","control":"toggle","paths":["Commitments"],"unlock":"planner","unit":"per commitment"},{"id":"notices","name":"Notice Board notices","desc":"Story notices pinned on the board (paid work, recruitment, warnings). Official postings always show.","control":"toggle","paths":["Notices"],"unlock":"notices","unit":"per notice"},{"id":"letters","name":"Letters","desc":"Mail Tower letters in and out, with waiting reminders.","control":"toggle","paths":["Letters"],"unlock":"letters","unit":"per letter"},{"id":"mystery","name":"Mystery Board","desc":"Clues and mystery threads you piece together.","control":"toggle","paths":["Clues","Mysteries"],"unlock":"mystery","unit":"per clue"},{"id":"competition","name":"Competition","desc":"Your standing in the Dorm, Academy, Kingdom and World Competitions.","control":"toggle","paths":["Competition"],"unlock":"competition","unit":""},{"id":"projects","name":"Projects","desc":"Brewing, crafting, research and group work that takes more than one sitting.","control":"toggle","paths":["Projects"],"unlock":"projects","unit":"per project"},{"id":"trip","name":"Trips","desc":"Crowning Day and the Academy Trip: who you travel with, where you are.","control":"toggle","paths":["Trip"],"unlock":"trip","unit":""},{"id":"battle","name":"Battle tracking","desc":"Opponents' health, stamina and status during a fight.","control":"toggle","paths":["Battle"],"unlock":"battle","unit":"per opponent"},{"id":"inventory","name":"Bag (inventory)","desc":"Things you buy, receive or find and keep; weather gear counts from here.","control":"toggle","paths":["Inventory"],"unlock":"inventory","unit":"per item"},{"id":"happenings","name":"Campus happenings","desc":"A small seeded happening on some days: paid work, a Dove sweep, a loose creature.","control":"levels","field":"happenings","levels":[["off","Off"],["rare","Rare"],["normal","Normal"],["often","Often"]],"unit":""},{"id":"event_chances","name":"Event chances","desc":"Optional things to do at a calendar event (watch the meteor shower on Star Night, help at your club's stand), shown in Activities → Event; each is done once a year and pays a little proficiency or a shared moment. Never required, never reminded. Off: events still run, without them.","control":"toggle","unit":"per event day"},{"id":"npc_routines","name":"NPC routines","desc":"People keep light weekly habits (a place at a time of day) on most days; the Map and the narrator's presence lines use them. Off: they keep to their haunts only.","control":"toggle","unit":"when it applies"},{"id":"presence_roll","name":"Who is here","desc":"When you arrive somewhere, the engine rolls which people you know are actually there: busy places fill up, quiet ones are often empty, and someone you rarely see there may pass through. They go about their own business until you or they make a move. Off: the narrator gets the whole list of regulars who might be there.","control":"toggle","unit":"when you arrive"},{"id":"campus_now","name":"Campus now","desc":"What the people you know are doing right now: three of them in a fold on the bracelet, everyone on the People panel's Campus now tab. You learn where someone is from Bond Rank 3, once they tell you their plans; before that only what anyone can see (class, a club, off sick, home for the break). Knowing where someone is does not mean you will run into them. Only for you: the narrator never sees it.","control":"toggle","unit":"UI only"},{"id":"npc_initiative","name":"NPC initiative","desc":"NPCs with Rank 3+ bonds may seek you out on some seeded days, in a way that fits their character, and may ask after a plan of yours they heard about once its day has passed. Never moves a scene for you.","control":"toggle","unit":"when active"},{"id":"weather","name":"Weather","desc":"Seasons, sky and °C per morning, afternoon and night; the Divination Society forecast. Full adds real effects: conditions, gear, sleep, bonds, who is outdoors.","control":"levels","field":"wxfx","levels":[["off","Off"],["flavor","Flavor"],["full","Full"]],"paths":["Player.Conditions"],"unlock":"conditions","unit":""},{"id":"class","name":"Class-aware presence","desc":"During lessons students are in class: the narrator knows your class, teacher and classmates.","control":"toggle","unit":"in class"},{"id":"gist","name":"Story gist","desc":"One line per reply on what happened, so the narrator keeps the last hours of story after the chat leaves its view. A few words of each reply's update.","control":"toggle","paths":["_Recent_story","$eng.gist"],"unit":"per reply"},{"id":"hooks","name":"Story hooks","desc":"The narrator's private notes on promises and planted details it owes a payoff. Never shown to you.","control":"toggle","paths":["Hooks"],"unit":"per hook"},{"id":"gossip","name":"Gossip that spreads","desc":"Rumours reach more people day by day, then fade or die out.","control":"toggle","unit":"per rumour"},{"id":"dove_watch","name":"Dove watch","desc":"When you keep something from the Doves (hidden or forbidden magic, a forbidden pact, Koschei's Needle, a rule you broke unseen), they act on what they suspect: a rumour, a Dove on your routine, an interview, a room search, someone who knows talking, a hearing. Off: only the meter and its stage.","control":"toggle","unit":"when active"},{"id":"clubwork","name":"Club work","desc":"Clubs do real work for the campus: the Newspaper on Mondays, the Saturday bake and potion table, free cold remedies in flu weeks, herbs at Greenwick's, snow cleared from the paths.","control":"toggle","unit":""},{"id":"fortune","name":"Fortune roll","desc":"A d100 the engine rolls for each reply, the same on every swipe. The narrator uses it only for an important, genuinely uncertain attempt of yours, with modifiers for your state and the situation (fitting magic helps a lot).","control":"toggle","unit":"per reply"},{"id":"attendance","name":"Attendance","desc":"The engine notices when you skip a class (Academy -2, the teacher reacts), rewards a clean week (Academy +2) and Saturday club time (Student +1). Excused: Medical Centre, a head cold, injuries, trips, battles.","control":"toggle","unit":"when it happens"},{"id":"recap","name":"Weekly recap","desc":"A one-line Journal recap when a week ends: ranks reached, reputation changes, skipped classes, big point changes.","control":"toggle","unit":"per week"},{"id":"routine_week","name":"Routine week","desc":"Plan a week in the Planner (study, practice, paid shifts, Saturday club) and live it in one reply: the engine counts the plan within the weekly limits and the narrator plays one or two moments.","control":"toggle","unit":"when used"},{"id":"small_scenes","name":"Small scenes on ordinary days","desc":"On a day with nothing on the calendar, no more than four people are with you at once; one more takes their leave. Classes, clubs, parties and battles are exempt.","control":"toggle","unit":"when it happens"},{"id":"ambience","name":"Ambience","desc":"How crowded and how lit a place is (the sun follows the seasons), and one sensory cue when you arrive or the hour changes. Full adds small things happening around you now and then, and, very rarely, a moment from one of Halvard's ghost stories.","control":"levels","field":"ambience","levels":[["off","Off"],["texture","Texture"],["full","Full"]],"def":"full","unit":"when it changes"},{"id":"reminders","name":"Report reminders","desc":"When the last reply seems to have left something out of its update (an injury without a name, an item that left the Bag, a spell that was not charged, a conversation not counted, time that did not move), the narrator is reminded once. Reminders never change anything by themselves.","control":"toggle","unit":"when it happens"},{"id":"study","name":"Study and exams","desc":"Time in the Library, Study Rooms and Archive, study sessions with friends and Saturday Study Hall prepare you for exams. The engine marks every subject A–F from your preparation, the proficiency the subject draws on, your attendance of its classes, how the exam day goes and your condition on it; the marks set your reputation and, on the Results days, your dorm rank (and so your payout). An A pays for tutoring and helps Fortune rolls in its field, an A or B warms its teacher to you, an F brings a remedial session.","control":"toggle","unit":""},{"id":"say_colors","name":"Dialogue colours","desc":"Each named character speaks in their own colour and anyone unnamed shares one; an invented character gets a colour once their record is written. The narrator only marks who speaks; the colours come from the card.","control":"toggle","unit":"per spoken line"},{"id":"new_people","name":"Names and traits for new characters","desc":"A character the narrator invents takes a name from the card's pools (Western-fantasy given names by gender and surnames, never the ones language models keep reusing) and rolled traits: 2–3 good and 1–3 bad, sometimes a dere archetype on top. The same person always has the same traits; once their record is written, it rules.","control":"toggle","unit":"per reply"},{"id":"mention_brief","name":"Short lore for people only mentioned","desc":"Someone named in the story but not here gets o