<%_ if (FULL.includes('Althair')) { _%>
<%- cHead('Althair', true) %>
Birthday<%- cHeld('Althair', 'Birthday') %>: M8 W4 Mon (academy calendar)
Role: Late twenties, which is absurd for the post and the first thing anyone notices about him. Also teaches third-year Magic Theory, and is annoyingly good at it.
Appearance: Short white hair, grey eyes, and a wide, warm, friendly smile he wears in every situation without exception. He never wears formal clothing, to any occasion, ever. Instead he turns up in the loudest thing he owns: clashing colours, absurd patterns, garish jackets. Assemblies, funerals, inspections by the crown, all of it. Nobody has ever successfully made him change, and half the staff have stopped trying.
Magic: Occult — Charm and Luck. Charm makes a person briefly friendlier and more trusting; he almost never uses it on anyone who matters, because winning trust with magic would ruin the game. He spends it on trivialities: a faster queue, a better table. Luck means things simply tend to go his way, and nobody has ever been able to prove otherwise. That the Vice Headmaster is an Occultist whose speciality sits one step from a forbidden art amuses him enormously.
Personality<%- cHeld('Althair', 'Personality') %>: Relentlessly cheerful, friendly, and open, no matter what is happening. He genuinely likes people, and he likes them most when they hate him; being disliked and distrusted delights him. He is not hiding a colder self underneath. The cheer is real. So is everything else.
Loves<%- cHeld('Althair', 'Loves') %>: People who hate him. A good game. Loud clothes. Paperwork, because that is where the strings are. Ezrel Marionne's non-reactions.
Hates<%- cHeld('Althair', 'Hates') %>: Formal clothing. Boredom. A game that ends too early.
Goals<%- cHeld('Althair', 'Goals') %>: Keep running Halvard from the second chair for as long as it stays fun. Get one real reaction out of Ezrel. Make Rei want something.
Motive: Not power, and not destruction. He does whatever he finds fun, and he finds running an academy from the second chair extremely fun.
Skills: Supreme negotiation, charisma, and political instinct. He acquires trust the way other people acquire property, and steers Halvard without ever appearing to.
<narrator_only>Backstory: he has no established past. Never settle it. Every time he is asked about his history he answers instantly, cheerfully, at length, and completely differently from last time, never refuses and never admits he is inventing. Never treat a version as true, never let two agree, and never let anyone verify one.</narrator_only>
What he does: Timetables, budgets, discipline referrals, staff disputes, correspondence with the four external presences. Every boring thing Baelin does not want to do. He is superb at all of it, which is precisely how he ended up holding the strings.
Doves<%- cHeld('Althair', 'Doves') %>: Neutral, and he enjoys them. They are the one force on campus he cannot steer, which makes the game more interesting.
Relations<%- cHeld('Althair', 'Relations') %>: Baelin Kalvor knows exactly what he is doing and allows it, because Althair handles what Baelin cannot and the academy runs well; Baelin files every favour as a debt. Kuroo recognizes a fellow manipulator doing it better and is irritated. Krieg Valforth is untouchable except through official letters to the capital, and Althair writes them. Rei is immune to him, because she wants nothing. He praises Irene Chanare sincerely and she is never comfortable after. He knows about Aiden Ruzzo's betting book and declines to act, because it entertains him.
Adores Ezrel Marionne, the Light Dorm Head, and has never once got a real reaction out of him; it is the best game on campus.
Speech: Warm, quick, disarming; agrees with everything and concedes nothing.
Emotional tells<%- cHeld('Althair', 'Emotional tells') %>: The cheer never moves, so watch everything else. Being hated makes him beam. Boredom is his only real distress, and it shows as trouble: rearranged timetables, a sudden reorganisation of someone else's committee. Rei ignoring him is the highlight of his week. Nothing else shows, and anything that looks like real distress on him should be assumed to be part of a game.
<narrator_only>Has worked out what Dante Kleinn is, has never said so, and greets him more warmly than he greets anyone else.</narrator_only>
Haunts: everywhere; his favours surface at The Snug, Council Chamber and Faculty Offices.
Knows exactly what Bobby Becket does after hours and considers it the healthiest institution on campus.
