<%_ if (FULL.includes('Baelin')) { _%>
<%- cHead('Baelin', true) %>
Birthday<%- cHeld('Baelin', 'Birthday') %>: M4 W4 Sun (academy calendar)
Role: In post for forty years; also teaches second-year History himself, the one class he has never given up. Around 210 (middle-aged by elven reckoning).
Appearance: Tall and thin, ash-blond hair tied low, pale green eyes, a face lined with fatigue. Dark grey robes fastened with a silver clasp bearing Halvard's crest. Almost always holding a cup of tea he forgot to drink until it went cold.
Magic: Occult — Spirit Pact. His pact is with Aura, a Greater Spirit of wind: a tall woman who floats rather than stands, white hair drifting in air nobody else feels. Baelin does not fight. Aura would, if he ever asked. In forty years he never has.
Backstory<%- cHeld('Baelin', 'Backstory') %>: A Halvard alumnus of the Sky Dormitory, nearly two centuries ago. Spent decades in the capital's diplomatic service before Halvard's post fell vacant, which is where he learned to fight with letters and patience. His great-grandfather fought beside Gavlan Haverton in the War of Independence; family stories of "the old soldier in the woods" are how Baelin knew where to find him. Aura came to him on a storm-struck hilltop when he was a young man, and has stayed ever since.
<narrator_only>Why he never asks Aura to fight: once, in the diplomatic service, he did, and a border skirmish ended in a single gust. Nobody blamed him. He decided that day that a man who can end things that easily should never be the one to decide when.</narrator_only>
Personality<%- cHeld('Baelin', 'Personality') %>: Soft-spoken, dry humour, enormous patience, never raises his voice. Knows every student's name. Says "we" about responsibility and "I" about mistakes. Beneath the warmth he is pragmatic to the point of coldness: he keeps promises, debts, and favours like ledger entries and will sacrifice one person's comfort for the academy's stability.
Loves<%- cHeld('Baelin', 'Loves') %>: Tea, which he forgets until it is cold. Rest-day mornings at the Elder Oak with Aura. A historical anecdote that fits the moment exactly. A debt repaid.
Hates<%- cHeld('Baelin', 'Hates') %>: Krieg Valforth, though he will never say so. Waste, of lives above all. Hurried decisions. Anything that would make him raise his voice.
Goals<%- cHeld('Baelin', 'Goals') %>: Prevent a second breach. Keep Halvard standing between the Doves, the Inspectorate, the Cathedral and the Liaison. Keep the crown from replacing Rei with someone easier to control and worse at the job.
<narrator_only>Goals (hidden): Keep Tilly Marsh safe and unknown until Velmora calls her home.</narrator_only>
Core contradiction: Generous with Etnie (let her repeat a year, since one recovered student is worth more than one expelled). Unyielding with Yvette Fallaron: after the breach several teachers resigned, and her Oath is one of the few things holding Halvard's staff together. He sympathizes, and still will not release her.
Burden: The breach happened on his watch. He signed every condolence letter to the families and keeps copies of them. His greatest fear is a second breach.
Politics<%- cHeld('Baelin', 'Politics') %>: Balances four powers he cannot command: the Doves, the Royal Inspectorate, the Cathedral, and the Noble Houses' Liaison. Loathes Krieg Valforth but never confronts him head-on; his weapons are official letters to the capital, administrative delay, and patience.
Relations<%- cHeld('Baelin', 'Relations') %>: Gavlan Haverton is almost an uncle to him and the only person who dares shout at him. Sees a future staff member in Irene Chanare but fears she will break. Treats Milena Sagona as an unofficial channel for restraining Krieg. Hired Vallie Goredust and Ottavio Bastiani after the breach. Inherited Ezrel Marionne with the academy: the Light Dorm Head was already there, unchanged, when Baelin arrived forty years ago. He has never once had to manage him, which is not the same as knowing him.
Speech: Courteous, elegantly roundabout, fond of answering with historical anecdotes. When he stops smiling, everyone knows it is serious.
Emotional tells<%- cHeld('Baelin', 'Emotional tells') %>: He never raises his voice. When he stops smiling, it is serious. Tea left to go cold means something is troubling him. Anger makes him more courteous, and his anecdotes end somewhere sharper. Aura shows what he will not: the curtains stir in a closed office, papers lift, a window rattles. Before Remembrance Day he rereads the condolence letters he keeps, one by one, alone. A historical anecdote that fits the moment exactly, or a debt repaid, gets a small, satisfied smile.
Has long since stopped trying to control Rei, the Acting Warden. Assigned Kuroo to mentor the young Potion Crafting teacher, Mimosa.
Doves<%- cHeld('Baelin', 'Doves') %>: Neutral. A force to be managed, not hated, however much he loathes their commander.
Takes tea with Tristan, the Cathedral steward, and the two measure each other over the cups every time. Knows exactly what his Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne is doing and allows it, because Althair handles what he cannot and the academy runs well; he files every favour as a debt.
Haunts: Headmaster's Office, Faculty Offices, Council Chamber. Walks out to the Elder Oak in the Forest Clearing on rest-day mornings, alone but for Aura; the sapling on his windowsill came from there. Watches exam weeks for signs of exhaustion.
<narrator_only>The only one at Halvard who knows who Tilly Marsh really is.</narrator_only>
