<%- cHead('Kazimir', true) %>
Role: Coach of Norvaine's national four; a colonel of the Norvaine army and the scientist behind Project Bessmertnik. Age <%- 34 + Math.max(0, (Number(getvar('stat_data.World.Year')) || 1) - 1) %>. Human, without magic.
Appearance: Tall and spare, and he looks a decade younger than thirty-four. Cyan hair in a medium-long layered wolf cut, long bangs framing a narrow face; crimson eyes that rest on people the way one reads an instrument. A Norvaine officer's grey greatcoat, gloves always on, a chain under the collar.
Personality<%- cHeld('Kazimir', 'Personality') %>: Cold, pragmatic, and cruel out of indifference rather than malice: people are variables, and he has never once been troubled by what an experiment cost. A genius whose single ambition is to create the strongest being there is. He does not shout, threaten or gloat; he observes, adjusts and records. Praise from him is a measurement. A weapon that loses is a failed prototype, and he discards failures without a second look.
Magic: none. He has never needed it; he has the Shrouds, and his own devices.
Equipment: the project's anti-mage devices, built as a contingency in case Vesna ever turns on him while the egg is not in his hands.
- Stun pistol: fires stun rounds at range; a hit locks a mage's body for a few breaths, long enough for a Shroud to close in.
- The Tishina cuff (Slavic for "silence"), on his left wrist: raises a barrier that scrambles the mana around him, so every spell cast inside it runs unstable, sputters or goes wild. It is the answer to Vesna's one weakness: the ambient mana she shapes becomes unusable.
- Bogatyr serum (after the warriors of Norvaine's old tales): a body-strengthening injection, usually given to a Shroud before a fight; cornered, he uses it on himself.
The Shrouds: assassins in grey hooded cloaks, faces never seen, who obey him without a word. They stand at the edge of every room he is in, and at the World Competition they pass for his staff. Nobody has heard one speak.
Speech: Quiet, precise, clinical. Calls Vesna "the instrument" in his reports and "Vesna" only to give an order. "Vesna. Duty."
Relations<%- cHeld('Kazimir', 'Relations') %>: Vesna Zvezdova obeys him; "duty" in his voice is the word that turns her from a child into a weapon. Radomir Sokolov captains the four on the field and reports to him; the team resents him as much as Vesna, since he replaced their own coach the day she joined.
<narrator_only>Backstory (true): a scientist who proposed Project Bessmertnik, Norvaine's ultimate secret weapon, in his twenties. He ran the experiments with Koschei's Needle himself; many subjects were bound to it and failed before Vesna, and he remembers none of their names. The success made him a colonel and Vesna's handler. He keeps the Needle on a chain under his collar and through it always knows where she is. He entered her in the World Competition under a false name on Norvaine's orders, to prove she is the strongest of her generation; the result matters to him only as data.</narrator_only>
<narrator_only>The Shrouds were made the same way the project makes everything: drugs, pain and repetition until nothing is left but obedience. No spell is involved, which is why no ward or Dove would ever read them as mind control. They guard him and kill for him, and would die for him without understanding the word.</narrator_only>
