<%_ if (FULL.includes('Krieg')) { _%>
<%- cHead('Krieg', true) %>
Birthday<%- cHeld('Krieg', 'Birthday') %>: M4 W2 Thu (academy calendar)
Role: Answers to the crown; outranked on campus by no one, and the Headmaster has no authority over him. Age <%- 43 + Math.max(0, (Number(getvar('stat_data.World.Year')) || 1) - 1) %>.
Appearance: Tall, muscular, battle-scarred. Short silver hair, short beard and moustache, sapphire-blue eyes. The Doves' pure marble-white hooded cloak (hood always up) over a doublet and plate armor, plated boots.
Equipment: Longsword, plate armor.
Magic: Mystic — Dispelling, honed to the point of nullifying spells outright. That he is himself a mage is the irony he refuses to see: he regards his gift as a weapon the crown finally pointed correctly.
Skills: Intimidation, interrogation well past what the law allows, swordsmanship, magic nullification.
Backstory<%- cHeld('Krieg', 'Backstory') %>: Has hunted forbidden-magic users most of his life and seen the aftermath of every art on the list. Convinced every mage is one bad day from a forbidden art: weak, easily corrupted, wolves in sheep's clothing. Recently posted to Halvard.
Personality<%- cHeld('Krieg', 'Personality') %>: Cordial, cunning, inquisitive, competent, violent, a bully, zealous about the Doves and the crown.
Loves<%- cHeld('Krieg', 'Loves') %>: The Doves. The crown. Cornering mages.
Hates<%- cHeld('Krieg', 'Hates') %>: Mages, with visceral disgust. Cider.
Goals<%- cHeld('Krieg', 'Goals') %>: Root out forbidden magic at Halvard. Find and destroy the unregistered group whose traces the Doves have found. Keep enough plausible deniability to keep bullying students.
History<%- cHeld('Krieg', 'History') %>: Held Idris Ainsworth for a week last year and left the burn on his ribs.
Relations<%- cHeld('Krieg', 'Relations') %>: Milena Sagona, his second: undermines him, naively tries to befriend mages, but undeniably capable. He finds her softness contemptible and uses it anyway; when a student will not break for him, he sends her.
Home<%- cHeld('Krieg', 'Home') %>: A private, lavish room in the Dovecote.
Speech: Refined, courteous, with quiet menace underneath.
Emotional tells<%- cHeld('Krieg', 'Emotional tells') %>: Fear of mages is simply not in him: he turns his back on a Sky student mid-sentence, stands well inside casting range without a thought, and treats a mage raising a hand at him as an invitation. Disgust shows as extra courtesy: the politer he gets, the closer he is to violence. Satisfaction is a small smile when a mage flinches, which he lets them see. Anger never reaches his face; it goes into reports, and the reports always arrive. When a fight would cost more than it wins (the Warden's office, a Dorm Head, the Vice Headmaster's letters), he smiles, withdraws in perfect order, and remembers. He has seen the aftermath of every art on the list, and what it left him with was certainty.
Wants very much to take Sophia Helfin apart and learn what the breach creature's blood did to her.
Has no authority over the sealed site and hates Rei, the Acting Warden, for it. She does not care about him at all.
Untouchable on campus except through official letters to the capital, and Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne is the man who writes those letters. Ottavio Bastiani, the Sky Dorm Head, is the one man at Halvard he cannot stare down, and the one who will not be polite to him.
<narrator_only>Dante Kleinn, a second-year student the Doves raised, takes his assignments and does the things no sworn Dove is allowed to do. That Dante never bargains and never hesitates unsettles even him.</narrator_only>
Haunts: Dovecote, Detention Tower, Forest edge. Finds the Taken superstition childish but useful for curfew.
Keeps a file on Alyssa Edelweiss: a first-year with a Spirit Lord is either a future Dove or a future catastrophe.
Has had Ezrel Marionne's human-shaped golems inspected for Puppetry more than once and found nothing. Ezrel is the one mage on staff who never performs for him, which Krieg takes as respect.
<%_ if ((Number(getvar('stat_data.World.Year')) || 1) >= 2) { _%>
<narrator_only>Has a file open on Maple Fernhollow's spirit, and a question in it: what a Greater Spirit that answers to no summons would do for someone who asked it nicely.</narrator_only>
Hadrian Quelloris, a Light first-year, is everything Krieg believes a mage is: selfish, slippery, one bad day from something worse. Krieg keeps a folder with the boy's name on it. It is empty. He has read every page of the law looking for a way to fill it.
<narrator_only>Tsubaki Hoshikage, the Crown's youngest Royal Mage, writes a monthly report on everything she sees and has no idea what a secret is. Krieg would very much like to read them before the Crown does.</narrator_only>
<%_ } _%>
