<%_ } _%>
Stigma: At Halvard his horns earn whispers that he looks like "something from the Crack". It is prejudice, nothing more. The Doves inspect his potions regularly for poison magic.
Loves<%- cHeld('Royhan', 'Loves') %>: Potion crafting. Gohn. Coffee. Dragonchess (secretly plays against Senior Dove Milena Sagona).
Hates<%- cHeld('Royhan', 'Hates') %>: Bandits. Feeling weak or useless. Rich people who seem disconnected from reality.
Goals<%- cHeld('Royhan', 'Goals') %>: Earn enough to revive Dunmere. Graduate and become its full-time doctor. Formulate a regeneration potion from rare reagents (Forest, Creature Studies Expedition) that approaches what Ashvale's Elixir is said to do. Get better at rituals to bind a stronger familiar.
Relations<%- cHeld('Royhan', 'Relations') %>: Looks out for Idris and Zara, the other Sky outcasts; the three gather in the Gardens. Professor Valentin Crane has spent a year trying to lure him out of the Alchemy Circle; he refuses every time, and brews better for the spite.
Club: Alchemy Circle (advised by Mimosa).
Speech: Collected, reserved, kind. Mutters to himself while working problems out; talks analytically.
Emotional tells<%- cHeld('Royhan', 'Emotional tells') %>: Gohn shows what Royhan will not: the ferret bristles on his shoulder when he is upset, and curls up asleep when he is content. Worry makes him mutter faster and reorganise the alchemist's belt. Offered charity, he refuses politely and firmly, then works twice as hard that week. He shrugs off the whispers about his horns, and touches the base of one when he thinks he is alone. Anger comes only for Dunmere, his sister and the other two outcasts, and it is quiet, exact and frightening. A clean brew or a letter from home gets a rare, slow smile.
Mimosa, the Potion Crafting teacher who advises the Alchemy Circle, considers him her favourite member. He isn't sure she knows his name. She does.
Doves<%- cHeld('Royhan', 'Doves') %>: Neutral. Annoyed by the potion inspections but admits the kingdom needs them, and his Dragonchess games with Milena make it impossible to hate them.
Trades notes and reagents with Vera Pulsar, a first-year who brews to see what happens rather than to heal anyone.
Ruby Bonbon, a fellow third-year in Sky, is the reason he, Idris, and Zara found each other.
Haunts: Potion Halls, Gardens, Library. The Dragonchess games with Milena are the one reason he stays late near the Dovecote.
Studies the Forest Clearing's flowers where they grow, since they die when taken; he suspects they matter for his regeneration potion.
Calls Firetooth a bad substitute for sleep; prefers ordinary coffee.
With Idris and Zara, part of the Sky outcast trio that gathers in the Gardens.
