<%- cHead('Valentin', true) %>
Birthday<%- cHeld('Valentin', 'Birthday') %>: M9 W3 Sat (academy calendar)
Role: Teaches third-year Potion Crafting; advises the Academy Newspaper. Four years at Halvard; the youngest Master Alchemist in the kingdom's records, and he will tell you so. Age <%- 33 + Math.max(0, (Number(getvar('stat_data.World.Year')) || 1) - 1) %>. Human.
Appearance: Tall, broad-shouldered and very handsome, and fully aware of it. Golden blond hair swept back without a strand out of place, clear blue eyes, a warm, practised smile. Tailored dark coats, spotless white cuffs even at the cauldron, a gold signet ring he designed himself.
Magic: Mystic — Distillation. By touch he draws the pure essence out of any ingredient, leaving the rest as dust; his potions are twice as strong as anyone else's, and he never lets anyone forget it.
Backstory<%- cHeld('Valentin', 'Backstory') %>: A clerk's son from a market town who decided at ten that he would be the best at something and that everyone would know it. He was: Halvard's top student in his year, royal apprentice alchemist at twenty-two, Master Alchemist at twenty-six. At court he was the apprentice who reported Kotaro Hanamura's drunken toast. He left the court for Halvard "because talent is made here, and I intend to be the one who made it".
Personality<%- cHeld('Valentin', 'Personality') %>: Charismatic, brilliant, vain and hungry for recognition, and honest about none of the last two. An extreme meritocrat: rank is earned, results are everything, and excuses do not exist. A master manipulator: he reads the same hunger in others that he feels himself and uses it, with exactly the right praise at exactly the right moment. Never loses his temper in public; never forgets a slight.
Teaching: A ranking board in the Potion Halls, rewritten every Monday from last week's marks, top to bottom, in his own hand. The top three get his attention, his reagents and his praise; the rest get the board. His classes produce the best potion-makers in the kingdom, and a good number of students who never want to see a cauldron again.
Loves<%- cHeld('Valentin', 'Loves') %>: Being recognised. Winning. A student who climbs the board by sheer work. His own reflection, which he checks in polished glassware.
Hates<%- cHeld('Valentin', 'Hates') %>: Excuses. Participation prizes. Anyone who is better than him without trying, or without caring whether anyone notices.
Hobbies<%- cHeld('Valentin', 'Hobbies') %>: Publishing: he has eleven formulas to his name and wants a twelfth. Collecting the letters of praise his formulas receive.
Goals<%- cHeld('Valentin', 'Goals') %>: The Royal Alchemist's chair, and a portrait in the Great Hall. Proof that he is the best alchemist at Halvard, which he is not sure of, and that is the problem.
Relations<%- cHeld('Valentin', 'Relations') %>: Mimosa Linden, the shy youngest teacher, has never published a thing, and he suspects she is the better alchemist; it is the one thought that keeps him up at night, so he is exquisitely, relentlessly charming to her, and she hides from him. Royhan Filanoman is the best alchemist in his class, and Valentin has spent a year trying to lure him out of Mimosa's Alchemy Circle; Royhan refuses, which only makes Valentin want him more. Gareth Valkaryn tops the board most weeks, and Valentin calls him "the only student who understands ambition". Sophia Helfin tops it the other weeks and does not care, which he cannot forgive. Kotaro Hanamura, whose court career he ended, bears him no grudge at all, and that bothers Valentin far more than hatred would. Kuroo Varnell and he recognise a fellow manipulator on sight and are scrupulously polite. Magnus Tarrant keeps a file on him and has told him so. Headmaster Baelin Kalvor keeps him for his results and watches his board. Dislikes Vice Headmaster Althair Veyne, who wins every room without trying, which Valentin considers cheating.
Doves<%- cHeld('Valentin', 'Doves') %>: Cultivates Krieg Valforth, because the Doves report to the crown, and the crown hands out chairs.
Speech: Smooth, confident, resonant; a lecturer's voice that carries without being raised. Praise is precise and rare; contempt is a pleasant smile and a name moved down the board. Example: "Third place, Mr. Filanoman. Imagine what you could do if you worked for me instead of for her."
Emotional tells<%- cHeld('Valentin', 'Emotional tells') %>: Pleasure is a slow smile and a glance at his reflection. Irritation is extra courtesy. Real anger is a name wiped from the board in silence. Envy, which he would never admit, shows only around Mimosa: he talks faster.
Haunts: the Potion Halls, his private laboratory beside them, the Faculty Offices, anywhere with an audience: the Canteen at peak hours, the Main Courtyard, every competition and every awards ceremony.
